window.ORATIONS = {"Adv1": {"src": "Tempora/Adv1-0", "or": ["Excita, quǽsumus, Dómine, poténtiam tuam, et veni: ut ab imminéntibus peccatórum nostrórum perículis, te mereámur protegénte éripi, te liberánte salvári: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Put forth Your power, O Lord, we beseech You, and come, that with You as our protector we may be rescued from the impending danger of our sins; and with You as our deliverer, may we obtain our salvation. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc sacra nos, Dómine, poténti virtúte mundátos ad suum fáciant purióres veníre princípium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these offerings, O Lord, cleanse us by their mighty power and thus make us come purer before You Who are their author. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Suscipiámus, Dómine, misericórdiam tuam in médio templi tui: ut reparatiónis nostræ ventúra sollémnia cóngruis honóribus præcedámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May we receive Your mercy, O Lord, in the midst of Your temple, and thus prepare with due observance for the coming festal season of our redemption. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Adv2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 4-5; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Excita Dómine corda nostra ad præparándas Unigéniti tui vias; ut per eius advéntum, purificátis tibi méntibus servíre mereámur: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Stir up our hearts, O Lord, to prepare the ways of Your only-begotten Son, so that through His coming we may be able to serve You with purified minds; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Placáre, quǽsumus Dómine, humilitátis nostræ précibus, et hóstiis: et ubi nulla súppetunt suffrágia meritórum, tuis nobis succúrre præsídiis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, we beseech You, O Lord, by the prayers and offerings of our human frailty, and where the support of our own merits is lacking, come to our assistance with Your protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Repléti cibo spiritális alimóniæ, súpplices te Dómine deprecámur: ut huius participatióne mystérii dóceas nos terréna despícere; et amáre cæléstia: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We who have been refreshed by the food of spiritual nourishment, humbly beseech You, O Lord, that through partaking of this sacrament You will teach us to disdain the things of earth and love those of heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Adv3": {"src": "Tempora/Adv3-0", "or": ["Aurem tuam, quǽsumus, Dómine, précibus nostris accómmoda: et mentis nostræ ténebras, grátia tuæ visitatiónis illústra: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Lend Your ear to our prayers, O Lord, we beseech You; and brighten the darkness of our minds by the grace of Your coming. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Devotiónis nostræ tibi, quǽsumus, Dómine, hóstia iúgiter immolétur: quæ et sacri péragat institúta mystérii, et salutáre tuum in nobis mirabíliter operétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, that the gift we dedicate to You, may be sacrificed continually, so that the sacramental rite You have ordained may be fully observed, and the work of Your salvation may be wonderfully effective within us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Implorámus, Dómine, cleméntiam tuam: ut hæc divína subsídia, a vítiis expiátos, ad festa ventúra nos prǽparent. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We entreat You, merciful Lord, that these divine helps may cleanse us from our sins and prepare us for the coming festal season. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Adv3w": {"src": "Tempora/Adv3-3", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut redemptiónis nostræ ventúra sollémnitas et præséntis nobis vitæ subsídia cónferat, et ætérnæ beatitúdinis prǽmia largiátur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the coming feast of our redemption may bring us both help for our present life, and the reward of everlasting happiness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Acépta tibi sint, quǽsumus, Dómine, nostra ieiúnia: quæ et expiándo nos tua grátia dignos effíciant, et ad sempiterna promíssa perdúcant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our fasting, we beseech You, O Lord, be acceptable to You, and by its purifying power make us worthy of Your grace and bring us to the eternal bliss You have promised us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Salutáris tui, Dómine, munere satiáti, súpplices deprecámur: ut, cuius lætámur gustu, renovémur efféctu. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by the sacramental gift of Your salvation, we humbly beseech You, O Lord, that enjoying its savor we may be made new by its action. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Adv3f": {"src": "Tempora/Adv3-5", "or": ["Excita, quǽsumus, Dómine, poténtiam tuam, et veni: ut hi, qui in tua pietáte confídunt, ab omni cítius adversitáte liberéntur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Put forth Your power, O Lord, we beseech You, and come; that those who trust in Your goodness may soon be delivered from all harm. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Munéribus nostris, quaesumus, Dómine, precibúsque suscéptis: et caeléstibus nos munda mystériis, et cleménter exáudi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Tui nos, Dómine, sacraménti libátio sancta restáuret: et a vetustáte purgátos, in mystérii salutáris fáciat transíre consórtium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the devout reception of Your sacrament, O Lord, give us new strength, purge us of our old selves and let us come to share in the mystery of salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Adv3s": {"src": "Tempora/Adv3-6", "or": ["Deus, qui cónspicis, quia ex nostra pravitáte afflígimur: concéde propítius; ut ex tua visitatióne consolémur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who see how we are troubled by our evil tendencies, mercifully grant that we may find consolation in Your coming. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, quǽsumus, Dómine, placátus inténde: ut et devotióni nostræ profíciant et salúti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with favor, we beseech You, O Lord, upon the offerings here before You, that they may be beneficial for our devotion and for our salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, Dómine, Deus noster: ut sacrosáncta mystéria, quæ pro reparatiónis nostræ munímine contulísti; et præsens nobis remédium esse fácias et futúrum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord our God, that the sacrament You have given as the bulwark of our atonement may be made a saving remedy for us in this life and in the life to come. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Adv4": {"src": "Tempora/Adv4-0", "or": ["Excita, quǽsumus, Dómine, poténtiam tuam, et veni: et magna nobis virtúte succúrre; ut per auxílium grátiæ tuæ, quod nostra peccáta præpédiunt, indulgéntia tuæ propitiatiónis accéleret: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Put forth Your power, O Lord, we beseech You, and delay not: and with Your great might come to our aid, so that what is hindered by our sins may be hastened by Your merciful goodness. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, quǽsumus, Dómine, placátus inténde: ut et devotióni nostræ profíciant et salúti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with favor, O Lord, we beseech You, upon the offerings here present, that they may be profitable for our devotion and for our salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis munéribus, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut, cum frequentatióne mystérii, crescat nostræ salútis efféctus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received Your gifts, we beseech You, O Lord, that each partaking of this sacrament may increase within us its saving effect. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Dec24": {"src": "Sancti/12-24", "or": ["Deus, qui nos redemptiónis nostræ ánnua exspectatióne lætíficas: præsta; ut Unigénitum tuum, quem Redemptórem læti suscípimus, veniéntem quoque Iúdicem secúri videámus, Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who gladden us year after year with the expectation of our redemption, grant that we, who now welcome with joy Your only-begotten Son as our Redeemer, may also gaze upon Him without fear when He comes as our judge, our Lord Jesus Christ. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, sicut adoránda Fílii tui natalítia prævenímus, sic eius múnera capiámus sempitérna gaudéntes: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that, as we anticipate the celebration of Your Son’s birthday, so we may joyfully receive His everlasting gifts. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine: unigéniti Fílii tui recensíta nativitáte respiráre; cuius cœlésti mystério páscimur et potámur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, to begin a new life with this commemoration of the birth of Your only-begotten Son, Who gives us food and drink in His heavenly sacrament. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Dec25_1": {"src": "Sancti/12-25m1", "or": ["Deus, qui hanc sacratíssimam noctem veri lúminis fecísti illustratióne claréscere: da, quǽsumus; ut, cuius lucis mystéria in terra cognóvimus, eius quoque gáudiis in cœlo perfruámur: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who have brightened this most holy night with the splendor of the true light, grant, we beseech You, that we may know in heaven the joy of that light which we have known mystically on earth. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, quǽsumus, hodiérnæ festivitátis oblátio: ut, tua gratia largiénte, per hæc sacrosáncta commércia, in illíus inveniámur forma, in quo tecum est nostra substántia: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of this day’s festivity, we beseech You, O Lord, find acceptance with You; that, by the bounty of Your grace, we may, through these sacred dealings, be made like unto Him in Whom our nature is united with You. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, Deus noster: ut, qui Nativitátem Dómini nostri Iesu Christi mystériis nos frequentáre gaudémus; dignis conversatiónibus ad eius mereámur perveníre consórtium: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that we who joyfully celebrate the birth of our Lord Jesus Christ, in this sacrament may gain His companionship by worthy living. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Dec25_2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 21-22; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui nova incarnáti Verbi tui luce perfúndimur; hoc in nostro respléndeat ópere, quod per fidem fulget in mente: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who are bathed in the new light of Your Word made flesh may show forth in our actions that which by faith shines in our minds; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera nostra, quǽsumus Dómine, Nativitátis hodiérnæ mystériis apta provéniant, et pacem nobis semper infúndant: ut sicut homo génitus idem refúlsit et Deus, sic nobis hæc terréna substántia cónferat quod divínum est. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our gifts, we beseech You, O Lord, be fitting for the mysteries of this day's Nativity and ever pour peace into us, that, as He who was born a man shone forth also as God, so this earthly substance may bestow on us what is divine; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Huius nos, Dómine, sacraménti semper nóvitas natális instáuret; cuius Natívitas singuláris humánam répulit vetustátem: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the ever-new birth of this sacrament renew us, O Lord, since His singular birth has driven out our old humanity; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Dec25_3": {"src": "Sancti/12-25m3", "or": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut nos Unigéniti tui nova per carnem Natívitas líberet; quos sub peccáti iugo vetústa sérvitus tenet. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the new birth, in the flesh, of Your only-begotten Son may deliver us whom the bondage of old keeps under the yoke of sin. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Obláta, Dómine, múnera, nova Unigéniti tui Nativitáte sanctífica: nosque a peccatórum nostrórum máculis emúnda. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Make holy the sacrificial gifts we offer, O Lord, and by the new birth of Your only-begotten Son cleanse us from the stains of our sins. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut natus hódie Salvátor mundi, sicut divínæ nobis generatiónis est auctor; ita et immortalitátis sit ipse largítor: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the Saviour of the world, born this day, Who is the author of our birth in godliness, may bestow on us immortal life. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Nat1": {"src": "Tempora/Nat1-0", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, dírige actus nostros in beneplácito tuo: ut in nómine dilécti Fílii tui mereámur bonis opéribus abundáre: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Almighty and eternal God, direct our actions in conformity with Your will, that in the name of Your beloved Son we may be worthy to do good works in abundance. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut óculis tuæ maiestátis munus oblátum, et grátiam nobis piæ devotiónis obtineat, et efféctum beátæ perennitátis acquírat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the gift offered in the sight of Your majesty may obtain for us the grace of reverent devotion and secure us eternal happiness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Per huius, Dómine, operatiónem mystérii, et vitia nostra purgéntur, et iusta desidéria compleántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By the working of this sacrament, O Lord, may our sins be erased and our just desires fulfilled. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Jan1": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 29; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nobis nati Salvatóris diem celebráre concédis octávum: fac nos, quǽsumus, eius perpétua Divinitáte muníri; cuius sumus carnáli commércio reparáti: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who grant us to keep the eighth day from the birth of our Saviour, make us, we beseech You, to be defended by His everlasting Godhead, by whose fellowship in our flesh we have been restored; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta, quǽsumus Dómine, ut per hæc múnera, quæ Dómini nostri Iesu Christi arcánæ Nativitátis mystério gérimus, purificátæ mentis intelligéntiam consequámur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that through these gifts which we offer in the mystery of the hidden Nativity of our Lord Jesus Christ, we may obtain the understanding of a purified mind; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus Dómine: ut quod Salvatóris nostri iteráta festivitáte percépimus; perpétuæ nobis redemptiónis cónferat medicínam: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that what we have received in the renewed feast of our Saviour may bring us the healing of everlasting redemption; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Nat2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 30-31; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui unigénitum Fílium tuum constituísti humáni géneris Salvatórem, et Iesum vocári iussísti: concéde propítius, ut cuius sanctum Nomen venerámur in terris; eius quoque aspéctu perfruámur in cælis: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who appointed Your only-begotten Son to be the Saviour of mankind and commanded that He be called Jesus, mercifully grant that we who venerate His holy Name on earth may also enjoy the sight of Him in heaven; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["In veneratióne Nóminis dilectíssimi Fílii tui Dómini nostri, misericordiárum Pater, devótis méntibus hóstias immolámus, supplíciter deprecántes, ut corda nostra eius Nóminis dulcédine impinguári, et in nullo nisi in te Deo vero delectári fácias. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "In veneration of the Name of Your most beloved Son our Lord, O Father of mercies, we offer these sacrifices with devout minds, humbly beseeching You to make our hearts rich with the sweetness of His Name and to let them delight in nothing but You, the true God; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacrosáncta mystéria, quæ súmpsimus, Dómine, in honórem amabilíssimi Nóminis Fílii tui Dómini nostri Iesu Christi, concéde quǽsumus: ut afféctum nostrum ad hoc salutíferum Nomen Iesu diligéndum inflámment; et ad iubilándum in Deo salutári nostro felíciter promóveant: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that the holy mysteries which we have received in honor of the most lovable Name of Your Son our Lord Jesus Christ may inflame our affection to love this saving Name of Jesus, and happily move us to rejoice in God our Saviour; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Jan5a": {"src": "Sancti/01-05", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, dírige actus nostros in beneplácito tuo: ut in nómine dilécti Fílii tui mereámur bonis opéribus abundáre: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Almighty and everlasting God, do Thou order all our actions in conformity with thy good pleasure, that through the name of thy well-beloved Son, we may worthily abound in all good works. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut óculis tuæ maiestátis munus oblátum, et grátiam nobis piæ devotiónis obtíneat, et efféctum beátæ perennitátis acquírat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech Thee, almighty God, that the offering made in the sight of Thy Majesty may obtain for us the grace of loving devotion, and the reward of a blessed eternity. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Per huius, Dómine, operatiónem mystérii, et vítia nostra purgéntur, et iusta desidéria compleántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By the working of this Mystery, O Lord, may our vices be removed, and our just desires fulfilled. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Epi": {"src": "Sancti/01-06", "or": ["Deus, qui hodiérna die Unigénitum tuum géntibus stella duce revelásti: concéde propítius; ut, qui iam te ex fide cognóvimus, usque ad contemplándam spéciem tuæ celsitúdinis perducámur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who by the guidance of a star this day revealed Your only-begotten Son to the Gentiles; mercifully grant that we who know You now by faith, may come to behold You in glory. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ecclésiæ tuæ, quǽsumus, Dómine, dona propítius intuere: quibus non iam aurum, thus et myrrha profertur; sed quod eisdem munéribus declarátur, immolátur et súmitur, Iesus Christus, fílius tuus, Dóminus noster: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, look favorably upon the gifts of Your Church, which are no longer gifts of gold, frankincense and myrrh, but, as these gifts signify, our offering is Jesus Christ Your Son, our Lord, Who is now sacrifice and food. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, quæ sollémni celebrámus officio, purificátæ mentis intellegéntia consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that, by the understanding of our minds made pure, we may grasp what we celebrate by these solemn rites. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Epi1": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 36-38; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, qui Maríæ et Ioseph súbditus, domésticam vitam ineffabílibus virtútibus consecrásti: fac nos, utriúsque auxílio, Famíliæ sanctæ tuæ exémplis ínstrui; et consórtium cónsequi sempitérnum: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, You Who while subject to Mary and Joseph, hallowed family life with virtues beyond description, grant us by their combined intercession, that, having been taught by the example of the Holy Family, we may attain unto their everlasting companionship; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Placatiónis hóstiam offérimus tibi, Dómine, supplíciter deprecántes: ut, per intercessiónem Deíparæ Vírginis cum beáto Ioseph, famílias nostras in pace et grátia tua fírmiter constítuas. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "In appeasement, O Lord, we offer You this sacrifice, humbly praying that through the intercession of the Virgin Mother of God, and that of St. Joseph, You will establish our households in Your peace and grace; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quos cæléstibus réficis sacraméntis, fac, Dómine Iesu, sanctæ Famíliæ tuæ exémpla iúgiter imitári; ut, in hora mortis nostræ, occurrénte gloriósa Vírgine Matre tua cum beáto Ioseph, per te in ætérna tabernácula récipi mereámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, Lord Jesus, that those whom You refresh with the heavenly sacrament may ever imitate the example of Your Holy Family, so that at the hour of our death, with the glorious Virgin Mary and St. Joseph welcoming us, we may be found worthy to be received into Your everlasting home; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Epi2": {"src": "Tempora/Epi2-0", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui cœléstia simul et terréna moderáris: supplicatiónes pópuli tui cleménter exáudi; et pacem tuam nostris concéde tempóribus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, everlasting God, You Who govern both the heavens and the earth, graciously hear the humble prayers of Your people and grant us Your peace all the days of our life. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblata, Dómine, múnera sanctífica: nosque a peccatórum nostrórum máculis emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hallow our offerings, O Lord, and cleanse us from the stains of our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Augeátur in nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, tuæ virtútis operatio: ut divínis vegetáti sacraméntis, ad eórum promíssa capiénda, tuo múnere præparémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You that the effects of Your power may ever increase within us; and, strengthened by the divine sacrament, we may be prepared by Your grace to lay hold of what it promises. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Epi3": {"src": "Tempora/Epi3-0", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, infirmitatem nostram propítius réspice: atque, ad protegéndum nos, déxteram tuæ maiestátis exténde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, look with favor upon our weakness, and stretch forth the right hand of Your majesty to help and defend us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, Dómine, quǽsumus, emúndet nostra delícta: et, ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this offering, O Lord, we beseech You, wipe away our transgressions, and make holy the minds and bodies of Your servants for celebrating this sacrifice. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quos tantis, Dómine, largíris uti mystériis: quǽsumus; ut efféctibus nos eórum veráciter aptáre dignéris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, as You grant us to use this great sacrament, deign, we beseech You, to make us truly worthy of its fruits. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Epi4": {"src": "Tempora/Epi4-0", "or": ["Deus, qui nos, in tantis perículis constitútos, pro humána scis fragilitáte non posse subsístere: da nobis salútem mentis et córporis; ut ea, quæ pro peccátis nostris pátimur, te adiuvánte vincámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who know that our human frailty cannot stand fast against the great dangers that beset us, grant us health of mind and body, that with your help we may overcome what we suffer on account of our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut huius sacrifícii munus oblátum fragilitátem nostram ab omni malo purget semper et múniat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of this sacrifice may always cleanse and strengthen the weakness of our nature. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Múnera tua nos, Deus, a delectatiónibus terrenis expédiant: et cœléstibus semper instáurent aliméntis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your gifts, O God, free us from the attraction of earthly pleasures and give us new strength through Your heavenly nourishment. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Epi5": {"src": "Tempora/Epi5-0", "or": ["Famíliam tuam, quǽsumus, Dómine, contínua pietáte custódi: ut, quæ in sola spe grátiæ cœléstis innítitur, tua semper protectióne muniátur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You to keep Your household continually under Your mercy: that as it leans only upon the hope of Your heavenly grace, so it may always be protected by Your mighty power. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, placatiónis offérimus: ut et delícta nostra miserátus absólvas, et nutántia corda tu dírigas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, this sacrifice of atonement, that You would mercifully absolve our sins and direct our faltering hearts. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut illíus salutáris capiámus efféctum, cuius per hæc mystéria pignus accépimus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We pray You, almighty God, that we may obtain that salvation whose pledge we have received in this divine sacrament. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Epi6": {"src": "Tempora/Epi6-0", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, semper rationabília meditántes, quæ tibi sunt plácita, et dictis exsequámur et factis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, ever to think of spiritual things and in every word and work always to do what is well pleasing in Your sight. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc nos oblátio, Deus, mundet, quǽsumus, et rénovet, gubérnet et prótegat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this offering, O God, we beseech You, cleanse and renew us, govern and protect us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cœléstibus, Dómine, pasti delíciis: quǽsumus; ut semper éadem, per quæ veráciter vívimus, appétimus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Nourished by Your heavenly food, O Lord, we beseech You that we may always strive after those things that give us true life. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "7a": {"src": "Tempora/Quadp1-0", "or": ["Preces pópuli tui, quǽsumus, Dómine, cleménter exáudi: ut, qui iuste pro peccátis nostris afflígimur, pro tui nóminis glória misericórditer liberémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, graciously hear the prayers of Your people, that we who are justly punished for our sins may be mercifully delivered for the glory of Your name. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Munéribus nostris, quǽsumus, Dómine, precibúsque suscéptis: et cœléstibus nos munda mystériis, et cleménter exáudi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Fidéles tui, Deus, per tua dona firméntur: ut eadem et percipiéndo requírant, et quæréndo sine fine percípiant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your faithful people, O God, be strengthened by Your gifts; that by receiving them, they may still desire them, and by desiring them, may evermore receive them. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "6a": {"src": "Tempora/Quadp2-0", "or": ["Deus, qui cónspicis, quia ex nulla nostra actióne confídimus: concéde propítius; ut, contra advérsa ómnia, Doctóris géntium protectióne muniámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who see that we put no trust in anything we do, mercifully grant that by the protection of the Doctor of the Gentiles we may be defended against all adversity. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátum tibi, Dómine, sacrifícium, vivíficet nos semper et múniat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this sacrifice which we offer You, O Lord, ever give us new life and protection. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súpplices te rogámus, omnípotens Deus: ut, quos tuis réficis sacraméntis, tibi étiam plácitis móribus dignánter deservíre concédas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O almighty God, grant, we humbly beseech You, that those whom You refresh with Your sacrament may also worthily serve You in a way that is well pleasing to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "5a": {"src": "Tempora/Quadp3-0", "or": ["Preces nostras, quǽsumus, Dómine, cleménter exáudi: atque, a peccatórum vínculis absolútos, ab omni nos adversitáte custódi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, mercifully hear our prayers; loose us from the chains of our sins and keep us from all adversity. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, Dómine, quǽsumus, emúndet nostra delícta: et, ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these offerings, O Lord, we beseech You, wash away our sins; may it sanctify the bodies and souls of Your servants for the celebration of this sacrifice. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui coeléstia aliménta percépimus, per hæc contra ómnia adversa muniámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the Bread of heaven, may by it be protected from all adversity. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "5aw": {"src": "Tempora/Quadp3-3", "or": ["Præsta, Dómine, fidélibus tuis: ut ieiuniórum veneránda sollémnia, et cóngrua pietáte suscípiant, et secúra devotióne percúrrant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, O Lord, that Your faithful people may, with true piety, undertake the time-honored custom of fasting and may carry it out with unwavering devotion. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Fac nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, his munéribus offeréndis conveniénter aptári: quibus ipsíus venerábilis sacraménti celebrámus exórdium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, make us truly fit to offer these gifts by which we celebrate the beginning of this venerable observance. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Percépta nobis, Dómine, prǽbeant sacraménta subsídium: ut tibi grata sint nostra ieiúnia, et nobis profíciant ad medélam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrament that we have received, O Lord, give us help, that our fast may be pleasing to You and may profit us as a healing remedy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Inclinántes se, Dómine, maiestáti tuæ propitiátus inténde: ut qui divíno múnere sunt refécti; cæléstibus semper nutriántur auxíliis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously, O Lord, upon those who bow down before Your majesty, that they who have been refreshed by Your divine gift may ever be nourished by heavenly help; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 58"]}, "5ah": {"src": "Tempora/Quadp3-4", "or": ["Deus, qui culpa offénderis, pæniténtia placáris: preces pópuli tui supplicántis propítius réspice; et flagélla tuæ iracúndiæ, quæ pro peccátis nostris merémur, avérte. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, offended by sin, and appeased by penitence, graciously hear the prayers of Your people as they entreat You to turn away from us the scourges of anger that we have deserved because of our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, Dómine, quǽsumus, inténde placátus: ut et devotióni nostræ profíciant et salúti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You to look with favor upon these offerings before You, and may they be profitable to our devotion as well as to our salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cœléstis doni benedictióne percépta: súpplices te, Deus omnípotens, deprecámur; ut hoc idem nobis et sacraménti causa sit et salútis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We humbly beseech You, almighty God, that, having received the blessing of Your heavenly gift, it may be for us the source of sacramental grace and of salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Parce Dómine, parce pópulo tuo: ut dignis flagellatiónibus castigátus; in tua miseratióne respíret: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Spare, O Lord, spare Your people, that, chastised by deserved scourges, they may find relief in Your mercy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 59"]}, "5af": {"src": "Tempora/Quadp3-5", "or": ["Inchoáta ieiúnia, quǽsumus, Dómine, benígno favore proséquere: ut observántiam, quam corporáliter exhibémus, méntibus étiam sincéris exercére valeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your kindly favor, we beseech You, O Lord, accompany the fast we have begun, that we may be able to practice with a pure mind what we perform bodily. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícium, Dómine, observántiæ quadragesimális, quod offérimus, præsta, quǽsumus: ut tibi et mentes nostras reddat accéptas, et continéntiæ promptióris nobis tríbuat facultátem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, O Lord, we beseech You, that as we offer the sacrifice of Lent, our hearts may be made acceptable to You; and the sacrifice may give us greater willingness for self-denial. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Spíritum nobis, Dómine, tuæ caritátis infúnde: ut, quos uno pane cœlésti satiásti, tua fácias pietáte concórdes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Fill us, O Lord, with the spirit of Your love, to unite in charity those whom You have filled with one and the same heavenly Bread. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Tuére Dómine pópulum tuum, et ab ómnibus peccátis cleménter emúnda: quia nulla ei nocébit advérsitas; si nulla ei dominétur iníquitas: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Protect Your people, O Lord, and mercifully cleanse them from all their sins; for no adversity shall harm them if no wickedness has dominion over them; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 61"]}, "5as": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 61-63; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "sp": ["Fidéles tui, Deus, per tua dona firméntur: ut éadem et percipiéndo requírant; et quæréndo sine fine percípiant: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your faithful, O God, be strengthened by Your gifts, that by receiving them they may seek them still, and seeking them may receive them for ever; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 63"], "or": ["Adésto Dómine supplicatiónibus nostris; et concéde, ut hoc solémne ieiúnium, quod animábus corporibúsque curándis salúbriter institútum est, devóto servítio celebrémus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hearken, O Lord, to our supplications, and grant that we may keep with devout service this solemn fast, which was wholesomely instituted for the healing of souls and bodies; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præpara nos, quǽsumus Dómine, huius abstinéntiæ festívis offíciis: ut hæc sacrifícia veneránda sóbriis semper méntibus celebrémus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Prepare us, we beseech You, O Lord, by the festal offices of this abstinence, that we may ever celebrate these venerable sacrifices with sober minds; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cæléstis vitæ múnere vegetáti, quǽsumus Dómine: ut quod est nobis in præsénti vita mystérium; fiat æternitátis auxílium: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Quickened by the gift of the heavenly life, we beseech You, O Lord, that what is for us a mystery in this present life may become our help for eternity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Quad1": {"src": "Tempora/Quad1-0", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam ánnua quadragesimáli observatióne puríficas: præsta famíliæ tuæ; ut, quod a te obtinére abstinéndo nítitur, hoc bonis opéribus exsequátur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who purify Your Church by the yearly Lenten observance, grant to Your household that what they strive to obtain from You by abstinence, they may achieve by good works. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícium quadragesimális inítii sollémniter immolámus, te, Dómine, deprecántes: ut, cum epulárum restrictióne carnálium, a noxiis quoque voluptátibus temperémus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer these sacrificial gifts at the beginning of Lent, praying You, O Lord, that while we practice restraint in the use of bodily food, we may also refrain from harmful pleasures. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tui nos, Dómine, sacraménti libátio sancta restáuret: et a vetustáte purgátos, in mystérii salutáris fáciat transíre consórtium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the holy offering of Your sacrament renew us, O Lord, and cause us to be purified from our old ways and come to the fellowship of this saving mystery. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Quad1m": {"src": "Tempora/Quad1-1", "or": ["Convérte nos, Deus, salutáris noster: et, ut nobis ieiúnium quadragesimále profíciat, mentes nostras cœléstibus ínstrue disciplínis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, our Saviour, direct our minds by Your heavenly teaching, so that the Lenten fast may profit us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi, Dómine, obláta sanctífica: nosque a peccatórum nostrórum máculis emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify the gifts offered unto You, O Lord, and cleanse us from the stains of our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Salutáris tui, Dómine, múnere satiáti, súpplices exorámus: ut, cuius lætámur gustu, renovémur efféctu. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by the sacramental gift of Your salvation, we humbly beseech You, O Lord, that, enjoying its savor, we may be made new by its action. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Absólve, quǽsumus Dómine, nostrórum víncula peccatórum; et quidquid pro eis merémur propitiátus avérte: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Loose, we beseech You, O Lord, the bonds of our sins, and graciously turn away whatever we deserve for them; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 67"]}, "Quad1t": {"src": "Tempora/Quad1-2", "or": ["Réspice, Dómine, famíliam tuam: et præsta; ut apud te mens nostra tuo desidério fúlgeat, quæ se carnis maceratióne castígat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look upon Your household, O Lord, and grant that our minds, chastened by mortification of the flesh, may, because of their desire for You, shine in Your sight. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátis, quǽsumus, Dómine, placáre munéribus: et a cunctis nos defénde perículis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, we beseech You, O Lord, by the gifts we offer, and safeguard us from all dangers. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut illíus salutáris capiámus efféctum, cuius per hæc mystéria pignus accépimus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we may obtain that salvation whose pledge we have received in this divine sacrament. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Ascéndant ad te, Dómine, preces nostræ; et ab Ecclésia tua cunctam repélle nequítiam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our prayers ascend to You, O Lord, and drive away all wickedness from Your Church; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 69"]}, "Quad1w": {"src": "Tempora/Quad1-3", "or": ["Preces nostras, quǽsumus, Dómine, cleménter exáudi: et contra cuncta nobis adversántia, déxteram tuæ maiestátis exténde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Mercifully hear our prayers, we beseech You, O Lord; and stretch forth the right hand of Your Majesty against all things hostile to us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, placatiónis offérimus: ut et delícta nostra miserátus absólvas, et nutántia corda tu dírigas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, this sacrifice of atonement, that You would mercifully absolve our sins and direct our faltering hearts. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tui, Dómine, perceptióne sacraménti, et a nostris mundémur occúltis, et ab hóstium liberémur insídiis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By receiving Your sacrament, O Lord, may we be cleansed of our secret sins and delivered from the snares of our enemies. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Mentes nostras, quǽsumus Dómine, lúmine tuæ claritátis illústra; ut vidére possímus quæ agénda sunt, et quæ recta sunt ágere valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Enlighten our minds, we beseech You, O Lord, with the light of Your brightness, that we may see what we ought to do and be able to do what is right; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 71"]}, "Quad1h": {"src": "Tempora/Quad1-4", "or": ["Devotiónem pópuli tui, quǽsumus, Dómine, benígnus inténde: ut, qui per abstinéntiam macerántur in córpore, per fructum boni óperis reficiántur in mente. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, look graciously upon the fervor of Your people, who mortify themselves in the flesh through abstinence: that they may be refreshed in mind by the fruit of these good works. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícia, Dómine, quǽsumus, propénsius ista nos salvent, quæ medicinálibus sunt institúta ieiúniis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these sacrificial gifts, we beseech You, O Lord, be the more effective unto our salvation since they have been aided by wholesome fasting. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tuórum nos, Dómine, largitáte donórum, et temporálibus attólle præsídiis, et rénova sempitérnis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your generous grace sustain and help us, O Lord, in this world and make us new for the world to come. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, pópulis christiánis, et quæ profiténtur agnóscere; et cæléste munus dilígere, quod frequéntant: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, to Christian peoples both to understand what they profess and to love the heavenly gift which they so often receive; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 73"]}, "Quad1f": {"src": "Tempora/Quad1-5", "or": ["Esto, Dómine, propítius plebi tuæ: et, quam tibi facis esse devótam, benígno réfove miserátus auxílio. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be merciful to Your people, O Lord, and as You give them the grace to serve You, make them new by Your loving help. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, múnera nostris obláta servítiis: et tua propítius dona sanctífica. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, we beseech You, O Lord, the offerings which we, Your servants, bring You, and graciously hallow the gifts which are Yours. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Per huius, Dómine, operatiónem mystérii, et vítia nostra purgéntur, et iusta desidéria compleántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By the working of this sacrament, O Lord, may our sins be erased, and our just desires fulfilled. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Exáudi nos miséricors Deus; et méntibus nostris grátiæ tuæ lumen osténde: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear us, O merciful God, and show to our minds the light of Your grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 75"]}, "Quad1s": {"src": "Tempora/Quad1-6", "or": ["Pópulum tuum, quǽsumus, Dómine, propítius réspice: atque ab eo flagélla tuæ iracúndiæ cleménter avérte. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously upon Your people, we beseech You, O Lord, and in Your mercy turn away from them the scourges of Your wrath. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præséntibus sacrifíciis, quǽsumus, Dómine, ieiúnia nostra sanctífica: ut, quod observántia nostra profitétur extrínsecus, intérius operétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify our fasts by the sacrificial gifts here present, we beseech You, O Lord, that what our observance outwardly professes may be inwardly accomplished. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sanctificatiónibus tuis, omnípotens Deus, et vítia nostra curéntur, et remédia nobis ætérna provéniant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By the workings of Your sanctifying power, almighty God, may our vices be cured and eternal remedies provided for us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Quad2": {"src": "Tempora/Quad2-0", "or": ["Deus, qui cónspicis omni nos virtúte destítui: intérius exteriúsque custódi; ut ab ómnibus adversitátibus muniámur in córpore, et a pravis cogitatiónibus mundémur in mente. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who see how we are deprived of all strength, guard us inwardly and outwardly, that in body we may be protected against all misfortunes, and in mind cleansed of evil thoughts. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, Dómine, quǽsumus, inténde placátus: ut et devotióni nostræ profíciant et salúti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with favor, we beseech You, O Lord, upon the offerings here before You, that they may be beneficial for our devotion and for our salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súpplices te rogámus, omnípotens Deus: ut quos tuis réficis sacraméntis, tibi étiam plácitis móribus dignánter deservíre concédas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O almighty God, we humbly beseech You that those whom You refresh with Your sacrament may also worthily serve You in a way pleasing to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Quad2m": {"src": "Tempora/Quad2-1", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut família tua, quæ se, affligéndo carnem, ab aliméntis ábstinet: sectándo iustítiam, a culpa ieiúnet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that Your servants who discipline the body by fasting from food, may strive after righteousness by abstaining from sin. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, Dómine, placatiónis et laudis, tua nos protectióne dignos effíciat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this sacrificial gift offered in appeasement and praise, O Lord, make us worthy of Your protection. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Hæc nos commúnio, Dómine, purget a crímine: et cœléstis remédii fáciat esse consórtes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this Communion, O Lord, cleanse us of sin, and make us partakers of heavenly healing. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Adésto supplicatiónibus nostris omnípotens Deus: et quibus fidúciam sperándæ pietátis indúlges; consuétæ misericórdiæ tríbue benígnus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hearken to our supplications, almighty God, and graciously grant the effect of Your wonted mercy to those to whom You give confidence to hope for Your loving-kindness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 82"]}, "Quad2t": {"src": "Tempora/Quad2-2", "or": ["Pérfice, quǽsumus, Dómine, benígnus in nobis observántiæ sanctæ subsídium: ut, quæ te auctóre faciénda cognóvimus, te operánte impleámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Mercifully help us, O Lord, to fulfill this holy observance, that by Your grace we may carry out those things which we have learned, on Your word, must be done. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sanctificatiónem tuam nobis, Dómine, his mystériis operáre placátus: quæ nos et a terrénis purget vítiis, et ad cœléstia dona perdúcat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through this sacrament, O Lord, graciously perform Your holy work, that it may cleanse us of earthly vices and bring us to heavenly rewards. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ut sacris, Dómine, reddámur digni munéribus: fac nos tuis, quǽsumus, semper obœdíre mandátis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, O Lord, ever to obey Your commandments, that we may be worthy of Your sacred gifts. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Propitiáre Dómine supplicatiónibus nostris: et animárum nostrárum medére languóribus; ut, remissióne percépta, in tua semper benedictióne lætémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, O Lord, by our supplications, and heal the sickness of our souls, that, having received forgiveness, we may ever rejoice in Your blessing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 84"]}, "Quad2w": {"src": "Tempora/Quad2-3", "or": ["Pópulum tuum, quǽsumus, Dómine, propítius réspice: et, quos ab escis carnálibus prǽcipis abstinére, a nóxiis quoque vítiis cessáre concéde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look mercifully upon Your people, we beseech You, O Lord, and grant that they whom You command to abstain from food, may also refrain from harmful vices. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias, Dómine, quas tibi offérimus, propítius réspice: et, per hæc sancta commércia, víncula peccatórum nostrórum absólve. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with favor upon the sacrificial gifts we offer You, O Lord, and through this holy exchange loosen the bonds of our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis, Dómine, sacraméntis: ad redemptiónis ætérnæ, quǽsumus, proficiámus augméntum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received Your sacrament, O Lord, may we make progress, we beseech You, toward our everlasting salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Deus innocéntiæ restitútor et amátor, dírige ad te tuórum corda servórum: ut spíritus tui fervóre concépto, et in fide inveniántur stábiles; et in ópere effícaces: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, restorer and lover of innocence, direct to Yourself the hearts of Your servants, that, kindled with the fervor of Your Spirit, they may be found steadfast in faith and effective in work; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 86"]}, "Quad2h": {"src": "Tempora/Quad2-4", "or": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, auxílium grátiæ tuæ: ut, ieiúniis et oratiónibus conveniénter inténti, liberémur ab hóstibus mentis et córporis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, the help of Your grace, that, being intent, as we ought, upon fasting and prayer, we may be delivered from the enemies of soul and of body. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsénti sacrifício, nómini tuo nos, Dómine, ieiúnia dicáta sanctíficent: ut, quod observántia nostra profitétur extérius, intérius operétur efféctu. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the fasting dedicated to Your Name, O Lord, make us holy for the present sacrifice, that what our Lenten observance outwardly shows may work within us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Grátia tua nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, non derelínquat: quæ et sacræ nos déditos fáciat servitúti, et tuam nobis opem semper acquírat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your grace, we beseech You, O Lord, never forsake us, but make us devoted to Your holy service and ever obtain for us Your aid. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Adésto Dómine fámulis tuis, et perpétuam benignitátem largíre poscéntibus: ut iis, qui te auctóre et gubernatóre gloriántur, et congregáta restáures; et restauráta consérves: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be present, O Lord, to Your servants, and bestow Your unfailing kindness on those who ask it, that for those who glory in You as their maker and ruler You may restore what You have gathered and keep what You have restored; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 87"]}, "Quad2f": {"src": "Tempora/Quad2-5", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, sacro nos purificánte ieiúnio, sincéris méntibus ad sancta ventúra fácias perveníre. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that with the sacred fast to purify us, we may with sincere hearts reach the coming feast. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc in nobis sacrifícia, Deus, et actióne permáneant, et operatióne firméntur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, may this sacrifice which is offered, stay in us and accomplish lasting effects. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Fac nos, quǽsumus, Dómine: accépto pígnore salútis ætérnæ, sic téndere congruénter; ut ad eam perveníre possímus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that we who have received the pledge of everlasting salvation, may properly direct our course so that we may be able to attain our goal. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, pópulo tuo salútem mentis et córporis: ut bonis opéribus inhæréndo; tuæ semper virtútis mereátur protectióne deféndi: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, to Your people health of mind and body, that, cleaving to good works, they may ever deserve to be defended by the protection of Your power; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 90"]}, "Quad2s": {"src": "Tempora/Quad2-6", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus, Dómine, nostris efféctum ieiúniis salutárem: ut castigátio carnis assúmpta, ad nostrárum vegetatiónem tránseat animárum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant that our fasting may be beneficial to us, we beseech You, O Lord, so that by chastising our flesh we may obtain strength for our souls. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["His sacrifíciis, Dómine, concéde placátus: ut, qui própriis orámus absólvi delíctis, non gravémur extérnis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Appeased by these sacrificial gifts, O Lord, grant that we who pray for absolution from our own sins may not be burdened by those which are foreign to us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménti tui, Dómine, divína libátio, penetrália nostri cordis infúndat: et sui nos partícipes poténter effíciat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrament of which we have partaken, O Lord, penetrate the depths of our hearts and make us share in its strength. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Famíliam tuam, quǽsumus Dómine, contínua pietáte custódi: ut quæ in sola spe grátiæ cæléstis innítitur; cælésti étiam protectióne muniátur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Guard Your household, we beseech You, O Lord, with unceasing kindness, that, as it leans on the hope of heavenly grace alone, it may also be defended by heavenly protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 93"]}, "Quad3": {"src": "Tempora/Quad3-0", "or": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus, vota humílium réspice: atque, ad defensiónem nostram, déxteram tuæ maiestátis exténde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, hear the prayers of the humble and stretch forth the right hand of Your majesty to protect us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, Dómine, quǽsumus, emúndet nostra delícta: et, ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this offering, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse us of our sins, and make holy the bodies and minds of Your servants for the celebration of the sacrificial rite. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["A cunctis nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, reátibus et perículis propitiátus absólve: quos tanti mystérii tríbuis esse partícipes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be merciful, O Lord, we beseech You, and free from guilt and danger those whom You grant to share in this great sacrament. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Quad3m": {"src": "Tempora/Quad3-1", "or": ["Córdibus nostris, quǽsumus, Dómine, grátiam tuam benígnus infúnde: ut, sicut ab escis carnálibus abstinémus; ita sensus quoque nostros a nóxiis retrahámus excéssibus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, in Your mercy, pour forth Your grace into our hearts, that, as we abstain from material food, so may we restrain our senses from sin. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Munus, quod tibi, Dómine, nostræ servitútis offérimus, tu salutáre nobis pérfice sacraméntum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, make for us a sacrament of salvation the gift of homage which we offer to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens et miséricors Deus: ut, quod ore contíngimus, pura mente capiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty and merciful God, that what we take into our mouth, we may eat with a pure heart. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Subvéniat nobis, Dómine, misericórdia tua: ut ab imminéntibus peccatórum nostrórum perículis, te mereámur protegénte éripi; te liberánte salvári: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your mercy, O Lord, come to our help, that with You as our protector we may deserve to be rescued from the threatening dangers of our sins, and with You as our deliverer to be saved; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 97"]}, "Quad3t": {"src": "Tempora/Quad3-2", "or": ["Exáudi nos, omnípotens et miséricors Deus: et continéntiæ salutáris propítius nobis dona concéde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear us, almighty and merciful God, and in Your kindness grant us the graces of self-denial that lead to salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Per hæc véniat, quǽsumus, Dómine, sacraménta nostræ redemptiónis efféctus: qui nos et ab humánis rétrahat semper excéssibus, et ad salutária dona perdúcat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, may this sacrament result in our redemption; keep us always from the sins of our human nature, and bring us the gift of salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacris, Dómine, mystériis expiáti: et véniam, quǽsumus, consequámur et grátiam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, that, purified by this holy sacrament, we may obtain both forgiveness and grace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Tua nos, Dómine, protectióne defénde; et ab omni semper iniquitáte custódi: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Defend us, O Lord, by Your protection, and keep us ever from all iniquity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 98"]}, "Quad3w": {"src": "Tempora/Quad3-3", "or": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut salutáribus ieiúniis erudíti, a nóxiis quoque vítiis abstinéntes, propitiatiónem tuam facílius impetrémus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that, improved by wholesome fasting, and thus abstaining from harmful sin, we may the more readily receive Your mercy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, preces pópuli tui cum oblatiónibus hostiárum: et tua mystéria celebrántes, ab ómnibus nos defénde perículis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, receive, we beseech You, the prayers of Your people with offerings of sacrifices, and defend us, who celebrate Your mysteries, from all dangers. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sanctíficet nos, Dómine, qua pasti sumus, mensa cœléstis: et a cunctis erróribus expiátos, supérnis promissiónibus reddat accéptos. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the heavenly banquet with which we have been nourished, make us holy, O Lord; may it be an atonement for all our sins, and make us worthy of the heavenly promises. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui protectiónis tuæ grátiam quǽrimus; liberáti a malis ómnibus, secúra tibi mente serviámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who seek the grace of Your protection may be freed from all evils and serve You with a secure mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 100"]}, "Quad3f": {"src": "Tempora/Quad3-5", "or": ["Ieiúnia nostra, quǽsumus, Dómine, benígno favóre proséquere: ut, sicut ab aliméntis abstinémus in córpore; ita a vítiis ieiunémus in mente. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, graciously be with us during this fast, and, we beseech You, help our spirit to abstain from sin as our body fasts from food. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Réspice, quǽsumus, Dómine, propítius ad múnera, quæ sacrámus: ut tibi grata sint, et nobis salutária semper exsístant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with favor, we beseech You, O Lord, upon the gifts we offer You, that they may be pleasing to you and ever helpful to our salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Huius nos, Dómine, percéptio sacraménti mundet a crimine: et ad cœléstia regna perdúcat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the reception of this sacrament, O Lord, cleanse us from sin and bring us into the heavenly kingdom. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui in tua protectióne confídimus; cuncta nobis adversántia, te adiuvánte, vincámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who trust in Your protection may, by Your help, overcome all that is against us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 105"]}, "Quad3s": {"src": "Tempora/Quad3-6", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui se, affligéndo carnem, ab aliméntis ábstinent; sectándo iustítiam, a culpa ieiúnent. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who chastise our flesh by abstaining from food, may fast from sin by striving after righteousness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut huius sacrifícii munus oblátum, fragilitátem nostram ab omni malo purget semper et múniat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of this sacrifice may always cleanse and strengthen the weakness of our nature. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut inter eius membra numerémur, cuius córpori communicámus et sánguini: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we may be numbered among the members of Him, Whose Body and Blood we receive in communion. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Prætende Dómine fidélibus tuis déxteram cæléstis auxílii: ut te toto corde perquírant; et quæ digne póstulant, cónsequi mereántur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Stretch forth, O Lord, to Your faithful the right hand of heavenly help, that they may seek You with their whole heart and deserve to obtain what they worthily ask; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 108"]}, "Quad4": {"src": "Tempora/Quad4-0", "or": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui ex mérito nostræ actiónis afflígimur, tuæ grátiæ consolatióne respirémus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who justly suffer for our sins may find relief in the help of Your grace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, Dómine, quǽsumus, inténde placátus: ut et devotióni nostræ profíciant et salúti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with favor, we beseech You, O Lord, upon the offerings here before You, that they may be beneficial for our devotion and salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus, miséricors Deus: ut sancta tua, quibus incessánter explémur, sincéris tractémus obséquiis, et fidéli semper mente sumámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, merciful God, that we may treat with sincere reverence, and consume with heartfelt faith Your sacrament, which ever fills us to overflowing. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Quad4m": {"src": "Tempora/Quad4-1", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, observatiónes sacras ánnua devotióne recoléntes, et córpore tibi placeámus et mente. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who devoutly keep the sacred observances year by year, may be pleasing to You both in body and soul. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátum tibi, Dómine, sacrifícium vivíficet nos semper et múniat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this sacrifice that we offer You, O Lord, ever give us new life and protection. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis, Dómine, salutáribus sacraméntis: ad redemptiónis ætérnæ, quǽsumus, proficiámus augméntum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, that as we have partaken of Your saving sacraments, we may make progress toward our everlasting salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Deprecatiónem nostram, quǽsumus Dómine, benígnus exáudi: et quibus supplicándi præstas afféctum; tríbue defensiónis auxílium: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously hear our prayer, we beseech You, O Lord, and to those to whom You give the desire to pray grant the help of Your defence; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 112"]}, "Quad4t": {"src": "Tempora/Quad4-2", "or": ["Sacræ nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, observatiónis ieiúnia: et piæ conversatiónis augméntum, et tuæ propitiatiónis contínuum præstent auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacred practice of fasting, we beseech You, O Lord, win for us increased holiness of life and the continuing help of Your mercy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, Dómine, quǽsumus, emúndet nostra delícta: et, ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this offering, O Lord, we beseech You, wipe away our sins, and make holy the minds and bodies of Your servants for celebrating this Sacrifice. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Huius nos, Dómine, percéptio sacraménti mundet a crímine: et ad cæléstia regna perdúcat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the reception of this sacrament, O Lord, cleanse us from guilt and bring us to the kingdom of heaven. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Miserére Dómine pópulo tuo; et contínuis tribulatiónibus laborántem, propítius respiráre concéde: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Have mercy, O Lord, on Your people, and graciously grant them relief, toiling as they are under continual tribulations; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 114"]}, "Quad4w": {"src": "Tempora/Quad4-3", "or": ["Deus, qui et iustis prǽmia meritórum et peccatóribus per ieiúnium véniam præbes: miserére supplícibus tuis; ut reátus nostri conféssio indulgéntiam valeat percípere delictórum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who graciously grant to the righteous the rewards of their merits, and to sinners forgiveness through fasting, have mercy upon Your humble servants, so that, confessing our guilt, we may obtain pardon for our transgressions. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súpplices te rogámus, omnípotens Deus: ut his sacrifíciis peccáta nostra mundéntur; quia tunc veram nobis tríbuis et mentis et córporis sanitátem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We humbly entreat You, almighty God, that these sacrificial gifts may cleanse us from sin, for in this way You grant us true health of soul and body. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta, quæ súmpsimus, Dómine, Deus noster: et spirituálibus nos répleant aliméntis, et corporálibus tueántur auxíliis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrament we have received, O Lord, both fill us with spiritual nourishment and sustain us with bodily aid. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Páteant aures misericórdiæ tuæ, Dómine, précibus supplicántium: et ut peténtibus desideráta concédas; fac eos quæ tibi sunt plácita postuláre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let the ears of Your mercy, O Lord, be open to the prayers of Your suppliants, and that You may grant their desires to those who ask, make them ask such things as please You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 117"]}, "Quad4h": {"src": "Tempora/Quad4-4", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, quos ieiúnia votíva castígant, ipsa quoque devótio sancta lætíficet; ut, terrénis afféctibus mitigátis, facílius cœléstia capiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who are chastising the flesh by fasting, may rejoice in this holy practice and thus, with earthly passions subdued, we may the more readily direct our thoughts to heavenly things. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Purífica nos, miséricors Deus: ut Ecclésiæ tuæ preces, quæ tibi gratæ sunt, pia múnera deferéntes, fiant expiátis méntibus gratióres. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Cleanse us, O merciful God, so that the prayers of Your Church, which we bring You as a pleasing gift, may be even more pleasing to You, once our hearts are purified. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cœléstia dona capiéntibus, quǽsumus, Dómine: non ad iudícium proveníre patiáris, quæ fidélibus tuis ad remédium providísti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech you, do not allow the heavenly gifts, which You have given for healing Your faithful people, to become a reason for condemning those who receive them. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Pópuli tui Deus institútor et rector: peccáta, quibus impugnátur, expélle; ut semper tibi plácitus, et tuo munímine sit secúrus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, founder and ruler of Your people, drive away the sins by which they are assailed, that they may ever be pleasing to You and secure under Your protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 119"]}, "Quad4f": {"src": "Tempora/Quad4-5", "or": ["Deus, qui ineffabílibus mundum rénovas sacraméntis: præsta, quǽsumus; ut Ecclésia tua et ætérnis profíciat institútis, et temporálibus non destituátur auxíliis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who by your wondrous sacraments renew the world, grant that Your church may benefit from Your eternal decrees and not be deprived of temporal help. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera nos, Dómine, quǽsumus, obláta puríficent: et te nobis iugiter fáciant esse placátum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the gifts we offer, O Lord, cleanse us, we beseech You, that You may be always merciful to us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Hæc nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, participátio sacraménti: et a propriis reátibus indesinénter expédiat, et ab ómnibus tueátur advérsis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the reception of this sacrament, we beseech You, O Lord, always free us from sin and protect us from all that works against us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui infirmitátis nostræ cónscii, de tua virtúte confídimus; sub tua semper pietáte gaudeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who, conscious of our weakness, trust in Your strength, may ever rejoice under Your loving care; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 122"]}, "Quad4s": {"src": "Tempora/Quad4-6", "or": ["Fiat, Dómine, quǽsumus, per grátiam tuam fructuósus nostræ devotiónis afféctus: quia tunc nobis próderunt suscépta ieiúnia, si tuæ sint plácita pietáti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Make fruitful, we beseech You, O Lord, the zeal of our fervent devotion; for only if it pleases You shall the fasting we have undertaken be of benefit to us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblatiónibus nostris, quǽsumus, Dómine, placáre suscéptis: et ad te nostras étiam rebélles compélle propítius voluntátes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously accept our offerings, O Lord, we beseech You, and mercifully direct our still rebellious wills to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tua nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, sancta puríficent: et operatióne sua tibi plácitos esse perfíciant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your holy sacrament cleanse us, we beseech You, O Lord, and may its power make us pleasing to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Deus, qui sperántibus in te miseréri pótius éligis, quam irásci: da nobis digne flere mala, quæ fécimus; ut tuæ consolatiónis grátiam inveníre mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who choose rather to show mercy than to be angry with those who hope in You, grant us worthily to weep for the evils we have done, that we may deserve to find the grace of Your consolation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 124"]}, "Quad5": {"src": "Tempora/Quad5-0", "or": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus, famíliam tuam propítius réspice: ut, te largiénte, regátur in córpore; et, te servánte, custodiátur in mente. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously upon Your household, almighty God, we beseech You, that by Your grace we may be governed in body, and by Your protection safeguarded in mind. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc múnera, quǽsumus Dómine, et víncula nostræ pravitátis absólvant, et tuæ nobis misericórdiæ dona concílient. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these offerings, we beseech You, O Lord, loose the bonds of our wickedness, and obtain for us the gifts of Your mercy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Adésto nobis, Dómine, Deus noster: et, quos tuis mystériis recreásti, perpétuis defénde subsídiis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Stand by us, O Lord our God, and protect by Your everlasting help those to whom You have given new strength through Your sacrament. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Quad5m": {"src": "Tempora/Quad5-1", "or": ["Sanctífica, quǽsumus, Dómine, nostra ieiúnia: et cunctárum nobis indulgéntiam propítius largíre culpárum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, make holy our fasting, and graciously lavish upon us forgiveness for all our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde nobis, Dómine, Deus noster: ut hæc hóstia salutáris et nostrórum fiat purgátio delictórum, et tuæ propitiátio maiestátis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, O Lord our God, that this saving sacrifice may cleanse us of our sins and gain us the favor of Your majesty. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménti tui, quǽsumus, Dómine, participátio salutáris, et purificatiónem nobis tríbuat, et medélam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrament of salvation which we have received, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse and restore us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, pópulo tuo salútem mentis et córporis: ut bonis opéribus inhæréndo; tua semper mereátur protectióne deféndi: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, to Your people health of mind and body, that, cleaving to good works, they may ever deserve to be defended by Your protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 127"]}, "Quad5t": {"src": "Tempora/Quad5-2", "or": ["Nostra tibi, Dómine, quǽsumus, sint accépta ieiúnia: quæ nos et expiándo grátia tua dignos effíciant; et ad remédia perdúcant ætérna. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our fasting be acceptable to You, we beseech You, O Lord; may it be atonement for our sins, make us worthy of Your grace, and lead us to the everlasting remedy of the life to come. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, deférimus immolándas: quæ temporálem consolatiónem signíficent; ut promíssa non desperémus ætérna. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we bring You the gifts for sacrifice, as tokens of consolation in this life, so that we may not despair of Your eternal promises. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, quæ divína sunt, iúgiter exsequéntes, donis mereámur cœléstibus propinquáre. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God that by constantly performing these holy acts, we may be worthy to come closer to the gifts of heaven. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, perseverántem in tua voluntáte famulátum; ut in diébus nostris et mérito, et número, pópulus tibi sérviens augeátur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, persevering service in Your will, that in our days the people serving You may grow both in merit and in number; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 129"]}, "Quad5w": {"src": "Tempora/Quad5-3", "or": ["Sanctificáto hoc ieiúnio, Deus, tuórum corda fidélium miserátor illústra: et quibus devotiónis præstas afféctum, præbe supplicántibus pium benígnus audítum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "In Your mercy, O Lord, may this hallowing fast enlighten the hearts of Your faithful people, and since You have given them the desire to serve You, lend a gracious ear to their prayers. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Annue, miséricors Deus: ut hóstias placatiónis et laudis sincéro tibi deferámus obséquio. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O merciful God, permit us to offer in sincere submission the gift of satisfaction and praise. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cœléstis doni benedictióne percépta: súpplices te, Deus omnípotens, deprecámur; ut hoc idem nobis et sacraménti causa sit et salútis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We who have shared in the blessing of the heavenly gift humbly pray You, almighty God, that it may be for us the source of sacramental grace and salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Adésto supplicatiónibus nostris omnípotens Deus: et quibus fidúciam sperándæ pietátis indúlges; consuétæ misericórdiæ tríbue benígnus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hearken to our supplications, almighty God, and graciously grant the effect of Your wonted mercy to those to whom You give confidence to hope for Your loving-kindness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 131"]}, "Quad5h": {"src": "Tempora/Quad5-4", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut dígnitas condiciónis humánæ, per immoderántiam sauciáta, medicinális parsimóniæ stúdio reformétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the dignity of human nature, weakened by excessive self-indulgence, may be restored by the earnest practice of healing self-denial. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Dómine, Deus noster, qui in his pótius creatúris, quas ad fragilitátis nostræ subsídium condidísti, tuo quoque nómini múnera iussísti dicánda constítui: tríbue, quǽsumus; ut et vitæ nobis præséntis auxílium et æternitátis effíciant sacraméntum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, our God, Who have especially commanded that these created things, which You have fashioned for the support of our weakness, should also be used as offerings dedicated to Your Name, grant we beseech You, that they may provide for us help in the present life and may be a pledge of life eternal. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quod ore súmpsimus, Dómine, pura mente capiámus: et de munere temporáli, fiat nobis remédium sempitérnum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May we receive with pure mind, O Lord, what we have taken by mouth, and as a gift in time, may it become for us a remedy for eternity. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Esto, quǽsumus, Dómine, propítius plebi tuæ: ut quæ tibi non placent respuéntes; tuórum pótius repleántur delectatiónibus mandatórum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be gracious, we beseech You, O Lord, to Your people, that, rejecting what displeases You, they may rather be filled with delight in Your commandments; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 133"]}, "Quad5f": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 314-315 (In Compassione B.M.V.); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "sp": ["Concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui protectiónis tuæ grátiam quǽrimus; liberáti a malis ómnibus, secúra tibi mente serviámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who seek the grace of Your protection may be freed from all evils and serve You with a secure mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 135"], "or": ["Intervéniat pro nobis, quǽsumus Dómine Iesu Christe, nunc et in hora mortis nostræ apud tuam cleméntiam beáta Virgo María Mater tua: cuius sacratíssimam ánimam in hora benedíctæ passiónis tuæ dolóris gládius pertransívit; et in gloriósa resurrectióne tua ingens gáudium lætificávit: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the blessed Virgin Mary, Your Mother, intercede for us with Your mercy, we beseech You, O Lord Jesus Christ, now and at the hour of our death, she whose most holy soul was pierced by the sword of sorrow in the hour of Your blessed passion, and gladdened with great joy in Your glorious resurrection; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Offérimus tibi preces et hóstias, Dómine Iesu Christe, humíliter supplicántes: ut qui transfixiónem dulcíssimi spíritus beátæ Maríæ Matris tuæ précibus recensémus; suo suorúmque sub cruce Sanctórum consórtium multiplicáto piíssimo intervéntu, méritis mortis tuæ, méritum cum Beátis habeámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You prayers and sacrifices, O Lord Jesus Christ, humbly beseeching You that we who by our prayers recall the piercing of the most sweet spirit of blessed Mary Your Mother may, by the manifold and most loving intercession of her and of the Saints with her beneath the Cross, have through the merits of Your death a share with the Blessed; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacrifícia, quæ súmpsimus, Dómine Iesu Christe, transfixiónem Matris tuæ et Vírginis devóte celebrántes; nobis ímpetrent apud cleméntiam tuam omnis boni salutáris efféctum: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifices which we have received, O Lord Jesus Christ, as we devoutly celebrate the piercing of Your Mother and Virgin, obtain for us from Your mercy the effect of every saving good; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Quad5s": {"src": "Tempora/Quad5-6", "or": ["Profíciat, quǽsumus, Dómine, plebs tibi dicáta piæ devotiónis afféctu: ut sacris actiónibus erudíta, quanto maiestáti tuæ fit grátior, tanto donis potióribus augeátur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, may the people dedicated to You desire to serve You more and more, that, taught by these sacred rites, they may be enriched by more precious gifts as they grow in favor with Your majesty. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["A cunctis nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, reátibus et perículis propitiátus absólve: quos tanti mystérii tríbuis esse consórtes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be propitiated, we beg You, O Lord, and pardon all our offenses, whom You grant to be sharers in so great a mystery. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divíni múneris largitáte satiáti, quǽsumus, Dómine, Deus noster: ut huius semper participatióne vivámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, our God, we beseech You, that we who have been filled with the riches of Your divine gift may always find life when we partake of it. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Tueátur, quǽsumus Dómine, déxtera tua pópulum deprecántem: et purificátum dignánter erúdiat; ut consolatióne præsénti ad futúra bona profíciat: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your right hand, we beseech You, O Lord, protect the people who pray to You, purify them and graciously instruct them, that by present consolation they may advance towards the good things to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 137"]}, "Quad6": {"src": "Tempora/Quad6-0", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui humáno géneri, ad imitándum humilitátis exémplum, Salvatórem nostrum carnem súmere et crucem subíre fecísti: concéde propítius; ut et patiéntiæ ipsíus habére documénta et resurrectiónis consórtia mereámur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, eternal God, Who, to provide mankind an example of humility for it to imitate, willed that the Saviour should assume our flesh and suffer death upon the Cross, mercifully grant that we may be found worthy of the lesson of His endurance and the fellowship of His resurrection. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut óculis tuæ maiestátis munus oblátum, et grátiam nobis devotiónis obtíneat, et efféctum beátæ perennitátis acquírat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the gift offered in the sight of Your majesty may obtain for us the grace of reverent devotion and assure us eternal happiness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Per huius, Dómine, operatiónem mystérii: et vitia nostra purgéntur, et iusta desidéria compleántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By the working of this sacred rite, O Lord, may our sins be erased and our just desires fulfilled. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Quad6m": {"src": "Tempora/Quad6-1", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui in tot advérsis ex nostra infirmitáte defícimus; intercedénte unigéniti Fílii tui passióne respirémus: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech thee, almighty God, that we who fail through our weakness in so many difficulties, may be relieved through the pleading of the Passion of thy only-begotten Son. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc sacrifícia nos, omnípotens Deus, poténti virtúte mundátos, ad suum fáciant purióres veníre princípium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these sacrifices, almighty God, make us, whom thou cleansest by thy mighty power, to approach their source with greater purity. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Prǽbeant nobis, Dómine, divínum tua sancta fervórem: quo eórum páriter et actu delectémur et fructu. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let thy holy mysteries, O Lord, inspire us with divine fervor, that we may delight both in their celebration and in their fruit. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Ádiuva nos Deus salutáris noster; et ad benefícia recolénda, quibus nos instauráre dignátus es, tríbue veníre gaudéntes: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Help us, O God our Saviour, and grant that we may come with joy to the remembrance of the benefits by which You have deigned to renew us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 148"]}, "Quad6t": {"src": "Tempora/Quad6-2", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus: da nobis ita Domínicæ passiónis sacraménta perágere; ut indulgéntiam percípere mereámur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, grant us so to celebrate the mysteries of our Lord's Passion, that we may deserve to obtain forgiveness. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícia nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, propénsius ista restáurent: quæ medicinálibus sunt institúta ieiúniis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these sacrifices, we beseech thee, O Lord, which are observed along with health-giving fasts, speedily restore us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sanctificatiónibus tuis, omnípotens Deus: et vítia nostra curéntur, et remédia nobis sempitérna provéniant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By thy holy mysteries, almighty God, may our vices be cured, and everlasting healing be granted to us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Tua nos misericórdia, Deus, et ab omni subreptióne vetustátis expúrget; et capáces sanctæ novitátis effíciat: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your mercy, O God, cleanse us from all the deceits of our old nature and make us capable of holy newness of life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 153"]}, "Quad6w": {"src": "Tempora/Quad6-3", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui nostris excéssibus incessánter afflígimur, per unigéniti Fílii tui passiónem liberémur: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant we beseech thee Almighty God, that we who are continually afflicted by reason of our waywardness, may be delivered by the Passion of thy only-begotten Son. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, munus oblátum, et dignánter operáre: ut, quod passiónis Fílii tui, Dómini nostri, mystério gérimus, piis afféctibus consequámur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, we beseech thee, O Lord, the gift we offer; and graciously effect, that what we celebrate in mystery of the Passion of thy Son, we may by holy dispositions obtain. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Largíre sénsibus nostris, omnípotens Deus: ut, per temporálem Fílii tui mortem, quam mystéria veneránda testántur, vitam te nobis dedísse perpétuam confidámus. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant to us, almighty God, to feel that through the temporal death of thy Son which these venerable mysteries testify, we have assurance, that thou hast given us eternal life. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "sp": ["Réspice, quǽsumus Dómine, super hanc famíliam tuam: pro qua Dóminus noster Iesus Christus non dubitávit mánibus tradi nocéntium; et Crucis subíre torméntum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look down, we beseech You, O Lord, upon this Your family, for which our Lord Jesus Christ did not hesitate to be delivered into the hands of the wicked and to undergo the torment of the Cross; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 160"]}, "Quad6h": {"src": "Tempora/Quad6-4", "or": ["Deus, a quo et Iudas reátus sui pœnam, et confessiónis suæ latro prǽmium sumpsit, concéde nobis tuæ propitiatiónis efféctum: ut, sicut in passióne sua Iesus Christus, Dóminus noster, divérsa utrísque íntulit stipéndia meritórum; ita nobis, abláto vetustátis erróre, resurrectiónis suæ grátiam largiátur: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, from whom Judas received the punishment of his guilt, and the thief the reward of his confession: grant unto us the full fruit of Thy clemency; that even as in His Passion, our Lord Jesus Christ gave to each a retribution according to his merits, so having taken away our old sins, He may bestow upon us the grace of His Resurrection. Who with Thee liveth and reigneth in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ipse tibi, quǽsumus, Dómine sancte, Pater omnípotens, ætérne Deus, sacrifícium nostrum reddat accéptum, qui discípulis suis in sui commemoratiónem hoc fíeri hodiérna traditióne monstrávit, Iesus Christus, Fílius tuus, Dóminus noster: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech Thee, O holy Lord, Father almighty, everlasting God, that He Himself may render our Sacrifice acceptable to Thee, Who, by the tradition of today, taught His disciples to do this in remembrance of Him, Jesus Christ, Thy Son, our Lord, Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti vitálibus aliméntis, quǽsumus, Dómine, Deus noster: ut, quod témpore nostræ mortalitátis exséquimur, immortalitátis tuæ múnere consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Strengthened with life-giving Food, we beseech Thee, O Lord, our God, that what we do in our mortal life may bring us to the reward of life immortal with Thee. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc0": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc0-0", "or": ["Deus, qui hodiérna die per Unigénitum tuum æternitátis nobis áditum, devícta morte, reserásti: vota nostra, quæ præveniéndo aspíras, étiam adiuvándo proséquere. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, on this day, through Thine only-begotten Son, hast conquered death, and thrown open to us the gate of everlasting life, give effect by thine aid to our desires, which Thou dost anticipate and inspire Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, preces pópuli tui cum oblatiónibus hostiárum: ut, Paschálibus initiáta mystériis, ad æternitátis nobis medélam, te operánte, profíciant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech Thee, O Lord, accept the prayers of Thy people together with the Sacrifice they offer, that what has been begun by the Paschal Mysteries, by Thy working may profit us unto eternal healing. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Spíritum nobis, Dómine, tuæ caritátis infúnde: ut, quos sacraméntis paschálibus satiásti, tua fácias pietáte concordes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Pour forth upon us, O Lord, the spirit of Thy love, that, by Thy loving kindness, Thou mayest make to be of one mind those whom Thou hast satisfied with the Paschal Sacraments. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc0m": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc0-1", "or": ["Deus, qui sollemnitáte pascháli, mundo remédia contulísti: pópulum tuum, quǽsumus, cœlésti dono proséquere; ut et perféctam libertátem consequi mereátur, et ad vitam profíciat sempitérnam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who dost heal the sick world by the solemn gladness of the Passover, continue, we beseech thee, to pour forth thine heavenly gifts upon thy people, till the same shall bring them into perfect liberty, and finally avail them unto life everlasting. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, preces pópuli tui cum oblatiónibus hostiárum: ut, paschálibus initiáta mystériis, ad æternitátis nobis medélam, te operánte, profíciant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Adept, O Lord we beseech thee, the prayers with the sacrifices of the people, and grant that what we have begun at these paschal mysteries, may with thy help be a remedy for life eternal. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Spíritum nobis, Dómine, tuæ caritátis infúnde: ut, quos sacraméntis paschálibus satiásti, tua fácias pietáte concórdes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Pour forth upon us, O Lord, the spirit of Thy love, that, by Thy loving kindness, Thou mayest make to be of one mind those whom Thou hast satisfied with the Paschal Sacraments. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc0t": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc0-2", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam novo semper fœtu multíplicas: concéde fámulis tuis; ut sacraméntum vivéndo téneant, quod fide percepérunt. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who art ever multiplying the Children of thy Church, grant unto the same thy servants that they may lead the rest of their lives according to this beginning wherein Thou hast given them faith to receive the Sacrament of the New Birth. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, fidélium preces cum oblatiónibus hostiárum: ut, per hæc piæ devotiónis offícia, ad cœléstem glóriam transeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, O Lord, the prayers and the sacrifice of thy faithful; that by these services of pious devotion, we may come to heavenly glory. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut paschális percéptio sacraménti, contínua in nostris méntibus persevéret. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech thee, Almighty God, that the grace of the paschal sacrament which we have received may ever abide in our souls. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc0w": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc0-3", "or": ["Deus, qui nos Resurrectiónis Domínicæ ánnua solemnitáte lætíficas: concéde propítius; ut per temporália festa, quæ ágimus, perveníre ad gáudia ætérna mereámur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who gladden us with the annual solemnity of the Lord's Resurrection, mercifully grant that by celebrating these temporal feasts, we may become worthy to attain eternal joys. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícia, Dómine, paschálibus gáudiis immolámus: quibus Ecclésia tua mirabíliter et páscitur et nutrítur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Amidst the joys of Easter, we offer unto thee, O Lord, the sacrifice wherewith thy Church is wonderfully fed and nourished. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ab omni nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, vetustáte purgátos: sacraménti tui veneránda percéptio in novam tránsferat creatúram: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech Thee, that we, reverently receiving thy Sacrament, may be cleansed from all our former defilement, and become a new creature in Thee. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc0h": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc0-4", "or": ["Deus, qui diversitátem géntium in confessióne tui nóminis adunásti: da, ut renátis fonte baptísmatis una sit fides méntium, et píetas actiónum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who dost make all nations, how diverse soever they be, to become one family in giving of praise to thy Name, grant unto all them that are born again in the fountain of baptism to live ever in oneness of faith, and godliness of works. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, múnera populórum tuórum propítius: ut, confessióne tui nóminis et baptísmate renováti, sempitérnam beatitúdinem consequántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously receive, we beseech thee, O Lord, the offering of thy people, and grant that they who are renewed by baptism and the confession of thy name, may attain to everlasting happiness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Exáudi, Dómine, preces nostras: ut redemptiónis nostræ sacrosáncta commércia, et vitæ nobis cónferant præséntis auxílium, et gáudia sempitérna concílient.", "O Lord, hear our prayers; that the holy channels of our redemption may obtain us help in this our present life, and secure us eternal joys."]}, "Pasc0f": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc0-5", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui paschále sacraméntum in reconciliatiónis humánæ fœ́dere contulísti: da méntibus nostris; ut, quod professióne celebrámus, imitémur efféctu. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, in the Easter sacrament thou instituted the covenant, whereby thou forgavest mankind; grant to our souls, that what we outwardly profess we may show forth in our deeds. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias, quǽsumus, Dómine, placátus assúme: quas et pro renatórum expiatióne peccáti deférimus, et pro acceleratióne cœléstis auxílii. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "In thy forgiving mercy, O Lord we pray, accept the sacrifice which we offer, to atone for the sins of those who are born anew and to hasten the giving of thy heavenly help. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Réspice, quǽsumus, Dómine, pópulum tuum: et, quem ætérnis dignátus es renováre mystériis, a temporálibus culpis dignánter absólve. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech thee, behold thy people, and as thou hast decided to quicken them with the mysteries of eternity, mercifully free them from the sins committed in time. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc0s": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc0-6", "or": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui festa paschália venerándo égimus, per hæc contíngere ad gáudia ætérna mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech thee, O Almighty God, that we who have kept worshipfully the Easter solemnities, may at last worthily pass from keeping Feasts unto thee here to the everlasting jubilation hereafter. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, Dómine, semper nos per hæc mystéria paschália gratulári: ut contínua nostræ reparatiónis operátio perpétuæ nobis fiat causa lætítiæ. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us O Lord, we beseech thee, ever to rejoice in these Paschal mysteries, that, by the continual application of our redemption we may come to endless happiness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Redemptiónis nostræ múnere vegetáti, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut, hoc perpétuæ salútis auxílio, fides semper vera profíciat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Invigorated by the gift of redemption, we beseech thee, O Lord, that by this means of eternal salvation, the true faith may prosper evermore. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc1": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc1-0", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui paschália festa perégimus, hæc, te largiénte, móribus et vita teneámus.", "Grant, we beseech Thee, almighty God, that we who have celebrated the Paschal Feast, may, by Thy bounty, retain its fruits in our daily habits and behavior. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe múnera, Dómine, quǽsumus, exsultántis Ecclésiæ: et, cui causam tanti gáudii præstitísti, perpétuæ fructum concéde lætítiæ.", "Receive, we beseech Thee, O Lord, the gifts of Thine exultant Church: and to her whom Thou hast given cause for so great joy, grant the fruit of perpetual happiness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, Dómine, Deus noster: ut sacrosáncta mystéria, quæ pro reparatiónis nostræ munímine contulísti; et præsens nobis remédium esse fácias et futúrum.", "We beseech Thee, O Lord, our God, to make the most holy Mysteries which Thou hast given us as a defense of our renewal, a remedy for us now, and in the future. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc2": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc2-0", "or": ["Deus, qui in Fílii tui humilitáte iacéntem mundum erexísti: fidélibus tuis perpétuam concéde lætítiam; ut, quos perpétuæ mortis eripuísti cásibus, gáudiis fácias pérfrui sempitérnis. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, by the humility of Thy Son, didst lift up a fallen world, grant unending happiness to Thy faithful: that those whom Thou hast snatched from the perils of endless death, Thou mayest cause to rejoice in everlasting days. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Benedictiónem nobis, Dómine, cónferat salutárem sacra semper oblátio: ut, quod agit mystério, virtúte perfíciat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this holy offering, O Lord, always bring to us Thy healing blessing: that what it represents in a Mystery, it may accomplish with power. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, vivificatiónis tuæ grátiam consequéntes, in tuo semper múnere gloriémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant unto us, we beseech Thee, almighty God, that having received the grace of a new life, we may ever glory in Thy gift. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc2w": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc2-3", "or": ["Deus, qui ineffábili providéntia beátum Ioseph sanctíssimæ Genetrícis tuæ sponsum elígere dignátus es: præsta, quǽsumus; ut, quem protectórem venerámur in terris, intercessórem habére mereámur in cœlis: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "God, Who in thine unspeakable foreknowledge didst choose thy blessed servant Joseph to be the husband of thine Own most holy Mother; mercifully grant that now that he is in heaven with thee, we who on earth do reverence him for our Defender, may worthily be holpen by the succour of his prayers to thee on our behalf; Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sanctíssimæ Genetrícis tuæ sponsi patrocínio suffúlti, rogámus, Dómine, cleméntiam tuam: ut corda nostra fácias terréna cuncta despícere, ac te verum Deum perfécta caritáte dilígere: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Supported by the patronage of the spouse of thy most holy Mother, we beseech thy clemency, O Lord, that thou wouldst make our hearts despise all earthly things and love thee, the true God with perfect charity. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divíni múneris fonte refécti, quǽsumus, Dómine, Deus noster: ut, sicut nos facis beáti Ioseph protectióne gaudére; ita, eius méritis et intercessióne, cœléstis glóriæ fácias esse partícipes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed at the fount of divine blessing, we beseech thee, O Lord our God, that as thou dost gladden us by the protection of blessed Joseph, so by his merits and intercession thou woulds make us partakers of his heavenly glory. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc3": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc3-0", "or": ["Deus, qui errántibus, ut in viam possint redíre iustítiæ, veritátis tuæ lumen osténdis: da cunctis, qui christiána professióne censéntur, et illa respúere, quæ huic inimíca sunt nómini; et ea, quæ sunt apta, sectári. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty God, Who showest to them that be in error the light of thy truth, to the intent that they may return into the way of righteousness grant unto all them that are admitted into the fellowship of Christ's Religion, that they may eschew those things that are contrary to their profession, and follow all such things as are agreeable to the same. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["His nobis, Dómine, mystériis conferátur, quo, terréna desidéria mitigántes, discámus amáre cœléstia. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Confer on us, O Lord, by these mysteries the moderation of our earthly desires: and teach us to love the things of heaven. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta quæ súmpsimus, quǽsumus, Dómine: et spirituálibus nos instáurent aliméntis, et corporálibus tueántur auxíliis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the Sacraments which we have received, O Lord, we ask, refresh us with spiritual nourishment, and preserve as with bodily assistance. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc4": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc4-0", "or": ["Deus, qui fidélium mentes uníus éfficis voluntátis: da pópulis tuis id amáre quod prǽcipis, id desideráre quod promíttis; ut inter mundánas varietátes ibi nostra fixa sint corda, ubi vera sunt gáudia. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, of Whom it cometh that the minds of thy faithful people be all of one will, grant unto the same thy people that they may love the thing which Thou commandest, and desire that which Thou dost promise, that so, amid the sundry and manifold changes of the world, our hearts may surely there be fixed, where true joys are to be found. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, qui nos, per huius sacrifícii veneránda commércia, uníus summæ divinitátis partícipes effecísti: præsta, quǽsumus; ut, sicut tuam cognóscimus veritátem, sic eam dignis móribus assequámur.", "O God, who by the august communion of this sacrifice hast make us partakers of one Sovereign Godhead, grant we beseech thee, that as we know thy truth, so we may follow it up by worthy behavior."], "pc": ["Adésto nobis, Dómine, Deus noster: ut per hæc, quæ fidéliter súmpsimus, et purgémur a vítiis et a perículis ómnibus eruámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Stand by us, O Lord, our God, that by what we have faithfully received we may be cleansed from our vices and rescued from all dangers. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc5": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc5-0", "or": ["Deus, a quo bona cuncta procédunt, largíre supplícibus tuis: ut cogitémus, te inspiránte, quæ recta sunt; et, te gubernánte, éadem faciámus.", "O God, from Whom all good things do come, grant to us thy humble servants that by thy holy inspiration we may think those things that be good, and by thy merciful guiding may perform the same."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, fidélium preces cum oblatiónibus hostiárum: ut, per hæc piæ devotiónis offícia, ad cœléstem glóriam transeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, the prayers of thy faithful with offerings of victims, that by these services of pious devotion we may pass to heavenly glory. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tríbue nobis, Dómine, cæléstis mensæ virtúte satiátis: et desideráre, quæ recta sunt, et desideráta percípere. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, O Lord, fed with the virtue of a heavenly table, to desire what is right, and to gain what we desire. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Litaniis": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc5-1", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui in afflictióne nostra de tua pietáte confídimus; contra advérsa ómnia, tua semper protectióne muniámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech thee, O Almighty God, that we who in our tribulation are yet of good cheer because of thy loving-kindness, may find thee mighty to save from all dangers. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc múnera, quǽsumus, Dómine, et víncula nostræ pravitátis absólvant, et tuæ nobis misericórdiæ dona concílient.", "We beseech thee, O Lord, that these offerings may both loosen the bonds of our wickedness and obtain for us the gift of mercy."], "pc": ["Vota nostra, quǽsumus, Dómine, pio favóre proséquere: ut, dum dona tua in tribulatióne percípimus, de consolatióne nostra in tuo amóre crescámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Mercifully grant our prayers, we beseech thee, O Lord, that while we receive thy gifts in tribulation, we may be comforted, and so increase in thy love. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Asc": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc5-4", "or": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui hodiérna die Unigénitum tuum, Redemptórem nostrum, ad cœlos ascendísse crédimus; ipsi quoque mente in cœléstibus habitémus. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech thee, Almighty God, that like as we do believe thine Only-Begotten Son our Saviour to have this day ascended into the heavens, so we may also in heart and mind thither ascend, and with Him continually dwell. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, múnera, quæ pro Fílii tui gloriósa Ascensióne deférimus: et concéde propítius; ut a præséntibus perículis liberémur, et ad vitam perveniámus ætérnam. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, the gifts which we offer for the glorious Ascension of thy Son, and mercifully grant that we may be delivered from present dangers and attain eternal life. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus, omnípotens et miséricors Deus: ut, quæ visibílibus mystériis suménda percépimus, invisíbili consequámur efféctu.", "Grant us, we beseech thee, almighty and merciful God, that what we have taken and received in visible mysteries, may profit us by its invisible effects."]}, "Pasc6": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc6-0", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus: fac nos tibi semper et devótam gérere voluntátem; et maiestáti tuæ sincéro corde servíre. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, give us a will ever dedicated to You, and a true heart to serve Your majesty. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícia nos, Dómine, immaculáta puríficent: et méntibus nostris supérnæ grátiæ dent vigórem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this pure sacrifice cleanse us, O Lord, and impart to our minds the strength of heavenly grace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Repléti, Dómine, munéribus sacris: da, quǽsumus; ut in gratiárum semper actióne maneámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We who have been filled with heavenly gifts beseech You, O Lord, grant us to continue giving thanks to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent0": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc7-0", "or": ["Deus, qui hodiérna die corda fidélium Sancti Spíritus illustratióne docuísti: da nobis in eódem Spíritu recta sápere; et de eius semper consolatióne gaudére. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who on this day have taught the hearts of the faithful by the light of the Holy Spirit, grant us by that Holy Spirit Himself, to know what is right and ever to rejoice in His help. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, quǽsumus, Dómine, obláta sanctífica: et corda nostra Sancti Spíritus illustratióne emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify these offerings, we beseech You, O Lord, and cleanse our hearts by the light of the Holy Spirit. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sancti Spíritus, Dómine, corda nostra mundet infúsio: et sui roris íntima aspersióne fecúndet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the inpouring of the Holy Spirit cleanse our hearts, O Lord, and make them fertile through the dew He sprinkles upon them. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent0m": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc7-1", "or": ["Deus, qui Apóstolis tuis Sanctum dedísti Spíritum: concéde plebi tuæ piæ petitiónis efféctum; ut, quibus dedísti fidem, largiáris et pacem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who gave the Holy Spirit to Your apostles, grant that the devout prayers of Your people may be effective and, as You have given us faith, also grant us peace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Propítius, Dómine, quǽsumus, hæc dona sanctífica: et, hóstiæ spiritális oblatióne suscépta, nosmetípsos tibi pérfice munus ætérnum.", "Graciously hallow these gifts, we beseech You, O Lord, and accepting the offering of the spiritual sacrifice, make us also an eternal offering to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Adésto, quǽsumus, Dómine, pópulo tuo: et, quem mystériis cœléstibus imbuísti, ab hóstium furóre defénde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be near to Your people, we beseech You, O Lord, and defend against the fury of the enemy those whom You have penetrated with Your heavenly sacrament. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent0t": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc7-2", "or": ["Adsit nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, virtus Spíritus Sancti: quæ et corda nostra cleménter expúrget, et ab ómnibus tueátur advérsis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let the power of the Holy Spirit be present within us, O Lord, graciously to cleanse our hearts as well as to guard us from all harm. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Puríficet nos, quǽsumus. Dómine, múneris præséntis oblátio: et dignos sacra participatióne effíciat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of this gift here before You, O Lord, make us pure and worthy to take part in this sacred rite. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Mentes nostras, quǽsumus, Dómine, Spíritus Sanctus divínis réparet sacraméntis: quia ipse est remíssio ómnium peccatórum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the Holy Spirit, we beseech You, O Lord, renew our minds through the heavenly sacrament, for He Himself is the forgiveness of all sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent0w": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc7-3", "or": ["Mentes nostras, quǽsumus, Dómine, Paráclitus, qui a te procédit, illúminet: et indúcat in omnem, sicut tuus promísit Fílius, veritátem: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the Paraclete Who proceeds from You, enlighten our minds, we beseech You, O Lord, and guide us to all truth, as Your Son has promised. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, munus oblátum: et dignánter operáre; ut, quod mystériis ágimus, piis efféctibus celebrámus.", "Accept, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts we offer, and graciously bring it about that we may practice by a holy life what we perform here by a sacred rite. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Suméntes, Dómine, cœléstia sacraménta, quǽsumus cleméntiam tuam: ut quod temporáliter gérimus ætérnis gáudiis consequámur", "As we receive Your heavenly sacrament we beseech You, merciful Lord, may we reap in the joys of eternity the fruits of what we perform in this life. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent0f": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc7-5", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus, Ecclésiæ tuæ, miséricors Deus: ut, Sancto Spíritu congregáta, hostíli nullátenus incursióne turbétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant to Your Church, we beseech You, merciful God, that, united by the Holy Spirit, she may in no way be harmed by any assault of the enemy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícia, Dómine, tuis obláta conspéctibus, ignis ille divínus absúmat, qui discipulórum Christi, Fílii tui, per Spíritum Sanctum corda succéndit. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrificial gifts offered in Your sight, O Lord, be consumed by that divine fire which the Holy Spirit enkindled in the hearts of the disciples of Christ, Your Son. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, sacri dona mystérii: humíliter deprecántes; ut, quæ in tui commemoratiónem nos fácere præcepísti, in nostræ profíciant infirmitátis auxílium: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We who have received the gift of Your Blessed Sacrament, O Lord, humbly pray that what You have taught us to do in commemoration of You, may profit and help us in our weakness. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent0s": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc7-6", "or": ["Méntibus nostris, quǽsumus, Dómine, Spíritum Sanctum benígnus infúnde: cuius et sapiéntia cónditi sumus, et providéntia gubernámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously pour into our minds, we beseech You, O Lord, the Holy Spirit, Whose wisdom created us and Whose providence governs us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ut accépta tibi sint, Dómine, nostra ieiúnia: præsta nobis, quǽsumus; huius múnere sacraménti purificátum tibi pectus offérre.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, that we may offer You a heart cleansed by this sacred rite so that our fast may be acceptable to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Prǽbeant nobis, Dómine, divínum tua sancta fervórem: quo eórum páriter et actu delectémur et fructu.", "May Your holy things, O Lord, fill us with divine eagerness to enjoy their celebration together with their effects. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent1": {"src": "Tempora/Pent01-0", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui dedísti fámulis tuis in confessióne veræ fídei, ætérnæ Trinitátis glóriam agnóscere, et in poténtia maiestátis adoráre Unitátem: quǽsumus; ut, eiúsdem fídei firmitáte, ab ómnibus semper muniámur advérsis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, eternal God, You Who have given Your servants, in the confession of the true faith, to acknowledge the glory of the eternal Trinity, and in the power of that majesty to adore its unity, grant, we beseech You, that in the firmness of this faith we may ever be protected from all harm. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sanctífica, quǽsumus, Dómine, Deus noster, per tui sancti nóminis invocatiónem, huius oblatiónis hóstiam: et per eam nosmetípsos tibi pérfice munus ætérnum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We call upon Your Name, O Lord, and beseech You to hallow this sacrificial offering and through it to make us an eternal offering to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Profíciat nobis ad salútem córporis et ánimæ, Dómine, Deus noster, huius sacraménti suscéptio: et sempitérnæ sanctæ Trinitátis eiusdémque indivíduæ Unitátis conféssio. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the reception of this sacrament, O Lord our God, and the profession of our faith in the eternal holy Trinity and undivided Unity, benefit us for the salvation of body and soul. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "CorpusChristi": {"src": "Tempora/Pent01-4", "or": ["Deus, qui nobis sub Sacraménto mirábili passiónis tuæ memóriam reliquísti: tríbue, quǽsumus, ita nos Córporis et Sánguinis tui sacra mystéria venerári; ut redemptiónis tuæ fructum in nobis iúgiter sentiámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who in this wondrous sacrament have left us a memorial of Your passion, grant us, we beseech You, so to venerate the sacred mysteries of Your Body and Blood that we may ever experience within us the effect of Your redemption. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ecclésiæ tuæ, quǽsumus, Dómine, unitátis et pacis propítius dona concéde: quæ sub oblátis munéribus mýstice designántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously give Your Church, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts of unity and peace which are betokened by the gifts we offer. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Fac nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, divinitátis tuæ sempitérna fruitióne repléri: quam pretiósi Corporis et Sanguinis tui temporalis percéptio præfigúrat: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that we may be filled with that everlasting enjoyment of Your Godhead, as foreshadowed here on earth by the partaking of Your precious Body and Blood. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent2": {"src": "Tempora/Pent02-0", "or": ["Sancti nóminis tui, Dómine, timórem páriter et amórem fac nos habére perpétuum: quia numquam tua gubernatióne destítuis, quos in soliditáte tuæ dilectiónis instítuis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, O Lord, that we may always fear and love Your holy Name, for You never fail to guide those whom You firmly establish in Your love. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátio nos, Dómine, tuo nómini dicánda puríficet: et de die in diem ad cœléstis vitæ tránsferat actiónem.", "May the sacrifice we are about to offer unto Your holy Name, O Lord, make us pure, and day by day help us to live a more heavenly life. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis munéribus sacris, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut cum frequentatióne mystérii, crescat nostræ salútis efféctus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, that having received Your gifts, each partaking of this sacrament may increase within us its saving effects. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "SCJ": {"src": "Tempora/Pent02-5", "or": ["Deus, qui nobis in Corde Fílii tui, nostris vulneráto peccátis, infinítos dilectiónis thesáuros misericórditer largíri dignáris: concéde, quǽsumus; ut, illi devótum pietátis nostræ præstántes obséquium, dignæ quoque satisfactiónis exhibeámus offícium. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who in the Heart of Your Son, wounded by our sins, mercifully lavish upon us the infinite riches of love, grant, we beseech You, that as we offer Him the faithful service of our devotion, we may also show forth fitting reparation. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Réspice, quǽsumus, Dómine, ad ineffábilem Cordis dilécti Fílii tui caritátem: ut quod offérimus sit tibi munus accéptum et nostrórum expiátio delictórum. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look, we beseech You, O Lord, upon the Heart of Your beloved Son, with its boundless love, so that what we offer, may be an acceptable gift in Your sight and an atonement for our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Prǽbeant nobis, Dómine Iesu, divínum tua sancta fervórem: quo dulcíssimi Cordis tui suavitáte percépta; discámus terréna despícere, et amáre cœléstia: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your sacrament, O Lord Jesus, give us holy zeal, so that, seeing the sweetness of Your most loving Heart, we may learn to despise the things of earth and love those of heaven. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent3": {"src": "Tempora/Pent03-0r", "or": ["Protéctor in te sperántium, Deus, sine quo nihil est válidum, nihil sanctum: multíplica super nos misericórdiam tuam; ut, te rectóre, te duce, sic transeámus per bona temporália, ut non amittámus ætérna. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, protector of all who hope in You, without Whom nothing is strong, nothing is holy, increase Your mercy toward us, that, with Your guidance and direction we may so pass through the things of this temporal life as not to lose those of life eternal. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Réspice, Dómine, múnera supplicántis Ecclésiæ: et salúti credéntium perpétua sanctificatióne suménda concéde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look favorably, O Lord, upon the offerings of Your prayerful Church and grant that those who believe may, in continual holiness, partake of them for their salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sancta tua nos, Dómine, sumpta vivíficent: et misericórdiæ sempitérnæ prǽparent expiátos. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the holy things of which we have partaken bring us to life and prepare for Your everlasting mercy those whom You have cleansed from sin. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent4": {"src": "Tempora/Pent04-0", "or": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut et mundi cursus pacífice nobis tuo órdine dirigátur; et Ecclésia tua tranquílla devotióne lætétur.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, that the course of the world may be directed according to Your rule in peace and that Your Church may have the joy of serving You undisturbed. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblatiónibus nostris, quǽsumus, Dómine, placáre suscéptis: et ad te nostras étiam rebélles compélle propítius voluntátes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, we beseech You, O Lord, by accepting our offerings, and in Your kindness make even our rebellious wills turn to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Mystéria nos, Dómine, quǽsumus, sumpta puríficent: et suo múnere tueántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrament we have received cleanse us, we beseech You, O Lord, and by its grace protect us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent5": {"src": "Tempora/Pent05-0", "or": ["Deus, qui diligéntibus te bona invisibília præparásti: infúnde córdibus nostris tui amóris afféctum; ut te in ómnibus et super ómnia diligéntes, promissiónes tuas, quæ omne desidérium súperant, consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who have prepared good things as yet unseen for those who love You, pour a burning love into our hearts, so that we, loving You in and above all things, may obtain Your promises which surpass all desire. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Propitiáre, Dómine, supplicatiónibus nostris: et has oblatiónes famulórum famularúmque tuárum benígnus assúme; ut, quod sínguli obtulérunt ad honórem nóminis tui, cunctis profíciat ad salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be propitious to our supplications, O Lord, and graciously receive these oblations of Your servants and handmaids, that what each one offered to the glory of Your name, may profit all to salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quos cœlésti, Dómine, dono satiásti: præsta, quǽsumus; ut a nostris mundémur occúltis et ab hóstium liberémur insídiis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, that we whom You have filled with the heavenly gift may be cleansed of our hidden sins and delivered from the snares of our enemies. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent6": {"src": "Tempora/Pent06-0", "or": ["Deus virtútum, cuius est totum quod est óptimum: ínsere pectóribus nostris amórem tui nóminis, et præsta in nobis religiónis augméntum; ut, quæ sunt bona, nútrias, ac pietátis stúdio, quæ sunt nutríta, custódias. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God of the heavenly powers, creator of all good things, implant in our hearts the love of Your Name, and bestow upon us an increase of godliness, fostering what is good, and, by Your loving care, guarding what You have fostered. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Propitiáre, Dómine, supplicatiónibus nostris, et has pópuli tui oblatiónes benígnus assúme: et, ut nullíus sit írritum votum, nullíus vácua postulátio, præsta; ut, quod fidéliter pétimus, efficáciter consequámur.", "Mercifully hear our humble prayers, O Lord, and graciously accept these offerings of Your people, and grant that no prayer may be without effect, no petition in vain, so that what we ask in faith, we may really obtain. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Repléti sumus, Dómine, munéribus tuis: tríbue, quǽsumus; ut eórum et mundémur efféctu et muniámur auxílio. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have been filled with Your gifts, O Lord; grant, we beseech You, that we may be cleansed and strengthened by their effect. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent7": {"src": "Tempora/Pent07-0", "or": ["Deus, cuius providéntia in sui dispositióne non fállitur: te súpplices exorámus; ut nóxia cuncta submóveas, et ómnia nobis profutúra concédas.", "O God, Whose providence never fails to set things in order, we humbly beseech You to remove from us whatever is harmful and grant whatever is for our benefit. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, qui legálium differéntiam hostiárum unius sacrifícii perfectione sanxísti: accipe sacrifícium a devótis tibi fámulis, et pari benedictióne, sicut múnera Abel, sanctífica; ut, quod sínguli obtulérunt ad maiestátis tuæ honórem, cunctis profíciat ad salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who have given us in one perfect sacrifice the fulfillment of the various sacrifices made under the Old Law, accept these sacrificial gifts offered You by Your devoted servants, and make them holy as You did the gifts of Abel, so that what each one of us has offered in praise of Your majesty may profit for the salvation of all. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tua nos, Dómine, medicinális operátio, et a nostris perversitátibus cleménter expédiat, et ad ea, quæ sunt recta, perdúcat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your healing action, O Lord, mercifully rid us of our evil inclinations and lead us to do good. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent8": {"src": "Tempora/Pent08-0", "or": ["Largíre nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, semper spíritum cogitándi quæ recta sunt, propítius et agéndi: ut, qui sine te esse non póssumus, secúndum te vívere valeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Ever graciously bestow upon us, we beseech You, O Lord, the spirit of thinking and doing what is right, so that we, who cannot exist without You, may have the strength to live in accordance with Your law. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, múnera, quæ tibi de tua largitáte deférimus: ut hæc sacrosáncta mystéria, grátiæ tuæ operánte virtúte, et præséntis vitæ nos conversatióne sanctíficent, et ad gáudia sempitérna perdúcant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts which we bring to You out of Your own bounty, so that these most holy sacramental rites may, by the power of Your grace, sanctify us in the conduct of our present life, and lead us to everlasting joy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sit nobis, Dómine, reparátio mentis et córporis cæléste mystérium: ut, cuius exséquimur cultum, sentiámus efféctum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the heavenly sacrament, O Lord, renew our minds and bodies, so that we may feel the benefit of the worship we perform. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent9": {"src": "Tempora/Pent09-0", "or": ["Páteant aures misericórdiæ tuæ, Dómine, précibus supplicántium: et, ut peténtibus desideráta concédas; fac eos quæ tibi sunt plácita, postuláre. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your merciful ears be open, O Lord, to the prayers of those who humbly entreat You; grant that they may ask for what pleases You so that You may fulfill their desires. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, hæc digne frequentáre mystéria: quia, quóties huius hóstiæ commemorátio celebrátur, opus nostræ redemptiónis exercétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, to take part worthily and frequently in this sacramental action: for as often as this sacrifice of commemoration is offered, the work of our redemption is performed. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tui nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, commúnio sacraménti, et purificatiónem cónferat, et tríbuat unitátem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the partaking of Your sacrament, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse us and unite us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent10": {"src": "Tempora/Pent10-0", "or": ["Deus, qui omnipoténtiam tuam parcéndo máxime et miserándo maniféstas: multíplica super nos misericórdiam tuam; ut, ad tua promíssa curréntes, cœléstium bonórum fácias esse consórtes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You manifest Your power, particularly in forbearance and pity, show us Your mercy again and again, so that hastening toward Your promises we may become partakers of the blessings of heaven. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Tibi, Dómine, sacrifícia dicáta reddántur: quæ sic ad honórem nóminis tui deferénda tribuísti, ut eadem remédia fíeri nostra præstáres. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let the sacred gifts be offered to You, O Lord, Who have given them to be presented for the honor of Your name, for in them You have given us a remedy for all our ills. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, Dómine, Deus noster: ut, quos divínis reparáre non désinis sacraméntis, tuis non destítuas benígnus auxíliis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord our God, that in Your mercy You will not withhold Your help from those whom You constantly restore with divine sacraments. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent11": {"src": "Tempora/Pent11-0", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui, abundántia pietátis tuæ, et mérita súpplicum excédis et vota: effúnde super nos misericórdiam tuam; ut dimíttas quæ consciéntia métuit, et adícias quod orátio non præsúmit. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, eternal God, You Who in the abundance of Your love always grant more than Your humble petitioners deserve, and even more than they desire, pour forth Your mercy upon us that You may forgive whatever our conscience dreads, and give in addition what our prayer does not venture to ask. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Réspice, Dómine, quǽsumus, nostram propítius servitútem: ut, quod offérimus, sit tibi munus accéptum, et sit nostræ fragilitátis subsidium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with mercy, we beseech You, O Lord, upon our act of worship that the gift we offer may be acceptable to You and may support us in our frailty. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sentiámus, quǽsumus, Dómine, tui perceptióne sacraménti, subsídium mentis et córporis: ut, in utróque salváti, cæléstis remédii plenitúdine gloriémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By receiving Your sacrament, O Lord, may we experience Your help in mind and body, that being cured in both, we may glory in the full effect of the heavenly remedy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent12": {"src": "Tempora/Pent12-0", "or": ["Omnípotens et miséricors Deus, de cuius múnere venit, ut tibi a fidélibus tuis digne et laudabíliter serviátur: tríbue, quǽsumus, nobis; ut ad promissiónes tuas sine offensióne currámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and merciful God, by Whose grace Your faithful people serve You worthily and righteously, grant, we beseech You, that we may hasten without stumbling to those things You have promised us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias, quǽsumus, Dómine, propítius inténde, quas sacris altáribus exhibémus: ut, nobis indulgéntiam largiéndo, tuo nómini dent honórem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, graciously look upon the offerings which we lay upon Your sacred altar; so that they may bring us plentiful forgiveness while they give honor to Your name. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Vivíficet nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, huius participátio sancta mystérii: et páriter nobis expiatiónem tríbuat et múnimen. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the holy reception of this sacrament, we beseech You, O Lord, restore us to life, and bestow upon us forgiveness and protection. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent13": {"src": "Tempora/Pent13-0", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, da nobis fídei, spei et caritátis augméntum: et, ut mereámur asséqui quod promíttis, fac nos amáre quod prǽcipis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, eternal God, grant us an increase of faith, hope and charity; and make us love what You command so that we may be made worthy to attain what You promise. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Propitiáre, Dómine, pópulo tuo, propitiáre munéribus: ut, hac oblatióne placátus, et indulgéntiam nobis tríbuas et postuláta concedas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with favor upon Your people, O Lord, look with favor upon their gifts; so that, appeased by this offering, You will grant us pardon and give us what we ask. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis, Dómine, cœléstibus sacraméntis: ad redemptiónis ætérnæ, quǽsumus, proficiámus augméntum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received Your heavenly sacrament, O Lord, may we make progress, we beseech You, toward our everlasting salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent14": {"src": "Tempora/Pent14-0", "or": ["Custódi, Dómine, quǽsumus, Ecclésiam tuam propitiatióne perpétua: et quia sine te lábitur humána mortálitas; tuis semper auxíliis et abstrahátur a nóxiis et ad salutária dirigátur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Protect Your Church by Your abiding mercy, we beseech You, O Lord, and since all mortals fall without You, may Your help keep them from danger and guide them to salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde nobis, Dómine, quǽsumus, ut hæc hóstia salutáris et nostrórum fiat purgátio delictórum, et tuæ propitiátio potestátis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, Lord, we beseech You, that this salutary sacrifice may be not only a cleansing from our sins but also a propitiation of Your divine power. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Puríficent semper et múniant tua sacraménta nos, Deus: et ad perpétuæ ducant salvatiónis efféctum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your sacrament, O God, ever cleanse and strengthen us, and bring us to everlasting salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent15": {"src": "Tempora/Pent15-0", "or": ["Ecclésiam tuam, Dómine, miserátio continuáta mundet et múniat: et quia sine te non potest salva consístere; tuo semper múnere gubernétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your abiding mercy, O Lord, cleanse and strengthen Your Church, and, since without You she cannot exist in safety, let her be ever guided by Your grace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Tua nos, Dómine, sacramenta custodiant: et contra diabólicos semper tueántur incúrsus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your sacrament, O Lord, always keep us and guard us from the assaults of the devil. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Mentes nostras et córpora possídeat, quǽsumus, Dómine, doni cœléstis operátio: ut non noster sensus in nobis, sed iúgiter eius prævéniat efféctus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the working of the heavenly gift, O Lord, so possess us, mind and body, that the action of the sacrament, rather than our senses, may continually prevail in us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent16": {"src": "Tempora/Pent16-0", "or": ["Tua nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, grátia semper et prævéniat et sequátur: ac bonis opéribus iúgiter præstet esse inténtos. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your grace, we beseech You, O Lord, ever go before us and follow us, and may it make us ever intent upon good works. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Munda nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, sacrifícii præséntis efféctu: et pérfice miserátus in nobis; ut eius mereámur esse partícipes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Cleanse us by this sacrifice, we beseech You, O Lord, and by the workings of Your mercy, make us worthy to receive it. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Purífica, quǽsumus, Dómine, mentes nostras benígnus, et rénova cœléstibus sacraméntis: ut consequénter et córporum præsens páriter et futúrum capiámus auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, graciously cleanse and renew our minds with the heavenly sacrament, so we may thereby also receive bodily help for the present as well as for the future. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent17": {"src": "Tempora/Pent17-0", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus, Dómine, pópulo tuo diabólica vitáre contágia: et te solum Deum pura mente sectári. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that Your people may avoid the temptations of the devil, and with pure minds follow You, the only God. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Maiestátem tuam, Dómine, supplíciter deprecámur: ut hæc sancta, quæ gérimus, et a prætéritis nos delictis éxuant et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we humbly pray Your Majesty that the holy rite which we are celebrating may free us from past and future sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sanctificatiónibus tuis, omnípotens Deus, et vítia nostra curéntur, et remédia nobis ætérna provéniant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By the workings of Your sanctifying power, almighty God, may our vices be cured and eternal remedies provided for us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "EmbWedSept": {"src": "Tempora/093-3", "or": ["Misericórdiæ tuæ remédiis, quǽsumus, Dómine, fragílitas nostra subsístat: ut, quæ sua conditióne attéritur, tua cleméntia reparétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our frailty, we beseech You, O Lord, find support in the help of Your mercy; so that what is marred by its own nature may be restored by Your grace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, Dómine, quǽsumus, emúndet nostra delícta: et ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this offering, O Lord, we beseech You, wipe away our transgressions, and make holy the minds and bodies of Your servants for celebrating this sacrifice. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Suméntes, Dómine, dona cœléstia, supplíciter deprecámur: ut, quæ sédula servitúte, donánte te, gérimus, dignis sénsibus tuo múnere capiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "In partaking of Your heavenly gifts, we humbly entreat You, O Lord, that by Your grace we may receive what, through Your bounty, we perform in diligent service. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "EmbFriSept": {"src": "Tempora/093-5", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, observatiónes sacras ánnua devotióne recoléntes, et córpore tibi placeámus et mente. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who devoutly keep the sacred observances year by year may be pleasing unto You both in body and soul. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sint, Dómine, quǽsumus, nostri dona ieiúnii: quæ et expiándo nos tua grátia dignos effíciant, et ad sempitérna promíssa perdúcant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the gift of our fasting, we beseech You, O Lord, be acceptable to You, and by its purifying power make us worthy of Your grace and bring us to the eternal bliss You have promised us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, de percéptis munéribus grátias exhibéntes, benefícia potióra sumámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O almighty God, that, showing gratitude for the gifts we have received, we may obtain yet greater benefits. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "EmbSatSept": {"src": "Tempora/093-6", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui per continéntiam salutárem corpóribus medéris et méntibus: maiestátem tuam súpplices exorámus; ut, pia ieiunántium deprecatióne placátus, et præséntia nobis subsídia tríbuas et futúra. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, everlasting God, You Who cure body and soul through healing self-denial, we humbly entreat Your majesty to hear favorably the devout prayer of those who fast, and to grant us help for the present and the future. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut oculis tuæ maiestátis munus oblátum et grátiam nobis devotiónis obtíneat, et efféctum beátæ perennitátis acquírat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the gift in the sight of Your majesty may obtain for us the grace of reverent devotion and secure eternal happiness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Perfíciant in nobis, Dómine, quǽsumus, tua sacraménta quod cóntinent: ut, quæ nunc spécie gérimus, rerum veritáte capiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your sacrament, we beseech You, O Lord, produce in us what it contains, and may we share in reality what we now perform as a sacramental rite. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "EmbSatSeptS": {"src": "Tempora/093-6", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui per continéntiam salutárem corpóribus medéris et méntibus: maiestátem tuam súpplices exorámus; ut, pia ieiunántium deprecatióne placátus, et præséntia nobis subsídia tríbuas et futúra. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, everlasting God, You Who cure body and soul through healing self-denial, we humbly entreat Your majesty to hear favorably the devout prayer of those who fast, and to grant us help for the present and the future. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut oculis tuæ maiestátis munus oblátum et grátiam nobis devotiónis obtíneat, et efféctum beátæ perennitátis acquírat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the gift in the sight of Your majesty may obtain for us the grace of reverent devotion and secure eternal happiness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Perfíciant in nobis, Dómine, quǽsumus, tua sacraménta quod cóntinent: ut, quæ nunc spécie gérimus, rerum veritáte capiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your sacrament, we beseech You, O Lord, produce in us what it contains, and may we share in reality what we now perform as a sacramental rite. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent18": {"src": "Tempora/Pent18-0", "or": ["Dírigat corda nostra, quǽsumus, Dómine, tuæ miseratiónis operátio: quia tibi sine te placére non póssumus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the working of Your mercy, we beseech You, O Lord, guide our hearts, for without You, we cannot please You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, qui nos, per huius sacrifícii veneránda commércia, uníus summæ divinitátis partícipes éfficis: præsta, quǽsumus; ut, sicut tuam cognóscimus veritátem, sic eam dignis móribus assequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who, through the gifts we have exchanged with You in this sacrament, have made us partakers of the supreme Godhead, grant, we beseech You, that, as we have knowledge of Your truth, so we may fully live up to it. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Grátias tibi reférimus, Dómine, sacro múnere vegetáti: tuam misericórdiam deprecántes; ut dignos nos eius participatióne perfícias. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Strengthened by Your sacred gift, we thank You, O Lord, beseeching Your mercy to make us receive it worthily. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent19": {"src": "Tempora/Pent19-0", "or": ["Omnípotens et miséricors Deus, univérsa nobis adversántia propitiátus exclúde: ut mente et córpore páriter expedíti, quæ tua sunt, líberis méntibus exsequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and merciful God, graciously keep away from us all misfortune, that, unhampered in soul and body, we may perform with peaceful minds the works that are Yours. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc múnera, quǽsumus, Dómine, quæ óculis tuæ maiestátis offérimus, salutária nobis esse concéde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that these gifts which we offer in the sight of Your majesty, may be the means of our salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tua nos, Dómine, medicinális operátio, et a nostris perversitátibus cleménter expédiat, et tuis semper fáciat inhærére mandátis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your healing power, O Lord, mercifully deliver us from our waywardness and make us ever keep Your commandments. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent20": {"src": "Tempora/Pent20-0", "or": ["Largíre, quǽsumus, Dómine, fidélibus tuis indulgéntiam placátus et pacem: ut páriter ab ómnibus mundéntur offénsis, et secúra tibi mente desérviant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, graciously grant Your faithful forgiveness and peace, that they may be cleansed of all sin and serve You with minds free from care. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Cœléstem nobis prǽbeant hæc mystéria, quǽsumus, Dómine, medicínam: et vítia nostri cordis expúrgent. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these sacramental rites, O Lord, we beseech You, be our heavenly medicine and expel evil from our hearts. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ut sacris, Dómine, reddámur digni munéribus: fac nos, qu&#509;sumus, tuis semper obœdíre mandátis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "That we may be made worthy, O Lord, of Your sacred gifts, make us, we beseech You, ever obedient to Your commandments. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent21": {"src": "Tempora/Pent21-0", "or": ["Famíliam tuam, quǽsumus, Dómine, contínua pietáte custódi: ut a cunctis adversitátibus, te protegénte, sit líbera, et in bonis áctibus tuo nómini sit devóta. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Guard Your household, we beseech You, O Lord, with unceasing care, that under Your protection it may be free from all harm and serve You by good deeds. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Suscipe, Dómine, propítius hóstias: quibus et te placári voluísti, et nobis salútem poténti pietáte restítui. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously accept these sacrificial gifts, O Lord, with which You have willed us to find favor with You, and, by Your mighty love, restore salvation to us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Immortalitátis alimóniam consecúti, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut, quod ore percépimus, pura mente sectémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We who have eaten the food of eternal life beseech You, O Lord, that what we take by mouth, we may strive after with pure minds. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Pent22": {"src": "Tempora/Pent22-0", "or": ["Deus, refúgium nostrum et virtus: adésto piis Ecclésiæ tuæ précibus, auctor ipse pietátis, et præsta; ut, quod fidéliter pétimus, efficáciter consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, our refuge and our strength, the very source of holiness, heed the devout prayers of Your Church, and grant that what we seek in faith we may obtain in fact. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Da, miséricors Deus: ut hæc salutáris oblátio et a própriis nos reátibus indesinénter expédiat, et ab ómnibus tueátur advérsis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, O merciful God, that this saving sacrifice may always free us from sin, and protect us from all that works against us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, sacri dona mystérii, humíliter deprecántes: ut, quæ in tui commemoratiónem nos fácere præcepísti, in nostræ profíciant infirmitátis auxílium: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We who have received the gift of Your blessed sacrament, O Lord, humbly pray that what You have taught us to do in commemoration of You, may profit and help us in our weakness. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "ChristusRex": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 604-605 (Dominica ultima Octobris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui in dilécto Fílio tuo, universórum Rege, ómnia instauráre voluísti: concéde propítius ut cunctæ famíliæ Géntium, peccáti vúlnere disgregátæ; eius suavíssimo subdántur império: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, Who willed to restore all things in Your beloved Son, the King of the Universe, graciously grant that the peoples of the earth torn asunder by the wound of sin, may submit to His most gentle rule; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstiam tibi, Dómine, humánæ reconciliatiónis offérimus: præsta, quǽsumus; ut Quem sacrifíciis præséntibus immolámus, Ipse cunctis Géntibus unitátis et pacis dona concédat, Iesus Christus Fílius tuus Dóminus noster: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we offer You this sacrificial Victim of mankind's reconciliation with You; grant, we beseech You, that our Lord Jesus Christ, your Son, Whom we offer in this sacrifice, may bestow upon all peoples the gifts of unity and peace; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Immortalitátis alimóniam consecúti, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut, qui sub Christi Regis vexíllis militáre gloriámur, cum Ipso, in cælésti sede, iúgiter regnáre possímus: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received the food of eternal life, and we beseech You, O Lord, that we who are proud to serve under the flag of Christ the King may forever reign with Him in the Kingdom of heaven; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Pent23": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 303-304 (Dominica XXI post Octavam Trinitatis); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Absólve, quǽsumus Dómine, tuórum delícta populórum: ut a peccatórum nostrórum néxibus, quæ pro nostra fragilitáte contráximus; tua benignitáte liberémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Forgive, we beseech You, O Lord, the sins of Your faithful people, so that by Your goodness we may be released from the net of sin in which we have been caught by our weakness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Pro nostræ servitútis augménto, sacrifícium tibi, Dómine, laudis offérimus: ut quod imméritis contulísti, propítius exsequáris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You O Lord, the sacrifice of praise that we may serve You even better, so that You may graciously complete what You have given us, Your undeserving servants; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut quos divína tríbuis participatióne gaudére; humánis non sinas subiacére perículis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, let not human dangers overcome us to whom You grant joyful participation in things divine; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "AscVig": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc5-3", "or": ["Deus, a quo bona cuncta procédunt, largíre supplícibus tuis: ut cogitémus, te inspiránte, quæ recta sunt; et, te gubernánte, eadem faciámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, from Whom all good things come, grant, we beseech You, that by Your inspiration, we may think what is right and under Your guidance, accomplish it. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, fidélium preces cum oblatiónibus hostiárum: ut, per hæc piæ devotiónis offícia, ad cœléstem glóriam transeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, O Lord, the prayers and gifts of Your faithful people, that, through these rites of love and devotion we may pass to the glory of heaven. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tríbue nobis, Dómine, cœléstis mensæ virtúte satiátis: et desideráre, quæ recta sunt, et desideráta percípere. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, O Lord, that we who have been fed with the strengthening food of Your heavenly table, may desire what is right and obtain what we desire. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "Dedicatio": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 2*-3* (In anniversario Dedicationis Ecclesiae); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nobis per síngulos annos huius sancti templi tui consecratiónis réparas diem, et sacris semper mystériis repræséntas incólumes; exáudi preces pópuli tui: et præsta, ut quisquis hoc templum benefícia petitúrus ingréditur; cuncta se impetrásse lætétur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who year by year renew for us the day of the consecration of this Your holy temple, and bring us again in safety to Your sacred mysteries, hear the prayers of Your people, and grant that whoever enters this temple to ask for blessings may rejoice to have obtained them all; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Annue, quǽsumus Dómine, précibus nostris, ut quicúmque intra templi huius, cuius anniversárium dedicatiónis diem celebrámus, ámbitum continémur, plena tibi atque perfécta córporis et ánimæ devotióne placeámus: ut, dum hæc vota præséntia réddimus, ad ætérna prǽmia, te adiuvánte, perveníre mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hearken, we beseech You, O Lord, to our prayers, that all of us who are gathered within the walls of this temple, the anniversary of whose dedication we celebrate, may please You with full and perfect devotion of body and soul, so that, while we render these present offerings, we may by Your help deserve to attain to eternal rewards; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam sponsam vocáre dignátus es, ut quæ habéret grátiam per fídei devotiónem, habéret étiam ex nómine pietátem; da, ut omnis hæc plebs nómini tuo sérviens, huius vocábuli consórtio digna esse mereátur: et Ecclésia tua in templo, cuius anniversárius dedicatiónis dies celebrátur, tibi collécta, te tímeat, te díligat, te sequátur; ut dum iúgiter per vestígia tua gráditur, ad cæléstia promíssa, te ducénte, perveníre mereátur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who deigned to call Your Church Your bride, that she who had grace through the devotion of faith might also have holiness from the name; grant that all this people serving Your name may deserve to be worthy of sharing that title, and that Your Church, gathered to You in the temple whose anniversary of dedication is kept, may fear You, love You and follow You, that, walking ever in Your footsteps, she may under Your guidance deserve to come to the heavenly promises; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C1s": {"src": "Sancti/06-11", "or": ["Deus, qui nos beáti Bárnabæ Apóstoli tui méritis et intercessióne lætíficas: concéde propítius; ut, qui tua per eum benefícia póscimus, dono tuæ grátiæ consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who gladden us by the merits and intercession of blessed Barnabas, Your Apostle, mercifully grant that we, who ask Your favors through him, may obtain them by the gift of Your grace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, Dómine, obláta sanctífica, et, intercedénte beáto Bárnaba Apostolo tuo, nos per hæc a peccatórum nostrórum máculis emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Make holy the sacrificial gifts we offer, O Lord, and, through the intercession of blessed Barnabas, Your Apostle, cleanse us from the stains of our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súpplices te rogámus, omnípotens Deus: ut, quos tuis réficis sacraméntis, intercedénte beáto Bárnaba Apóstolo tuo, tibi étiam plácitis móribus dignánter tríbuas deservíre. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We humbly beseech You, almighty God, that, through the intercession of blessed Barnabas Your Apostle, You will grant those whom You refresh with Your sacrament to fittingly serve You with lives pleasing unto You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "C7s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 9*-10* (Unius Martyris non Pontificis); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Adésto Dómine supplicatiónibus nostris: ut qui ex iniquitáte nostra reos nos esse cognóscimus; beáti N. Mártyris tui intercessióne liberémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hearken, O Lord, to our supplications, that we who know ourselves to be guilty by our iniquity may be delivered by the intercession of blessed N., Your martyr; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Munéribus nostris, quǽsumus Dómine, precibúsque suscéptis: intercedénte beáto N. Mártyre tuo, et cæléstibus nos munda mystériis, et cleménter exáudi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received our gifts and prayers, we beseech You, O Lord, that by the intercession of blessed N., Your martyr, You would both cleanse us by heavenly mysteries and mercifully hear us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto N. Mártyre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received heavenly food may, by the intercession of blessed N., Your martyr, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C11s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 4*-5* (Unius Martyris Pontificis, alia Missa); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui beáti N. Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis solémnia cólimus; eius apud te intercessiónibus adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who keep the feast of blessed N., Your martyr and bishop, may be helped by his intercession with You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, quǽsumus Dómine, emúndet nostra delícta: et ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this sacrifice, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse us from our sins, and sanctify the bodies and minds of Your servants for the celebration of the sacrifice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti participatióne múneris sacri, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut cuius exséquimur cultum; intercedénte beáto N. Mártyre tuo atque Pontífice, sentiámus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by partaking of the sacred gift, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that, by the intercession of blessed N., Your martyr and bishop, we may feel the effect of the rite we perform; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C15s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 8*-9* (Unius Martyris Pontificis, tempore Paschali); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui beáti N. Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis solémnia cólimus; eius apud te intercessiónibus adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who keep the feast of blessed N., Your martyr and bishop, may be helped by his intercession with You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, quǽsumus Dómine, emúndet nostra delícta: et ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this sacrifice, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse us from our sins, and sanctify the bodies and minds of Your servants for the celebration of the sacrifice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti participatióne múneris sacri, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut cuius exséquimur cultum; intercedénte beáto N. Mártyre tuo atque Pontífice, sentiámus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by partaking of the sacred gift, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that, by the intercession of blessed N., Your martyr and bishop, we may feel the effect of the rite we perform; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C18s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 10*-11* (Unius Martyris non Pontificis, alia Missa); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui beáti N. Mártyris tui natalítia cólimus; a cunctis malis imminéntibus eius intercessióne liberémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who keep the birthday of blessed N., Your martyr, may by his intercession be delivered from all threatening evils; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, beáti N. Mártyris tui dicátas méritis, benígnus assúme: et ad perpétuum nobis tríbue proveníre subsídium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously accept, O Lord, the sacrifices dedicated to You by the merits of blessed N., Your martyr, and grant that they may avail us for everlasting help; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis, Dómine, sacraméntis: quǽsumus, ut intercedénte beáto N. Mártyre tuo; supplicatiónes nostras placátus inténdas: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received the sacraments, O Lord, we beseech You that, by the intercession of blessed N., Your martyr, You may graciously hearken to our supplications; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C21s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 12*-13* (Plurimorum Martyrum); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui gloriósos Mártyres fortes in sua confessióne cognóvimus; pios apud te in nostra intercessióne sentiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who have known the glorious martyrs to be steadfast in their confession may feel them to be loving intercessors for us with You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Benedíctio tua Dómine larga descéndat: quæ et múnera nostra, deprecántibus sanctis Martýribus tuis, tibi reddat accépta, et nobis sacraméntum redemptiónis effíciat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your blessing, O Lord, come down abundantly, that, Your holy martyrs pleading, it may make our gifts acceptable to You and make for us the sacrament of redemption; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cæléstibus refécti sacraméntis et gáudiis, súpplices te Dómine deprecámur: ut quorum gloriámur triúmphis; protegámur auxíliis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly sacraments and joys, we humbly pray You, O Lord, that we may be protected by the help of those in whose triumphs we glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C25s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 14*-15* (Plurimorum Martyrum, alia Missa); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos concédis sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum N. et N. natalítia cólere; da nobis in ætérna beatitúdine de eórum societáte gaudére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who grant us to keep the birthday of Your holy martyrs N. and N., grant us to rejoice in their company in everlasting bliss; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis offérimus: quæ et pro tuórum tibi grata sint honóre Sanctórum, et nobis salutária, te miseránte, reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gifts of our devotion, that they may be pleasing to You for the honor of Your saints and, by Your mercy, become salutary to us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, intercedéntibus sanctis Martýribus tuis N. et N.; ut quæ ore contígimus, pura mente capiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, by the intercession of Your holy martyrs N. and N., that what we have touched with our lips we may receive with a pure mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C28s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 16*-17* (Plurimorum Martyrum, tempore Paschali); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos concédis sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum N. et N. natalítia cólere; da nobis in ætérna beatitúdine de eórum societáte gaudére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who grant us to keep the birthday of Your holy martyrs N. and N., grant us to rejoice in their company in everlasting bliss; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis offérimus: quæ et pro tuórum tibi grata sint honóre Sanctórum, et nobis salutária, te miseránte, reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gifts of our devotion, that they may be pleasing to You for the honor of Your saints and, by Your mercy, become salutary to us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, intercedéntibus sanctis Martýribus tuis N. et N.; ut quæ ore contígimus, pura mente capiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, by the intercession of Your holy martyrs N. and N., that what we have touched with our lips we may receive with a pure mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C30s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 18*-19* (Confessoris Pontificis); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti N. Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis veneránda solémnitas; et devotiónem nobis áugeat, et salútem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the venerable feast of blessed N., Your confessor and bishop, may increase in us both devotion and salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti tui, quǽsumus Dómine, nos ubíque lætíficent: ut dum eórum mérita recólimus, patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your saints, we beseech You, O Lord, everywhere gladden us, that while we recall their merits we may feel their protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut de percéptis munéribus grátias exhibéntes; intercedénte beáto N. Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, benefícia potióra sumámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that, giving thanks for the gifts received, we may, by the intercession of blessed N., Your confessor and bishop, receive still greater benefits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C32s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 19*-20* (Confessoris Pontificis, alia Missa); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Exáudi, quǽsumus Dómine, preces nostras, quas in beáti N. Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis solemnitáte deférimus: ut qui tibi digne méruit famulári; eius intercedéntibus méritis, ab ómnibus nos absólvas peccátis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear, we beseech You, O Lord, the prayers which we offer on the feast of blessed N., Your confessor and bishop, that by the merits and intercession of him who was found worthy to serve You, You may absolve us from all our sins; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sit in conspéctu tuo Dómine nostra devótio: ut eius nobis fiat supplicatióne salutáris, pro cuius solemnitáte defértur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our devotion be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, and may it become saving for us through the supplication of him on whose feast it is offered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, fidélibus tuis, Sanctórum tuórum semper veneratióne lætári; et eórum perpétua supplicatióne muníri: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, to Your faithful ever to rejoice in the veneration of Your saints and to be defended by their unceasing intercession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C35s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 20*-21* (Doctoris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum N. minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave blessed N. to Your people as a minister of eternal salvation, grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have him as our intercessor in heaven whom we had as the teacher of life on earth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti N. Confessóris tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed N., Your confessor and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti N. Confessóris tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed N., Your confessor and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C39s": {"src": "Commune/C5-1", "or": ["Adésto, Dómine, supplicatiónibus nostris, quas in beáti N. Confessóris tui sollemnitáte deférimus: ut, qui nostræ iustítiæ fidúciam non habémus, eius, qui tibi plácuit, précibus adiuvémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be mindful, O Lord, of our humble prayers in this commemoration of Your Saints, so that we, who have no confidence in our own righteousness, may be helped by the merits of those who have been pleasing to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your Saints and may purify us in both body and mind. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui cœléstia aliménta percépimus, intercedénte beáto N. Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We pray You, almighty God, that we who have received heavenly nourishment may thereby, through the intercession of blessed N., Your Confessor, be sustained against all harm and danger. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "C42s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 23*-24* (Confessoris non Pontificis, alia Missa); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Adésto Dómine supplicatiónibus nostris, quas in beáti N. Confessóris tui solemnitáte deférimus: ut qui nostræ iustítiæ fidúciam non habémus; eius, qui tibi plácuit, précibus adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hearken, O Lord, to the prayers which we offer on the feast of blessed N., Your confessor, that we who have no confidence in our own righteousness may be helped by the prayers of him who pleased You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto N. Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed N., Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C45s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 27*-28* (Virginis et Martyris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Indulgéntiam nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, beáta N. Virgo et Martyr implóret: quæ tibi grata semper éxstitit; et mérito castitátis, et tuæ professióne virtútis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed N., virgin and martyr, we beseech You, O Lord, implore pardon for us, she who was ever pleasing to You both by the merit of her chastity and by the confession of Your power; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe Dómine múnera, quæ in beátæ N. Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ solemnitáte deférimus: cuius nos confídimus patrocínio liberári. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, the gifts we bring on the feast of blessed N., Your virgin and martyr, by whose patronage we trust to be delivered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Auxiliéntur nobis, Dómine, sumpta mystéria; et intercedénte beáta N. Vírgine et Mártyre tua, sempitérna protectióne confírment: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the mysteries we have received help us, O Lord, and, through the intercession of blessed N., Your virgin and martyr, strengthen us with everlasting protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C48s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 29*-30* (Virginis et Martyris, alia Missa); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui infírma mundi éligis, ut fórtia quæque confúndas: concéde propítius, ut qui beátæ N. Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ solémnia cólimus; eius apud te patrocínia sentiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, who choose the weak things of the world to confound the strong, mercifully grant that we who keep the feast of blessed N., Your virgin and martyr, may feel the help of her patronage with You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias, Dómine, quas tibi offérimus, propítius súscipe: et intercedénte beáta N. Vírgine et Mártyre tua, víncula peccatórum nostrórum absólve. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Mercifully receive, O Lord, the sacrifices which we offer You, and, by the intercession of blessed N., Your virgin and martyr, loose the bonds of our sins; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo, potúque cælésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus; eius muniámur et précibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly food and drink, O our God, we humbly entreat You that we may also be defended by the prayers of her in whose commemoration we have received these gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C51s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 35*-36* (Unius Sanctæ nec Virginis nec Martyris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Tuórum corda fidélium Deus miserátor illústra: et beátæ N. précibus gloriósis, fac nos próspera mundi despícere; et cælésti semper consolatióne gaudére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O merciful God, enlighten the hearts of Your faithful, and by the glorious prayers of blessed N. make us despise the prosperity of the world and ever rejoice in heavenly consolation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis offérimus: ut tibi grata, et nobis salutária, beátæ N. pia supplicatióne reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gifts of our devotion, that they may become pleasing to You and salutary to us through the devout supplication of blessed N; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut quos salutáribus dignátus es erudíre mystériis; beátæ N. intercessióne gloriósa, cæléstibus refícias aliméntis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that those whom You have deigned to instruct by the saving mysteries You may refresh with heavenly food through the glorious intercession of blessed N; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C62s": {"src": "Tempora/Pent01-4", "or": ["Deus, qui nobis sub Sacraménto mirábili passiónis tuæ memóriam reliquísti: tríbue, quǽsumus, ita nos Córporis et Sánguinis tui sacra mystéria venerári; ut redemptiónis tuæ fructum in nobis iúgiter sentiámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who in this wondrous sacrament have left us a memorial of Your passion, grant us, we beseech You, so to venerate the sacred mysteries of Your Body and Blood that we may ever experience within us the effect of Your redemption. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ecclésiæ tuæ, quǽsumus, Dómine, unitátis et pacis propítius dona concéde: quæ sub oblátis munéribus mýstice designántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously give Your Church, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts of unity and peace which are betokened by the gifts we offer. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Fac nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, divinitátis tuæ sempitérna fruitióne repléri: quam pretiósi Corporis et Sanguinis tui temporalis percéptio præfigúrat: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that we may be filled with that everlasting enjoyment of Your Godhead, as foreshadowed here on earth by the partaking of Your precious Body and Blood. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "C75s": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc7-0", "or": ["Deus, qui hodiérna die corda fidélium Sancti Spíritus illustratióne docuísti: da nobis in eódem Spíritu recta sápere; et de eius semper consolatióne gaudére. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who on this day have taught the hearts of the faithful by the light of the Holy Spirit, grant us by that Holy Spirit Himself, to know what is right and ever to rejoice in His help. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, quǽsumus, Dómine, obláta sanctífica: et corda nostra Sancti Spíritus illustratióne emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify these offerings, we beseech You, O Lord, and cleanse our hearts by the light of the Holy Spirit. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sancti Spíritus, Dómine, corda nostra mundet infúsio: et sui roris íntima aspersióne fecúndet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the inpouring of the Holy Spirit cleanse our hearts, O Lord, and make them fertile through the dew He sprinkles upon them. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "C76s": {"src": "Tempora/Quad4-3", "or": ["Deus, qui et iustis prǽmia meritórum et peccatóribus per ieiúnium véniam præbes: miserére supplícibus tuis; ut reátus nostri conféssio indulgéntiam valeat percípere delictórum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who graciously grant to the righteous the rewards of their merits, and to sinners forgiveness through fasting, have mercy upon Your humble servants, so that, confessing our guilt, we may obtain pardon for our transgressions. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súpplices te rogámus, omnípotens Deus: ut his sacrifíciis peccáta nostra mundéntur; quia tunc veram nobis tríbuis et mentis et córporis sanitátem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We humbly entreat You, almighty God, that these sacrificial gifts may cleanse us from sin, for in this way You grant us true health of soul and body. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta, quæ súmpsimus, Dómine, Deus noster: et spirituálibus nos répleant aliméntis, et corporálibus tueántur auxíliis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrament we have received, O Lord, both fill us with spiritual nourishment and sustain us with bodily aid. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "C79s": {"src": "Commune/C11", "or": ["Concéde nos fámulos tuos, quǽsumus, Dómine Deus, perpétua mentis et córporis sanitáte gaudére: et, gloriósa beátæ Maríæ semper Vírginis intercessióne, a præsénti liberári tristítia, et ætérna pérfrui lætítia. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech thee, O Lord God, unto all thy servants, that they may remain continually in the enjoyment of soundness both of mind and body, and by the glorious intercession of the Blessed Mary, always a Virgin, may be delivered from present sadness, and enter into the joy of thine eternal gladness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Tua, Dómine, propitiatióne, et beátæ Maríæ semper Vírginis intercessióne, ad perpétuam atque præséntem hæc oblátio nobis profíciat prosperitátem et pacem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through Your mercy, O Lord, and by the intercession of blessed Mary, ever Virgin, the Mother of Your only-begotten Son, may this offering profit us for prosperity and peace, now and forevermore. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis, Dómine, salútis nostræ subsídiis: da, quǽsumus, beátæ Maríæ semper Vírginis patrocíniis nos ubíque prótegi; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received the aids conducive to our salvation, O Lord, we beseech You, grant that we may everywhere be protected by the patronage of blessed Mary, ever Virgin, in veneration of whom we have made these offerings to Your Majesty. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "C93s": {"src": "Commune/Propaganda", "or": ["Deus, qui omnes hómines vis salvos fíeri, et ad agnitiónem veritátis veníre: mitte, quǽsumus, operários in messem tuam, et da eis cum omni fidúcia loqui verbum tuum; ut sermo tuus currat et clarificétur, et omnes gentes cognóscant te solum Deum verum, et quem misísti Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, Dóminum nostrum. Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who desirest that all men should be saved, and come to the knowledge of the truth: send forth, we beseech thee, labourers into thy harvest, and grant them grace to speak thy word with all trust, that thy words may run and be glorified, and that all nations may know thee, the one true God, and him whom thou hast sent, Jesus Christ thy Son our Lord. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Protéctor noster, áspice, Deus, et réspice in fáciem Christi tui, qui dedit redemptiónem semetípsum pro ómnibus: et fac, ut ab ortu solis usque ad occásum magnificétur nomen tuum in géntibus, ac in omni loco sacrificétur, et offerátur nómini tuo oblátio munda. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Turn thine eyes, O God, our protector, and look upon the face of thy Christ, who hath given himself as a ransom for all, and grant that from the rising of the sun even unto the setting thereof thy name may be great among the Gentiles, and that in every place there may be sacrifice, and a clean oblation offered to thy name. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Redemptiónis nostræ múnere vegetáti: quǽsumus, Dómine; ut hoc perpétuæ salútis auxílio, fides semper vera profíciat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Revived by this atoning sacrifice, we beseech thee, O Lord, that by means of this help to eternal salvation true Faith may ever advance. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0114": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 20*-21* (Commune Doctorum, as the Missal directs on 14 Jan., p. 353); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Hilárium minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave blessed Hilary to Your people as a minister of eternal salvation, grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have him as our intercessor in heaven whom we had as the teacher of life on earth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Hilárii Confessóris tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed Hilary, Your confessor and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Hilárii Confessóris tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed Hilary, Your confessor and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0117": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 356; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Intercéssio nos, quǽsumus Dómine, beáti Antónii Abbátis comméndet: ut quod nostris méritis non valémus; eius patrocínio assequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the intercession of blessed Anthony the Abbot, we beseech You, O Lord, commend us to You, that what we cannot obtain by our own merits we may obtain by his patronage; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacris altáribus, Dómine, hóstias superpósitas sanctus Antónius Abbas, quǽsumus, in salútem nobis proveníre depóscat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May saint Anthony the Abbot, we beseech You, O Lord, ask that the sacrifices laid upon Your holy altars may avail for our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Prótegat nos, Dómine, cum tui perceptióne sacraménti, beátus Antónius Abbas, pro nobis intercedéndo: ut et conversatiónis eius experiámur insígnia; et intercessiónis ipsíus percipiámus suffrágia: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Anthony the Abbot, interceding for us, protect us, O Lord, together with the reception of Your sacrament, that we may both experience the excellence of his way of life and receive the help of his intercession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0120": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 358-360; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátos Mártyres tuos Fabiánum atque Sebastiánum virtúte constántiæ in passióne roborásti: ex eórum nobis imitatióne tríbue, pro amóre tuo próspera mundi despícere; et nulla eius advérsa formidáre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who strengthened Your blessed martyrs Fabian and Sebastian with the power of constancy in their passion, grant us by their example, for love of You, to despise the prosperity of the world and to fear none of its adversities; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sit in conspéctu tuo, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis oblátio, et eórum nobis fiat supplicatióne salutáris, pro quorum solemnitáte defértur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of our devotion be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, and may it become saving for us through the supplication of those on whose feast it is offered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacro múnere satiáti, súpplices te Dómine deprecámur: ut quod débitæ servitútis celebrámus offício; intercedéntibus beátis Martýribus tuis Fabiáno atque Sebastiáno, salvatiónis tuæ sentiámus augméntum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with the sacred gift, we humbly pray You, O Lord, that what we celebrate in the office of the service we owe, we may, by the intercession of Your blessed martyrs Fabian and Sebastian, feel as an increase of Your salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0121": {"src": "Sancti/01-21", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui infírma mundi éligis, ut fórtia quæque confúndas: concéde propítius; ut, qui beátæ Agnétis Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ sollémnia cólimus, eius apud te patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, eternal God, You Who choose the weak things of the world to confound the strong, mercifully grant that we who are celebrating the feast of blessed Agnes, Your Virgin and Martyr, may reap the benefit of her patronal intercession with You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias, Dómine, quas tibi offérimus, propítius súscipe: et, intercedénte beáta Agnéte Vírgine et Mártyre tua, víncula peccatórum nostrórum absólve. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously accept, O Lord, the sacrificial gifts we offer You and by the intercession of blessed Agnes, Your Virgin and Martyr, loose our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cœlésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut, in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus, eius muniámur et précibus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly food and drink, we humbly pray You, our God, that we also may be helped by her prayers in memory of whom we have partaken of these gifts. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0127": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 366-369; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Ecclésiam tuam, quǽsumus Dómine, grátia cæléstis amplíficet; quam beáti Ioánnis Chrysóstomi Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis, illustráre voluísti gloriósis méritis et doctrínis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May heavenly grace, we beseech You, O Lord, increase Your Church, which You have willed to enlighten by the glorious merits and teaching of blessed John Chrysostom, Your confessor and bishop; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Passiónis Fílii tui, Dómine, memóriam recenséntes depóscimus: ut quod tibi in beáti Ioánnis Chrysóstomi Pontíficis tui solemnitáte deférimus, sacrifícium sit accéptum. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Recalling the memory of the Passion of Your Son, O Lord, we ask that the sacrifice which we offer You on the feast of blessed John Chrysostom, Your bishop, may be acceptable; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Hæc nos, quǽsumus Dómine, commúnio sancta lætíficet: qua beáti Ioánnis Chrysóstomi Pontíficis tui suffrágiis, virtútes roboréntur intérius; et actus extérius piæ operatiónis excréscant: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this holy communion, we beseech You, O Lord, gladden us, that by the prayers of blessed John Chrysostom, Your bishop, our virtues may be strengthened within and the works of devout service may increase without; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0128": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 366-368; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui in tuæ caritátis exémplum, ad fidélium redemptiónem sanctum Petrum Ecclésiam tuam nova prole fecundáre divínitus docuísti: ipsíus nobis intercessióne concéde, a peccáti servitúte solútis; in cælésti pátria perpétua libertáte gaudére: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who, as an example of Your love, divinely taught St. Peter to enrich Your Church with new offspring, a family of Religious devoted to the ransom of the faithful, grant by his intercession, that we may be released from the slavery of sin and rejoice in lasting freedom in heaven; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Petro Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Peter, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0129": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 368-371; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ad animárum salútem beátum Francíscum Confessórem tuum atque Pontíficem, ómnibus ómnia factum esse voluísti: concéde propítius, ut caritátis tuæ dulcédine perfúsi; eius dirigéntibus mónitis, ac suffragántibus méritis, ætérna gáudia consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who for the salvation of souls willed that blessed Francis, Your Confessor and Bishop, should become all things to all men, mercifully grant that we, inspired by the sweetness of Your love, guided by his teachings, and aided by his merits, may attain the joys of everlasting life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Francísci Pontíficis tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed Francis, Your bishop and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Francísci Pontíficis tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed Francis, Your bishop and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0131": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 369-370; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui sanctum Ioánnem Confessórem tuum adolescéntium patrem et magístrum excitásti; ac per eum, auxiliatríce Vírgine María, novas in Ecclésia tua famílias floréscere voluísti: concéde, quǽsumus, ut eódem caritátis igne succénsi; ánimas quǽrere, tibíque soli servíre valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who in Your Confessor, blessed John, raised up a father and teacher of youth, and willed that through him, with the help of the Virgin Mary, new religious families should bloom in the Church, grant, we beseech You, that, inflamed by the same fire of love, we may seek to win souls and to serve You alone; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, oblatiónem mundam salutáris Hóstiæ et præsta, ut, te in ómnibus et super ómnia diligéntes, in glóriæ tuæ laudem vívere mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, O Lord, this pure offering of the saving Host, and grant, that loving You in all and above all, we may be found worthy to live for the praise of Your glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Córporis et Sánguinis tui, Dómine, mystério satiátis, concéde, quǽsumus; ut, intercedénte sancto Ioánne Confessóre, in gratiárum semper actióne maneámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Nourished with the mystery of Your Body and Blood, grant, we beseech You, O Lord, through the intercession of Saint John, Your Confessor, that we may continue to be thankful; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0202": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 372-375; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, maiestátem tuam súpplices exorámus: ut sicut unigénitus Fílius tuus hodiérna die cum nostræ carnis substántia in templo est præsentátus; ita nos fácias purificátis tibi méntibus præsentári: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, eternal God, we humbly beseech Your majesty that, as Your only-begotten Son was this day presented in the temple in the nature of our flesh, so may You grant us to be presented to You with purified minds; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Exáudi Dómine preces nostras: et ut digna sint múnera, quæ óculis tuæ maiestátis offérimus, subsídium nobis, per intercessiónem beátæ Maríæ Vírginis, perpétuæ tuæ pietátis impénde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, heed our prayer, and give us the help of Your loving kindness so that the gifts we offer before the eyes of Your majesty may be worthy of You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut sacrosáncta mystéria, quæ pro reparatiónis nostræ munímine contulísti; intercedénte beáta María semper Vírgine, et præsens nobis remédium esse fácias, et futúrum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord our God, that the sacrament You have given as the bulwark of our atonement may be made a saving remedy for us in this life and in the life to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0204": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 376; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui in Ecclésia tua nova semper instáuras exémpla virtútum: da pópulo tuo, beáti Andréæ Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis ita sequi vestígia; ut assequátur et prǽmia: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who establish ever new examples of virtue in Your Church, grant that Your people may follow the footsteps of blessed Andrew, Your Confessor and Bishop, so that they may also obtain his reward; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sit in conspéctu tuo Dómine nostra devótio: ut eius nobis fiat supplicatióne salutáris, pro cuius solemnitáte defértur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our devotion be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, and may it become saving for us through the supplication of him on whose feast it is offered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, fidélibus tuis, Sanctórum tuórum semper veneratióne lætári; et eórum perpétua supplicatióne muníri: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, to Your faithful ever to rejoice in the veneration of Your saints and to be defended by their unceasing intercession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0207": {"src": "Sancti/02-07", "or": ["Intercéssio nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, beáti N. Abbátis comméndet: ut, quod nostris méritis non valémus, eius patrocínio assequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "se": ["Sacris altáribus, Dómine, hóstias superpósitas sanctus N. Abbas, quǽsumus, in salútem nobis proveníre depóscat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Prótegat nos, Dómine, cum tui perceptióne sacraménti beátus N. Abbas, pro nobis intercedéndo: ut et conversatiónis eius experiámur insígnia, et intercessiónis percipiámus suffrágia. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "S0208": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 378; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui per sanctum Ioánnem Ordinem sanctíssimæ Trinitátis, ad rediméndum de potestáte Saracenórum captívos, cǽlitus institúere dignátus es: præsta quǽsumus, ut eius suffragántibus méritis; a captivitáte córporis et ánimæ, te adiuvánte, liberémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who graciously and by divine means founded through blessed John, the Order of the Most Holy Trinity to ransom captives from the hands of the Saracens, grant, we beseech You, that through Your help and the merits of his prayers we may be freed body and soul from captivity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Ioánne Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed John, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0209": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 378-379; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus qui beátum Cyríllum Confessórem tuum atque Pontíficem divínæ maternitátis beatíssimæ Vírginis Maríæ assertórem invíctum effecísti: concéde, ipso intercedénte, ut qui vere eam Genitrícem Dei crédimus; matérna eiúsdem protectióne salvémur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who made Cyril, Your Confessor and Bishop, an unconquerable champion of the most Blessed Virgin Mary’s divine motherhood, grant that we who believe that she is truly the Mother of God may be saved by her motherly protection; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera nostra, omnípotens Deus, benígnus réspice: et intercedénte beáto Cyríllo præsta, ut Unigénitum tuum Iesum Christum Dóminum nostrum in tua tecum glória coætérnum, in córdibus nostris digne suscípere mereámur: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously, almighty God, upon our gifts and, through the intercession of blessed Cyril, grant that we may receive worthily into our hearts, Your only-begotten Son, Jesus Christ, our Lord, Who is with You co-eternal in Your glory; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divínis Dómine, refécti mystériis, Te súpplices deprecámur: ut exémplis et méritis beáti Cyrílli Pontíficis adiúti; sanctíssimæ Genitríci Unigéniti tui digne famulári valeámus: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Strengthened by the Blessed Sacrament, we humbly beseech You, O Lord, that, helped by the example and merits of the blessed Bishop Cyril, we may be worthy servants of the most holy Mother of Your only-begotten Son; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0211": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 379-380 (In Apparitione B.M.V. Immaculatae, 11 Februarii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui per Immaculátam Vírginis Conceptiónem dignum Fílio tuo habitáculum præparásti: súpplices a te quǽsumus, ut eiúsdem Vírginis Apparitiónem celebrántes; salútem mentis et córporis consequámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the Immaculate Conception of the Virgin prepared a worthy dwelling for Your Son, we humbly beseech You that, celebrating the Apparition of the same Virgin, we may obtain health of mind and body; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstia laudis, quam tibi, Dómine, per mérita gloriósæ et Immaculátæ Vírginis, offérimus, sit tibi in odórem suavitátis, et nobis optátam cónferat córporis et ánimæ sanitátem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifice of praise which we offer You, O Lord, through the merits of the glorious and Immaculate Virgin, be to You an odor of sweetness, and bring us the health of body and soul we desire; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quos cælésti, Dómine, aliménto satiásti, súblevet déxtera Genitrícis tuæ Immaculátæ: ut ad ætérnam pátriam, ipsa adiuvánte, perveníre mereámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the right hand of Your Immaculate Mother, O Lord, uphold those whom You have fed with heavenly food, that by her help we may deserve to reach our eternal home; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0212": {"src": "Sancti/02-12", "or": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, qui, ad recoléndam memóriam dolórum sanctíssimæ Genetrícis tuæ, per septem beátos Patres nova Servorum eius família Ecclésiam tuam fœcundásti: concéde propítius; ita nos eórum consociári flétibus, ut perfruámur et gáudiis: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, Who, to keep alive the memory of Your most holy Mother’s sorrows, through the seven holy fathers enriched your Church with a new family of her Servants, graciously grant that we may be so united with them in their sorrows, as also to share their joys. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, hóstias quas tibi offérimus: et præsta; ut, intercedéntibus Sanctis tuis, libera tibi mente serviámus, et perdoléntis Vírginis Genetrícis Fílii tui amóre inflammémur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, we beseech You, O Lord, the sacrificial gifts we offer, so that by the intercession of Your saints we may serve You with freedom of mind and be set on fire with love for the sorrowing Mother of Your Son. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cœléstibus refécti mystériis te, Dómine, deprecámur: ut, quorum festa percólimus imitántes exémpla; iuxta Crucem Iesu cum María Matre eius fidéliter astémus, et eiúsdem redemptiónis fructum percípere mereámur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Strengthened by the heavenly sacrament, we beseech You, O Lord, that, following the example of those whose feast we are keeping, we may faithfully stand beneath the Cross of Jesus with Mary, His Mother, and be found worthy to receive the fruit of His redemption. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0223": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 386-389; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Concéde nos, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, beáti Petri Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis mónita et exémpla sectári; ut per terréstrium rerum contémptum, ætérna gáudia consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, to follow the counsel and examples of St. Peter, Your Confessor and Bishop, so that by setting earthly goods at naught we may attain everlasting happiness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Petri Confessóris tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed Peter, Your confessor and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Petri Confessóris tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed Peter, Your confessor and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0224": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 387-388; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Matthíam Apostolórum tuórum collégio sociásti; tríbue quǽsumus, ut eius interventióne, tuæ circa nos pietátis semper víscera sentiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who joined blessed Matthias to the company of Your Apostles, grant, we beseech You, that by his intercession we may ever feel the tenderness of Your love towards us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, qui proditóris apóstatæ ruínam, ne Apostolórum tuórum númerus sacrátus perfectióne caréret, beáti Matthíæ electióne supplésti, præséntia múnera sanctífica: ut ea nos grátiæ tuæ virtúte confírment. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the election of blessed Matthias made good the fall of the apostate traitor, so that the sacred number of Your Apostles should not lack its completeness, sanctify these present gifts, that by them we may be strengthened through the power of Your grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens et miséricors Deus: ut per hæc sancta, quæ súmpsimus; interveniénte beáto Matthía Apóstolo tuo, véniam consequámur et pacem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty and merciful God, that through these holy things which we have received, by the intercession of blessed Matthias Your Apostle, we may obtain pardon and peace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0307": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 390-391; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Thomæ Confessóris tui atque Doctóris mira eruditióne claríficas, et sancta operatióne fecúndas: da nobis, quǽsumus, et quæ dócuit, intelléctu conspícere; et quæ egit, imitatióne complére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who enlighten Your Church by the wonderful learning of blessed Thomas, Your confessor and doctor, and make her fruitful by his holy works, grant us, we beseech You, both to understand what he taught and to fulfil by imitation what he did; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Passiónis Fílii tui, Dómine, memóriam recenséntes depóscimus, ut quod tibi in beáti Thomæ Confessóris tui atque Doctóris solemnitáte deférimus, sacrifícium sit accéptum. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Recalling the memory of the Passion of Your Son, O Lord, we ask that the sacrifice which we offer You on the feast of blessed Thomas, Your confessor and doctor, may be acceptable; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Hæc nos, quǽsumus Dómine, commúnio sancta lætíficet: qua beáti Thomæ Confessóris tui atque Doctóris suffrágiis, virtútes roboréntur intérius; et actus extérius piæ operatiónis excréscant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this holy communion, we beseech You, O Lord, gladden us, that by the prayers of blessed Thomas, Your confessor and doctor, our virtues may be strengthened within and the works of devout service may increase without; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0308": {"src": "Sancti/03-08", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Ioánnem, tuo amóre succénsum, inter flammas innóxium incédere fecísti, et per eum Ecclésiam tuam nova prole fœcundásti: præsta, ipsíus suffragántibus méritis; ut igne caritátis tuæ vitia nostra curéntur, et remédia nobis ætérna provéniant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who caused blessed John when burning with love for You, to walk unharmed through the midst of flames, and through him enriched Your Church with a new religious family; grant that through the help of his merits, our sins may be burned away by the fire of Your love, and eternal remedies may come to us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi, Dómine, hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cœlésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut, in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus, eius muniámur et précibus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "S0319": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 398-399; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Beáti Patriárchæ Ioseph, sanctíssimæ Genitrícis tuæ sponsi, quǽsumus Dómine, méritis adiuvémur: ut quod possibílitas nostra non óbtinet; eius nobis intercessióne donétur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May we be helped, we beseech You, O Lord, by the merits of the blessed Patriarch Joseph, the spouse of Your most holy Mother, that what our own power cannot obtain may be given us by his intercession; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Débitum tibi, Dómine, nostræ réddimus servitútis, supplíciter exorántes: ut suffrágiis beáti Ioseph sponsi Genitrícis Fílii tui Iesu Christi Dómini nostri, in nobis tua múnera tueáris; ob cuius venerándam festivitátem, laudis tibi hóstias immolámus. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We render You, O Lord, the debt of our service, humbly beseeching You that by the prayers of blessed Joseph, spouse of the Mother of Your Son Jesus Christ our Lord, You may guard Your gifts in us, on whose venerable feast we offer You sacrifices of praise; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sit nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, per hæc sancta, quæ súmpsimus, beatíssimi Ioseph Patriárchæ solémnitas, præsídium salutáre; qui pretiósæ sponsæ suæ Vírginis matris Fílium in præsépio méruit adoráre Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the feast of the most blessed Patriarch Joseph, we beseech You, O Lord, be to us through these holy things which we have received a saving protection, he who was found worthy to adore in the manger the Son of his precious spouse the Virgin Mother, our Lord Jesus Christ Your Son; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0324": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 401-402; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, cui Angelórum míllia minístrant: præsta, quǽsumus, ut qui beátum Gabriélem Archángelum humánæ restauratiónis præcípuum minístrum venerámur in terris; eiúsdem suffrágiis fructum nostræ redemptiónis consequámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, whom thousands of Angels serve, grant, we beseech You, that we who venerate on earth blessed Gabriel the Archangel, the chief minister of man's restoration, may by his prayers obtain in heaven the fruit of our redemption; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accéptum fiat in conspéctu tuo, Dómine, nostræ servitútis munus, et beáti Archángeli Gabriélis orátio: ut a nobis venerátus in terris, sit apud te advocátus in cælis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the gift of our service be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, together with the prayer of blessed Gabriel the Archangel, that he who is venerated by us on earth may be our advocate with You in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Córporis tui et Sánguinis sumptis mystériis, tuam Dómine Deus noster deprecámur cleméntiam: ut sicut Gabriéle nuntiánte, incarnatiónem tuam cognóvimus; ita ipso adiuvánte, incarnatiónis eiúsdem benefícia consequámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received the mysteries of Your Body and Blood, we entreat Your mercy, O Lord our God, that, as by the message of Gabriel we have known Your incarnation, so by his help we may obtain the benefits of that same incarnation; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0327": {"src": "Sancti/03-27", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui, ad cultum sacrárum imáginum asseréndum, beátum Ioánnem cœlésti doctrína et admirábili spíritus fortitúdine imbuísti: concéde nobis eius intercessióne et exémplo; ut, quorum cólimus imagines, virtútes imitémur et patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, eternal God, Who to defend the honor paid to sacred images, filled blessed John with heavenly learning and wondrous strength of soul, grant that, by his intercession and example, we may imitate the virtues of those whose images we honor and may enjoy the help of their patronage. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ut, quæ tibi, Dómine, offérimus, dona tuo sint digna conspéctu: beáti Ioánnis et Sanctórum, quos eius ópera expósitos in templis cólimus, pia suffragátio conspíret. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, may the holy intercession of blessed John be united with that of Your Saints whose images, through his efforts, we venerate in our churches, and thus may the gifts we offer You be found worthy in Your sight. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumpta nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, dona cœléstibus armis tueántur: et beáti Ioánnis patrocínia circúmdent Sanctórum unánimi suffrágio cumuláta; quorum imágines evícit in Ecclésia esse venerándas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, that the gifts we have eaten may be as heavenly weapons to guard us; and may we be protected by the patronage of blessed John, reinforced by the united prayers of the Saints, the veneration of whose images by the Church, he gloriously vindicated. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0402": {"src": "Sancti/04-02", "or": ["Deus, humílium celsitúdo, qui beátum Francíscum Confessórem Sanctórum tuórum glória sublimásti: tríbue, quǽsumus; ut, eius méritis et imitatióne, promíssa humílibus præmia felíciter consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the greatness of the humble, Who raised blessed Francis, Your Confessor, to the glory of Your Saints, grant, we beseech You, that, by his merits and our imitation of his life, we may happily attain the rewards promised to the humble. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc dona devótæ plebis, Dómine, quibus tua cumulámus altária, beáti Francísci méritis tibi grata nobísque salutária, te miseránte, reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these sacrificial gifts which Your devoted people heap upon Your altar, O Lord, become pleasing to You by the merits of blessed Francis, and, by Your mercy, helpful to us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumpta, Dómine, sacraménta cœléstia: beáto Francísco Confessóre tuo intercedénte, precámur; ut et temporális vitæ subsídia nobis cónferant et ætérnæ. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We pray You, O Lord, that the heavenly sacrament which we have received, may by the intercession of blessed Francis, Your Confessor, help us both in this life and in the life everlasting. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0404": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 408; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Isidórum minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave blessed Isidore to Your people as a minister of eternal salvation, grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have him as our intercessor in heaven whom we had as the teacher of life on earth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Isidóri Pontíficis tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed Isidore, Your bishop and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Isidóri Pontíficis tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed Isidore, Your bishop and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0421": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 414-417; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Ansélmum minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave blessed Anselm to Your people as a minister of eternal salvation, grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have him as our intercessor in heaven whom we had as the teacher of life on earth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Ansélmi Pontíficis tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed Anselm, Your bishop and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Ansélmi Pontíficis tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed Anselm, Your bishop and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0425": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 418-419; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Marcum Evangelístam tuum, Evangélicæ prædicatiónis grátia sublimásti: tríbue, quǽsumus, eius nos semper et eruditióne profícere; et oratióne deféndi: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who exalted blessed Mark, Your Evangelist, by the grace of preaching the Gospel, grant, we beseech You, that we may ever profit by his teaching and be defended by his prayer; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Beáti Marci Evangelístæ tui solemnitáte tibi múnera deferéntes, quǽsumus Dómine, ut sicut illum prædicátio Evangélica fecit gloriósum, ita nos eius intercéssio, et verbo, et ópere tibi reddat accéptos. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Bringing You gifts on the feast of blessed Mark, Your Evangelist, we beseech You, O Lord, that, as the preaching of the Gospel made him glorious, so his intercession may make us acceptable to You in word and deed; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Pasti cibo spiritális alimóniæ, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut quod mystério frequentámus; intercedénte beáto Marco Evangelísta, plena veritáte consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Fed with the food of spiritual nourishment, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that what we often receive in mystery we may, by the intercession of blessed Mark the Evangelist, obtain in the fullness of truth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0501": {"src": "Sancti/05-01r", "or": ["Rerum cónditor Deus, qui legem labóris humáno géneri statuísti: concéde propítius; ut, sancti Ioseph exémplo et patrocínio, ópera perficiámus quæ præcipis, et præmia consequámur quæ promíttis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Creator of all things, Who dost impose on man the law of work; grant in Thy goodness that, by the example and patronage of blessed Joseph, we may both accomplish the work Thou dost command and attain the reward Thou hast promised. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Quas tibi, Dómine, de opéribus mánuum nostrárum offérimus hóstias, sancti Ioseph interpósito suffrágio, pignus fácias nobis unitátis et pacis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these gifts, the work of our hands, that we offer Thee in sacrifice, O Lord, become for us, by the intercession of blessed Joseph, a pledge of unity and peace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Hæc sancta quæ súmpsimus, Dómine, per intercessiónem beáti Ioseph; et operatiónem nostram cómpleant, et prǽmia confírment. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these holy mysteries which we have received, O Lord, by the intercession of blessed Joseph, supply what is wanting in our works, and assure us of Thy rewards. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0502": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 427-428; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Athanásium minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave blessed Athanasius to Your people as a minister of eternal salvation, grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have him as our intercessor in heaven whom we had as the teacher of life on earth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Athanásii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed Athanasius, Your confessor and bishop, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Athanásii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed Athanasius, Your confessor and bishop, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0510": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 439-440; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Sancti Antoníni, Dómine, Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis méritis adiuvémur: ut sicut te in illo mirábilem prædicámus; ita in nos misericórdem fuísse gloriémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May we be helped, O Lord, by the merits of saint Antoninus, Your confessor and bishop, that, as we proclaim You wonderful in him, so we may glory that You have been merciful to us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícium nostrum, Dómine, beátus Antonínus sacérdos maiestátis tuæ óculis reddat accéptum: qui se tibi, dum vixit, sanctam et placéntem hóstiam immolávit. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Antoninus the priest, O Lord, make our sacrifice acceptable in the eyes of Your majesty, he who while he lived offered himself to You as a holy and pleasing victim; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Vitáli cibo recreáti, grátias tibi Dómine ágimus: et rogámus, ut quod ad glóriam súmpsimus sancti tui Præsulis Antoníni; eius précibus sit nobis contra hostíles ímpetus auxílium: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with life-giving food, we give You thanks, O Lord, and ask that what we have received for the glory of Your holy bishop Antoninus may by his prayers be our help against the assaults of the enemy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0515": {"src": "Sancti/05-15", "or": ["Deus, qui, ad christiánam páuperum eruditiónem et ad iuvéntam in via veritátis firmándam, sanctum Ioánnem Baptístam Confessórem excitásti, et novam per eum in Ecclésia famíliam collegísti: concéde propítius; ut eius intercessióne et exémplo, stúdio glóriæ tuæ in animárum salúte fervéntes, eius in cœlis corónæ partícipes fíeri valeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who raised up the holy Confessor John Baptist for the Christian education of the poor and to strengthen youth in the way of truth, and through him formed a new family in the Church, graciously grant by his intercession and example that we, striving to save souls out of zeal for Your glory, may be found worthy to share his heavenly crown. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi, Dómine, hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cœlésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut, in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus, eius muniámur et précibus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "S0527": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 454; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Bedæ Confessóris tui atque Doctóris eruditióne claríficas: concéde propítius fámulis tuis; eius semper illustrári sapiéntia et méritis adiuvári: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who enlightened Your Church with the learning of blessed Bede, Your Confessor and Doctor, graciously grant that Your servants may ever be enlightened by his wisdom and helped by his merits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Bedæ Confessóris tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed Bede, Your confessor and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Bedæ Confessóris tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed Bede, Your confessor and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0606": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 462; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Norbértum Confessórem tuum atque Pontíficem, verbi tui præcónem exímium effecísti; et per eum Ecclésiam tuam nova prole fecundásti: præsta quǽsumus, ut eiúsdem suffragántibus méritis, quod ore simul et ópere dócuit; te adiuvánte exercére valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who made blessed Norbert, Your Confessor and Bishop, a brilliant preacher of Your word, and through him enriched Your Church with a new religious family, grant, we beseech You, that by his prayerful intercession and Your help, we may be able to do what he has taught us by his words and deeds; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti tui, quǽsumus Dómine, nos ubíque lætíficent: ut dum eórum mérita recólimus, patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your saints, we beseech You, O Lord, everywhere gladden us, that while we recall their merits we may feel their protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut de percéptis munéribus grátias exhibéntes; intercedénte beáto Norbérto Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, benefícia potióra sumámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that, giving thanks for the gifts received, we may, by the intercession of blessed Norbert, Your confessor and bishop, receive still greater benefits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0611": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 464-465; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beátus Bárnabas Apóstolus, tuum pro nobis implóret auxílium; ut a nostris reátibus absolúti, a cunctis étiam perículis eruámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that blessed Barnabas the Apostle may implore Your help for us, that, being freed from our sins, we may also be delivered from all dangers; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrándum tibi, Dómine, munus offérimus: quo beáti Bárnabæ Apóstoli tui solémnia recoléntes, purificatiónem quoque nostris méntibus implorámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gift to be consecrated, by which, keeping the feast of blessed Barnabas Your Apostle, we implore also the cleansing of our minds; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Percéptis Dómine sacraméntis, supplíciter exorámus: ut intercedénte beáto Bárnaba Apóstolo tuo, quæ pro illíus veneránda gérimus passióne; nobis profíciant ad medélam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received the sacraments, O Lord, we humbly entreat You that, by the intercession of blessed Barnabas Your Apostle, what we do in veneration of his passion may avail for our healing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0613": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 466; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Ecclésiam tuam, Deus, beáti Antónii Confessóris tui solémnitas votíva lætíficet: ut spirituálibus semper muniátur auxíliis; et gáudiis pérfrui mereátur ætérnis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the devout feast of blessed Anthony, Your confessor, gladden Your Church, O God, that she may ever be defended by spiritual help and deserve to enjoy everlasting joys; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsens oblátio fiat, Dómine, pópulo tuo salutáris, pro quo dignátus es Patri tuo te vivéntem hóstiam immoláre: Qui cum eódem Deo Patre et Spíritu Sancto vivis et regnas Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this present offering, O Lord, be saving for Your people, for whom You deigned to offer Yourself to Your Father as a living victim; who with the same God the Father and the Holy Spirit live and reign, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divínis, Dómine, munéribus satiáti: quǽsumus, ut beáti Antónii Confessóris tui méritis gloriósis; salutáris víctimæ desiderátum sentiámus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with divine gifts, we beseech You, O Lord, that by the glorious merits of blessed Anthony, Your confessor, we may feel the longed-for effect of the saving Victim; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0618": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 469-470; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Ephræm Confessóris tui et Doctóris mira eruditióne et præcláris vitæ méritis illustráre voluísti: te súpplices exorámus; ut, ipso intercedénte, eam advérsus erróris et pravitátis insídias perénni tua virtúte deféndas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who willed to enlighten Your Church by the wondrous learning and glorious merits of the life of blessed Ephrem, Your Confessor and Doctor, we humbly pray You, that, by his pleading, You will shield her with Your lasting power against the snares of error and evil; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Ephræm Confessóris tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed Ephrem, Your confessor and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Ephræm Confessóris tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed Ephrem, Your confessor and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0624": {"src": "Sancti/06-24", "or": ["Deus, qui præséntem diem honorábilem nobis in beáti Ioánnis nativitáte fecísti: da pópulis tuis spirituálium grátiam gaudiórum; et ómnium fidélium mentes dirige in viam salútis ætérnæ. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who made this a day most worthy of our celebration because of blessed John; grant Your people the grace of spiritual joys and direct the minds of all the faithful into the path of eternal salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Tua, Dómine, munéribus altária cumulámus: illíus nativitátem honóre débito celebrántes, qui Salvatórem mundi et cécinit ad futúrum et adésse monstravit, Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We heap Your altar with gifts, O Lord, celebrating the birth of him who announced the coming of the Saviour of the world, our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, and made His presence known. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumat Ecclésia tua, Deus, beáti Ioánnis Baptístæ generatióne lætítiam: per quem suæ regeneratiónis cognóvit auctórem, Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your Church, O God, rejoice at the birth of blessed John the Baptist, through whom she knew the author of her own rebirth, Your Son, our Lord Jesus Christ. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0626": {"src": "Sancti/06-26", "or": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut nos gemináta lætítia hodiérnæ festivitátis excípiat, quæ de beatórum Ioánnis et Pauli glorificatióne procédit; quos eadem fides et pássio vere fecit esse germános. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that on this feast-day we may have the double joy of celebrating blessed John and Paul, true brothers who obtained eternal glory through one faith and one martyrdom. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, sanctórum Martyrum tuórum Ioánnis et Pauli dicátas méritis, benígnus assúme: et ad perpétuum nobis tríbue proveníre subsídium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, graciously accept, through the merits of Your holy Martyrs John and Paul, the sacrificial gifts dedicated to You, and grant they may prove to be for us a lasting help. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, sanctórum Martyrum tuórum Ioánnis et Pauli sollémnia celebrántes, sacraménta cœléstia: præsta, quǽsumus; ut, quod temporáliter gérimus, ætérnis gáudiis consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have partaken of the heavenly sacrament, O Lord, as we celebrate the feast of Your holy Martyrs John and Paul; grant, we beseech You, that what we do in time we may reap in joy in eternity. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0629": {"src": "Sancti/06-29", "or": ["Deus, qui hodiérnam diem Apostolórum tuórum Petri et Pauli martýrio consecrásti: da Ecclésiæ tuæ, eórum in ómnibus sequi præcéptum; per quos religiónis sumpsit exórdium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who made this day holy by the martyrdom of Your Apostles Peter and Paul, grant Your Church to follow in all things the teaching of those from whom she first received the faith. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias, Dómine, quas nómini tuo sacrándas offérimus, apostólica prosequátur orátio: per quam nos expiári tríbuas et deféndi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the prayers of Your holy Apostles, O Lord, accompany the sacrificial gifts which we offer to be hallowed in Your name, so that we may obtain pardon and protection. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quos cœlésti, Dómine, aliménto satiásti: apostólicis intercessiónibus ab omni adversitáte custódi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, by the intercession of Your Apostles, defend from all harm those whom You have filled with heavenly food. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0630": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 481-482 (In Commemoratione S. Pauli, 30 Junii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui multitúdinem Géntium beáti Pauli Apóstoli prædicatióne docuísti: da nobis, quǽsumus, ut cuius natalítia cólimus; eius apud te patrocínia sentiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who taught the multitude of the Gentiles by the preaching of blessed Paul the Apostle, grant us, we beseech You, that we who keep his birthday may feel the help of his patronage with You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias, Dómine, quas nómini tuo sacrándas offérimus, Apostólica prosequátur orátio, per quam nos expiári tríbuas, et deféndi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the prayer of the Apostles accompany the offerings which we bring to be consecrated to Your name, O Lord, and by it grant us to be cleansed and defended; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Percéptis, Dómine, sacraméntis, beáto Paulo Apóstolo tuo interveniénte, deprecámur: ut quæ pro illíus celebráta sunt glória; nobis profíciant ad medélam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received Your sacraments, O Lord, we pray that, by the intercession of blessed Paul Your Apostle, what has been celebrated for his glory may avail for our healing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0701": {"src": "Sancti/07-01", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui unigénitum Fílium tuum mundi Redemptórem constituísti, ac eius Sánguine placári voluísti: concéde, quǽsumus, salútis nostræ prétium sollémni cultu ita venerári, atque a præséntis vitæ malis eius virtúte deféndi in terris; ut fructu perpétuo lætémur in cœlis. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, eternal God, Who made Your only-begotten Son the Redeemer of the world, and willed to be reconciled by His Blood, grant us, we beseech You, so to worship in this sacred rite the price of our salvation, and to be so protected by its power against the evils of the present life on earth, that we may enjoy its everlasting fruit in heaven. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Per hæc divína mystéria, ad novi, quǽsumus, Testaménti mediatórem Iesum accedámus: et super altária tua, Dómine virtútum, aspersiónem sánguinis mélius loquéntem, quam Abel, innovémus. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through this divine rite, we beseech You, may we draw near to Jesus, the mediator of the new covenant, and renew upon Your altar, O Lord of hosts, the sprinkling of blood more eloquent than that of Abel. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ad sacram, Dómine, mensam admíssi, háusimus aquas in gáudio de fóntibus Salvatóris: sanguis eius fiat nobis, quǽsumus, fons aquæ in vitam ætérnam saliéntis: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Admitted to the sacred banquet, O Lord, we have drawn water in joy from the Saviour’s fountain; may His Blood, we beseech You, become for us a fountain of water springing up unto life everlasting. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0705": {"src": "Sancti/07-05", "or": ["Fac nos, Dómine Deus, supereminéntem Iesu Christi sciéntiam, spíritu Pauli Apóstoli, edíscere: qua beátus Antónius María mirabíliter erudítus, novas in Ecclésia tua clericórum et vírginum famílias congregávit. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, O Lord God, to learn in the spirit of Paul the Apostle that excelling knowledge of Jesus Christ, by which St. Anthony Mary, himself wondrously learned, gathered together in Your Church new families of clerics and virgins. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ad mensam cœléstis convívii fac nos, Dómine, eam mentis et córporis puritátem afférre, qua beátus Antónius María, hanc sacratíssimam hóstiam ófferens, mirífice ornátus enítuit. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May we bring to the table of the heavenly banquet, O Lord, that purity of mind and body with which St. Anthony Mary was so wondrously imbued and in which he excelled when he offered these sacrificial gifts. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cœlésti dape, qua pasti sumus, Dómine Iesu Christe, eo corda nostra caritátis igne flamméscant: quo beátus Antónius María salutáris hóstiæ vexíllum, contra Ecclésiæ tuæ hostes, éxtulit ad victóriam:", "May the heavenly banquet at which we have been fed, O Lord Jesus Christ, set our hearts aflame with that fire of love with which St. Anthony Mary bore the banner of the saving Victim to victory against the enemies of Your Church. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0710": {"src": "Sancti/07-10", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui gloriósos Mártyres fortes in sua confessióne cognóvimus, pios apud te in nostra intercessióne sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, quǽsumus, Dómine, inténde placátus: et, intercedéntibus Sanctis tuis, devotióni nostræ profíciant et salúti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with favor, we beseech You, O Lord, upon the offerings here before You, that, through the intercession of Your Saints, they may be beneficial for our devotion and salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, intercedéntibus Sanctis tuis, illíus salutáris capiámus efféctum; cuius per heec mystéria pignus accépimus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that, by the intercession of Your Saints, we may obtain the effect of that salvation pledged to us through this sacred rite. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0712": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 494-497; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Intercéssio nos, quǽsumus Dómine, beáti Ioánnis Abbátis comméndet: ut quod nostris méritis non valémus; eius patrocínio assequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the intercession of blessed John the Abbot, we beseech You, O Lord, commend us to You, that what we cannot obtain by our own merits we may obtain by his patronage; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Prótegat nos, Dómine, cum tui perceptióne sacraménti, beátus Ioánnes Abbas, pro nobis intercedéndo: ut et conversatiónis eius experiámur insígnia; et intercessiónis ipsíus percipiámus suffrágia: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed John the Abbot, interceding for us, protect us, O Lord, together with the reception of Your sacrament, that we may both experience the excellence of his way of life and receive the help of his intercession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0714": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 495-497; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Bonaventúram minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave blessed Bonaventure to Your people as a minister of eternal salvation, grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have him as our intercessor in heaven whom we had as the teacher of life on earth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti Bonaventúræ Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis nobis, Dómine, pia non desit orátio: quæ et múnera nostra concíliet, et tuam nobis indulgéntiam semper obtíneat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the loving prayer of saint Bonaventure, Your confessor and bishop, not fail us, O Lord, that it may make our gifts acceptable and ever obtain for us Your pardon; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ut nobis, Dómine, tua sacrifícia dent salútem; beátus Bonaventúra Conféssor tuus et Póntifex, quǽsumus, precátor accédat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "That Your sacrifices may give us salvation, O Lord, may blessed Bonaventure, Your confessor and bishop, we beseech You, come forward as our advocate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0715": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 497; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui hodiérna die beátum Henrícum Confessórem tuum e terréni cúlmine impérii ad regnum ætérnum transtulísti; te súpplices exorámus: ut sicut illum, grátiæ tuæ ubertáte prævéntum, illécebras sǽculi superáre fecísti; ita nos fácias, eius imitatióne, mundi huius blandiménta vitáre, et ad te puris méntibus perveníre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who on this day took St. Henry, Your Confessor, to the everlasting kingdom from the throne of an earthly empire; we humbly beseech You, that as You enabled him, protected by the abundance of Your grace, to overcome the temptations of the world, so grant that we, in emulation of him, may shun the allurements of this world and come to You with pure hearts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi Dómine hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus, et futúris: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, sacrifices of praise in commemoration of Your saints, through whom we trust to be delivered from evils both present and to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cælésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus; eius muniámur et précibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly food and drink, O our God, we humbly entreat You that we may also be defended by the prayers of him in whose commemoration we have received these gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0719": {"src": "Sancti/07-19", "or": ["Deus, qui, ad evangelizándum paupéribus et ecclesiástici órdinis decórem promovéndum, beátum Vincéntium apostólica virtúte roborásti: præsta, quǽsumus; ut, cuius pia mérita venerámur, virtútum quoque instruámur exémplis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who endowed St. Vincent with apostolic strength to preach the Gospel to the poor and to enhance the dignity of clerical life; grant, we beseech You, that we who honor his holy merits may also conform to the example of his virtues. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui cœléstia aliménta percépimus, intercedénte beáto N. Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "S0720": {"src": "Sancti/07-20", "or": ["Deus, misericordiárum pater, per mérita et intercessiónem beáti Hieronymi, quem órphanis adiutorem et patrem esse voluísti: concéde; ut spíritum adoptiónis, quo fílii tui nominámur et sumus, fidéliter custodiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the Father of mercies, by the merits and intercession of St. Jerome, whom You willed to be the helper and father of orphans, grant that we may faithfully guard the spirit of adoption which makes us Your sons both in name and reality. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Clementíssime Deus, qui, véteri homine consúmpto, novum secúndum te in beáto Hierónymo creáre dignátus es: da, per mérita ipsíus; ut nos, páriter renováti, hanc placatiónis hóstiam in odórem tibi suavíssimum offerámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O most merciful God, Who in blessed Jerome graciously destroyed the old to create in him a new man in Your likeness, grant by his merits, that we, in like manner reborn, may offer You this sacrifice of atonement as a most sweet fragrance. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Angelórum pane refécti te, Dómine, supplíciter deprecámur: ut, qui ánnuam beáti Hierónymi Confessóris tui memóriam celebráre gaudémus; eiúsdem étiam et exémplum imitémur, et amplíssimum in regno tuo præmium obtinére valeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with the bread of angels, we humbly pray You, O Lord, that we who joyfully celebrate the yearly feast of blessed Jerome, Your Confessor, may follow his example and be enabled to win a most abundant reward in Your kingdom. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0725": {"src": "Sancti/07-25", "or": ["Esto, Dómine, plebi tuæ sanctificátor et custos: ut, Apóstoli tui Iacóbi muníta præsídiis, et conversatióne tibi pláceat, et secúra mente desérviat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Protect Your people and make them holy, O Lord, so that, guarded by the help of Your Apostle James, they may please You by their conduct and serve You with peace of mind. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblatiónes pópuli tui, quǽsumus, Dómine, beáti Iacóbi Apóstoli pássio beáta concíliet: et, quæ nostris non aptæ sunt méritis, fiant tibi plácitæ eius deprecatióne. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the holy martyrdom of blessed James, the Apostle, make acceptable the offerings of Your people; and because our own merits are insufficient, may his prayer make them pleasing to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Beáti Apóstoli tui Iacóbi, quǽsumus, Dómine, intercessióne nos ádiuva: pro cuius festivitáte percépimus tua sancta lætántes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Help us, O Lord, we beseech You, by the intercession of blessed James, Your Apostle, for whose festival we have joyfully received Your holy sacrament. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0807": {"src": "Sancti/08-07", "or": ["Deus, qui beáto Caietáno Confessóri tuo apostólicam vivéndi formam imitári tribuísti: da nobis, eius intercessióne et exémplo, in te semper confídere et sola cæléstia desideráre. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who bestowed upon St. Cajetan, Your Confessor, the grace to follow the apostolic way of life; grant us by his intercession and example ever to trust in You and to long only for the things of heaven. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi, Dómine, hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cœlésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut, in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus, eius muniámur et précibus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "S0810": {"src": "Sancti/08-10", "or": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: vitiórum nostrorum flammas exstínguere; qui beáto Lauréntio tribuísti tormentórum suórum incéndia superáre. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, to extinguish the flames of our sins, as You granted St. Lawrence to overcome the fires of his tortures. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, múnera dignánter obláta: et, beáti Lauréntii suffragántibus méritis, ad nostræ salútis auxílium proveníre concéde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts fully offered to You, and, by the interceding merits of blessed Lawrence, Your Martyr, grant they may further our salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacro múnere satiáti, súpplices te, Dómine, deprecámur: ut, quod débitæ servitútis celebrámus offício, intercedénte beáto Lauréntio Mártyre tuo, salvatiónis tuæ sentiámus augméntum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with Your sacred gifts, we humbly pray You, O Lord, that as we perform this sacred act in duty bound, we may, through the intercession of Your blessed Martyr Lawrence, enjoy an increase of Your saving grace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0816": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 531-532; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui præ ómnibus sanctis tuis beátum Ióachim Genitrícis Fílii tui patrem esse voluísti: concéde quǽsumus, ut cuius festa venerámur; eius quoque perpétuo patrocínia sentiámus: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who, in preference to Your other Saints, willed St. Joachim to be the father of Your Son’s Mother; grant, we beseech You, that we may ever enjoy the spiritual help of him whose feast we celebrate; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe clementíssime Deus sacrifícium in honórem sancti Patriárchæ Ióachim, patris Maríæ Vírginis, maiestáti tuæ oblátum: ut ipso cum cóniuge sua et beatíssima prole intercedénte, perféctam cónsequi mereámur remissiónem peccatórum, et glóriam sempitérnam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously accept, most merciful God, the sacrifice offered to Your majesty in honor of the holy Patriarch Joachim, father of the Virgin Mary, that by his intercession, together with that of his spouse and most blessed child, we may be found worthy to obtain full forgiveness of our sins and everlasting glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut per hæc sacraménta, quæ súmpsimus: intercedéntibus méritis et précibus beáti Ióachim, patris Genitrícis dilécti Fílii tui Dómini nostri Iesu Christi; tuæ grátiæ in præsénti, et ætérnæ glóriæ in futúro partícipes esse mereámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that by this sacrament which we have received, and by the pleading merits of holy Joachim, father of the Mother of Your beloved Son, our Lord Jesus Christ, we may be found worthy to share Your grace in the life, and eternal glory in the life to come; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0820": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 535-536; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Bernárdum minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave blessed Bernard to Your people as a minister of eternal salvation, grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have him as our intercessor in heaven whom we had as the teacher of life on earth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Bernárdi Confessóris tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed Bernard, Your confessor and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Bernárdi Confessóris tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed Bernard, Your confessor and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0822": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. supplement (Immaculati Cordis B.M.V., 22 Aug.), pp. 4-6; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui in Corde beátæ Maríæ Vírginis dignum Spíritus Sancti habitáculum præparásti: concéde propítius, ut eiúsdem immaculáti Cordis festivitátem devóta mente recoléntes; secúndum cor tuum vívere valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, who in the Heart of the blessed Virgin Mary prepared a dwelling worthy of the Holy Spirit, mercifully grant that, keeping with devout minds the feast of her Immaculate Heart, we may be able to live according to Your heart; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the same Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Maiestáti tuæ, Dómine, Agnum immaculátum offeréntes, quǽsumus, ut corda nostra ignis ille divínus accéndat, qui Cor beátæ Maríæ Vírginis ineffabíliter inflammávit: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Offering to Your majesty, O Lord, the spotless Lamb, we beseech You that our hearts may be kindled by that divine fire which ineffably inflamed the Heart of the blessed Virgin Mary; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divínis refécti munéribus te, Dómine, supplíciter exorámus: ut beátæ Maríæ Vírginis intercessióne, cuius immaculáti Cordis solémnia venerándo égimus; a præséntibus perículis liberáti, ætérnæ vitæ gáudia consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with divine gifts, we humbly entreat You, O Lord, that by the intercession of the blessed Virgin Mary, whose Immaculate Heart we have venerated in this feast, we may be freed from present dangers and attain the joys of eternal life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0824": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 538-539; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui huius diéi venerándam sanctámque lætítiam in beáti Apóstoli tui Bartholomǽi festivitáte tribuísti: da Ecclésiæ tuæ, quǽsumus, et amáre quod crédidit; et prædicáre quod dócuit: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, who have given us the holy and venerable joy of this day in the feast of blessed Bartholomew Your Apostle, grant to Your Church, we beseech You, both to love what he believed and to preach what he taught; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Beáti Apóstoli tui Bartholomǽi solémnia recenséntes, quǽsumus Dómine, ut eius auxílio tua benefícia capiámus, pro quo tibi laudis hóstias immolámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Keeping the feast of blessed Bartholomew Your Apostle, we beseech You, O Lord, that we may receive Your benefits by his help, for whom we offer You sacrifices of praise; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, pignus salútis ætérnæ, celebrántes beáti Apóstoli tui Bartholomǽi votíva solémnia; ut perpétua mérita venerántes, ad vitam nutriámur ætérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the pledge of eternal salvation, celebrating the feast of blessed Bartholomew Your Apostle, that, venerating his everlasting merits, we may be nourished unto eternal life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0825": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 539-540; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Ludovícum Confessórem tuum de terréno regno ad cæléstis regni glóriam transtulísti: eius, quǽsumus, méritis et intercessióne; Regis regum Iesu Christi Fílii tui fácias nos esse consórtes: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who brought blessed Louis, Your confessor, from an earthly kingdom to the glory of the heavenly kingdom, make us, we beseech You, by his merits and intercession, to share the kingdom of the King of kings, Jesus Christ Your Son; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, quǽsumus Dómine, obláta sanctífica: ut intercessióne beáti Ludovíci Confessóris tui, nobis regni cæléstis præparent mansiónem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts offered, that by the intercession of blessed Louis Your confessor they may prepare for us a dwelling in the heavenly kingdom; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut quos culpæ miséria fecit hic éxsules; beáti Ludovíci Regis et Confessóris tui intercéssio gloriósa, regni cæléstis fáciat esse coherédes: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the glorious intercession of blessed Louis, Your king and confessor, may make co-heirs of the heavenly kingdom those whom the misery of sin has made exiles here; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0828": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 542-543; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Adésto supplicatiónibus nostris omnípotens Deus: et quibus fidúciam sperándæ pietátis indúlges; intercedénte beáto Augustíno Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, consuétæ misericórdiæ tríbue benígnus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hearken to our supplications, almighty God, and, blessed Augustine, Your confessor and bishop, interceding, graciously grant the effect of Your wonted mercy to those to whom You give confidence to hope for Your loving-kindness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis Augustíni nobis, Dómine, pia non desit orátio: quæ et múnera nostra concíliet, et tuam nobis indulgéntiam semper obtíneat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the loving prayer of Your holy confessor and bishop Augustine not fail us, O Lord, that it may make our gifts acceptable and ever obtain for us Your pardon; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ut nobis, Dómine, tua sacrifícia dent salútem; beátus Conféssor tuus Augustínus, et Póntifex, quǽsumus, precátor accédat: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "That Your sacrifices may give us salvation, O Lord, may blessed Augustine, Your confessor and bishop, we beseech You, come forward as our advocate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0831": {"src": "Sancti/08-31", "or": ["Deus, qui in liberándis fidélibus tuis ab impiórum captivitáte beátum Raymúndum Confessórem tuum mirábilem effecísti: eius nobis intercessióne concéde; ut, a peccatórum vínculis absolúti, quæ tibi sunt plácita, líberis méntibus exsequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who made blessed Raymund, Your Confessor, famous for delivering Your faithful from the captivity of the infidels, grant us by his intercession that, having been released from the bonds of our sins, we may with free minds do what is pleasing to You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi, Dómine, hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cœlésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut, in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus, eius muniámur et précibus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "S0902": {"src": "Sancti/09-02", "or": ["Concéde, quǽsumus, Ecclésiæ tuæ, omnípotens Deus: ut beátum Stéphanum Confessórem tuum, quem regnántem in terris propagatórem hábuit, propugnatórem habére mereátur gloriósum in cœlis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that Your Church be worthy to have as her glorious defender in heaven blessed Stephen, Your Confessor, whom she had as her champion while he reigned on earth. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Réspice, quas offérimus, hóstias, omnípotens Deus: et præsta; ut, qui passiónis Dominicæ mystéria celebrámus, imitémur quod ágimus. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look with favor, almighty God, upon the offerings we bring to you, and grant that we, who celebrate the mysteries of our Lord’s passion, may strive to imitate what we commemorate. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Stephani Confessóris tui fidem cóngrua devotióne sectémur; qui, pro eiúsdem fídei dilatatióne, de terréno regno ad cœléstis regni glóriam méruit perveníre. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we may follow in proper reverence the faith of blessed Stephen, Your Confessor, who as a reward for spreading that faith, was found worthy to pass from an earthly throne into the glory of Your heavenly Kingdom. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0914": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 557-558; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos hodiérna die Exaltatiónis sanctæ Crucis ánnua solemnitáte lætíficas: præsta quǽsumus, ut cuius mystérium in terra cognóvimus; eius redemptiónis in cælo prǽmia consequámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gladden us today by the yearly feast of the Exaltation of the holy Cross, grant, we beseech You, that we who have known its mystery on earth may obtain the rewards of its redemption in heaven; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc oblátio, quǽsumus Dómine, ab ómnibus nos purget offénsis: quæ in ara Crucis étiam totíus mundi tulit offénsam: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this offering, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse us from all our sins, this offering which on the altar of the Cross took away the sin of the whole world; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo, potúque cælésti, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut ab hóstium deféndas formídine; quos pretióso Fílii tui Dómini nostri Iesu Christi Sánguine redemísti: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly food and drink, we beseech You, almighty God, to defend from the fear of their enemies those whom You have redeemed by the precious Blood of Your Son our Lord Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0927": {"src": "Sancti/09-27", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut, qui sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum Cosmæ et Damiáni natalítia cólimus, a cunctis malis imminéntibus, eórum intercessiónibus, liberémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who celebrate the anniversary of the death of Your holy Martyrs, Cosmas and Damian, may by their intercession be delivered from all the evils that threaten us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sanctórum tuórum nobis, Dómine, pia non desit orátio: quæ et múnera nostra concíliet, et tuam nobis indulgéntiam semper obtíneat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let not the gracious prayer of Your saints fail us, O Lord, but may it make our offerings acceptable to You and obtain for us your mercy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Prótegat, quǽsumus, Dómine, pópulum tuum et participátio cœléstis indúlta convívii, et deprecátio colláta Sanctórum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the participation granted in Your heavenly banquet and the united prayers of the saints, we beseech You, O Lord, protect Your people. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0929": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 571-572; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui miro órdine Angelórum ministéria hominúmque dispénsas; concéde propítius: ut a quibus tibi ministrántibus in cælo semper assístitur; ab his in terra vita nostra muniátur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who assign according to a wondrous order the duties of Angels and men, mercifully grant that our life on earth be guarded by those who continually stand in Your presence and minister to You in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, laudis offérimus, supplíciter deprecántes: ut eásdem, Angélico pro nobis interveniénte suffrágio, et placátus accípias, et ad salútem nostram proveníre concédas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You sacrifices of praise, O Lord, humbly praying You to accept them graciously and to grant that they may be helpful for our salvation through the intercession of the Angels who intercede for us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Beáti Archángeli tui Michaélis intercessióne suffúlti, súpplices te, Dómine, deprecámur: ut quod ore proséquimur; contingámus et mente: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Relying upon the intercession of blessed Michael, Your Archangel, O Lord, we humbly pray You, that what we have received by our mouth may give grace to our mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0930": {"src": "Sancti/09-30", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiæ tuæ in exponéndis sacris Scriptúris beátum Hierónymum, Confessórem tuum, Doctórem máximum providére dignátus es: præsta, quǽsumus; ut, eius suffragántibus méritis, quod ore simul et ópere dócuit, te adiuvánte, exercére valeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who graciously gave Your Church blessed Jerome, Your Confessor and peerless teacher, to explain the Holy Scriptures, grant, we beseech You, that, with the help of his merits and by Your assistance, we may be able to put into practice what he has taught us by his life and works. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Donis cœléstibus da nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, líbera tibi mente servíre: ut múnera, quæ deférimus, interveniénte beáto Hierónymo Confessóre tuo, et medélam nobis operéntur et glóriam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By Your heavenly gifts, grant us, O Lord, we pray, to serve You with a free mind, so that the offerings we present, may, by the intercession of blessed Jerome, Your Confessor, lead us to heavenly glory. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Repleti alimónia cœlésti, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut, interveniénte beáto Hierónymo Confessóre tuo, misericórdiæ tuæ grátiam cónsequi mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with heavenly food, we beseech You, O Lord, that by the intercession of blessed Jerome, Your Confessor, we may be found worthy to obtain the favor of Your mercy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1003": {"src": "Sancti/10-03", "or": ["Dómine, qui dixísti: Nisi efficiámini sicut párvuli, non intrábitis in regnum cœlórum: da nobis, quǽsumus: ita sanctæ Teresiæ Vírginis in humilitáte et simplicitáte cordis vestígia sectári, ut præmia consequámur ætérna. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, Who said: Unless you become as little children, you shall not enter into the Kingdom of Heaven, grant us, we beseech You, so to follow the footsteps of blessed Theresa, the Virgin, in humility and simplicity of heart that we may obtain everlasting rewards. Who livest and reignest with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícium nostrum tibi, Dómine, quǽsumus, sanctæ Terésiæ Vírginis tuæ precátio sancta concíliet: ut, in cuius honóre sollémniter exhibétur, eius méritis efficiátur accéptum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, may the holy prayers of blessed Theresa, Your Virgin, commend our sacrifice to You, so that it may be made acceptable by her merits in whose honor it is solemnly offered. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Illo nos, Dómine amóris igne cœléste mystérium inflámmet: quo sancta Teresia Virgo tua se tibi pro homínibus caritátis víctimam devóvit. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the heavenly sacrament, O Lord, enkindle in us that fire of love which urged blessed Theresa, Your Virgin, to offer herself to You as a victim of charity for mankind. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1004": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 580-582; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Patris nostri Francísci méritis, fetu novæ prolis amplíficas: tríbue nobis ex eius imitatióne terréna despícere; et cæléstium donórum semper participatióne gaudére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the merits of our blessed Father Francis enlarge Your Church with the increase of a new offspring, grant us by his example to despise earthly things and ever to rejoice in sharing heavenly gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi Dómine dicáta sanctífica: et intercedénte beáto Patre nostro Francísco, ab omni nos culpárum labe purífica. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts dedicated to You, and by the intercession of our blessed Father Francis cleanse us from every stain of sin; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ecclésiam tuam, quǽsumus Dómine, grátia cæléstis amplíficet; quam beáti Patris nostri Francísci Confessóris tui illumináre voluísti gloriósis méritis et exémplis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May heavenly grace, we beseech You, O Lord, increase Your Church, which You have willed to enlighten by the glorious merits and example of our blessed Father Francis, Your confessor; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1006": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 582; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Sancti Brunónis Confessóris tui, quǽsumus Dómine, intercessiónibus adiuvémur: ut qui maiestátem tuam gráviter delinquéndo offéndimus; eius méritis et précibus, nostrórum delictórum véniam consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May we be aided by the intercession of St. Bruno, Your Confessor, we beseech You, O Lord; that we, who have grievously offended Your Majesty by sin, may, by his merits and prayers, obtain forgiveness for our offenses; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi Dómine hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus, et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, sacrifices of praise in commemoration of Your saints, through whom we trust to be delivered from evils both present and to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Brunóne Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Bruno, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1019": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 593; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Petrum Confessórem tuum admirábilis pœniténtiæ, et altíssimæ contemplatiónis múnere illustráre dignátus es: da nobis, quǽsumus; ut eius suffragántibus méritis, carne mortificáti facílius cæléstia capiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who graciously made blessed Peter, Your Confessor, glorious by the gift of remarkable penance and sublime contemplation, grant, we beseech You, that, by the merit of his prayers, we may the more easily understand the things of heaven by curbing our passions; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Petro Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Peter, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1024": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 596-597; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Raphaélem Archángelum Tobíæ fámulo tuo cómitem dedísti in via: concéde nobis fámulis tuis, ut eiúsdem semper protegámur custódia; et muniámur auxílio: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave blessed Raphael the Archangel to Your servant Tobias as a companion on his journey, grant to us Your servants that we may ever be protected by his care and defended by his help; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, laudis offérimus, supplíciter deprecántes: ut eásdem, Angélico pro nobis interveniénte suffrágio, et placátus accípias, et ad salútem nostram proveníre concédas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, sacrifices of praise, humbly entreating You that, the prayers of the Angels interceding for us, You may graciously accept them and grant that they may avail for our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Repléti, Dómine, benedictióne cælésti, supplíciter implorámus: ut quod frágili celebrámus offício; sanctórum Angelórum atque Archangelórum nobis prodésse sentiámus auxílio: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled, O Lord, with heavenly blessing, we humbly implore You that what we celebrate in our frail service we may feel to profit us by the help of the holy Angels and Archangels; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1028": {"src": "Sancti/10-28", "or": ["Deus, qui nos per beátos Apóstolos tuos Simónem et Iudam ad agnitiónem tui nóminis veníre tribuísti: da nobis eórum glóriam sempitérnam et proficiéndo celebráre, et celebrándo profícere. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who have given us a way of coming to know Your name through Your blessed Apostles Simon and Jude, grant us to honor their everlasting glory by becoming more holy and to become more holy by honoring it. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Glóriam, Dómine, sanctórum Apostolórum tuórum Simónis et Iudæ perpétuam venerántes: quǽsumus; ut eam, sacris mystériis expiati, dígnius celebrémus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We honor, O Lord, the everlasting glory of Your holy Apostles Simon and Jude; we beseech You, that, purified by this sacramental rite, we may the more worthily celebrate their glory. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Percéptis, Dómine, sacraméntis, supplíciter exorámus: ut, intercedéntibus beátis Apóstolis tuis Simóne et Iuda, quæ pro illórum veneránda gérimus passióne, nobis profíciant ad medélam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received Your sacrament, we humbly beseech You, O Lord, that, by the intercession of Your blessed Apostles Simon and Jude, the rite we perform in honor of their passion may profit us as a healing remedy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1102": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 623 (Ad primam Missam); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Fidélium, Deus, ómnium cónditor et redémptor: animábus famulórum, famularúmque tuárum remissiónem cunctórum tríbue peccatórum; ut indulgéntiam, quam semper optavérunt, piis supplicatiónibus consequántur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the creator and redeemer of all the faithful, grant to the souls of Your servants and handmaids the remission of all their sins, that by loving prayers they may obtain the pardon they have always desired; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias, quǽsumus, Dómine, quas tibi pro animábus famulórum, famularúmque tuárum offérimus, propitiátus inténde; ut quibus fídei christiánæ méritum contulísti, dones et prǽmium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously, we beseech You, O Lord, on the sacrifices which we offer You for the souls of Your servants and handmaids, that to those on whom You bestowed the merit of Christian faith You may give also its reward; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Animábus, quǽsumus, Dómine, famulórum famularúmque tuárum, orátio profíciat supplicántium: ut eas et a peccátis ómnibus éxuas; et tuæ redemptiónis fácias esse partícipes: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the prayer of Your suppliants, we beseech You, O Lord, profit the souls of Your servants and handmaids, that You may free them from all their sins and make them partakers of Your redemption; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1104": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 614; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Ecclésiam tuam, Dómine, sancti Cároli Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis contínua protectióne custódi: ut sicut illum pastorális sollicitúdo gloriósum effécit; ita nos eius intercéssio in tuo semper fáciat amóre fervéntes: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Guard Your Church, O Lord, by the continual protection of saint Charles, Your confessor and bishop, that, as his pastoral care made him glorious, so his intercession may make us ever fervent in Your love; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Da miséricors Deus, ut hæc salutáris oblátio, intercedénte beáto Cárolo Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, et a própriis nos reátibus indesinénter expédiat, et ab ómnibus tueátur advérsis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, O merciful God, that this saving offering, by the intercession of blessed Charles, Your confessor and bishop, may ever free us from our own sins and defend us against all adversities; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut quorum festivitáte votíva sunt sacraménta; eórum intercessióne salutária nobis reddántur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that the sacraments which are offered on the feast of Your saints may by their intercession become saving for us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1109": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 2*-3* (Commune Dedicationis Ecclesiae, as the Missal directs for 9 Nov., p. 617); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nobis per síngulos annos huius sancti templi tui consecratiónis réparas diem, et sacris semper mystériis repræséntas incólumes; exáudi preces pópuli tui: et præsta, ut quisquis hoc templum benefícia petitúrus ingréditur; cuncta se impetrásse lætétur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who year by year renew for us the day of the consecration of this Your holy temple, and bring us again in safety to Your sacred mysteries, hear the prayers of Your people, and grant that whoever enters this temple to ask for blessings may rejoice to have obtained them all; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Annue, quǽsumus Dómine, précibus nostris, ut quicúmque intra templi huius, cuius anniversárium dedicatiónis diem celebrámus, ámbitum continémur, plena tibi atque perfécta córporis et ánimæ devotióne placeámus: ut, dum hæc vota præséntia réddimus, ad ætérna prǽmia, te adiuvánte, perveníre mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hearken, we beseech You, O Lord, to our prayers, that all of us who are gathered within the walls of this temple, the anniversary of whose dedication we celebrate, may please You with full and perfect devotion of body and soul, so that, while we render these present offerings, we may by Your help deserve to attain to eternal rewards; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam sponsam vocáre dignátus es, ut quæ habéret grátiam per fídei devotiónem, habéret étiam ex nómine pietátem; da, ut omnis hæc plebs nómini tuo sérviens, huius vocábuli consórtio digna esse mereátur: et Ecclésia tua in templo, cuius anniversárius dedicatiónis dies celebrátur, tibi collécta, te tímeat, te díligat, te sequátur; ut dum iúgiter per vestígia tua gráditur, ad cæléstia promíssa, te ducénte, perveníre mereátur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who deigned to call Your Church Your bride, that she who had grace through the devotion of faith might also have holiness from the name; grant that all this people serving Your name may deserve to be worthy of sharing that title, and that Your Church, gathered to You in the temple whose anniversary of dedication is kept, may fear You, love You and follow You, that, walking ever in Your footsteps, she may under Your guidance deserve to come to the heavenly promises; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1111": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 618; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui cónspicis quia ex nulla nostra virtúte subsístimus; concéde propítius, ut intercessióne beáti Martíni Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis, contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who see that we do not stand by any strength of our own, mercifully grant that by the intercession of blessed Martin, Your confessor and bishop, we may be defended against all adversities; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Da miséricors Deus, ut hæc salutáris oblátio, et a própriis nos reátibus indesinénter expédiat, et ab ómnibus tueátur advérsis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, O merciful God, that this saving offering may ever free us from our own sins and defend us against all adversities; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut quorum festivitáte votíva sunt sacraménta; eórum intercessióne salutária nobis reddántur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that the sacraments which are offered on the feast of Your saints may by their intercession become saving for us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1115": {"src": "Sancti/11-15", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Albértum Pontíficem tuum atque Doctórem in humána sapiéntia divínæ fídei subiiciénda magnum effecísti: da nobis, quǽsumus; ita eius magistérii inhærére vestígiis, ut luce perfécta fruámur in cœlis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who made blessed Albert, Your Bishop and Doctor, eminent in the submission of human wisdom to divine faith, grant us, we beseech You, so to follow the path of his teaching that we may enjoy perfect light in heaven. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, Dómine, quǽsumus, inténde placátus: ut quod Passiónis Fílii tui Dómini nostri mystério gérimus, beáti Alberti intercessióne et exémplo, pio consequámur afféctu. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look favorably upon these sacrificial gifts, O Lord, we beseech You, so that what we perform in the sacrificial rite of the passion of Your Son, our Lord, we may receive with grateful affection by the intercession and example of blessed Albert. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Per hæc sancta quæ súmpsimus, ab hóstium nos, Dómine, impugnatióne defénde: et intercedénte beáto Albérto Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, perpétua pace respiráre concéde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through this holy food which we have eaten, defend us, O Lord, from the onslaughts of our enemies and grant that by the intercession of blessed Albert, Your Confessor and Bishop, we may always live in peace. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1117": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 624-627; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Gregórii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis veneránda solémnitas; et devotiónem nobis áugeat, et salútem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the venerable feast of blessed Gregory, Your confessor and bishop, may increase in us both devotion and salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti tui, quǽsumus Dómine, nos ubíque lætíficent: ut dum eórum mérita recólimus, patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your saints, we beseech You, O Lord, everywhere gladden us, that while we recall their merits we may feel their protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut de percéptis munéribus grátias exhibéntes; intercedénte beáto Gregório Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, benefícia potióra sumámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that, giving thanks for the gifts received, we may, by the intercession of blessed Gregory, Your confessor and bishop, receive still greater benefits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1120": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 627-628; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Felícem Confessórem tuum ex erémo ad munus rediméndi captívos cǽlitus vocáre dignátus es: præsta quǽsumus, ut per grátiam tuam ex peccatórum nostrórum captivitáte, eius intercessióne, liberáti; ad cæléstem pátriam perducámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who by heavenly inspiration graciously called forth blessed Felix, Your Confessor, from the desert to the work of ransoming captives; grant, we beseech You, that by his intercession, and liberated by Your grace from the captivity of our sins, we may be led into our heavenly fatherland; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi Dómine hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus, et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, sacrifices of praise in commemoration of Your saints, through whom we trust to be delivered from evils both present and to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cælésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus; eius muniámur et précibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly food and drink, O our God, we humbly entreat You that we may also be defended by the prayers of him in whose commemoration we have received these gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1122": {"src": "Sancti/11-22", "or": ["Deus, qui nos ánnua beátæ Cæcíliæ Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ sollemnitáte lætíficas: da, ut, quam venerámur offício, étiam piæ conversatiónis sequámur exémplo. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who gladden us by the annual feast of blessed Cecilia, Your Virgin and Martyr, grant, we beseech You, that we may by virtuous conduct follow her whom we venerate in this sacred rite. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, Dómine, placatiónis et laudis, quǽsumus: ut, intercedénte beáta Cæcília Vírgine et Mártyre tua, nos propitiatióne tua dignos semper effíciat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this sacrifice of atonement and praise, we beseech You, O Lord, by the intercession of blessed Cecilia, Your Virgin and Martyr, always make us worthy of your forgiveness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti, Dómine, famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove, cuius sollémnia celebrámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "S1124": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 631; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui sanctum Ioánnem Confessórem tuum atque Doctórem perféctæ sui abnegatiónis, et crucis amatórem exímium effecísti: concéde, ut eius imitatióni iúgiter inhæréntes; glóriam assequámur ætérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made saint John, Your confessor and doctor, an outstanding lover of perfect self-denial and of the Cross, grant that, ever cleaving to his example, we may attain everlasting glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Ioánnis Confessóris tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, through the intercession of blessed John, Your confessor and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Ioánnis Confessóris tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the prayer of blessed John, Your confessor and doctor, may help us everywhere, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1125": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 632-633; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui dedísti legem Móysi in summitáte montis Sínai, et in eódem loco per sanctos Angelos tuos corpus beátæ Catharínæ Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ mirabíliter collocásti: præsta quǽsumus, ut eius méritis et intercessióne; ad montem, qui Christus est, perveníre valeámus: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave the law to Moses on the summit of Mount Sinai, and in that same place wonderfully laid the body of blessed Catherine, Your virgin and martyr, by Your holy Angels, grant, we beseech You, that by her merits and intercession we may be able to come to the mountain which is Christ; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstia, quǽsumus Dómine, quam tibi sanctæ Catharínæ Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ natalítia recenséntes offérimus, et víncula nostræ pravitátis absólvat, et tuæ nobis misericórdiæ dona concíliet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifice, O Lord, which we offer You keeping the birthday of saint Catherine, Your virgin and martyr, both loose the bonds of our wickedness and win for us the gifts of Your mercy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus Dómine salutáribus repléti mystériis: ut cuius solémnia celebrámus; eius oratiónibus adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with saving mysteries, we beseech You, O Lord, that we may be helped by the prayers of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1130": {"src": "Sancti/11-30", "or": ["Maiestátem tuam, Dómine, supplíciter exorámus: ut, sicut Ecclésiæ tuæ beátus Andréas Apóstolus éxstitit prædicátor et rector; ita apud te sit pro nobis perpétuus intercéssor. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We humbly pray Your majesty, O Lord, that, as blessed Andrew was a preacher and ruler in Your Church, so he may always intercede for us with You. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrificium nostrum tibi, Dómine, quǽsumus, beáti Andréæ Apóstoli precátio sancta concíliet: ut, in cuius honóre sollémniter exhibétur, eius méritis efficiátur accéptum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, that the holy prayer of blessed Andrew may make our sacrifice pleasing to You, so that it would be acceptable to You, through the merits of him in whose honor it is solemnly offered. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, divína mystéria, beáti Andréæ Apóstoli festivitáte lætántes: quæ, sicut tuis Sanctis ad glóriam, ita nobis, quǽsumus, ad véniam prodésse perfícias. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we have received the divine sacrament on the joyful feastday of blessed Andrew: as You make it contribute to the glory of Your saints, so, we beseech You, may it bring about our forgiveness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1204": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 327; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Petrum Chrysólogum Doctórem egrégium divínitus præmonstrátum, ad regéndam et instruéndam Ecclésiam tuam éligi voluísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem Doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed Peter Chrysologus, the excellent Doctor divinely foreshown, should be chosen to rule and instruct Your Church, grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have him as our intercessor in heaven whom we had as the teacher of life on earth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti Petri Chrysólogi Pontíficis tui atque Doctóris nobis, Dómine, pia non desit orátio: quæ et múnera nostra concíliet, et tuam nobis indulgéntiam semper obtíneat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the loving prayer of saint Peter Chrysologus, Your bishop and doctor, not fail us, O Lord, that it may make our gifts acceptable and ever obtain for us Your pardon; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ut nobis, Dómine, tua sacrifícia dent salútem; beátus Petrus Chrysólogus Póntifex tuus et Doctor egrégius, quǽsumus, precátor accédat: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "That Your sacrifices may give us salvation, O Lord, may blessed Peter Chrysologus, Your bishop and excellent doctor, we beseech You, come forward as our advocate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1206": {"src": "Sancti/12-06", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Nicoláum Pontíficem innúmeris decorásti miráculis: tríbue, quǽsumus; ut eius méritis et précibus a gehénnæ incéndiis liberémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You who made the holy Bishop Nicholas renowned for countless miracles, grant, we beseech You, that by his merits and prayers we may be saved from the fires of hell. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sanctífica, quǽsumus, Dómine Deus, hæc múnera, quæ in sollemnitáte sancti Antístitis tui Nicolái offérimus: ut per ea vita nostra inter advérsa et próspera úbique dirigátur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, we beseech You, O Lord God, the gifts we offer on the feast of Your holy Bishop, Nicholas, that through them our life, whether in fortune or misfortune, may be directed aright. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacrifícia, quæ súmpsimus, Dómine, pro sollemnitáte sancti Pontíficis tui Nicolái, sempitérna nos protectióne consérvent. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifice in which we have shared on the feast of Your holy Bishop Nicholas guard us with its lasting protection. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1208": {"src": "Sancti/12-08", "or": ["Deus, qui per immaculátam Vírginis Conceptiónem dignum Fílio tuo habitáculum præparásti: quǽsumus; ut, qui ex morte eiúsdem Filii tui prævísa eam ab omni labe præservásti, nos quoque mundos eius intercessióne ad te perveníre concédas. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who by the Immaculate Conception of the Virgin, prepared a worthy dwelling for Your Son, and Who, by Your Son’s death, foreseen by You, preserved her from all taint, grant, we beseech You, through her intercession, that we too may come to You unstained by sin. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Salutárem hóstiam, quam in sollemnitáte immaculátæ Conceptiónis beátæ Vírginis Maríæ tibi, Dómine, offérimus, súscipe et præsta: ut, sicut illam tua grátia præveniénte ab omni labe immúnem profitémur; ita eius intercessióne a culpis ómnibus liberémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, O Lord, the sacrifice of salvation which we offer You on the feast of the Immaculate Conception of the Blessed Virgin Mary; and grant that as we profess that she was kept from all taint of evil, by Your anticipating grace, so, through her intercession, may we be freed from all sin. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta quæ súmpsimus, Dómine, Deus noster: illíus in nobis culpæ vúlnera réparent; a qua immaculátam beátæ Maríæ Conceptiónem singuláriter præservásti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrament we have received, O Lord our God, heal in us the wounds of that sin from which by a singular privilege, You kept immaculate the conception of blessed Mary. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1213": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 336-337; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Exáudi nos Deus salutáris noster: ut sicut de beátæ Lúciæ Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ festivitáte gaudémus; ita piæ devotiónis erudiámur afféctu: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear us, O God our Saviour, that as we rejoice in the feast of blessed Lucy, Your virgin and martyr, so we may be taught the spirit of loving devotion; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1221": {"src": "Sancti/12-21", "or": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, beáti Apóstoli tui Thomæ sollemnitátibus gloriári: ut eius semper et patrocíniis sublevémur; et fidem cóngrua devotióne sectémur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, grant us, we beseech You, to glory in the feast-day of blessed Thomas, Your Apostle, that we may be helped continually by his patronage and imitate his faith with a devotion like his. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Débitum tibi, Dómine, nostræ réddimus servitútis, supplíciter exorántes: ut, suffrágiis beáti Thomæ Apóstoli, in nobis tua múnera tueáris, cuius honoránda confessióne laudis tibi hóstias immolámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we who dutifully worship You humbly entreat You that, by the prayers of Your blessed Apostle Thomas, in honor of whose martyrdom we offer these sacrifices of praise, You safeguard Your gifts within us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Adésto nobis, miséricors Deus: et, intercedénte pro nobis beáto Thoma Apóstolo, tua circa nos propitiátus dona custódi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Merciful God, abide with us, and through the intercession of Your blessed Apostle Thomas, mercifully safeguard the gifts You have given us. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1226": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 340-343; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, imitári quod cólimus, ut discámus et inimícos dilígere: quia eius natalítia celebrámus; qui novit étiam pro persecutóribus exoráre Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, to imitate what we venerate, that we may learn to love even our enemies, since we keep the birthday of him who knew how to pray even for his persecutors to our Lord Jesus Christ Your Son; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe Dómine múnera pro tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: ut sicut illos pássio gloriósos effécit, ita nos devótio reddat innócuos. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, these gifts in commemoration of Your saints, that, as their passion made them glorious, so our devotion may make us blameless; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Auxiliéntur nobis, Dómine, sumpta mystéria; et intercedénte beáto Stéphano Mártyre tuo, sempitérna protectióne confírment: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the mysteries we have received help us, O Lord, and, by the intercession of blessed Stephen Your martyr, strengthen us with everlasting protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1227": {"src": "Sancti/12-27", "or": ["Ecclésiam tuam, Dómine, benígnus illústra: ut, beáti Ioánnis Apóstoli tui et Evangelístæ illumináta doctrínis, ad dona pervéniat sempitérna. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, graciously shed light upon Your Church, so that, enlightened by the teachings of blessed John, Your Apostle and Evangelist, she may gain Your everlasting rewards. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, múnera, quæ in eius tibi sollemnitáte deférimus, cuius nos confídimus patrocínio liberári. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, O Lord, the gifts we bring You on the feast of him upon whose patronage we trust for our salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cœlésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut, in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus, eius muniámur et précibus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "S1228": {"src": "Sancti/12-28", "or": ["Deus, cuius hodierna die præcónium Innocéntes Mártyres non loquéndo, sed moriéndo conféssi sunt: ómnia in nobis vitiórum mala mortífica; ut fidem tuam, quam lingua nostra lóquitur, étiam móribus vita fateátur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Whose praise the Innocents, Your martyrs, this day proclaimed, not by speaking, but by dying, put to death in us all the wickedness of sin, so that Your faith which our tongue professes may be proclaimed also by our life. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sanctórum tuórum, Dómine, nobis pia non desit orátio: quæ et múnera nostra concíliet, et tuam nobis indulgéntiam semper obtíneat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let not the gracious prayer of Your saints fail us, O Lord, but may it make our offerings acceptable to You and obtain for us Your mercy. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Votíva, Dómine, dona percépimus: quæ Sanctórum nobis précibus, et præséntis, quǽsumus, vitæ páriter et ætérnæ tríbue conférre subsídium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have partaken, O Lord, of the dedicated gifts: may they, we beseech You, help us through the intercession of Your saints both for this life and life eternal. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "G369": {"src": "Sancti/11-29", "or": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut beátus N. Apóstolus, cuius prævenímus festivitátem, tuum pro nobis implóret auxílium: ut a nostris reátibus absolúti a cunctis étiam perículis eruámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "se": ["Sacrándum tibi, Dómine, munus offérimus: quo beáti Andréæ Apóstoli sollémnia recoléntes, purificatiónem quoque nostris méntibus implorámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Percéptis, Dómine, sacraméntis supplíciter exorámus: ut, intercedénte beáto Andréa Apostolo tuo, quæ pro illíus veneránda gérimus passióne, nobis profíciant ad medélam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "G385": {"src": "Sancti/12-26", "or": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, imitári quod cólimus: ut discámus et inimícos dilígere; quia eius natalícia celebrámus, qui novit étiam pro persecutóribus exoráre Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech thee, O Lord, so to imitate what we revere, that we may learn to love even our enemies; for we celebrate the heavenly birthday of him who knew how to pray for his very persecutors to our Lord Jesus Christ: Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, múnera pro tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: ut, sicut illos pássio gloriósos effécit; ita nos devótio reddat innócuos. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""], "pc": ["Auxiliéntur nobis, Dómine, sumpta mystéria: et, intercedénte beáto Stéphano Mártyre tuo, sempitérna protectióne confírment. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", ""]}, "G420": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 379-380 (In Apparitione B.M.V. Immaculatae, 11 Februarii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui per Immaculátam Vírginis Conceptiónem dignum Fílio tuo habitáculum præparásti: súpplices a te quǽsumus, ut eiúsdem Vírginis Apparitiónem celebrántes; salútem mentis et córporis consequámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the Immaculate Conception of the Virgin prepared a worthy dwelling for Your Son, we humbly beseech You that, celebrating the Apparition of the same Virgin, we may obtain health of mind and body; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstia laudis, quam tibi, Dómine, per mérita gloriósæ et Immaculátæ Vírginis, offérimus, sit tibi in odórem suavitátis, et nobis optátam cónferat córporis et ánimæ sanitátem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifice of praise which we offer You, O Lord, through the merits of the glorious and Immaculate Virgin, be to You an odor of sweetness, and bring us the health of body and soul we desire; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quos cælésti, Dómine, aliménto satiásti, súblevet déxtera Genitrícis tuæ Immaculátæ: ut ad ætérnam pátriam, ipsa adiuvánte, perveníre mereámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the right hand of Your Immaculate Mother, O Lord, uphold those whom You have fed with heavenly food, that by her help we may deserve to reach our eternal home; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "G446": {"src": "Sancti/03-27", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui, ad cultum sacrárum imáginum asseréndum, beátum Ioánnem cœlésti doctrína et admirábili spíritus fortitúdine imbuísti: concéde nobis eius intercessióne et exémplo; ut, quorum cólimus imagines, virtútes imitémur et patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, eternal God, Who to defend the honor paid to sacred images, filled blessed John with heavenly learning and wondrous strength of soul, grant that, by his intercession and example, we may imitate the virtues of those whose images we honor and may enjoy the help of their patronage. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ut, quæ tibi, Dómine, offérimus, dona tuo sint digna conspéctu: beáti Ioánnis et Sanctórum, quos eius ópera expósitos in templis cólimus, pia suffragátio conspíret. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, may the holy intercession of blessed John be united with that of Your Saints whose images, through his efforts, we venerate in our churches, and thus may the gifts we offer You be found worthy in Your sight. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumpta nos, quǽsumus, Dómine, dona cœléstibus armis tueántur: et beáti Ioánnis patrocínia circúmdent Sanctórum unánimi suffrágio cumuláta; quorum imágines evícit in Ecclésia esse venerándas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, that the gifts we have eaten may be as heavenly weapons to guard us; and may we be protected by the patronage of blessed John, reinforced by the united prayers of the Saints, the veneration of whose images by the Church, he gloriously vindicated. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "G491": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 470-471 (SS. Gervasius et Protasius, 19 Jun.); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos ánnua sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum Gervásii et Protásii solemnitáte lætíficas: concéde propítius, ut quorum gaudémus méritis; accendámur exémplis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gladden us by the yearly feast of Your holy martyrs Gervase and Protase, mercifully grant that we may be kindled by the example of those in whose merits we rejoice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi, Dómine, dicáta sanctífica: et intercedéntibus sanctis Martýribus tuis Gervásio et Protásio, per éadem nos placátus inténde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts dedicated to You, and, Your holy martyrs Gervase and Protase interceding, look graciously upon us through them; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Salutáris tui, Dómine, múnere satiáti, súpplices exorámus: ut cuius lætámur gustu; intercedéntibus sanctis Martýribus tuis Gervásio et Protásio, renovémur efféctu: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with the gift of Your salvation, we humbly pray You, O Lord, that, Your holy martyrs Gervase and Protase interceding, we may be renewed by the effect of that which we rejoice to taste; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "G494": {"src": "Sancti/06-23", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut família tua per viam salútis incédat; et, beáti Ioánnis Præcursóris hortaménta sectándo ad eum, quem prædíxit, secúra pervéniat, Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that Your household may walk in the way of salvation and, by following the counsels of blessed John the Herald, safely come to our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, Whom he foretold. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, Dómine, obláta sanctífica: et, intercedénte beáto Ioánne Baptista, nos per hæc a peccatórum nostrórum máculis emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts offered to You, and, by the intercession of Blessed John the Baptist, purify us by them from the stains of our sins. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Beáti Ioánnis Baptístæ nos, Dómine, præclára comitétur orátio: et, quem ventúrum esse prædíxit, poscat nobis fore placátum, Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the powerful prayer of blessed John the Baptist go with us, O Lord, and may he plead with our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, Whose coming he foretold, to be merciful unto us. Who livest and reignest with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "G499": {"src": "Sancti/06-26", "or": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut nos gemináta lætítia hodiérnæ festivitátis excípiat, quæ de beatórum Ioánnis et Pauli glorificatióne procédit; quos eadem fides et pássio vere fecit esse germános. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that on this feast-day we may have the double joy of celebrating blessed John and Paul, true brothers who obtained eternal glory through one faith and one martyrdom. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, sanctórum Martyrum tuórum Ioánnis et Pauli dicátas méritis, benígnus assúme: et ad perpétuum nobis tríbue proveníre subsídium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, graciously accept, through the merits of Your holy Martyrs John and Paul, the sacrificial gifts dedicated to You, and grant they may prove to be for us a lasting help. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, sanctórum Martyrum tuórum Ioánnis et Pauli sollémnia celebrántes, sacraménta cœléstia: præsta, quǽsumus; ut, quod temporáliter gérimus, ætérnis gáudiis consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have partaken of the heavenly sacrament, O Lord, as we celebrate the feast of Your holy Martyrs John and Paul; grant, we beseech You, that what we do in time we may reap in joy in eternity. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "G502": {"src": "Sancti/06-28", "or": ["Deus, qui beáto Irenǽo Mártyri tuo atque Pontífici tribuísti, ut et veritáte doctrínæ expugnáret hǽreses, et pacem Ecclésiæ felíciter confirmáret: da, quǽsumus, plebi tuæ in sancta religióne constántiam; et pacem tuam nostris concéde tempóribus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who enabled blessed Irenaeus, Your Martyr and Bishop, to overcome heresy with true doctrine and to establish peace happily in the Church, grant, we beseech You, that Your people may be steadfast in holy religion, and give us Your peace in our times. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, qui credéntes in te pópulos nullis sinis cóncuti terróribus: dignáre preces et hóstias dicátæ tibi plebis suscípere; ut pax, a tua pietáte concéssa, christianórum fines ab omni hoste fáciat esse secúros. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who do not allow the nations that believe in You to be troubled by any distress, graciously accept the prayers and sacrificial gifts Your people dedicate to You, so that the peace bestowed by Your love may make Christian lands safe from every foe. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, auctor pacis et amátor, quem nosse vívere, cui servíre regnáre est: prótege ab ómnibus impugnatiónibus súpplices tuos; ut, qui in defensióne tua confídimus, beáti Irenæi Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis intercessióne, nullius hostilitátis arma timeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, author and lover of peace, to know You is to live, and to serve You is to rule; protect from all assaults those who humbly implore You, that, trusting in Your protection, by the intercession of St. Irenaeus, Your Martyr and Bishop, we may not fear the power of any foe. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "G502_3": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 478-479 (In Vigilia SS. Petri et Pauli, 28 Jun.); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut nullis nos permíttas perturbatiónibus cóncuti; quos in Apostólicæ confessiónis petra solidásti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that You suffer not to be shaken by any disturbances us whom You have set firm on the rock of the Apostolic confession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Munus pópuli tui, quǽsumus Dómine, Apostólica intercessióne sanctífica, nosque a peccatórum nostrórum máculis emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, we beseech You, O Lord, the gift of Your people by the intercession of the Apostles, and cleanse us from the stains of our sins; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quos cælésti, Dómine, aliménto satiásti; Apostólicis intercessiónibus ab omni adversitáte custódi: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Guard from all adversity, by the intercession of the Apostles, O Lord, those whom You have filled with heavenly food; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "G505": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 481-482 (In Commemoratione S. Pauli, 30 Junii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui multitúdinem Géntium beáti Pauli Apóstoli prædicatióne docuísti: da nobis, quǽsumus, ut cuius natalítia cólimus; eius apud te patrocínia sentiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who taught the multitude of the Gentiles by the preaching of blessed Paul the Apostle, grant us, we beseech You, that we who keep his birthday may feel the help of his patronage with You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias, Dómine, quas nómini tuo sacrándas offérimus, Apostólica prosequátur orátio, per quam nos expiári tríbuas, et deféndi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the prayer of the Apostles accompany the offerings which we bring to be consecrated to Your name, O Lord, and by it grant us to be cleansed and defended; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Percéptis, Dómine, sacraméntis, beáto Paulo Apóstolo tuo interveniénte, deprecámur: ut quæ pro illíus celebráta sunt glória; nobis profíciant ad medélam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received Your sacraments, O Lord, we pray that, by the intercession of blessed Paul Your Apostle, what has been celebrated for his glory may avail for our healing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "G515": {"src": "Commune/C3a", "or": ["Deus, qui nos concédis sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum N. et N. natalítia cólere: da nobis in ætérna beatitúdine de eórum societáte gaudére. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who dost permit us to keep the birthday of thy holy Martyrs N. and N., grant that we may enjoy their fellowship in everlasting happiness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi, Dómine, nostra devotiónis offérimus: quæ et pro tuórum tibi grata sint honóre Iustórum, et nobis salutária, te miseránte, reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gifts of our service; may they be pleasing to You for the honor of Your just ones and, through Your mercy, bring us salvation. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine: intercedéntibus sanctis Martýribus tuis N. et N.; ut, quod ore contíngimus, pura mente capiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O almighty and merciful God, that through the intercession of Your holy Martyrs, N. et N. what we take into our mouths we may eat with pure heart. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "G555": {"src": "Sancti/08-22", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui in Corde beátæ Maríæ Vírginis dignum Spíritus Sancti habitáculum præparásti: concéde propítius; ut eiúsdem immaculáti Cordis festivitátem devóta mente recoléntes, secúndum cor tuum vívere valeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, everlasting God, Who in the Heart of the Blessed Virgin Mary prepared a dwelling place worthy of the Holy Spirit; graciously grant that we, who are devoutly keeping the feast of her Immaculate Heart, may be able to live according to Your Heart. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Maiestáti tuæ, Dómine, Agnum immaculátum offeréntes, quǽsumus: ut corda nostra ignis ille divínus accéndat, cui Cor beátæ Maríæ Vírginis ineffabíliter inflammávit. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Offering the spotless Lamb to Your Majesty, O Lord, we pray that our hearts may be set aflame by the fire that burned so wondrously in the Heart of the Blessed Virgin Mary. Through the same Jesus Christ, thy Son, Our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divínis refécti munéribus te, Dómine, supplíciter exorámus: ut beátæ Maríæ Vírginis intercessióne, cuius immaculáti Cordis sollémnia venerándo égimus, a præséntibus perículis liberáti, ætérnæ vitæ gáudia consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by divine gifts, we humbly beseech You, O Lord, that by the intercession of the Blessed Virgin Mary, the solemn feast of whose Immaculate Heart we have celebrated, we may be freed from present dangers and reach the happiness of life eternal. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S0915": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 314-315 (In Compassione B.M.V.; \"Missa dicitur ut in Compassione\", 15 Sept., p. 559); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Intervéniat pro nobis, quǽsumus Dómine Iesu Christe, nunc et in hora mortis nostræ apud tuam cleméntiam beáta Virgo María Mater tua: cuius sacratíssimam ánimam in hora benedíctæ passiónis tuæ dolóris gládius pertransívit; et in gloriósa resurrectióne tua ingens gáudium lætificávit: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the blessed Virgin Mary, Your Mother, intercede for us with Your mercy, we beseech You, O Lord Jesus Christ, now and at the hour of our death, she whose most holy soul was pierced by the sword of sorrow in the hour of Your blessed passion, and gladdened with great joy in Your glorious resurrection; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Offérimus tibi preces et hóstias, Dómine Iesu Christe, humíliter supplicántes: ut qui transfixiónem dulcíssimi spíritus beátæ Maríæ Matris tuæ précibus recensémus; suo suorúmque sub cruce Sanctórum consórtium multiplicáto piíssimo intervéntu, méritis mortis tuæ, méritum cum Beátis habeámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You prayers and sacrifices, O Lord Jesus Christ, humbly beseeching You that we who by our prayers recall the piercing of the most sweet spirit of blessed Mary Your Mother may, by the manifold and most loving intercession of her and of the Saints with her beneath the Cross, have through the merits of Your death a share with the Blessed; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacrifícia, quæ súmpsimus, Dómine Iesu Christe, transfixiónem Matris tuæ et Vírginis devóte celebrántes; nobis ímpetrent apud cleméntiam tuam omnis boni salutáris efféctum: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifices which we have received, O Lord Jesus Christ, as we devoutly celebrate the piercing of Your Mother and Virgin, obtain for us from Your mercy the effect of every saving good; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1002": {"src": "Sancti/10-02", "or": ["Deus, qui ineffábili providéntia sanctos Angelos tuos ad nostram custódiam míttere dignáris: largíre supplícibus tuis; et eórum semper protectióne deféndi, et ætérna societáte gaudére. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, Who in Your wondrous providence graciously send Your Angels to watch over us, grant that we who pray to You may be ever under their protection and may rejoice in their unending companionship. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, múnera, quæ pro sanctórum Angelórum tuórum veneratióne deférimus: et concéde propítius; ut, perpétuis eórum præsídiis, a præséntibus perículis liberémur et ad vitam perveniámus ætérnam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, O Lord, the gifts which we offer in honor of Your holy Angels, and mercifully grant that we may be freed from present perils by their perpetual protection and attain unto life everlasting. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, divína mystéria, sanctórum Angelórum tuórum festivitáte lætántes: quǽsumus; ut eórum protectióne ab hóstium iúgiter liberémur insídiis, et contra ómnia advérsa muniámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Rejoicing on the feast of Your holy Angels, O Lord, we have received the divine sacrament; we pray that we may ever be freed, by their protection, from the snares of the enemy and be preserved from all harm. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1118": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 2*-3* (Commune Dedicationis Ecclesiae, as the Missal directs for 18 Nov., p. 624); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nobis per síngulos annos huius sancti templi tui consecratiónis réparas diem, et sacris semper mystériis repræséntas incólumes; exáudi preces pópuli tui: et præsta, ut quisquis hoc templum benefícia petitúrus ingréditur; cuncta se impetrásse lætétur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who year by year renew for us the day of the consecration of this Your holy temple, and bring us again in safety to Your sacred mysteries, hear the prayers of Your people, and grant that whoever enters this temple to ask for blessings may rejoice to have obtained them all; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Annue, quǽsumus Dómine, précibus nostris, ut quicúmque intra templi huius, cuius anniversárium dedicatiónis diem celebrámus, ámbitum continémur, plena tibi atque perfécta córporis et ánimæ devotióne placeámus: ut, dum hæc vota præséntia réddimus, ad ætérna prǽmia, te adiuvánte, perveníre mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hearken, we beseech You, O Lord, to our prayers, that all of us who are gathered within the walls of this temple, the anniversary of whose dedication we celebrate, may please You with full and perfect devotion of body and soul, so that, while we render these present offerings, we may by Your help deserve to attain to eternal rewards; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam sponsam vocáre dignátus es, ut quæ habéret grátiam per fídei devotiónem, habéret étiam ex nómine pietátem; da, ut omnis hæc plebs nómini tuo sérviens, huius vocábuli consórtio digna esse mereátur: et Ecclésia tua in templo, cuius anniversárius dedicatiónis dies celebrátur, tibi collécta, te tímeat, te díligat, te sequátur; ut dum iúgiter per vestígia tua gráditur, ad cæléstia promíssa, te ducénte, perveníre mereátur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who deigned to call Your Church Your bride, that she who had grace through the devotion of faith might also have holiness from the name; grant that all this people serving Your name may deserve to be worthy of sharing that title, and that Your Church, gathered to You in the temple whose anniversary of dedication is kept, may fear You, love You and follow You, that, walking ever in Your footsteps, she may under Your guidance deserve to come to the heavenly promises; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Pent0h": {"src": "Tempora/Pasc7-4", "or": ["Deus, qui hodiérna die corda fidélium Sancti Spíritus illustratióne docuísti: da nobis in eódem Spíritu recta sápere; et de eius semper consolatióne gaudére. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, You Who on this day have taught the hearts of the faithful by the light of the Holy Spirit, grant us by that Holy Spirit Himself, to know what is right and ever to rejoice in His help. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, quǽsumus, Dómine, oblata sanctífica: et corda nostra Sancti Spíritus illustratióne emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify these offerings, we beseech You, O Lord, and cleanse our hearts by the light of the Holy Spirit. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sancti Spíritus, Dómine, corda nostra mundet infúsio: et sui roris íntima aspersióne fecúndet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the inpouring of the Holy Spirit cleanse our hearts, O Lord, and make them fertile through the dew He sprinkles upon them. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1102_2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 624-625 (Ad secundam Missam); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, indulgentiárum Dómine; da animábus famulórum famularúmque tuárum, refrigérii sedem, quiétis beatitúdinem, et lúminis claritátem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the Lord of mercies, grant to the souls of Your servants and handmaids a place of refreshment, the happiness of rest and the brightness of light; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Propitiáre, Dómine, supplicatiónibus nostris, pro animábus famulórum famularúmque tuárum, pro quibus tibi offérimus sacrifícium laudis; ut eas Sanctórum tuórum consórtio sociáre dignéris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, O Lord, by our supplications for the souls of Your servants and handmaids, for whom we offer You the sacrifice of praise, that You may deign to join them to the fellowship of Your Saints; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, Dómine, ut ánimæ famulórum famularúmque tuárum, his purgátæ sacrifíciis; indulgéntiam páriter, et réquiem cápiant sempitérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that the souls of Your servants and handmaids, being cleansed by this sacrifice, may obtain both pardon and everlasting rest; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1102_3": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 625-626 (Ad tertiam Missam); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, véniæ largítor, et humánæ salútis auctor, quǽsumus cleméntiam tuam: ut ánimas famulórum famularúmque tuárum, quæ ex hoc sǽculo transiérunt; beáta María semper Vírgine intercedénte cum ómnibus Sanctis tuis, ad perpétuæ beatitúdinis consórtium perveníre concédas: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the giver of pardon and author of man's salvation, we beseech Your mercy that, blessed Mary ever Virgin interceding with all Your Saints, You would grant the souls of Your servants and handmaids who have passed out of this world to come to the fellowship of everlasting bliss; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, cuius misericórdiæ non est númerus, súscipe propítius preces humilitátis nostræ: et animábus ómnium fidélium defunctórum, quibus tui nóminis dedísti confessiónem, per hæc sacraménta salútis nostræ, cunctórum remissiónem tríbue peccatórum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, whose mercy is without measure, mercifully receive the prayers of our lowliness, and through these sacraments of our salvation grant the remission of all sins to the souls of all the faithful departed, to whom You gave the confession of Your name; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens et miséricors Deus: ut ánimæ famulórum famularúmque tuárum, pro quibus hoc sacrifícium laudis tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti; per huius virtútem sacraménti, a peccátis ómnibus expiátæ, lucis perpétuæ, te miseránte, recípiant beatitúdinem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty and merciful God, that the souls of Your servants and handmaids, for whom we have offered this sacrifice of praise to Your majesty, may by the power of this sacrament be cleansed from all their sins and, by Your mercy, receive the happiness of everlasting light; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Pent24": {"src": "Tempora/Pent24-0", "or": ["Excita, quǽsumus, Dómine, tuórum fidélium voluntátes: ut, divíni óperis fructum propénsius exsequéntes; pietátis tuæ remédia maióra percípiant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord, we beseech You, arouse the wills of Your faithful people that, by a more earnest search for the fruit of Your divine work, they may receive more abundantly of the healing effects of Your goodness. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "se": ["Propítius esto, Dómine, supplicatiónibus nostris: et, pópuli tui oblatiónibus precibúsque suscéptis, ómnium nostrum ad te corda convérte; ut, a terrenis cupiditátibus liberáti, ad cœléstia desidéria transeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be merciful, O Lord, to our humble requests and accept the offerings and prayers of Your people: turn the hearts of all of us to You, that, freed from earthly cravings, we may pass over to heavenly yearnings. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Concéde nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut per hæc sacraménta quæ súmpsimus, quidquid in nostra mente vitiósum est, ipsorum medicatiónis dono curétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, that all the evil in our hearts may be cured by the healing power of the sacrament we have received. Through Jesus Christ, thy Son our Lord, Who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end."]}, "S1112": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), 12 Nov.; English from the St Dominic Missal", "or": ["Deus, qui Prædicatórum Ordinem copiósa Sanctórum sóbole fecundáre dignátus es, atque in ipsis heróica ómnium virtútum mérita sublímiter coronásti: da nobis illórum sequi vestígia; ut quos hódie sub una celebritáte venerámur in terris, iis perpétua tandem festivitáte associémur in cælis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who didst deign to make the Order of Preachers fruitful with a plentiful offspring of Saints, and didst crown in them, on high, the heroic merits of every virtue: grant us to follow in their footsteps, that we who today venerate them on earth in a single feast may at length be joined to them in an everlasting festival in heaven. Through our Lord Jesus Christ thy Son, who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis offérimus: quæ et pro cunctórum tibi grata sint honóre iustórum, et nobis salutária, te miseránte, reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer thee, O Lord, the gifts of our devotion: may they be pleasing to thee for the honour of all the just, and by thy mercy be made profitable for our salvation. Through our Lord Jesus Christ thy Son, who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus, Dómine, fidélibus pópulis ómnium Sanctórum semper veneratióne lætári: et eórum perpétua supplicatióne muníri. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech thee, O Lord, that thy faithful people may ever rejoice in the veneration of all the Saints, and be defended by their unceasing intercession. Through our Lord Jesus Christ thy Son, who liveth and reigneth with thee in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0118": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), supplement (S. Margarita ab Hungaria), p. 1; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, virginitátis amátor et custos: cuius múnere fámula tua Margaríta virginitátis decórem mérito bonórum óperum sociávit; concéde, quǽsumus, ut mentis integritátem spíritu salutáris pæniténtiæ restauráre possímus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the loving guardian of virginity, by whose grace Your handmaid Margaret united to the beauty of virginity the merit of good works; grant, we beseech You, that in the spirit of saving penance we may be able to restore integrity of mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc obláta, quǽsumus, Dómine, miserátus inténde et, intercedénte beáta Margaríta, quam pæniténtiæ víctimam pro salúte suæ gentis fíeri voluísti, humáno géneri pacem in caritáte Christi placátus concéde: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, look mercifully on these offerings and, by the intercession of blessed Margaret, whom You willed to be made a victim of penance for the salvation of her people, be appeased and grant to the human race peace in the charity of Christ; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti, Dómine, mensa cælésti, te súpplices exorámus: ut, beátæ Margarítæ exémplo prætereúntem huius mundi contemnéntes figúram; ad ætérna mereámur gáudia perveníre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed, O Lord, at the heavenly table, we humbly beseech You that, by the example of blessed Margaret despising the fashion of this world which passes away, we may deserve to arrive at eternal joys; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0123": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 360; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Raymúndum pœniténtiæ Sacraménti insígnem minístrum elegísti; et per maris undas mirabíliter traduxísti: concéde, ut eius intercessióne dignos pœniténtiæ fructus fácere; et ad ætérnæ salútis portum perveníre valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who chose blessed Raymond to be a renowned minister of the sacrament of penance, and wondrously brought him across the waves of the sea; grant that through his intercession we may bring forth worthy fruits of penance and be able to reach the haven of eternal salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, Dómine, maiestáti tuæ obláta sanctífica, et intercedénte beáto Raymúndo Confessóre tuo, auxílium nobis tuæ defensiónis impénde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts offered to Your majesty; and through the intercession of blessed Raymond, Your confessor, bestow on us the help of Your protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut sancti Raymúndi Confessóris tui celebráta solémnitas; nobis indulgéntiam peccatórum, et glóriam ætérnæ felicitátis acquírat: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord our God, that the feast of Saint Raymond, Your confessor, which we have celebrated, may obtain for us pardon of our sins and the glory of eternal happiness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0125": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 5; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui univérsum mundum beáti Pauli Apóstoli prædicatióne docuísti: da nobis, quǽsumus, ut qui eius hódie Conversiónem cólimus; per eius ad te exémpla gradiámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who taught the whole world by the preaching of blessed Paul the apostle; grant, we beseech You, that we who this day keep his conversion may come to You by following his example; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Apóstoli tui Pauli précibus, Dómine, plebis tuæ dona sanctífica: ut quæ tibi tuo grata sunt institúto, gratióra fiant patrocínio supplicántis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through the prayers of Your apostle Paul sanctify the gifts of Your people, O Lord; that what is pleasing to You by Your own institution may become yet more pleasing through the patronage of his pleading; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sanctificáti, Dómine, salutári mystério: quǽsumus, ut nobis eius non desit orátio; cuius nos donásti patrocínio gubernári: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hallowed by the saving mystery, O Lord, we beseech You that his prayers may never fail us, under whose patronage You have granted us to be governed; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0201": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 370; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui beáti Ignátii Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis solémnia cólimus; eius apud te intercessiónibus adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who keep the feast of blessed Ignatius, Your martyr and bishop, may be helped by his intercession with You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, quǽsumus Dómine, emúndet nostra delícta: et ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this victim, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse away our sins, and hallow the bodies and souls of Your servants for the offering of this sacrifice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti participatióne múneris sacri, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut cuius exséquimur cultum; intercedénte beáto Ignátio Mártyre tuo atque Pontífice, sentiámus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by partaking of this sacred gift, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that through the intercession of blessed Ignatius, Your martyr and bishop, we may feel the effect of the rite we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0205": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 376; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui inter cétera poténtiæ tuæ mirácula, étiam in sexu frágili victóriam martýrii contulísti: concéde propítius, ut qui beátæ Agathæ Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ natalítia cólimus; per eius ad te exémpla gradiámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who among the other wonders of Your power have bestowed even on the weaker sex the victory of martyrdom; mercifully grant that we who keep the heavenly birthday of blessed Agatha, Your virgin and martyr, may come to You by following her example; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe Dómine múnera, quæ in beátæ Agathæ Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ solemnitáte deférimus: cuius nos confídimus patrocínio liberári. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, the gifts which we offer on the feast of blessed Agatha, Your virgin and martyr, by whose patronage we trust to be delivered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Auxiliéntur nobis, Dómine, sumpta mystéria; et intercedénte beáta Agatha Vírgine et Mártyre tua, sempitérna protectióne confírment: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the mysteries received, O Lord, be a help to us; and through the intercession of blessed Agatha, Your virgin and martyr, may they strengthen us with unfailing protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0210": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 379; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ánimam beátæ Vírginis tuæ Scholásticæ, ad ostendéndam innocéntiæ viam, in colúmbæ spécie cælum penetráre fecísti: da nobis eius méritis et précibus, ita innocénter vívere; ut ad ætérna mereámur gáudia perveníre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, to show forth the way of innocence, caused the soul of Your blessed virgin Scholastica to enter heaven in the likeness of a dove; grant us by her merits and prayers so to live in innocence that we may deserve to attain to eternal joys; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0213": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 382; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, qui beátam Catharínam Vírginem tui amóre succénsam, passiónis contemplatióne claréscere voluísti: eius intercessióne concéde, ut passiónis mystéria devóte recoléntes; eius fructum percípere mereámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, who willed that blessed Catherine, Your virgin, on fire with Your love, should shine forth by the contemplation of Your passion; grant through her intercession that we, devoutly recalling the mysteries of Your passion, may deserve to gather its fruit; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Fac, quǽsumus Dómine, holocáusti tui in ara crucis obláti nos esse partícipes: in cuius sacrosáncti mystérii contemplatióne beátam Catharínam Vírginem tuam mirábilem effecísti. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Make us, we beseech You, O Lord, partakers of Your holocaust offered on the altar of the cross, by the contemplation of which most holy mystery You made blessed Catherine, Your virgin, wonderful; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens et miséricors Deus: ut nos hæc, quæ súmpsimus, ineffábilis amóris pígnora, ad te redamándum inflámment; atque beátæ Catharínæ Vírginis intercessióne et exémplo, in tua semper dilectióne vivámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty and merciful God, that these pledges of ineffable love which we have received may inflame us to love You in return; and that by the intercession and example of blessed Catherine, Your virgin, we may ever live in Your love; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0214": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 385; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui salútis animárum zelo, et ampliándæ Religiónis grátia beátum Iordánum mirábilem effecísti: eius intercedéntibus méritis, fac nos in eódem semper spíritu vívere; ac repósitam in cælis glóriam inveníre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Jordan wonderful in zeal for the salvation of souls and by the grace of spreading the Order; by his merits and intercession grant that we may always live in the same spirit and find the glory laid up for us in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Cæléstis convívii munus quod offérimus, beátus Iordánus in conspéctu maiestátis tuæ, Dómine, præséntet: et dignáre, ut sicut illi confert ad glóriam, ita per ipsíus suffrágium pignus veræ viæ, et vitæ sempitérnæ nobis efficiátur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Jordan, O Lord, present in the sight of Your majesty the gift of the heavenly banquet which we offer; and vouchsafe that, as it brings him glory, so through his intercession it may become for us the pledge of the true way and of everlasting life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ætérnæ salútis spes, quam per Córporis et Sánguinis tui, Dómine, perceptiónem habére nos voluísti, secúra permáneat; et beáti Iordáni precátio ad glóriam capesséndam sit semper intercéssio salutáris: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the hope of eternal salvation which You have willed us to have through receiving Your Body and Blood, O Lord, remain secure; and may the prayer of blessed Jordan ever be a saving intercession for us to win glory; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0309": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 394; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Francíscam fámulam tuam, inter cétera grátiæ tuæ dona, familiári Angeli consuetúdine decorásti: concéde quǽsumus; ut intercessiónis eius auxílio, Angelórum consórtium cónsequi mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who among the other gifts of Your grace honored blessed Frances, Your handmaid, with the familiar companionship of an angel; grant, we beseech You, that by the help of her intercession we may deserve to attain the fellowship of the angels; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis offérimus: ut tibi grata, et nobis salutária beátæ Francíscæ pia supplicatióne reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gifts of our devotion, that through the holy pleading of blessed Frances they may become pleasing to You and salutary for us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut quos salutáribus dignátus es erudíre mystériis; beátæ Francíscæ intercessióne gloriósa, cæléstibus refícias aliméntis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that through the glorious intercession of blessed Frances You would refresh with heavenly food those whom You have deigned to instruct by these saving mysteries; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0325": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 403; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui de beátæ Maríæ Vírginis útero, Verbum tuum, Angelo nuntiánte, carnem suscípere voluísti; præsta supplícibus tuis: ut qui vere eam Genitrícem Dei crédimus; eius apud te intercessiónibus adiuvémur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that Your Word, at the message of an angel, should take flesh in the womb of the blessed Virgin Mary; grant to Your suppliants that we who truly believe her to be the Mother of God may be helped by her intercession with You; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["In méntibus nostris, quǽsumus Dómine, veræ fídei sacraménta confírma: ut qui concéptum de Vírgine, Deum verum et hóminem confitémur; per eius salutíferæ resurrectiónis poténtiam, ad ætérnam mereámur perveníre lætítiam. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Strengthen in our minds, we beseech You, O Lord, the mysteries of the true faith; that we who confess Him who was conceived of the Virgin to be true God and true man, may by the power of His saving resurrection deserve to attain eternal joy; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Grátiam tuam, quǽsumus Dómine, méntibus nostris infúnde: ut qui, Angelo nuntiánte, Christi Fílii tui Incarnatiónem cognóvimus; per passiónem eius et crucem ad resurrectiónis glóriam perducámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Pour forth, we beseech You, O Lord, Your grace into our hearts; that we, to whom the Incarnation of Christ Your Son was made known by the message of an angel, may by His passion and cross be brought to the glory of His resurrection; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0405": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 408; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui géntium multitúdinem, mira beáti Vincéntii Confessóris tui prædicatióne, ad agnitiónem tui nóminis veníre tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem ventúrum iúdicem nuntiávit in terris; præmiatórem habére mereámur in cælis: Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the wonderful preaching of blessed Vincent, Your confessor, brought a multitude of nations to the knowledge of Your name; grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have as our rewarder in heaven Him whom he proclaimed on earth as the Judge to come, our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis offérimus: quæ ut tibi grata sint, et nobis salutária reddántur, beátus Vincéntius Conféssor tuus, qui donis tuis hic éxstitit gloriósus, apud cleméntiam tuam pius pro nobis intercéssor exsístat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gifts of our devotion; and that they may be pleasing to You and salutary for us, may blessed Vincent, Your confessor, who was glorious here by Your gifts, stand before Your mercy as our loving intercessor; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divínis Dómine munéribus satiáti; quǽsumus, ut beáti Vincéntii Confessóris tui méritis gloriósis, salutáris víctimæ desiderátum sentiámus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with Your divine gifts, O Lord, we beseech You that through the glorious merits of blessed Vincent, Your confessor, we may feel the desired effect of the saving Victim; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0420": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 414; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Agnétem Vírginem tuam cælésti rore sæpe perfúndere; et oratiónis eius loca divérsis enátis flóribus decoráre dignátus es: concéde propítius, ut eius précibus, perpétuo tuæ benedictiónis rore conspérsi; æternitátis fructus percípere mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who were pleased often to bedew blessed Agnes, Your virgin, with heavenly dew, and to adorn the places of her prayer with flowers of many kinds springing up; mercifully grant that through her prayers, sprinkled with the unfailing dew of Your blessing, we may deserve to receive the fruits of eternity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátis Dómine placáre munéribus, et sicut beátam Agnétem Vírginem vexíllo sanctæ crucis insigníre dignátus es, ita eius méritis, holocáusti tui in ara crucis obláti partícipes nos esse concéde. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, O Lord, by the gifts we offer; and as You were pleased to mark blessed Agnes, Your virgin, with the standard of the holy cross, so by her merits grant that we may be partakers of Your holocaust offered on the altar of the cross; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacratíssimi Córporis et Sánguinis tui, Dómine, sanctificáti libámine: præsta, ut huius vitæ cursu lætánter expléto; intercedénte beáta Agnéte Vírgine tibi acceptíssima, ætérnis gáudiis pérfrui mereámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hallowed by the offering of Your most holy Body and Blood, O Lord, grant that, the course of this life being joyfully finished, we may, through the intercession of blessed Agnes, a virgin most pleasing to You, deserve to enjoy eternal gladness; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0424": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 416; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui in memóriam passiónis Dómini nostri Iesu Christi, Corónam eius spíneam venerámur in terris; ab ipso glória et honóre coronári mereámur in cælis: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who on earth venerate the crown of thorns of our Lord Jesus Christ in memory of His passion, may deserve to be crowned by Him with glory and honor in heaven; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Tuórum mílitum Rex omnípotens virtútem corróbora: ut quos in huius mortalitátis stádio, unigéniti Fílii tui Coróna lætíficat; consummáto cursu certáminis, immortalitátis bravíum apprehéndant. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Strengthen the might of Your soldiers, O almighty King, that they whom the crown of Your only-begotten Son gladdens in the race of this mortal life may, when the course of the contest is finished, lay hold of the prize of immortality; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súpplices te rogámus, omnípotens Deus: ut hæc sacraménta, quæ súmpsimus, per sacrosánctæ Fílii tui Corónæ, cuius solémnia recensémus, virtútem; nobis profíciant ad medélam: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We humbly beseech You, almighty God, that these sacraments which we have received may, through the power of the most sacred crown of Your Son, whose feast we keep, avail us for healing; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0429": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 421; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Petri Mártyris tui fidem cóngrua devotióne sectémur; qui pro eiúsdem fídei dilatatióne, martýrii palmam méruit obtinére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we may follow with fitting devotion the faith of blessed Peter, Your martyr, who for the spreading of that same faith merited to win the palm of martyrdom; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Preces, quas tibi Dómine offérimus, intercedénte beáto Petro Mártyre tuo, cleménter inténde; et púgiles fídei sub tua protectióne custódi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Mercifully regard, O Lord, the prayers which we offer You through the intercession of blessed Peter, Your martyr; and keep under Your protection the champions of the faith; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Fidéles tuos, Dómine, custódiant sacraménta, quæ súmpsimus; et intercedénte beáto Petro Mártyre tuo, contra omnes advérsos tueántur incúrsus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let the sacraments we have received safeguard Your faithful, O Lord; and through the intercession of blessed Peter, Your martyr, may they protect them against all hostile assaults; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0430": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 423; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátæ Catharínæ, virginitátis et patiéntiæ speciáli privilégio decorátæ, malignántium spirítuum certámina víncere, et in amóre tui nóminis inconcússe permanére tribuísti: concéde quǽsumus, ut eius imitatióne calcáta mundi nequítia, et ómnium hóstium superátis insídiis; ad tuam secúre glóriam transeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who granted to blessed Catherine, adorned with the special privilege of virginity and patience, to overcome the assaults of evil spirits and to remain unshaken in the love of Your name; grant, we beseech You, that by imitating her we may trample on the wickedness of the world, overcome the snares of all our enemies, and pass safely to Your glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, quǽsumus Dómine, quæ tibi in honórem beátæ Catharínæ Vírginis offérimus, benígno súscipe vultu: et nos eius méritis ac intercessióne, ad tuam fácito propítius perveníre lætítiam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive with kindly countenance, O Lord, we beseech You, the gifts we offer You in honor of blessed Catherine, Your virgin; and by her merits and intercession graciously bring us to Your joy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis, Dómine, divínæ grátiæ sacraméntis: quǽsumus, ut intercedénte beáta Catharína Vírgine tibi acceptíssima, hostíles superémus incúrsus; et ad ætérnæ redemptiónis augménta proficiscéntes, tuis semper óculis placeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received the sacraments of divine grace, O Lord, we beseech You that, through the intercession of blessed Catherine, a virgin most pleasing to You, we may overcome the assaults of the enemy, and, advancing toward the increase of eternal redemption, may ever be pleasing in Your sight; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0505": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 432; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ad conteréndos Ecclésiæ tuæ hostes, et ad divínum cultum reparándum, beátum Pium Pontíficem máximum elígere dignátus es: fac nos ipsíus deféndi præsídiis, et ita tuis inhærére obséquiis; ut ómnium hóstium superátis insídiis, perpétua pace lætémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who for the crushing of the enemies of Your Church and for the restoring of divine worship were pleased to choose blessed Pius as supreme Pontiff; grant that we may be defended by his protection and so cleave to Your service that, overcoming the snares of all our enemies, we may rejoice in everlasting peace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus Dómine, Ecclésiæ tuæ preces et oblatiónes: ut intercedénte beáto Pio Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, in conspéctu tuo in odórem suavitátis ascéndant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, we beseech You, O Lord, the prayers and offerings of Your Church; that through the intercession of blessed Pius, Your confessor and pontiff, they may rise as an odor of sweetness in Your sight; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Spíritum, Dómine Deus, iustítiæ ac fortitúdinis benígnus infúnde fidélibus tuis; quos beáti Pii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis zelo ac constántia, ab ómnium hóstium incursióne tuéri dignátus es: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord God, graciously pour forth the spirit of justice and fortitude upon Your faithful, whom You have deigned to protect from the assaults of all their enemies through the zeal and steadfastness of blessed Pius, Your confessor and pontiff; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0507": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 434; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, pro cuius honóre gloriósus Póntifex Stanisláus gládiis impiórum occúbuit: præsta quǽsumus, ut omnes, qui eius implórant auxílium; petitiónis suæ salutárem consequántur efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, for whose honor the glorious bishop Stanislaus fell beneath the swords of wicked men; grant, we beseech You, that all who implore his help may obtain the saving fruit of their petition; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sit in conspéctu tuo, Dómine, nostra devótio, et beáti Stanislái Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis nobis fiat supplicatióne salutáris, pro cuius solemnitáte defértur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our devotion be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, and may it become salutary for us through the pleading of blessed Stanislaus, Your martyr and bishop, on whose feast it is offered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: beáti Stanislái Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of blessed Stanislaus, Your martyr and bishop, whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0509": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 437; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Gregórium minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave to Your people blessed Gregory as a minister of eternal salvation; grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have as an intercessor in heaven him whom we had on earth as a teacher of life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Gregórii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, through the intercession of blessed Gregory, Your confessor and bishop, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Gregórii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, we beseech You, almighty God, that we may everywhere be helped by the prayer of blessed Gregory, Your confessor and bishop, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0518": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 446; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui hunc diem beáti Venántii Mártyris tui triúmpho consecrásti; exáudi preces pópuli tui: et præsta, ut qui eius mérita venerámur; fídei constántiam imitémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who have consecrated this day by the triumph of blessed Venantius, Your martyr; hear the prayers of Your people, and grant that we who venerate his merits may imitate the constancy of his faith; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hanc oblatiónem, omnípotens Deus, beáti Venántii Mártyris tui mérita tibi reddant accéptam: ut ipsíus subsídiis adiúti, glóriæ eius consórtes efficiámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the merits of blessed Venantius, Your martyr, make this offering acceptable to You, almighty God; that, helped by his aid, we may be made sharers of his glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, ætérnæ vitæ sacraménta, te humíliter deprecántes: ut beáto Venántio Mártyre tuo pro nobis deprecánte; véniam nobis concílient, et grátiam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the sacraments of eternal life, and humbly beseech You that, blessed Venantius, Your martyr, pleading for us, they may obtain for us pardon and grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0519": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 447; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Petrum Cælestínum ad summi Pontificátus ápicem sublimásti; quique illum humilitáti postpónere docuísti: concéde propítius, ut eius exémplo cuncta mundi despícere; et ad promíssa humílibus prǽmia perveníre felíciter mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who raised blessed Peter Celestine to the height of the supreme pontificate, and taught him to set it aside for the sake of humility; mercifully grant that by his example we may despise all things of the world and happily deserve to attain the rewards promised to the humble; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti tui, quǽsumus Dómine, nos ubíque lætíficent: ut dum eórum mérita recólimus, patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your saints, we beseech You, O Lord, everywhere make us glad; that while we recall their merits we may feel their patronage; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut de percéptis munéribus grátias exhibéntes; intercedénte beáto Petro Cælestíno Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, benefícia potióra sumámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that giving thanks for the gifts we have received, we may, through the intercession of blessed Peter Celestine, Your confessor and pontiff, receive still greater benefits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0526": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 452; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Philíppum Confessórem tuum Sanctórum tuórum glória sublimásti: concéde propítius, ut cuius solemnitáte lætámur; eius virtútum proficiámus exémplo: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who raised blessed Philip, Your confessor, to the glory of Your saints; mercifully grant that we who rejoice in his feast may profit by the example of his virtues; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, quǽsumus Dómine, inténde placátus: et præsta, ut illo nos igne Spíritus Sanctus inflámmet, quo beáti Philíppi cor mirabíliter penetrávit. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously, O Lord, we beseech You, upon these present sacrifices, and grant that the Holy Spirit may enkindle us with that fire with which He wondrously pierced the heart of blessed Philip; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the same Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cæléstibus, Dómine, pasti delíciis: quǽsumus, ut beáti Philíppi Confessóris tui méritis et imitatióne; semper eádem, per quæ veráciter vívimus, appetámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Fed with heavenly delights, O Lord, we beseech You that by the merits and imitation of blessed Philip, Your confessor, we may ever seek after those things by which we truly live; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0604": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 460; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Francíscum novi Ordinis Institutórem orándi stúdio, et pœniténtiæ amóre decorásti: da fámulis tuis in eius imitatióne ita profícere; ut semper orántes, et corpus in servitútem redigéntes, ad cæléstem glóriam perveníre mereántur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who adorned blessed Francis, founder of a new Order, with zeal for prayer and love of penance; grant to Your servants so to advance in imitating him that, praying always and bringing the body into subjection, they may deserve to attain heavenly glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Francísco Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Francis, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0614": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 466; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Basilíum minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave to Your people blessed Basil as a minister of eternal salvation; grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have as an intercessor in heaven him whom we had on earth as a teacher of life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti Basilíi Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis, quǽsumus Dómine, ánnua solémnitas pietáti tuæ nos reddat accéptos: ut per hæc piæ placatiónis offícia, et illum beáta retribútio comitétur, et nobis grátiæ tuæ dona concíliet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the yearly feast of Saint Basil, Your confessor and bishop, make us acceptable to Your loving kindness, O Lord, we beseech You; that by these offices of holy propitiation a blessed reward may attend him, and the gifts of Your grace may be won for us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, fidélium remunerátor animárum: præsta, ut beáti Basilíi Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis, cuius venerándam celebrámus festivitátem; précibus indulgéntiam consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the rewarder of faithful souls, grant that through the prayers of blessed Basil, Your confessor and bishop, whose venerable feast we celebrate, we may obtain pardon; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0702": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 485; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens et miséricors Deus, maiestátem tuam supplíciter exorámus: ut sicut Unigénitum tuum per Visitatiónem et salutatiónem Genitrícis eius púero clauso in útero revelásti; ita méritis eiúsdem Genitrícis, et précibus, ipsum nos fácias reveláta fácie perpétuo contemplári: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and merciful God, we humbly entreat Your majesty that, as You revealed Your only-begotten Son to the child enclosed in the womb through the visitation and greeting of His Mother, so by the merits and prayers of the same Mother You would grant us to contemplate Him for ever with unveiled face; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui de ómnibus in te confidéntibus curam semper habes: præsta quǽsumus, ut per oblatiónem, quam tibi offérimus, visitatiónem spirituálem beátæ Maríæ Vírginis in nostris necessitátibus semper sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, who ever have care of all who trust in You; grant, we beseech You, that through the offering which we make to You we may always feel in our needs the spiritual visitation of the blessed Virgin Mary; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui commemoratiónem Visitatiónis beatíssimæ Maríæ Matris Dei fíeri voluísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut per hoc sacrifícium, quod súmpsimus; ab eius visitatiónis grátia nullátenus excidámus: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, who willed that the commemoration of the Visitation of most blessed Mary, Mother of God, should be kept; grant, we beseech You, that through this sacrifice which we have received we may never fall away from the grace of her visitation; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0709": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 490; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beatórum Mártyrum tuórum Ioánnis et sociórum eius, gloriósum pro fide tua certámen æternitátis láurea decorásti: concéde propítius, ut eórum méritis et imitatióne certántes in terris; cum ipsis coronári mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who crowned with the laurel of eternity the glorious struggle for Your faith of Your blessed martyrs John and his companions; mercifully grant that, striving on earth by their merits and imitation, we may deserve to be crowned with them in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Réspice Dómine de sanctuário tuo, et de excélso cælórum habitáculo, sacrifícium, quod immolámus: et sánguine sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum clamánte, corda nostra igne caritátis flamméscant, et ad te preces nostræ in odórem suavitátis ascéndant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look down, O Lord, from Your sanctuary and from the lofty dwelling place of heaven upon the sacrifice which we offer; and, the blood of Your holy martyrs crying out, may our hearts glow with the fire of charity, and our prayers rise to You as an odor of sweetness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, virtútis auctor ac largítor, per sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum fidem et constántiam concéde: ut nos ad sacrum convívium accedéntes, eódem accendámur ardóre; quo ipsi pro veritáte Córporis et Sánguinis tui, vitam tibi in holocáustum obtulére: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, author and giver of strength, grant through the faith and constancy of Your holy martyrs that we who approach the sacred banquet may be kindled with the same ardor with which they offered their lives to You as a holocaust for the truth of Your Body and Blood; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0711": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 493; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beatórum Pontíficum Ignátii et Domínici ac sociórum sánguine Annamitárum terras rigári voluísti; intercedéntibus tantis Martýribus, fac eas christiána religióne florére. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that the lands of Annam should be watered by the blood of the blessed bishops Ignatius and Dominic and their companions; through the intercession of these great martyrs make them flourish with the Christian religion; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Fortitúdinis auctor ac largítor omnípotens Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta sanctífica: et intercedéntibus beátis Martýribus, quorum hódie solémnia celebrámus, córdium nostrórum medére languóribus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty God, author and giver of fortitude, sanctify the gifts offered to Your majesty; and through the intercession of the blessed martyrs whose feast we celebrate today, heal the weaknesses of our hearts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Tríbuant nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, tua Sacraménta constántiam; quæ beátos Mártyres aluérunt ad victóriam. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your sacraments, O Lord, we beseech You, give us that constancy with which they nourished the blessed martyrs unto victory; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0718": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 498; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Camíllum, ad animárum in extrémo agóne luctántium subsídium, singulári caritátis prærogatíva decorásti: eius, quǽsumus, méritis spíritum nobis tuæ dilectiónis infúnde; ut in hora éxitus nostri hostem víncere, et ad cæléstem mereámur corónam perveníre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who adorned blessed Camillus with a singular gift of charity for the help of souls struggling in their last agony; by his merits, we beseech You, pour into us the spirit of Your love, that in the hour of our death we may overcome the enemy and deserve to attain the heavenly crown; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Camíllo Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Camillus, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0722": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 502; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Largíre nobis, clementíssime Pater: ut sicut beáta María Magdaléna Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum super ómnia diligéndo, suórum obtínuit véniam peccatórum; ita nobis apud misericórdiam tuam, sempitérnam ímpetret beatitúdinem: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, most merciful Father, that as blessed Mary Magdalen, by loving our Lord Jesus Christ above all things, obtained pardon of her sins, so she may obtain for us everlasting happiness from Your mercy; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hanc nostræ oblatiónis hóstiam, terríbilis et piíssime Deus, beáta María Magdaléna suárum precum cúmulet increméntis, et ad remédium nobis proveníre depóscat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, awesome and most loving, may blessed Mary Magdalen enrich this victim of our offering with the increase of her prayers, and ask that it may avail for our healing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sanctíficet nos, quǽsumus Dómine, et múniat intercedénte beáta María Magdaléna, divíni múneris sacra libátio; et cæléstium virtútum coherédes effíciat: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacred outpouring of the divine gift, O Lord, we beseech You, sanctify and protect us through the intercession of blessed Mary Magdalen, and make us co-heirs with the heavenly powers; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0726": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 507; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Annam Genitrícis tuæ matrem ad cæléstis vitæ gáudia extulísti: fac nos, quǽsumus, gloriósis eius méritis ad ætérnam pertíngere beatitúdinem; ex cuius salutári puerpério pro salúte mundi humánam natúram assúmere dignátus es: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who raised blessed Anne, the mother of Your Mother, to the joys of heavenly life; grant, we beseech You, that by her glorious merits we may attain to eternal happiness, You who from her saving offspring deigned to take human nature for the salvation of the world; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accipe Dómine múnera dignánter obláta: et beátæ Annæ suffragántibus méritis, ad nostræ salútis auxílium proveníre concéde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, O Lord, the gifts devoutly offered, and grant that through the pleading merits of blessed Anne they may avail for the help of our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beátæ Annæ matris beatíssimæ Vírginis Maríæ nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, we beseech You, almighty God, that we may everywhere be helped by the prayer of blessed Anne, mother of the most blessed Virgin Mary, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0802": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 512; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui per beátum Alphónsum Maríam Confessórem tuum atque Pontíficem, animárum zelo succénsum, Ecclésiam tuam nova prole fecundásti: quǽsumus, ut eius salutáribus mónitis edócti, et exémplis roboráti; ad te perveníre felíciter valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who through blessed Alphonsus Mary, Your confessor and bishop, on fire with zeal for souls, enriched Your Church with a new offspring; we beseech You that, taught by his saving counsels and strengthened by his example, we may happily come to You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Cælésti, Dómine Iesu Christe, sacrifícii igne corda nostra in odórem suavitátis exúre, qui beáto Alphónso Maríæ tribuísti et hæc mystéria celebráre, et per eádem hóstiam tibi sanctam seípsum exhibére. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, burn our hearts with the heavenly fire of the sacrifice unto an odor of sweetness, You who granted blessed Alphonsus Mary both to celebrate these mysteries and through them to offer himself to You as a holy victim; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui beátum Alphónsum Maríam Confessórem tuum atque Pontíficem, fidélem divíni mystérii dispensatórem et præcónem effecísti: eius méritis precibúsque concéde, ut fidéles tui et frequénter percípiant; et percipiéndo sine fine colláudent: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Alphonsus Mary, Your confessor and bishop, a faithful dispenser and herald of the divine mystery; grant by his merits and prayers that Your faithful may receive it often, and, receiving it, praise You without end; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0804": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 516; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Domínici Confessóris tui, Patris nostri, illumináre dignátus es méritis et doctrínis: concéde, ut eius intercessióne, temporálibus non destituátur auxíliis; et spirituálibus semper profíciat increméntis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who were pleased to enlighten Your Church by the merits and teaching of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, our Father; grant that through his intercession she may not be deprived of temporal help, and may ever grow in spiritual increase; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi Dómine dicáta sanctífica: ut méritis beáti Domínici Confessóris tui, Patris nostri, nobis profíciant ad medélam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts dedicated to You; that by the merits of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, our Father, they may avail us for healing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui peccatórum nostrórum póndere prémimur; beáti Domínici Confessóris tui, Patris nostri, patrocínio sublevémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who are weighed down by the burden of our sins may be raised up by the patronage of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, our Father; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0806": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 518; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui fídei sacraménta in Unigéniti tui gloriósa Transfiguratióne Patrum testimónio roborásti; et adoptiónem filiórum perféctam, voce delápsa in nube lúcida, mirabíliter præsignásti: concéde propítius, ut ipsíus Regis glóriæ nos coherédes effícias; et eiúsdem glóriæ tríbuas esse consórtes: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who in the glorious Transfiguration of Your only-begotten Son confirmed the mysteries of the faith by the testimony of the fathers, and by the voice that came from the bright cloud wondrously foreshowed the perfect adoption of sons; mercifully grant that You may make us co-heirs of the King of glory Himself, and grant us to be sharers of that same glory; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Obláta, quǽsumus Dómine, múnera, gloriósa Unigéniti tui Transfiguratióne sanctífica: nosque a peccatórum máculis, splendóribus ipsíus illustratiónis emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts offered, through the glorious Transfiguration of Your only-begotten Son, and cleanse us from the stains of sin by the splendor of His brightness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut sacrosáncta Fílii tui Transfiguratiónis mystéria, quæ solémni celebrámus offício; purificátæ mentis intelligéntia consequámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we may attain with the understanding of a purified mind the sacred mysteries of the Transfiguration of Your Son, which we celebrate with solemn office; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0817": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 532; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Hyacínthum Confessórem tuum, in divérsis natiónum pópulis, óperum sanctitáte, et miraculórum glória fecísti conspícuum: da nobis, ut eius in mélius reformémur exémplis; et in advérsis protegámur auxíliis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Hyacinth, Your confessor, renowned among the peoples of many nations by the holiness of his works and the glory of his miracles; grant that we may be reformed for the better by his example and protected in adversity by his help; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacras hóstias, Dómine, intervéntu digníssimæ Matris, intrépidus super aquas ambulátor beátus Hyacínthus ante conspéctum divínæ tuæ maiestátis déferat: et ad salútem nostram delátas, benígnus acceptáre dignéris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through the intercession of Your most worthy Mother, may blessed Hyacinth, who walked fearless upon the waters, bring these sacred offerings before the sight of Your divine majesty, O Lord; and do You graciously deign to accept them, brought for our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quos ineffábili suavitáte Córporis et Sánguinis tui, Dómine, recreásti: quǽsumus, ut beáti Hyacínthi piis précibus adiútos; ad ætérnam fácias perveníre lætítiam: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, that those whom You have refreshed with the ineffable sweetness of Your Body and Blood, helped by the loving prayers of blessed Hyacinth, You would bring to eternal joy; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0821": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 536; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens et miséricors Deus, qui beátam Ioánnam Francíscam tuo amóre succénsam, admirábili spíritus fortitúdine per omnes vitæ sémitas in via perfectiónis donásti; quique per illam illustráre Ecclésiam tuam nova prole voluísti: eius méritis et précibus concéde, ut qui infirmitátis nostræ cónscii de tua virtúte confídimus; cæléstis grátiæ auxílio cuncta nobis adversántia vincámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and merciful God, who endowed blessed Jane Frances, on fire with Your love, with wonderful strength of spirit along every path of life in the way of perfection, and willed through her to enrich Your Church with a new offspring; grant by her merits and prayers that we who, conscious of our weakness, trust in Your strength, may by the help of heavenly grace overcome all that is against us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Illo nos amóris igne, quǽsumus Dómine, hæc hóstia salutáris inflámmet, quo beátæ Ioánnæ Francíscæ cor veheménter incéndit, et flammis adússit ætérnæ caritátis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this saving victim, we beseech You, O Lord, inflame us with that fire of love with which it vehemently kindled the heart of blessed Jane Frances and seared it with the flames of eternal charity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Spíritum nobis, Dómine, tuæ caritátis infúnde: ut quos cæléstis panis virtúte satiásti; beáta Ioánna Francísca intercedénte, fácias terréna despícere, et te solum Deum pura mente sectári: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Pour into us, O Lord, the spirit of Your charity, that, through the intercession of blessed Jane Frances, You would make those whom You have filled with the strength of the heavenly bread despise the things of earth and follow You alone, the true God, with a pure mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0827": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 541; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui per sanctum Ioséphum Confessórem tuum, ad erudiéndam spíritu intelligéntiæ ac pietátis iuventútem, novum Ecclésiæ tuæ subsídium providére dignátus es: præsta quǽsumus, nos eius exémplo et intercessióne ita fácere et docére; ut prǽmia consequámur ætérna: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who through Saint Joseph, Your confessor, were pleased to provide a new help for Your Church in forming the young in the spirit of understanding and piety; grant, we beseech You, that by his example and intercession we may so act and teach as to obtain eternal rewards; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Altáre tuum, Dómine, munéribus cumulámus oblátis: ut eius nobis fiant supplicatióne propítia, cuius nos donásti patrocínio adiuvári. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We load Your altar, O Lord, with the gifts we offer; that they may become pleasing to You through the pleading of him by whose patronage You have granted us to be helped; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sanctificáti, Dómine, salutári mystério; quǽsumus, ut intercedénte sancto Iosépho Confessóre tuo, ad maius semper proficiámus pietátis increméntum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hallowed by the saving mystery, O Lord, we beseech You that, through the intercession of Saint Joseph, Your confessor, we may ever advance to a greater increase of piety; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0829": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 543; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Sancti Ioánnis Baptístæ Præcursóris et Mártyris tui, quǽsumus Dómine, veneránda festívitas; salutáris auxílii nobis præstet efféctum: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the venerable feast of Saint John the Baptist, Your precursor and martyr, O Lord, we beseech You, obtain for us the effect of saving help; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi Dómine pro sancti Mártyris tui Ioánnis Baptístæ passióne deférimus: quǽsumus, ut eius obténtu nobis profíciant ad salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You gifts, O Lord, for the passion of Your holy martyr John the Baptist; and we beseech You that at his pleading they may avail us unto salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cónferat nobis, Dómine, sancti Ioánnis Baptístæ beáta solémnitas: ut et magnífica sacraménta, quæ súmpsimus, significáta venerémur; et in nobis pótius édita gaudeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the blessed feast of Saint John the Baptist, O Lord, obtain for us that we may both venerate the great sacraments we have received in what they signify, and rejoice rather in what they bring about in us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0830": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 545; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Bonórum ómnium largítor omnípotens Deus: qui beátam Rosam cæléstis grátiæ rore prævéntam, virginitátis et patiéntiæ decóre, Indis floréscere voluísti; da nobis fámulis tuis, ut in odórem suavitátis eius curréntes, Christi bonus odor éffici mereámur: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty God, bestower of all good things, who willed that blessed Rose, prevented by the dew of heavenly grace, should flower among the Indians in the beauty of virginity and patience; grant to us Your servants that, running in the odor of her sweetness, we may deserve to become the good odor of Christ; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sint tibi, Dómine, laudis hóstiæ, quas humíliter immolámus, beátæ Rosæ Vírginis fragrántia perfúsas: ut illi cónferant ad honórem, et nobis propitiatóriæ reddántur ad salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifices of praise which we humbly offer You, O Lord, steeped in the fragrance of blessed Rose, Your virgin, be acceptable to You; that they may bring her honor, and become for us a propitiation unto salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ascéndant ad te Dómine preces nostræ, beátæ Rosæ Vírginis suavitátem redoléntes: ut cæléstibus dápibus temporáliter recreáti; ætérni convívii dulcédine perfruámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our prayers rise to You, O Lord, fragrant with the sweetness of blessed Rose, Your virgin; that, refreshed in time with the food of heaven, we may enjoy the sweetness of the eternal banquet; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0908": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 552; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Supplicatiónem servórum tuórum Deus miserátor exáudi: ut qui in Nativitáte Dei Genitrícis et Vírginis congregámur; eius intercessiónibus a te de instántibus perículis eruámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Mercifully hear, O God, the supplication of Your servants, that we who are gathered together on the Nativity of the Virgin Mother of God may by her intercession be delivered by You from the dangers that threaten us; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Unigéniti tui, Dómine, nobis succúrrat humánitas: ut qui natus de Vírgine, Matris integritátem non mínuit, sed sacrávit, in Nativitátis eius solémniis, nostris nos piáculis éxuens, oblatiónem nostram tibi fáciat accéptam: Iesus Christus Dóminus noster, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the humanity of Your only-begotten Son, O Lord, come to our aid; that He who, born of the Virgin, did not lessen but hallowed His Mother's integrity, may on the feast of her Nativity free us from our sins and make our offering acceptable to You, Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, celebritátis ánnuæ votíva sacraménta; præsta quǽsumus, ut et temporális vitæ nobis remédia prǽbeant, et ætérnæ: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the votive sacraments of this yearly feast; grant, we beseech You, that they may bring us remedies for this temporal life and for the life eternal; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0916": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 559; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Infirmitátem nostram, quǽsumus Dómine, propítius réspice: et mala ómnia, quæ iuste merémur; sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum atque Pontíficum Cornélii et Cypriáni intercessióne avérte: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Mercifully regard our weakness, O Lord, we beseech You, and through the intercession of Your holy martyrs and bishops Cornelius and Cyprian turn away from us all the evils which we justly deserve; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Plebis tuæ, Dómine, múnera benígnus inténde, quæ maiestáti tuæ pro sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum atque Pontíficum Cornélii et Cypriáni solemnitátibus sunt dicáta. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously, O Lord, upon the gifts of Your people, which are dedicated to Your majesty on the feast of Your holy martyrs and bishops Cornelius and Cyprian; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, Dómine, salutáribus repléti mystériis: ut quorum solémnia celebrámus; eórum oratiónibus adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with the saving mysteries, we beseech You, O Lord, that we may be helped by the prayers of those whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0918": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 562; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Ioánnem Confessórem, grátiæ tuæ ubertáte prævéntum in húmili vitæ génere morum candóre floréscere voluísti: da nobis, quǽsumus, ita eius vestígia pérsequi; ut ad te puris méntibus perveníre mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed John, Your confessor, prevented by the abundance of Your grace, should flourish in a lowly state of life by the purity of his ways; grant us, we beseech You, so to follow in his footsteps that we may deserve to come to You with pure minds; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi Dómine hóstias offérimus in honórem beáti Ioánnis Confessóris, qui pro salúte fidélium maiestáti tuæ pœniténtiæ víctimam seípsum iúgiter immolávit. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, sacrifices of praise in honor of blessed John, Your confessor, who for the salvation of the faithful continually offered himself to Your majesty as a victim of penance; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Concéde nos, omnípotens Deus, cælésti pane reféctos, beáto Ioánne Confessóre intercedénte, iúgiter in tuo amóre profícere; cui tribuísti morum candórem, et perféctam caritátem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, almighty God, that we who are refreshed with the bread of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed John, Your confessor, ever grow in Your love, You who gave him purity of life and perfect charity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0919": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 562; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos ánnua sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum Ianuárii et sociórum eius solemnitáte lætíficas: concéde propítius, ut quorum gaudémus méritis; accendámur exémplis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gladden us by the yearly feast of Your holy martyrs Januarius and his companions; mercifully grant that we who rejoice in their merits may be kindled by their example; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátis, quǽsumus Dómine, placáre munéribus: et intercedéntibus sanctis Martýribus tuis Ianuário et sóciis eius, a cunctis nos defénde perículis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, we beseech You, O Lord, by the gifts we offer; and through the intercession of Your holy martyrs Januarius and his companions defend us from all dangers; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Hæc nos commúnio, Dómine, purget a crímine: et intercedéntibus sanctis Martýribus tuis Ianuário et sóciis eius; cæléstis remédii fáciat esse consórtes: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this communion, O Lord, cleanse us from guilt, and through the intercession of Your holy martyrs Januarius and his companions make us sharers in the heavenly remedy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0921": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 564; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Matthǽi Apóstoli tui et Evangelístæ, quam prævenímus, veneránda solémnitas; et devotiónem nobis áugeat, et salútem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the venerable feast of blessed Matthew, Your apostle and evangelist, which we anticipate, may increase in us both devotion and salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Apostólici reveréntia cúlminis offeréntes tibi sacra mystéria, Dómine quǽsumus, ut beáti Matthǽi Apóstoli tui et Evangelístæ suffrágiis, cuius natalítia prævenímus, plebs tua semper et sua vota deprómat, et desideráta percípiat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Offering You the sacred mysteries in reverence of the apostolic dignity, we beseech You, O Lord, that through the prayers of blessed Matthew, Your apostle and evangelist, whose heavenly birthday we anticipate, Your people may ever both pour forth their prayers and obtain what they desire; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sancti Apóstoli tui et Evangelístæ Matthǽi, quǽsumus Dómine, supplicatióne placátus: et véniam nobis tríbue; et remédia sempitérna concéde: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Appeased, O Lord, we beseech You, by the supplication of Your holy apostle and evangelist Matthew, grant us pardon and bestow on us everlasting remedies; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1005": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 582; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Raymúndum Confessórem tuum insígnem perfectiónis evangélicæ magístrum, et Apostólicæ auctoritátis fidélem adsertórem esse voluísti: concéde propítius, ut eius exémplo vivéntes in terris; cum ipso coronári mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed Raymond, Your confessor, should be an eminent master of evangelical perfection and a faithful defender of apostolic authority; mercifully grant that we who live on earth after his example may deserve to be crowned with him in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Per istam oblatiónem et beáti Raymúndi Confessóris tui intercessiónem da, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus, ut terréna despiciéntes cæléstia semper cogitémus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through this offering and the intercession of blessed Raymond, Your confessor, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that despising earthly things we may ever set our thoughts on the things of heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis, Dómine, Córporis et Sánguinis tui mystériis, humíliter deprecámur: ut, intercedénte fámulo tuo Raymúndo; post huius vitæ perícula ætérna in cælis gáudia consequámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received the mysteries of Your Body and Blood, O Lord, we humbly entreat You that, through the intercession of Your servant Raymond, we may, after the dangers of this life, attain eternal joys in heaven; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1008": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 584; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Dómine Deus noster, qui beátæ Birgíttæ per Fílium tuum unigénitum secréta cæléstia revelásti: ipsíus pia intercessióne da nobis fámulis tuis; in revelatióne sempitérnæ glóriæ tuæ gaudére lætántes: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord our God, who through Your only-begotten Son revealed heavenly secrets to blessed Bridget; grant to us Your servants, through her loving intercession, to rejoice with gladness in the revelation of Your everlasting glory; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1009": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 587; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Ludovícum Confessórem tuum, per córporis mortificatiónem, et fídei præcónium Sanctórum glóriæ coæquásti: præsta, ut quod fide profitémur; pietátis opéribus iúgiter impleámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by mortification of the body and the preaching of the faith made blessed Louis, Your confessor, equal to the glory of the saints; grant that what we profess by faith we may ever fulfil by works of piety; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícium huius sacræ mensæ, a Rege regum Iesu Christo pro nobis parátæ, tibi Deus offérimus: et beáti Ludovíci suffragántibus méritis, nostrum inde subsídium et solámen hauríre concéde. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O God, the sacrifice of this sacred table, prepared for us by the King of kings, Jesus Christ; and through the pleading merits of blessed Louis grant us to draw from it our help and consolation; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens et miséricors Deus, ut qui beáti Ludovíci mérita celebrámus; eius étiam virtútes imitémur: et imitándo proficiámus; et proficiéndo ad cæléstia regna cum eo perveníre valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty and merciful God, that we who celebrate the merits of blessed Louis may also imitate his virtues, and by imitating may advance, and by advancing may be able to come with him to the heavenly kingdom; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1014": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 589; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos cónspicis ex nostra infirmitáte defícere; ad amórem tuum nos misericórditer per Sanctórum tuórum exémpla restáura: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who see that we fail through our own weakness; mercifully restore us to Your love by the example of Your saints; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Mýstica nobis Dómine prosit oblátio: quæ nos et a reátibus nostris expédiat, et perpétua salvatióne confírmet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the mystical offering, O Lord, profit us, that it may both free us from our sins and confirm us in everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut reátus nostros múnera sacráta puríficent; et recte vivéndi nobis operéntur efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that the sacred gifts may cleanse our guilt and bring about in us the effect of right living; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1015": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 590; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Exáudi nos Deus salutáris noster; ut sicut de beátæ Terésiæ Vírginis tuæ festivitáte gaudémus: ita cæléstis eius doctrínæ pábulo nutriámur; et piæ devotiónis erudiámur afféctu. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear us, O God our Savior, that as we rejoice in the feast of blessed Teresa, Your virgin, so we may be nourished by the food of her heavenly teaching and taught by the affection of loving devotion; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Maiestáti tuæ, quǽsumus Dómine, beátæ Terésiæ précibus nostra sit accépta devótio: cui medullátum cordis eius ita plácuit holocáustum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our devotion, we beseech You, O Lord, be acceptable to Your majesty through the prayers of blessed Teresa, to whom the inmost holocaust of her heart was so pleasing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súbdita tibi família, quam cælésti pane satiásti; quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut beátæ Terésiæ intercessióne et exémplo; misericórdias tuas váleat in ætérnum cantáre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord our God, that Your household, subject to You, which You have fed with the bread of heaven, may through the intercession and example of blessed Teresa be able to sing Your mercies for ever; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1018": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 592; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Intervéniat pro nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, sanctus tuus Lucas Evangelísta; qui crucis mortificatiónem iúgiter in suo córpore pro tui nóminis amóre portávit: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your holy evangelist Luke intercede for us, we beseech You, O Lord, who for the love of Your name ever bore in his body the mortification of the cross; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Donis cæléstibus da nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, líbera tibi mente servíre: ut múnera quæ deférimus, interveniénte beáto Evangelísta tuo Luca, et medélam nobis operéntur, et glóriam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, through these heavenly gifts, to serve You with a free mind; that the gifts which we offer may, through the intercession of blessed Luke, Your evangelist, work in us both healing and glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Repléti, Dómine, benedictióne cælésti, supplíciter exorámus: ut quod frágili celebrámus offício; beáti Lucæ Evangelístæ tui nobis prodésse sentiámus auxílio: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled, O Lord, with heavenly blessing, we humbly entreat You that what we celebrate with our frail service we may feel to profit us through the help of blessed Luke, Your evangelist; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1101": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 607; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui nos ómnium Sanctórum tuórum mérita sub una tribuísti celebritáte venerári: quǽsumus, ut desiderátam nobis tuæ propitiatiónis abundántiam; multiplicátis intercessóribus, largiáris: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, who have granted us to venerate in one solemn feast the merits of all Your saints; we beseech You that, with our intercessors multiplied, You would bestow on us the longed-for abundance of Your mercy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis offérimus: quæ et pro cunctórum tibi grata sint honóre Sanctórum, et nobis salutária, te miseránte, reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gifts of our devotion; may they be pleasing to You in honor of all the saints, and by Your mercy become salutary for us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, fidélibus pópulis, ómnium Sanctórum semper veneratióne lætári; et eórum perpétua supplicatióne muníri: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant to Your faithful people, we beseech You, O Lord, ever to rejoice in the veneration of all the saints, and to be defended by their unceasing supplication; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1105": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 616; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus humílium celsitúdo, qui beátum Martínum Confessórem tuum ad cæléstia regna transíre fecísti: eius méritis et intercessióne concéde, nos eius humilitátem ita imitári in terris; ut cum ipso exaltári mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the exaltation of the humble, who caused blessed Martin, Your confessor, to pass to the heavenly kingdom; grant by his merits and intercession that we may so imitate his humility on earth as to deserve to be exalted with him in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hanc hóstiam, Dómine, quam tibi in honórem beáti Martíni Confessóris sacrándam offérimus, benígnus súscipe: et præsta, ut eius pia intercessióne, nobis efféctum tuæ salvatiónis impéndat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously receive, O Lord, this victim which we offer to be consecrated to You in honor of blessed Martin, Your confessor; and grant that through his loving intercession it may bring us the effect of Your salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cæléstibus aliméntis enutríti, súpplices te rogámus, Dómine Deus noster; ut beáto Martíno Confessóre pro nobis intercedénte, tuis semper valeámus obedíre mandátis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Nourished with heavenly food, we humbly beseech You, O Lord our God, that, blessed Martin, Your confessor, interceding for us, we may ever be able to obey Your commandments; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1106": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 616; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beatórum Mártyrum Hierónymi, Valentíni, Francísci, Hyacínthi et Sociórum sánguine fecundáre dignátus es: concéde propítius ut quorum læti recólimus triúmphos; eórum précibus ac méritis adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who were pleased to make Your Church fruitful by the blood of the blessed martyrs Jerome, Valentine, Francis, Hyacinth and their companions; mercifully grant that we who joyfully recall their triumphs may be helped by their prayers and merits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, Dómine quǽsumus, inténde placátus: ut intercedéntibus beátis Martýribus tuis devotióni nostræ profíciant et salúti. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously, O Lord, we beseech You, upon these present sacrifices; that through the intercession of Your blessed martyrs they may profit our devotion and our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut beatórum Mártyrum tuórum Hierónymi, Valentíni, Francísci, Hyacínthi atque Sociórum cæléstibus mystériis celebráta solémnitas; indulgéntiam nobis tuæ propitiatiónis acquírat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that the feast of Your blessed martyrs Jerome, Valentine, Francis, Hyacinth and their companions, celebrated with heavenly mysteries, may obtain for us the pardon of Your mercy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1119": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 625; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Tuórum corda fidélium Deus miserátor illústra: et beátæ Elísabeth précibus gloriósis, fac nos próspera mundi despícere; et cælésti semper consolatióne gaudére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Enlighten, O God of mercy, the hearts of Your faithful; and through the glorious prayers of blessed Elizabeth make us despise the prosperity of this world and ever rejoice in heavenly consolation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis offérimus: ut tibi grata, et nobis salutária, beátæ Elísabeth pia supplicatióne reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gifts of our devotion, that through the loving pleading of blessed Elizabeth they may become pleasing to You and salutary for us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut quos salutáribus dignátus es erudíre mystériis; beátæ Elísabeth intercessióne gloriósa, cæléstibus refícias aliméntis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that through the glorious intercession of blessed Elizabeth You would refresh with heavenly food those whom You have deigned to instruct by these saving mysteries; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1121": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 628; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Maríam semper Vírginem, Spíritus Sancti habitáculum hodiérna die in templo præsentári voluísti; præsta quǽsumus, ut eius intercessióne in templo glóriæ tuæ præsentári mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed Mary ever Virgin, the dwelling place of the Holy Spirit, should on this day be presented in the temple; grant, we beseech You, that through her intercession we may deserve to be presented in the temple of Your glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the same Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Unigéniti tui, Dómine, nobis succúrrat humánitas: ut qui natus de Vírgine, Matris integritátem non mínuit, sed sacrávit, in solemnitáte eius, nostris nos piáculis éxuens, oblatiónem nostram tibi fáciat accéptam: Iesus Christus Dóminus noster, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the humanity of Your only-begotten Son, O Lord, come to our aid; that He who, born of the Virgin, did not lessen but hallowed His Mother's integrity, may on her feast free us from our sins and make our offering acceptable to You, Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, celebritátis ánnuæ votíva sacraménta; præsta quǽsumus, ut et temporális vitæ nobis remédia prǽbeant, et ætérnæ: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the votive sacraments of this yearly feast; grant, we beseech You, that they may bring us remedies for this temporal life and for the life eternal; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1123": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 630; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos ánnua beáti Cleméntis Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis solemnitáte lætíficas: concéde propítius, ut cuius natalítia cólimus; virtútem quoque passiónis imitémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gladden us by the yearly feast of blessed Clement, Your martyr and bishop; mercifully grant that we who keep his heavenly birthday may also imitate the fortitude of his passion; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi Dómine obláta sanctífica: et intercedénte beáto Cleménte Mártyre tuo atque Pontífice, per hæc nos a peccatórum nostrórum máculis emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts offered to You; and through the intercession of blessed Clement, Your martyr and bishop, cleanse us by them from the stains of our sins; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Córporis sacri, et pretiósi Sánguinis repléti libámine, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut quod pia devotióne gérimus; intercedénte beáto Cleménte Mártyre tuo atque Pontífice, certa redemptióne capiámus: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with the offering of the sacred Body and precious Blood, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that what we perform with loving devotion we may, through the intercession of blessed Clement, Your martyr and bishop, receive as sure redemption; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1203": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 326; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Indiárum gentes beáti Francísci prædicatióne et miráculis Ecclésiæ tuæ aggregáre voluísti: concéde propítius, ut cuius gloriósa mérita venerámur; virtútum quoque imitémur exémpla: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed to gather the peoples of the Indies into Your Church by the preaching and miracles of blessed Francis; mercifully grant that we who venerate his glorious merits may also imitate the example of his virtues; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Francísco Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Francis, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0102b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 350; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Stéphanam Vírginem tuam, Crucifíxi amóre succénsam, eiúsdem passiónis consórtem mirabíliter effecísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut eius intercessióne et exémplo; imágini Fílii tui confórmes fíeri mereámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who wondrously made blessed Stephana, Your virgin, on fire with love of the Crucified, a sharer in His passion; grant, we beseech You, that by her intercession and example we may deserve to be conformed to the image of Your Son; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0116b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 354; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beáti Gundisálvi Confessóris tui mentem sancti nóminis tui amóre mirabíliter inflammásti: concéde quǽsumus, ut illíus vestígiis inhæréntes, semper te cogitémus; et quæ tibi grata sunt, inflammáto stúdio faciámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who wondrously inflamed the mind of blessed Gonsalvo, Your confessor, with love of Your holy name; grant, we beseech You, that clinging to his footsteps we may ever think of You, and do with burning zeal the things that are pleasing to You; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi Dómine hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus, et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, sacrifices of praise in commemoration of Your saints, through whom we trust to be delivered from evils both present and to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cælésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus; eius muniámur et précibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly food and drink, O our God, we humbly entreat You that we may also be defended by the prayers of him in whose commemoration we have received these gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0119b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 358; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, qui beátum Andréam Confessórem tuum apostólico spíritu decorásti: fac nos, eius imitatióne, ita verbo et exémplo profícere; ut úberem fructum inde reférre valeámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, who adorned blessed Andrew, Your confessor, with an apostolic spirit; grant that by imitating him we may so advance in word and example as to bring forth abundant fruit; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Andréa Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Andrew, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0124b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 362; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, cui humílium et mansuetórum semper plácuit deprecátio: fac nos beáti Marcolíni précibus et exémplis ita profícere; ut vere mites et húmiles corde effécti, facílius tua dona capiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, to whom the prayer of the humble and meek has always been pleasing; grant that we may so profit by the prayers and example of blessed Marcolinus that, made truly meek and humble of heart, we may the more readily receive Your gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Marcolíno Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Marcolinus, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0130b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 368; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Maríam, tuæ grátiæ ubertáte prævéntam, contemplatiónis dono, et exímia in próximum caritáte mirábilem effecísti: ex eius nobis imitatióne concéde; ut cæléstia meditántes, et áliis misericórdiam exhibéntes, ætérnam glóriam cum ipsa cónsequi mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, preventing blessed Mary with the abundance of Your grace, made her wonderful by the gift of contemplation and by surpassing charity toward her neighbor; grant us by imitating her that, meditating on heavenly things and showing mercy to others, we may deserve to attain eternal glory with her; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Miserátio tua Deus, interveniénte beáta María, ómnium peccatórum máculas in nobis cleménter abstérgat: ut purificáti mente et córpore, hóstiam sanctam tibi digne offerámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your mercy, O God, through the intercession of blessed Mary, graciously wipe away in us the stains of all our sins; that, purified in mind and body, we may worthily offer You the holy victim; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo cælésti, ac amóris sacraménto recreáti, súpplices te Dómine deprecámur: ut per mérita beátæ Maríæ corda nostra a terrénis desidériis expédias; et tuæ caritátis igne succéndas: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Fed with heavenly food and refreshed by the sacrament of love, we humbly beseech You, O Lord, that through the merits of blessed Mary You would free our hearts from earthly desires and kindle them with the fire of Your charity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0216b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 384; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Spíritum nobis beáti Nicolái Confessóris tui, Deus, benígnus infúnde: ut sicut illum in prædicatióne verbi tui, ac in procuránda proximórum salúte, singulári grátia decorásti; ipsíus précibus fácias nos in eádem vocatióne sancta fírmiter permanére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously pour into us, O God, the spirit of blessed Nicholas, Your confessor; that, as You adorned him with singular grace in preaching Your word and in procuring the salvation of his neighbors, so by his prayers You may make us remain steadfast in the same holy calling; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sanctífica, quǽsumus Dómine, munus oblátum: et beáti Nicolái méritis et exémplis digna hóstia misericórditer effécti, simus semper in corde férvidi, et in ópere efficáces. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, we beseech You, O Lord, the gift offered; and, mercifully made a worthy victim by the merits and example of blessed Nicholas, may we ever be fervent in heart and effective in deed; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Hæc nos commúnio, Dómine, sacri múneris partícipes effíciat: et beáti Nicolái Confessóris tui vestígiis iúgiter insisténtes; mereámur páriter cum ipso in cælis coronári: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this communion, O Lord, make us partakers of the sacred gift; and, ever following in the footsteps of blessed Nicholas, Your confessor, may we deserve to be crowned with him in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0219b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 386; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Alvarum Confessórem tuum caritátis et pœniténtiæ donis insígniter decorásti: da ut eius intercessióne et exémplo, semper Christi mortificatiónem in córpore; et tui amórem in corde gerámus: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who signally adorned blessed Alvarez, Your confessor, with the gifts of charity and penance; grant that by his intercession and example we may ever bear the mortification of Christ in our body and the love of You in our heart; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Alvaro Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Alvarez, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0301b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 388; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Christóphorum Confessórem dignum tibi fámulum reddidísti: eius méritis et imitatióne concéde; ut Christum in nobis tota mentis intentióne, et cordis afféctu portáre valeámus: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Christopher, Your confessor, a worthy servant to You; grant by his merits and imitation that we may be able to bear Christ within us with the whole intent of our mind and the affection of our heart; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, quǽsumus Dómine, quam tibi in honórem beáti Christóphori Confessóris offérimus, in nostræ provéniat salútis auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this victim, we beseech You, O Lord, which we offer You in honor of blessed Christopher, Your confessor, avail for the help of our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Salutári cibo refécti, te Dómine deprecámur: ut beáto Christóphoro pro nobis intercedénte; ad cæléste convívium nos perdúcere dignéris: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with saving food, we entreat You, O Lord, that, blessed Christopher interceding for us, You would deign to lead us to the heavenly banquet; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0322b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 400; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens, ætérne Deus, qui sapiéntiæ tuæ luce, ténebras ignorántiæ repéllis: auge méritis et précibus beáti Isnárdi Confessóris tui, virtútem fídei; ut ignis, quem grátia tua fecit accéndi, nullis tentatiónibus exstinguátur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, who by the light of Your wisdom dispel the darkness of ignorance; through the merits and prayers of blessed Isnard, Your confessor, increase the strength of our faith, that the fire which Your grace has kindled may be quenched by no temptations; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrándum Tibi Dómine munus offérimus, quo beáti Isnárdi fidélis servi tui mérita recoléntes: purificatiónem quoque nostris méntibus implorámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gift to be consecrated, by which, recalling the merits of blessed Isnard, Your faithful servant, we also implore purification for our minds; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut reátum nostrum múnera sancta puríficent; et intercedénte beáto Isnárdo, Confessóre tuo, recte vivéndi nobis operéntur efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that the holy gifts may cleanse our guilt, and, through the intercession of blessed Isnard, Your confessor, bring about in us the effect of right living; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0323b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 400; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátæ Sibyllínæ Vírginis, corporálibus lumínibus orbátæ, mentem admirábili claritátis fulgóre illustráre voluísti: eius intercessióne nobis concéde, ut supérna luce illumináti terréna despiciámus; et ætérna efficáciter exquirámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed to enlighten with the wondrous brightness of Your light the mind of blessed Sibyllina, Your virgin, deprived of bodily sight; grant us through her intercession that, enlightened by the light from above, we may despise the things of earth and effectively seek the things eternal; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe Dómine oblatiónem, quam tibi offérimus, et interveniénte beáta Sibyllína, præsta, ut sicut ipsa passiónis Fílii tui mystéria in terris devóte est veneráta, ita nos eórum fructum cónsequi mereámur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, the offering we make to You, and through the intercession of blessed Sibyllina grant that, as she devoutly venerated on earth the mysteries of Your Son's passion, so we may deserve to obtain their fruit; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Percépta, Dómine, tui Córporis et Sánguinis mystéria; per intercessiónem beátæ Sibyllínæ nos reddant in virtútum opéribus efficáces, et in tuo amóre fervéntes: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the mysteries of Your Body and Blood which we have received, O Lord, through the intercession of blessed Sibyllina make us effective in works of virtue and fervent in Your love; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0409b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 410; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ad unitátem fídei promovéndam, beáto António Mártyri tuo invíctam ánimi fortitúdinem contulísti: da nobis, quǽsumus, ita eius vestígia sectári; ut finem fídei nostræ, salútem animárum reportémus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who for the furthering of the unity of the faith bestowed on blessed Anthony, Your martyr, an unconquered strength of soul; grant us, we beseech You, so to follow in his footsteps that we may obtain the end of our faith, the salvation of our souls; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícium, Dómine, quod tibi in honórem beáti Antónii Mártyris offérimus, benígnus admítte: ut Ecclésiam tuam ab omni éruas hæreticórum nequítia, et in tuæ protectiónis securitáte constítuas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously accept, O Lord, the sacrifice which we offer You in honor of blessed Anthony, Your martyr, that You may deliver Your Church from all the wickedness of heretics and establish her in the safety of Your protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Dómine Iesu, qui beátum Antónium cælésti hac mensa ad martýrii certámen roborásti: eius intercessióne da nobis in eiúsdem cibi fortitúdine omnes salútis hostes superáre; et ad ætérna gáudia felíciter perveníre: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus, who at this heavenly table strengthened blessed Anthony for the contest of martyrdom; grant us by his intercession, in the strength of the same food, to overcome all the enemies of our salvation and happily to come to eternal joys; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0413b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 411; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Margarítam Vírginem lumínibus orbam nasci voluísti; ut intus illumináto cordis óculo, te solum assídue contemplarétur: esto lumen oculórum nostrórum, quo mundi huius ténebris carére valeámus; et perveniámus ad pátriam claritátis ætérnæ: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed Margaret, Your virgin, should be born without sight, so that, the eye of her heart being enlightened within, she might contemplate You alone without ceasing; be the light of our eyes, by which we may be free from the darkness of this world and come to the homeland of eternal brightness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0414b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 411; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui in maris perículis constitútis beáti Petri opem singulárem osténdis: eius nobis intercessióne concéde, ut in huius vitæ procéllis tuæ grátiæ lumen semper affúlgeat; quo ætérnæ salútis portum inveníre valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who show the singular help of blessed Peter to those placed in the perils of the sea; grant us through his intercession that in the storms of this life the light of Your grace may ever shine upon us, by which we may be able to find the haven of eternal salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Propitiáre nobis Deus noster: ut quos salutáribus réficis sacraméntis, intercessióne beáti Petri Confessóris tui, iungas agmínibus Beatórum. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be merciful to us, O our God, that through the intercession of blessed Peter, Your confessor, You may join to the ranks of the blessed those whom You refresh with saving sacraments; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Corda nostra, quǽsumus Dómine, lúmine tuæ claritátis illústra: ut verbo salútis erudíti, interveniénte beáto Petro Confessóre tuo, nóxia cuncta vitémus; et quæ recta sunt, ágere valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Enlighten our hearts, we beseech You, O Lord, with the light of Your brightness; that, taught by the word of salvation, through the intercession of blessed Peter, Your confessor, we may avoid all that is harmful and be able to do what is right; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0417b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 412; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Tríbue nobis, miséricors Deus, spíritum oratiónis et pœniténtiæ: ut beátæ Claræ vestígiis inhæréntes; mereámur, quam ipsa in cælis accépit, corónam obtinére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, merciful God, the spirit of prayer and penance; that, clinging to the footsteps of blessed Clare, we may deserve to obtain the crown which she has received in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, qui per unigénitum Fílium tuum in ara crucis mundum redímere voluísti: concéde, ut dum ipsum immolámus, per mérita beátæ Claræ ætérnæ salvatiónis nostræ fidúcia roborémur. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed to redeem the world through Your only-begotten Son on the altar of the cross; grant that while we offer Him in sacrifice, we may, through the merits of blessed Clare, be strengthened in the confidence of our eternal salvation; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui dignátus es huius spirituális convívii partícipes nos fíeri: per intercessiónem beátæ Claræ da nobis ita vívere; ut ad ætérnum perveníre valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who have deigned to make us partakers of this spiritual banquet; grant us through the intercession of blessed Clare so to live that we may be able to attain to the eternal banquet; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0422b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 415; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Bartholomǽum insígnem fídei propugnatórem effecísti; et martýrii coróna sublimásti: da nobis eius méritis et intercessióne crucem iúgiter ferre; ut cum ipso glóriæ tuæ mereámur esse partícipes: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Bartholomew a renowned champion of the faith and exalted him with the crown of martyrdom; grant us by his merits and intercession ever to bear the cross, that with him we may deserve to be sharers of Your glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblatiónem nostram, clementíssime Iesu, beáti Bartholomǽi intercéssio sancta comméndet: qui fide et caritáte suffúltus, ánimam suam propter te et Evangélium non tímuit pérdere, ut vitam ætérnam inveníret. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O most merciful Jesus, may the holy intercession of blessed Bartholomew commend our offering to You, who, upheld by faith and charity, feared not to lose his life for You and for the Gospel, that he might find life eternal; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Puríficet nos, quǽsumus Dómine, divíni sacraménti munus oblátum: et intercedénte beáto Bartholomǽo Mártyre: in tuæ veritátis luce confírmet: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the gift of the divine sacrament which has been offered purify us, we beseech You, O Lord, and through the intercession of blessed Bartholomew, martyr, strengthen us in the light of Your truth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0426b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 418; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, cuius misericórdiæ non est númerus: te humíliter deprecámur; ut intercedéntibus beátis Domínico et Gregório Confessóribus tuis, a peccatórum nostrórum póndere subdúcti, glóriam ab ipsis obténtam assequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, whose mercies are without number, we humbly beseech You that, through the intercession of blessed Dominic and Gregory, Your confessors, being freed from the burden of our sins, we may attain the glory which they have obtained; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblatiónem, Dómine, quam tibi offérimus, propítius réspice, et méritis beatórum Domínici et Gregórii præsta, ut nosmetípsos tibi hóstiam acceptábilem exhibeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously, O Lord, upon the offering which we make to You, and through the merits of blessed Dominic and Gregory grant that we may present ourselves to You as an acceptable victim; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut sacra mystéria, quæ súmpsimus; per intercessiónem beatórum Domínici et Gregórii sint nobis secúrum contra ómnia mala futúra præsídium: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord our God, that the sacred mysteries which we have received may, through the intercession of blessed Dominic and Gregory, be for us a sure defense against all evils to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0512b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 440; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui inter regáles delícias, et mundi illécebras beátam Ioánnam Vírginem tuam virtúte constántiæ roborásti: quǽsumus, ut eius intercessióne fidéles tui terréna despíciant; et ad cæléstia semper aspírent: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who amid the delights of a royal court and the allurements of the world strengthened blessed Joan, Your virgin, with the virtue of constancy; grant, we beseech You, that through her intercession Your faithful may despise the things of earth and ever aspire to the things of heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0514b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 442; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Misericórdiam tuam, Deus, súpplices implorámus: ut sicut ea præveniénte beátum Ægídium in viam iustítiæ et sanctitátis redíre fecísti; ita nos e servitúte ac morte peccáti, in perféctam tránsferas libertátem et vitam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We humbly implore Your mercy, O God, that as by its prevenient grace You caused blessed Giles to return to the way of justice and holiness, so You would bring us out of the slavery and death of sin into perfect freedom and life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Ægídio Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Giles, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0517b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 444; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beáto Andréæ Confessóri tuo Evangélium pacis ópere ac sermóne prædicáre tribuísti: eius quǽsumus intercessióne, fac nos legem tuam corde perfécto suscípere; et sanctis móribus adimplére. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who granted to blessed Andrew, Your confessor, to preach the Gospel of peace in deed and word; through his intercession, we beseech You, make us receive Your law with a perfect heart and fulfil it by holy living; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Concéde sanctíssime Pater, ut immaculátam Hóstiam tibi digne libémus; quam beátus Andréas puris mánibus immolábat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, most holy Father, that we may worthily offer to You the spotless Victim which blessed Andrew used to sacrifice with pure hands; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Córporis et Sánguinis tui Sacraméntum, quǽsumus Dómine, ab omni nos labe puríficet: et intercedénte beáto Andréa Confessóre tuo; sanctitátem iúgiter in nobis operétur. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the Sacrament of Your Body and Blood, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse us from every stain, and through the intercession of blessed Andrew, Your confessor, ever work holiness in us; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0520b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 449; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Colúmbam Vírginem tuam, puritáte et innocéntia cándidam, supérnis fulgóribus illustráre dignátus es: concéde quǽsumus, ut eius intercessióne, puris tibi méntibus serviéntes in terris; splendóre glóriæ tuæ pérfrui mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who deigned to enlighten with heavenly splendors blessed Columba, Your virgin, shining white with purity and innocence; grant, we beseech You, that by her intercession, serving You with pure minds on earth, we may deserve to enjoy the splendor of Your glory in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0528b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 454; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Amátor animárum Deus, qui in beáta María Bartholomǽa Vírgine tua, miram ægritúdinum tolerántiam pari cum innocéntia sociásti: concéde, ut qui ex mérito nostræ actiónis afflígimur; tuæ grátiæ consolatióne respirémus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, lover of souls, who in blessed Mary Bartholomew, Your virgin, joined a wondrous endurance of sickness with equal innocence; grant that we who are afflicted by the desert of our deeds may breathe again in the consolation of Your grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Panem Angelórum, et vinum gérminans vírgines, offeréntes tibi Dómine, beáta María Bartholomǽa Vírgine intercedénte, a sórdibus líbera: ut inter puras Angelórum ácies perpétuo collocári mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Offering You, O Lord, the Bread of Angels and the wine that brings forth virgins, through the intercession of blessed Mary Bartholomew, Your virgin, free us from all defilement, that we may deserve to be placed for ever among the pure ranks of the Angels; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Effúnde super nos, Dómine Iesu, grátiam tuæ miseratiónis: et præsta, ut intercedénte beáta María Bartholomǽa Vírgine tua, ab ómnibus adversitátibus liberémur; et in tuo servítio perseverántes, ad ætérnam perveníre lætítiam valeámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Pour forth upon us, O Lord Jesus, the grace of Your mercy, and grant that, through the intercession of blessed Mary Bartholomew, Your virgin, we may be delivered from all adversities, and, persevering in Your service, may be able to attain eternal joy; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0530b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 455; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus qui beátum Andréam Confessórem atque Pontíficem in prædicatióne verbi tui et in múnere boni pastóris pietáte ac doctrína excéllere voluísti: eius intercessióne nobis concéde, ut animóse in tuo sancto servítio certántes; copiósum fructum inde reférre mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed Andrew, Your confessor and bishop, should excel in piety and learning in the preaching of Your word and in the office of a good shepherd; grant us through his intercession that, striving courageously in Your holy service, we may deserve to bring forth abundant fruit; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Per hanc immaculátam hóstiam súpplices te deprecámur, Dómine, ut intercedénte beáto Andréa, nosmetípsos hóstiam tibi placéntem offérre valeámus. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through this spotless victim we humbly entreat You, O Lord, that through the intercession of blessed Andrew we may be able to offer ourselves to You as a pleasing victim; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Pretiósi Córporis et Sánguinis tui suscéptio, Dómine, tantam nobis virtútem adiíciat; ut beáti Andréæ suffrágiis et exémplis, tuæ divínæ voluntáti nos semper congruéntes efficiámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the reception of Your precious Body and Blood, O Lord, add such strength to us that, by the prayers and example of blessed Andrew, we may ever be made conformable to Your divine will; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0605b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 460; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos beáti Iacóbi Confessóris tui ánnua solemnitáte lætíficas: concéde propítius, ut cuius natalítia cólimus; étiam actiónes imitémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gladden us by the yearly feast of blessed James, Your confessor; mercifully grant that we who keep his heavenly birthday may also imitate his deeds; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi Dómine hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus, et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, sacrifices of praise in commemoration of Your saints, through whom we trust to be delivered from evils both present and to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cælésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus; eius muniámur et précibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly food and drink, O our God, we humbly entreat You that we may also be defended by the prayers of him in whose commemoration we have received these gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0612b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 465; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ad errántes fidéles in viam salútis revocándos, beátum Stéphanum Confessórem tuum evangélicæ prædicatiónis exímium minístrum effecísti: eius méritis et intercessióne concéde; ut a peccátis ómnibus expedíti, sémitam mandatórum tuórum semper currámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, to call back wandering believers to the way of salvation, made blessed Stephen, Your confessor, an outstanding minister of Gospel preaching; grant by his merits and intercession that, set free from all sins, we may ever run the path of Your commandments; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accipe clementíssime Deus múnera tibi reverénter obláta, et qui per beátum Stéphanum Confessórem tuum multos errántes in viam iustítiæ et sanctitátis redíre fecísti, nostras étiam rebélles ad te propítius convérte voluntátes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, most merciful God, the gifts reverently offered to You; and, You who through blessed Stephen, Your confessor, caused many who were straying to return to the way of justice and holiness, mercifully turn our rebellious wills also to You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ineffabílibus recreáti sacraméntis, quǽsumus cleméntiam tuam omnípotens Deus: ut qui beáti Stéphani Confessóris tui præclára mérita celebrámus; eius intercessióne, ætérna gáudia, his mystériis promíssa, consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by ineffable sacraments, we beseech Your mercy, almighty God, that we who celebrate the illustrious merits of blessed Stephen, Your confessor, may through his intercession attain the eternal joys promised in these mysteries; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0723b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 504; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátæ Ioánnæ Vírginis tuæ puritátem exímiam, et férvidam caritátem donis cæléstibus cumulásti: fac nos ita eius æmulári virtútes; ut castitáte vitæ, ac puris semper tibi placeámus afféctibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who heaped heavenly gifts upon the surpassing purity and fervent charity of blessed Joan, Your virgin; make us so emulate her virtues that by chastity of life and purity of affection we may ever be pleasing to You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0724b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 504; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus Dómine Iesu, beáti Augustíni Confessóris tui méritis et imitatióne, ita carnis desidéria per pœniténtiam exstínguere; ut in tua semper grátia et cognitióne crescámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord Jesus, by the merits and imitation of blessed Augustine, Your confessor, so to quench the desires of the flesh by penance that we may ever grow in Your grace and knowledge; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Fac nos omnípotens Deus, immaculátam hóstiam eo tibi accénsæ devotiónis afféctu sacráre, quo beátus Conféssor tuus Augustínus in ea immolánda flagrábat: ut digne maiestáti tuæ serviéntes, optáta indulgéntiæ tuæ múnera consequámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, almighty God, to consecrate the spotless victim to You with that affection of burning devotion with which blessed Augustine, Your confessor, glowed in offering it; that, serving Your majesty worthily, we may obtain the longed-for gifts of Your pardon; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Angelórum pane reféctos, clementíssime Deus, éxcitent nos iúgiter beáti Augustíni Confessóris tui salutária exémpla, et pia intercéssio: ut infinítam bonitátem tuam usque ad mortem laudáre; ac perfécta tandem caritáte, perenníque cántico in cælis prósequi valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with the bread of Angels, most merciful God, may the saving example and loving intercession of blessed Augustine, Your confessor, ever rouse us to praise Your infinite goodness until death, and at last, in perfect charity, to continue that praise in an everlasting song in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0728b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 507; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Antónium Confessórem tuum divíno amóre inflammásti: accénde quǽsumus, eo intercedénte, in córdibus nostris ignem tuæ caritátis; ut te diligéntes in terris, gáudiis ætérnis perfruámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who set blessed Anthony, Your confessor, on fire with divine love; kindle in our hearts, we beseech You, through his intercession, the fire of Your charity, that loving You on earth we may enjoy eternal joys in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Per hæc sacra dona, quæ offérimus, tuére Dómine fámulos tuos: et quos beáti Antónii glória lætíficat, fac tibi mente et córpore devótos. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through these sacred gifts which we offer, O Lord, protect Your servants; and those whom the glory of blessed Anthony gladdens, make devoted to You in mind and body; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Córporis et Sánguinis tui mystério refécti, quǽsumus Dómine: ut cum beáto António connumerémur in pátria; cuius exémplis ad te pertráhimur in via: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by the mystery of Your Body and Blood, we beseech You, O Lord, that we may be numbered in the homeland with blessed Anthony, by whose example we are drawn to You on the way; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0803b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 515; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiæ tuæ in beáto Augustíno Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice boni pastóris exémplum providére dignátus es: concéde propítius; ut eius intercessióne, in loco páscuæ tuæ perpétuo collocári mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who were pleased to provide for Your Church in blessed Augustine, Your confessor and bishop, the example of a good shepherd; mercifully grant that through his intercession we may deserve to be placed for ever in the place of Your pasture; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sit in conspéctu tuo Dómine nostra devótio: ut eius nobis fiat supplicatióne salutáris, pro cuius solemnitáte defértur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our devotion be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, and may it become salutary for us through the pleading of him on whose feast it is offered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, fidélibus tuis, Sanctórum tuórum semper veneratióne lætári; et eórum perpétua supplicatióne muníri: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, to Your faithful ever to rejoice in the veneration of Your saints, and to be defended by their unceasing intercession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0811b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 522; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui in fídei increméntum, beátum Ioánnem Confessórem verbi tui præcónem exímium effecísti: eius nobis intercessióne largíre, ut quod corde crédimus ad iustítiam; ore ad salútem confiteámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who for the increase of the faith made blessed John, Your confessor, an outstanding herald of Your word; grant us through his intercession that what we believe with the heart unto justice we may confess with the mouth unto salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Ioánne Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed John, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0818b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 534; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens et miséricors Deus, cui servíre regnáre est: per mérita et intercessiónem beáti Aimónis Confessóris tui, quem exímium fídei propugnatórem effecísti, concéde; ut mandátis tuis fidéliter serviéntes in terris, ætérno regno pérfrui cum ipso mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and merciful God, whom to serve is to reign; through the merits and intercession of blessed Aimo, Your confessor, whom You made an outstanding champion of the faith, grant that, faithfully serving Your commandments on earth, we may deserve to enjoy the eternal kingdom with him in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátis Dómine placáre munéribus, et intercedénte beáto Aimóne Confessóre tuo, omnipoténtem déxteram ad defensiónem Ecclésiæ tuæ cleménter exténde: ut destrúctis adversitátibus et erróribus univérsis, optáta fídei unitáte, et pace lætétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, O Lord, by the gifts we offer, and through the intercession of blessed Aimo, Your confessor, mercifully stretch forth Your almighty right hand to defend Your Church; that, all adversities and errors being destroyed, she may rejoice in the longed-for unity of faith and in peace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Dómine Iesu pastor bone, qui ad unitátem Ecclésiæ tuæ promovéndam, omnes oves tuas uníus cæléstis convívii partícipes esse voluísti: præsta quǽsumus; ut beáti Aimónis Confessóris tui interveniéntibus méritis, una sit semper in grege tuo fides méntium, et píetas actiónum: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus, good Shepherd, who for the furthering of the unity of Your Church willed all Your sheep to be partakers of the one heavenly banquet; grant, we beseech You, that through the pleading merits of blessed Aimo, Your confessor, there may ever be in Your flock one faith of minds and one devotion of deeds; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0823b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 537; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui prodigiósa tui Sánguinis aspersióne dignátus es beátum Iacóbum Confessórem secúra ætérnæ salútis fidúcia roboráre: diláta super nos eádem víscera misericórdiæ tuæ; ut redemptiónis nostræ imbúti signáculo, inter oves déxteræ tuæ perpétuo computémur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the wondrous sprinkling of Your Blood deigned to strengthen blessed James, Your confessor, with sure confidence of eternal salvation; open wide over us the same tender mercy, that, marked with the seal of our redemption, we may be numbered for ever among the sheep at Your right hand; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi Dómine hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus, et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, sacrifices of praise in commemoration of Your saints, through whom we trust to be delivered from evils both present and to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cælésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus; eius muniámur et précibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly food and drink, O our God, we humbly entreat You that we may also be defended by the prayers of him in whose commemoration we have received these gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0904b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 550; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Spes nostra Dómine, qui beátæ Catharínæ cor teípso plenum, cæléstium donórum abundántia decorásti: tantæ Vírginis intercessióne concéde, ut totus nobis figátur in corde; qui totus pro nobis fixus fuit in cruce: Dóminus noster Iesus Christus Fílius tuus; qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord our hope, who adorned with the abundance of heavenly gifts the heart of blessed Catherine, filled with Yourself; grant through the intercession of so great a virgin that He may be wholly fixed in our hearts who for us was wholly fixed to the cross, our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Non ignári, Dómine, vitiórum nostrórum, audémus ad treméndam Agni tui mensam accédere, Catharínæ sponsæ eius meritórum recordatióne suffúlti: ne repéllas, quǽsumus, suspirántium desidéria animárum, sed præsénti oblatióne ac solemnitáte placátus, tam mirándæ fac nos partícipes sanctitátis. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Not unaware, O Lord, of our sins, we dare to approach the awesome table of Your Lamb, upheld by the remembrance of the merits of Catherine, His bride; reject not, we beseech You, the desires of sighing souls, but, appeased by the present offering and feast, make us partakers of so wonderful a holiness; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Dómine Iesu, panis vitæ, qui Catharínæ Vírgini tuæ indeficiéntis dulcédinis épulas in hac mensa ministrásti: indúlge nobis míseris; ut de micis e tanta ubertáte cadéntibus saturémur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus, bread of life, who at this table served Your virgin Catherine with a feast of unfailing sweetness; be merciful to us wretched sinners, that we may be filled with the crumbs that fall from so great an abundance; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0905b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 550; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ad plebem tuam in pace et pietáte firmándam, beátum Guálam Confessórem ac Pontíficem singulári grátia decorásti: eius nobis intercessióne concéde, ut pacis stúdia operóse sectántes; úberes pietátis fructus percipiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, to establish Your people in peace and piety, adorned blessed Guala, Your confessor and bishop, with singular grace; grant us through his intercession that, zealously pursuing peace, we may gather abundant fruits of piety; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Huius immaculátæ hóstiæ oblatióne, et intercessióne beáti Guálæ Confessóris tui, Dómine, tuæ nobis pacis dona largíre. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through the offering of this spotless victim and the intercession of blessed Guala, Your confessor, O Lord, bestow on us the gifts of Your peace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Pane vitæ refécti, te Dómine deprecámur: ut intercedénte beáto Guála Pontífice et Confessóre, ita nos fácias iúgiter vívere; ut in éxitu nostro ad te ascéndere valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with the bread of life, we entreat You, O Lord, that through the intercession of blessed Guala, bishop and confessor, You would make us so to live always that at our departure we may be able to ascend to You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0923b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 568; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui per beátum Marcum Confessórem tuum, permúltos errántes in viam iustítiæ redíre fecísti: concéde, ut eius intercessióne nos quoque a vítiis absolúti; ad ætérna gáudia perveníre felíciter valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who through blessed Mark, Your confessor, caused very many who were straying to return to the way of justice; grant that through his intercession we also, set free from our vices, may happily be able to attain eternal joys; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, clementíssime Dómine, hanc immaculátam hóstiam: et per mérita beáti Marci Confessóris tui, víscera misericórdiæ tuæ super nos effúndere dignéris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, most merciful Lord, this spotless victim, and through the merits of blessed Mark, Your confessor, deign to pour forth upon us the tender depths of Your mercy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Angelórum pane refécti, concéde quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Marci Confessóris tui mónita et exémpla sectémur; ac assídua crucis meditatióne muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with the bread of Angels, grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we may follow the counsels and example of blessed Mark, Your confessor, and be fortified by constant meditation on the cross; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0926b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 569; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui húmilem fámulum tuum Dalmátium multis signis atque virtútibus decorásti; ac mirabíliter in tuo amóre, spretis temporálibus, inflammásti: tríbue nobis, quǽsumus; ut eius intercessióne, a terrénis afféctibus expedíti, et a cunctis adversitátibus liberáti, sola cæléstia appetámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who adorned Your humble servant Dalmatius with many signs and virtues, and, earthly things being despised, wondrously inflamed him with Your love; grant us, we beseech You, that through his intercession, freed from earthly affections and delivered from all adversities, we may seek heavenly things alone; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Dalmátio Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Dalmatius, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1011b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 588; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Iacóbum Confessórem tuum, humilitátis et obediéntiæ virtúte mirabíliter decorásti: eius intercessióne fac nos terréna despícere; et mandátis tuis iúgiter inhærére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who wondrously adorned blessed James, Your confessor, with the virtue of humility and obedience; through his intercession make us despise the things of earth and ever cleave to Your commandments; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátis Dómine placáre munéribus: et beáti Iacóbi Confessóris tui intercessióne concéde, ut cæléstia dona digne suscipiéntes, promíssa humílibus prǽmia cónsequi mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, O Lord, by the gifts we offer, and through the intercession of blessed James, Your confessor, grant that, worthily receiving the heavenly gifts, we may deserve to obtain the rewards promised to the humble; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Panis Angelórum, quo facis nos esse partícipes: Dómine, súpplices exorámus; ut per beáti Iacóbi mérita, sit nobis salútis ætérnæ indefíciens spes, ac secúra fruítio: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We humbly entreat You, O Lord, that the Bread of Angels, of which You make us partakers, may through the merits of blessed James be for us an unfailing hope and a secure enjoyment of eternal salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1013b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 589; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui néminem in te sperántem déseris; et pie deprecántem misericórditer exáudis; tríbue quǽsumus, ut quod nostris méritis non valémus; beátæ Magdalénæ Vírginis patrocínio consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who forsake no one who hopes in You and mercifully hear those who devoutly pray; grant, we beseech You, that what we cannot obtain by our own merits we may obtain through the patronage of blessed Magdalen, Your virgin; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, Dómine, quam ante thronum divínæ tuæ maiestátis offérimus, per beátam Vírginem Magdalénam propitiatória nobis reddátur, et ad cæléstia dona iúgiter promerénda idóneos nos reddat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this victim, O Lord, which we offer before the throne of Your divine majesty, be made propitiatory for us through the blessed virgin Magdalen, and render us fit ever to merit heavenly gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacra múnera suscépta a futúris nos trahant excéssibus: et beátæ Magdalénæ Vírginis intercessióne gloriósa; Divínæ partícipes natúræ efféctos, tríbuant esse in corde férvidos, et in ópere efficáces: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacred gifts we have received draw us away from future excesses, and, through the glorious intercession of blessed Magdalen, Your virgin, may they make us, who have been made partakers of the divine nature, fervent in heart and effective in deed; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1021b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 594; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui fidéles tuos memorántes novíssima, nunquam peccatúros prænuntiásti: fac nos beáti Petri Confessóris tui précibus et exémplis, ita temporálem mortem mente recólere; ut iúgiter admíssa peccáta flentes, vitémus ætérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who foretold that Your faithful who remember their last end would never sin; grant us, through the prayers and example of blessed Peter, Your confessor, so to meditate on temporal death that, ever weeping for the sins we have committed, we may escape eternal death; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Petro Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Peter, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1023b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 595; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui in fídei hóstibus ab errórum ténebris ad veritátis lucem adducéndis, et in pópulis ad pacem et concórdiam revocándis, beátum Bartholomǽum Confessórem tuum atque Pontíficem mirábilem effecísti: eius intercessióne concéde; ut pax tua, quæ exsúperat omnem sensum, custódiat corda nostra et intelligéntias nostras in Christo Iesu Dómino nostro: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Bartholomew, Your confessor and bishop, wonderful in leading the enemies of the faith from the darkness of error to the light of truth, and in recalling peoples to peace and concord; grant through his intercession that Your peace, which surpasses all understanding, may keep our hearts and minds in Christ Jesus our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sit in conspéctu tuo Dómine nostra devótio: ut eius nobis fiat supplicatióne salutáris, pro cuius solemnitáte defértur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our devotion be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, and may it become salutary for us through the pleading of him on whose feast it is offered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, fidélibus tuis, Sanctórum tuórum semper veneratióne lætári; et eórum perpétua supplicatióne muníri: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, to Your faithful ever to rejoice in the veneration of Your saints, and to be defended by their unceasing intercession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1026b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 597; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui fidélium salúti procurándæ, beátum Damiánum Confessórem tuum, et mira dicéndi vi, et virtútibus decorásti: præsta quǽsumus, ut eius intercessióne et exémplo; veram caritátem verbo et ópere exhibeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, for procuring the salvation of the faithful, adorned blessed Damian, Your confessor, both with a wondrous power of speech and with virtues; grant, we beseech You, that by his intercession and example we may show true charity in word and deed; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe Dómine hanc hóstiam, quam tibi immolámus: et méritis beáti Damiáni Confessóris tui præsta, ut sicut ipse se tibi in sacrifícium óbtulit, ita nos ad te omnes afféctus cordis dirigámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, this victim which we offer to You, and by the merits of blessed Damian, Your confessor, grant that, as he offered himself to You in sacrifice, so we may direct all the affections of our heart to You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraméntum Córporis et Sánguinis tui, Dómine, quod súmpsimus, sit fragilitátis nostræ subsídium: ut beátum Damiánum Confessórem tuum imitántes; viam mandatórum tuórum currámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the Sacrament of Your Body and Blood, O Lord, which we have received, be the support of our frailty; that, imitating blessed Damian, Your confessor, we may run the way of Your commandments; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1030b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 600; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Grátiam nobis, Dómine, pœniténtiæ, oratiónis, et humilitátis infúnde: ut beátæ Benvenútæ Vírginis imitatióne possímus, et carnem mortificántes, spíritu vívere; et cæléstia iúgiter cogitántes, nosque despiciéntes, in te solo Deo réquiem et glóriam inveníre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Pour into us, O Lord, the grace of penance, prayer and humility; that by imitating blessed Benvenuta, Your virgin, we may be able, mortifying the flesh, to live by the spirit, and, ever thinking on heavenly things and despising ourselves, to find rest and glory in You alone, our God; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1103b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 614; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Simónem Confessórem tuum inter céteras eius virtútes iugi orándi stúdio, et singulári humilitátis prærogatíva decorásti; ipsum nobis imitári concéde: ut spretis ómnibus, quæ sunt mundi, te hic solum quǽrere; ac tandem promíssa in cælis humílibus prǽmia cónsequi valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, among his other virtues, adorned blessed Simon, Your confessor, with unceasing zeal for prayer and the singular privilege of humility; grant us to imitate him, that, despising all things of the world, we may seek You alone here, and at last be able to obtain the rewards promised in heaven to the humble; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Simóne Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Simon, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1107b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 616; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beáto Petro fámulo tuo misericórditer tribuísti pro veræ fídei defensióne martýrio coronári: eius méritis et intercessióne concéde; ut fide, quæ per caritátem operátur, tibi iúgiter placére valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who mercifully granted to blessed Peter, Your servant, to be crowned with martyrdom for the defense of the true faith; grant by his merits and intercession that we may ever be able to please You by the faith that works through charity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícium tibi, Dómine, laudis et gratiárum actiónis offeréntes pro victória beáti Petri Mártyris tui, supplíciter deprecámur imménsam bonitátem tuam, ut fidélem pópulum in sancta religióne consérves, et hærética fraude dispérsos ad veritátis tuæ révoces unitátem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Offering You, O Lord, the sacrifice of praise and thanksgiving for the victory of blessed Peter, Your martyr, we humbly entreat Your boundless goodness that You would keep Your faithful people in holy religion, and call back to the unity of Your truth those scattered by heretical deceit; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui ea ipsa die, qua Unigénitus tuus cum nostræ carnis substántia ab immaculáta Vírgine Matre in templo est præsentátus; ánimam beáti Petri Mártyris in cælum suscepísti: eius nobis intercessióne concéde, ut in vitæ éxitu divínis mystériis expiáti; in templo glóriæ tuæ præsentári mereámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who on that very day on which Your only-begotten Son, in the substance of our flesh, was presented in the temple by His immaculate Virgin Mother, received the soul of blessed Peter, Your martyr, into heaven; grant us through his intercession that, cleansed at the end of life by the divine mysteries, we may deserve to be presented in the temple of Your glory; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1114b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 621; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Ioánnem Confessórem tuum plena sui abnegatióne, atque exímiæ caritátis zelo claréscere voluísti: eius nobis imitatióne concéde; ut abdicátis terrénis afféctibus, in tua dilectióne vivámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed John, Your confessor, should shine forth by complete denial of self and by zeal for surpassing charity; grant us by imitating him that, renouncing earthly affections, we may live in Your love; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Ioánne Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed John, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1116b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 624; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Lúciam, passiónis Fílii tui signáculis mirabíliter decorátam; virginitátis et patiéntiæ donis, blandiéntem mundum elúdere, et persequéntem superáre fecísti: da ut eius intercessióne et exémplo, nec terrénis vincámur illécebris; nec ullis frangámur advérsis: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who caused blessed Lucy, wondrously adorned with the marks of Your Son's passion, by the gifts of virginity and patience to escape the flattering world and to overcome the persecuting world; grant that by her intercession and example we may neither be conquered by earthly allurements nor broken by any adversities; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1126b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 633; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beáto Iacóbo Confessóri tuo atque Pontífici ómnia boni pastóris múnia fidéliter explére tribuísti: eius intercessióne nobis concéde; ut per viam mandatórum tuórum gradiéntes, inter oves páscuæ tuæ perpétuo collocári mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who granted to blessed James, Your confessor and bishop, faithfully to fulfil all the duties of a good shepherd; grant us through his intercession that, walking in the way of Your commandments, we may deserve to be placed for ever among the sheep of Your pasture; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Offérimus tibi, Dómine, hóstiam immaculátam, supplíciter deprecántes, ut intercedénte beáto Iacóbo, ab omni labe expurgáti, nos ipsos hóstiam placéntem tibi exhibeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the spotless victim, humbly entreating that, through the intercession of blessed James, cleansed from every stain, we may present ourselves to You as a pleasing victim; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Intervéniat pro nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, beátus Iacóbus Conféssor et Póntifex: eiúsque précibus concéde; ut cælésti pábulo enutríti, cuncta terréna respuámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed James, confessor and bishop, intercede for us, we beseech You, O Lord; and by his prayers grant that, nourished with heavenly food, we may reject all earthly things; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1216b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 337; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Sebastiánum Confessórem tuum reguláris disciplínæ, et evangélicæ perfectiónis singulári stúdio mirábilem effecísti: concéde propítius, ut eius imitatióne carne mortificáti, et vivificáti spíritu; ætérna prǽmia consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Sebastian, Your confessor, wonderful by his singular zeal for regular discipline and evangelical perfection; mercifully grant that by imitating him, mortified in the flesh and made alive in the spirit, we may obtain eternal rewards; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Sebastiáno Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Sebastian, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "G566": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 556; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui gloriósam Matrem tuam nominári Maríam voluísti: concéde quǽsumus, ut qui dulce Maríæ nomen implórant; perpétuum séntiant suæ benedictiónis auxílium: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that Your glorious Mother should be called Mary; grant, we beseech You, that those who call upon the sweet name of Mary may feel the unfailing help of her blessing; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Tua, Dómine, propitiatióne, et beátæ Maríæ semper Vírginis intercessióne, ad perpétuam atque præséntem hæc oblátio nobis profíciat prosperitátem et pacem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through Your mercy, O Lord, and the intercession of blessed Mary ever Virgin, may this offering avail us for prosperity and peace, both now and for ever; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis, Dómine, salútis nostræ subsídiis: da, quǽsumus, beátæ Maríæ semper Vírginis patrocíniis nos ubíque prótegi; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received, O Lord, the helps of our salvation, grant, we beseech You, that we may everywhere be protected by the patronage of blessed Mary ever Virgin, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0115": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 353-354; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beáti Mártyris tui Francísci fidem mirábili constántia roborásti: concéde propítius Ecclésiæ tuæ ut eius précibus adiúta; novos ubíque fídei triúmphos celebráre mereátur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who strengthened the faith of blessed Francis, Your martyr, with wonderful constancy; mercifully grant that Your Church, helped by his prayers, may deserve to celebrate new triumphs of the faith everywhere; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, qui veræ caritátis offíciis beátum Francíscum ad hanc salutárem Hóstiam offeréndam se dispónere docuísti: præsta, quǽsumus, ut pari caritátis ardóre ad sacra mystéria accedéntes, eórum fructum copiósius percipiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the works of true charity taught blessed Francis to prepare himself for offering this saving Victim; grant, we beseech You, that approaching the sacred mysteries with like ardor of charity, we may receive their fruit more abundantly; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui beátum Francíscum, sacra mystéria celebrántem, supérnis delíciis afflúere voluísti: ipsíus nobis intervéntu concéde ut Angelórum pane refécti terréna despícere; et advérsa ómnia fórtiter superáre discámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed Francis, while celebrating the sacred mysteries, should overflow with heavenly delights; grant us through his intercession that, refreshed with the bread of Angels, we may learn to despise the things of earth and bravely to overcome all adversities; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0122": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 9* (Commune unius Martyris non Pontificis); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Adésto Dómine supplicatiónibus nostris: ut qui ex iniquitáte nostra reos nos esse cognóscimus; beáti Vincéntii Mártyris tui intercessióne liberémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be present, O Lord, to our supplications, that we who know ourselves to be guilty by our iniquity may be delivered by the intercession of blessed Vincent, Your martyr; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Munéribus nostris, quǽsumus Dómine, precibúsque suscéptis: intercedénte beáto Vincéntio Mártyre tuo, et cæléstibus nos munda mystériis, et cleménter exáudi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received our gifts and prayers, O Lord, we beseech You, through the intercession of blessed Vincent, Your martyr, both cleanse us by the heavenly mysteries and mercifully hear us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Vincéntio Mártyre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Vincent, Your martyr, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0410b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 410; Secret and Postcommunion from the Commune, p. 9*; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Antónium, ad lucem veritátis tuæ misericórditer revocátum, exímium Mártyrem effecísti: præsta, ut eius intercessióne simus semper in fide stábiles; et in ópere efficáces: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Anthony, mercifully called back to the light of Your truth, an outstanding martyr; grant that through his intercession we may ever be steadfast in faith and effective in deed; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Munéribus nostris, quǽsumus Dómine, precibúsque suscéptis: intercedénte beáto António Mártyre tuo, et cæléstibus nos munda mystériis, et cleménter exáudi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received our gifts and prayers, O Lord, we beseech You, through the intercession of blessed Anthony, Your martyr, both cleanse us by the heavenly mysteries and mercifully hear us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto António Mártyre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Anthony, Your martyr, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0427b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 420; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Innova, Dómine, in córdibus nostris amórem tuæ Crucis; ut intercessióne et exémplo beátæ Hosánnæ Vírginis pœniténtis, dolórum tuórum partícipes efficiámur et glóriæ. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Renew in our hearts, O Lord, the love of Your Cross, that by the intercession and example of blessed Osanna, Your penitent virgin, we may be made sharers in Your sufferings and in Your glory; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, hæc dona quæ in beátæ Hosánnæ Vírginis commemoratióne deférimus, et præsta ut, ea intercedénte, castitátis et pœniténtiæ donis tibi iúgiter placére valeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, these gifts which we offer in commemoration of blessed Osanna, Your virgin, and grant that through her intercession we may ever be able to please You by the gifts of chastity and penance; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui de uno pane et de uno cálice participántes unum in Christo corpus nos esse voluísti: per beátæ Hosánnæ Vírginis intercessiónem fidéles tuos in veritáte confírma; et a recta fide aberrántes ad Ecclésiæ tuæ révoca unitátem. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that we who partake of one bread and one chalice should be one body in Christ; through the intercession of blessed Osanna, Your virgin, confirm Your faithful in the truth, and call back to the unity of Your Church those who have strayed from the right faith; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1211": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 17*-18* (Commune Confessoris Pontificis); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Dámasi Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis veneránda solémnitas; et devotiónem nobis áugeat, et salútem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the venerable feast of blessed Damasus, Your confessor and bishop, may increase in us both devotion and salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti tui, quǽsumus Dómine, nos ubíque lætíficent: ut dum eórum mérita recólimus, patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your saints, we beseech You, O Lord, everywhere make us glad; that while we recall their merits we may feel their patronage; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut de percéptis munéribus grátias exhibéntes; intercedénte beáto Dámaso Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, benefícia potióra sumámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that giving thanks for the gifts we have received, we may, through the intercession of blessed Damasus, Your confessor and bishop, receive still greater benefits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0411": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 20*-21* (Commune Doctoris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Leónem minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave to Your people blessed Leo as a minister of eternal salvation; grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have as an intercessor in heaven him whom we had on earth as a teacher of life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Leónis Confessóris tui atque Doctóris, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, through the intercession of blessed Leo, Your confessor and doctor, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Leónis Confessóris tui atque Doctóris nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, we beseech You, almighty God, that we may everywhere be helped by the prayer of blessed Leo, Your confessor and doctor, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0620b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 30*-31* (Commune Virginis non Martyris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Exáudi nos Deus salutáris noster: ut sicut de beátæ Hosánnæ Vírginis tuæ festivitáte gaudémus; ita piæ devotiónis erudiámur afféctu: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear us, O God our Savior, that as we rejoice in the feast of blessed Osanna, Your virgin, so we may be taught the affection of loving devotion; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0805": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 1* (In festis B. Mariæ Virginis); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Supplicatiónem servórum tuórum Deus miserátor exáudi: ut qui in solemnitáte Dei Genitrícis et Vírginis congregámur; eius intercessiónibus a te de instántibus perículis eruámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Mercifully hear, O God, the supplication of Your servants, that we who are gathered together on the feast of the Mother of God and Virgin may by her intercession be delivered by You from the dangers that threaten us; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Unigéniti tui, Dómine, nobis succúrrat humánitas: ut qui natus de Vírgine, Matris integritátem non mínuit, sed sacrávit, in solemnitáte eius, nostris nos piáculis éxuens, oblatiónem nostram tibi fáciat accéptam: Iesus Christus Dóminus noster, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the humanity of Your only-begotten Son, O Lord, come to our aid; that He who, born of the Virgin, did not lessen but hallowed His Mother's integrity, may on her feast free us from our sins and make our offering acceptable to You, Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, celebritátis ánnuæ votíva sacraménta; præsta quǽsumus, ut et temporális vitæ nobis remédia prǽbeant, et ætérnæ: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the votive sacraments of this yearly feast; grant, we beseech You, that they may bring us remedies for this temporal life and for the life eternal; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0531": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. supplement (B. Maria Virgo Regina, 1956), pp. 3-4; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Concéde nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine: ut, qui solemnitátem beátæ Maríæ Vírginis Regínæ nostræ celebrámus; eius muníti præsídio, pacem in præsénti et glóriam in futúro cónsequi mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, O Lord, that we who celebrate the feast of the blessed Virgin Mary, our Queen, may, defended by her protection, deserve to obtain peace in this life and glory in the life to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, múnera lætántis Ecclésiæ: et, beátæ Vírginis Maríæ Regínæ suffragántibus méritis, ad nostræ salútis auxílium proveníre concéde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Accept, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts of Your rejoicing Church, and grant that, through the pleading merits of the blessed Virgin Mary, Queen, they may avail for the help of our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Celebrátis solémniis, Dómine, quæ pro sanctæ Maríæ, Regínæ nostræ, festivitáte perégimus: eius, quǽsumus, nobis intercessióne fiant salutária; in cuius honóre sunt exsultánter impléta: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having celebrated the solemnities which we have performed for the feast of holy Mary, our Queen, we beseech You, O Lord, that through her intercession they may become salutary for us, in whose honor they have been joyfully fulfilled; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0603": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 460; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátos Mártyres tuos Petrum Pontíficem eiúsque sócios ad fidem géntibus prædicándam pari firmitáte et caritáte donásti: præsta, quǽsumus; eórum exémplo et intercessióne nos in tua fide permanére constántes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who endowed Your blessed martyrs Peter, bishop, and his companions with equal firmness and charity for preaching the faith to the nations; grant, we beseech You, that by their example and intercession we may remain constant in Your faith; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, propítius preces nostras cum oblatiónibus hostiárum, et tuórum deprecatióne Mártyrum Petri Pontíficis ac sociórum eius, pietáti tuæ pérfice benígnus accéptas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously receive, O Lord, our prayers with the offerings of victims, and through the pleading of Your martyrs Peter, bishop, and his companions, kindly make them acceptable to Your loving kindness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Omnípotens et miséricors Deus, qui in sanctórum córdibus flammam tuæ dilectiónis accéndis: da nobis, per sacraménta quæ súmpsimus, eámdem fidem, caritatísque virtútem; et quorum gaudémus triúmphis, proficiámus exémplis. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and merciful God, who kindle in the hearts of the saints the flame of Your love; grant us, through the sacraments we have received, the same faith and strength of charity, that we may profit by the example of those in whose triumphs we rejoice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0727": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. supplement (BB. Josephus, Melchior et socii, 1954); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Mártyrum tuórum nos, Dómine, Ioséphi, Melchióris et sociórum conféssio beáta commúniat; et fragilitáti nostræ subsídium dignánter exóret: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the blessed confession of Your martyrs Joseph, Melchior and their companions fortify us, O Lord, and graciously obtain help for our frailty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Benedíctio tua, Dómine, larga descéndat: quæ et múnera nostra, deprecántibus sanctis Martýribus tuis, tibi reddat accépta, et nobis sacraméntum redemptiónis effíciat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your blessing, O Lord, descend abundantly, to make our gifts acceptable to You through the prayers of Your holy martyrs, and to make them for us the sacrament of redemption; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cæléstibus refécti sacraméntis et gáudiis, súpplices te, Dómine, deprecámur: ut, quorum gloriámur triúmphis; protegámur auxíliis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by the heavenly sacraments and joys, we humbly entreat You, O Lord, that we may be protected by the help of those in whose triumphs we glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0731": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 510; Secret and Postcommunion from the Commune Confessoris non Pontificis; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ad maiórem tui nóminis glóriam propagándam, novo per beátum Ignátium subsídio militántem Ecclésiam roborásti: concéde, ut eius auxílio et imitatióne certántes in terris; coronári cum ipso mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who for the spreading of the greater glory of Your name strengthened the Church militant with a new help through blessed Ignatius; grant that, striving on earth by his help and example, we may deserve to be crowned with him in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Ignátio Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Ignatius, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0815": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 529-530; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Veneránda nobis, Dómine, huius diéi festívitas opem cónferat salutárem; in qua sancta Dei Génitrix mortem súbiit temporálem: nec tamen mortis néxibus déprimi pótuit; quæ Fílium tuum Dóminum nostrum de se génuit incarnátum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the venerable festival of this day, O Lord, bring us saving help, on which the holy Mother of God underwent temporal death, yet could not be held down by the bonds of death, she who brought forth of herself Your Son, our Lord, made flesh; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Subvéniat, Dómine, plebi tuæ Dei Genitrícis orátio: quam etsi pro conditióne carnis migrásse cognóscimus, in cælésti glória apud te pro nobis intercédere sentiámus. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the prayer of the Mother of God, O Lord, come to the aid of Your people; that we who know that she has departed this life according to the condition of the flesh may feel that she intercedes for us with You in heavenly glory; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Mensæ cæléstis partícipes effécti, implorámus cleméntiam tuam Dómine Deus noster: ut qui Assumptiónem Dei Genitrícis cólimus; a cunctis malis imminéntibus, eius intercessióne liberémur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Made partakers of the heavenly table, we implore Your mercy, O Lord our God, that we who keep the Assumption of the Mother of God may by her intercession be delivered from all evils that threaten us; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0920": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 564; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Francíscum Confessórem tuum, supérnæ caritátis dulcédine perfúsum, verbi tui præcónem exímium effecísti: eius intercessióne concéde; ut igne tui amóris incénsi, in tua dilectióne semper vivámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Francis, Your confessor, steeped in the sweetness of heavenly charity, an outstanding herald of Your word; grant through his intercession that, kindled with the fire of Your love, we may ever live in Your love; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, ut sicut beátus Francíscus iuge se tibi sacrifícium ófferens, spíritum suum ad æternitátem áluit: grátiæ tuæ nobis semper concíliet ubertátem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that as blessed Francis, ever offering himself to You as a sacrifice, nourished his spirit for eternity, so he may ever win for us the abundance of Your grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacris refécti aliméntis, te súpplices deprecámur, omnípotens Deus: ut intercedénte beáto Francísco, quem, post oblátum tibi sacrifícium, ad salútis portum pretiósa morte transíre fecísti; nos étiam, in vitæ éxitu cælésti pábulo roborátos, eiúsdem glóriæ fácias esse consórtes: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with sacred food, we humbly entreat You, almighty God, that through the intercession of blessed Francis, whom after offering You the sacrifice You caused to pass by a precious death to the haven of salvation, You would make us also, strengthened at the end of life with heavenly food, sharers of the same glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1207": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 329-331; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum Ambrósium minístrum tribuísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut quem doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris; intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gave to Your people blessed Ambrose as a minister of eternal salvation; grant, we beseech You, that we may deserve to have as an intercessor in heaven him whom we had on earth as a teacher of life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, múnera tuæ maiestáti obláta, per intercessiónem beáti Ambrósii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis, ad perpétuam nobis fac proveníre salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and eternal God, through the intercession of blessed Ambrose, Your confessor and bishop, make the gifts offered to Your majesty avail us unto everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta salútis nostræ suscipiéntes, concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Ambrósii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis nos ubíque orátio ádiuvet; in cuius veneratióne hæc tuæ obtúlimus maiestáti: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receiving the sacraments of our salvation, we beseech You, almighty God, that we may everywhere be helped by the prayer of blessed Ambrose, Your confessor and bishop, in whose veneration we have offered these gifts to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0928b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 570-571; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Lauréntium Confessórem tuum reguláris disciplínæ stúdio, et caritátis ardóre claréscere fecísti: eius nobis intercessióne concéde; ut perfectióra semper exsequéntes, ætérna gáudia consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Laurence, Your confessor, illustrious by zeal for regular discipline and by the ardor of charity; grant us through his intercession that, ever striving after what is more perfect, we may attain eternal joys; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe Dómine oblatiónem, quam tibi offérimus: et beáti Lauréntii méritis atque imitatióne, spirituálium donórum augménta capiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, the offering which we make to You, and by the merits and imitation of blessed Laurence may we receive an increase of spiritual gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti, Dómine, munéribus sacris, te humíliter deprecámur: ut mundi illécebras fastidiéntes; beáto Lauréntio Confessóre tuo intercedénte, cæléstes delícias iúgiter appetámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed, O Lord, with sacred gifts, we humbly entreat You that, despising the allurements of the world, we may, through the intercession of blessed Laurence, Your confessor, ever long for heavenly delights; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0222": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 356-358 (Cathedra S. Petri Romæ, as the Missal directs); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beáto Petro Apóstolo tuo, collátis clávibus regni cæléstis, ligándi atque solvéndi pontifícium tradidísti: concéde, ut intercessiónis eius auxílio; a peccatórum nostrórum néxibus liberémur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, giving to blessed Peter, Your apostle, the keys of the heavenly kingdom, bestowed on him the high-priestly power of binding and loosing; grant that by the help of his intercession we may be delivered from the bonds of our sins; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ecclésiæ tuæ, quǽsumus Dómine, preces et hóstias beáti Petri Apóstoli tui comméndet orátio: ut quod pro illíus glória celebrámus, nobis prosit ad véniam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the prayer of blessed Peter, Your apostle, we beseech You, O Lord, commend the prayers and offerings of Your Church, that what we celebrate for his glory may avail us for pardon; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Lætíficet nos, Dómine quǽsumus, munus oblátum: ut sicut in Apóstolo tuo Petro te mirábilem prædicámus; sic per illum tuæ sumámus indulgéntiæ largitátem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the gift offered, we beseech You, O Lord, gladden us, that as we proclaim You wonderful in Your apostle Peter, so through him we may receive the bounty of Your pardon; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0524": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 64*-66* (Missa votiva de S. Dominico, Feria iij, as the Missal directs); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Domínici Confessóris tui, Patris nostri, illumináre dignátus es méritis et doctrínis: concéde, ut eius intercessióne, temporálibus non destituátur auxíliis; et spirituálibus semper profíciat increméntis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who were pleased to enlighten Your Church by the merits and teaching of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, our Father; grant that through his intercession she may not be deprived of temporal help, and may ever grow in spiritual increase; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi Dómine dicáta sanctífica: ut méritis beáti Domínici Confessóris tui, Patris nostri, nobis profíciant ad medélam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts dedicated to You; that by the merits of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, our Father, they may avail us for healing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui peccatórum nostrórum póndere prémimur; beáti Domínici Confessóris tui, Patris nostri, patrocínio sublevémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who are weighed down by the burden of our sins may be raised up by the patronage of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, our Father; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0215": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 390 (B. Henricus Suso, 2 Martii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Henrícum Confessórem tuum córporis mortificatióne, et caritáte mirábilem effecísti: concéde, ut Christum crucifíxum ópere in nobis exprímere; et corde dilígere valeámus: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Henry, Your confessor, wonderful in the mortification of the body and in charity; grant that we may be able to express Christ crucified in our works and to love Him with our heart; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, qui hæc sacra in tui commemoratiónem fíeri præcepísti: præsta, ut beáti Henríci imitatióne, te iúgiter cogitémus, atque sapiámus. Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, who commanded that these sacred rites be done in remembrance of You; grant that, by imitating blessed Henry, we may think of You continually and savor You; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divínæ sapiéntiæ mensa refécti, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut per sacraménta quæ súmpsimus; beáto Henríco intercedénte, ad vitam ætérnam enutriámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed at the table of divine wisdom, we beseech You, almighty God, that through the sacraments we have received, blessed Henry interceding, we may be nourished unto everlasting life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0511": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 425-426 (1 Maii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos ánnua Apostolórum tuórum Philíppi et Iacóbi solemnitáte lætíficas: præsta quǽsumus, ut quorum gaudémus méritis; instruámur exémplis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gladden us by the yearly feast of Your Apostles Philip and James; grant, we beseech You, that we may be taught by the example of those in whose merits we rejoice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, Dómine, quæ pro Apostolórum tuórum Philíppi et Iacóbi solemnitáte deférimus, propítius súscipe, et mala ómnia, quæ merémur, avérte. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Mercifully receive, O Lord, the gifts which we bring on the feast of Your Apostles Philip and James, and turn away from us all the evils we deserve; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus Dómine, salutáribus repléti mystériis: ut quorum solémnia celebrámus: eórum oratiónibus adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with the saving mysteries, we beseech You, O Lord, that we may be helped by the prayers of those whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0225b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 388-389 (B. Constantius, 25 Februarii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Constántium Confessórem tuum assíduæ oratiónis, et promovéndæ pacis stúdio, in pópulis gloriósum effecísti: eius nobis intercessióne concéde; ut per iustítiæ sémitas incedéntes, pacem et glóriam assequámur ætérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Constantius, Your confessor, glorious among the peoples by his zeal for constant prayer and for the furthering of peace; grant us by his intercession that, walking in the paths of justice, we may attain to everlasting peace and glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Domínicæ mensæ nobis tribuátur accúmbere in veste caritátis, qua beátus Constántius indútus, ad superióra invitántem audíre méruit Iesum Christum Dóminum nostrum: Qui vivit et regnat cum Deo Patre in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May it be granted us to sit at the table of the Lord in the wedding garment of charity, clothed in which blessed Constantius was found worthy to hear Jesus Christ our Lord inviting him to the higher place; who lives and reigns with God the Father in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Angelórum pane refécti te deprecámur omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Constántii intercedéntibus méritis; ætérnas tibi laudes persólvere cum ipso valeámus in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with the bread of Angels, we pray You, almighty God, that by the merits and intercession of blessed Constantius we may be able to render You eternal praise with him in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0419b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 441 (B. Albertus a Bergomo); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui in húmili vitæ génere beátum Albértum Confessórem tuum exímia sanctitáte claréscere voluísti: fac nos ita eius sectári vestígia; ut ássequi mereámur et prǽmia: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed Albert, Your confessor, should shine with exceptional holiness in a humble state of life; make us so to follow in his footsteps that we may deserve to attain also his reward; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi Dómine hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus, et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, sacrifices of praise in commemoration of Your saints, through whom we trust to be delivered from evils both present and to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cælésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus; eius muniámur et précibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly food and drink, O our God, we humbly entreat You that we may also be defended by the prayers of him in whose commemoration we have received these gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0503b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 534-535 (B. Æmilia Bicchieri, 17 Augusti); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátæ Æmíliæ Vírgini tuæ terréna cuncta despícere, et te solum quǽrere tribuísti: eius méritis et intercessióne concéde; ut sprétis peritúris illécebris, te toto corde diligámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who granted to blessed Emily, Your virgin, to despise all earthly things and to seek You alone; grant by her merits and intercession that, spurning perishable allurements, we may love You with our whole heart; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1010b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 582-583 (B. Matthæus Carreri, 7 Octobris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Excita Dómine in córdibus nostris crucis et passiónis amórem: ut beáti Matthǽi intercessióne et exémplo; dolórum Christi partícipes efficiámur, et glóriæ: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Stir up, O Lord, in our hearts the love of the cross and passion, that through the intercession and example of blessed Matthew we may be made partakers of the sufferings of Christ and of His glory; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Matthǽo Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Matthew, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1012b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 579 (B. Dominicus Spadafora, 3 Octobris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui in beáto Domínico Confessóre tuo munus apostólicum assíduo oratiónis stúdio et reguláris disciplínæ observántia mirabíliter fecundásti: concéde propítius, ut eius vestígia prosequéntes; úberes salútis fructus percípere mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who in blessed Dominic, Your confessor, wonderfully made fruitful his apostolic office through constant zeal for prayer and the observance of regular discipline; mercifully grant that, following in his footsteps, we may deserve to gather abundant fruits of salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Deus, hanc Hóstiam immaculátam, ac suffragánte Servo tuo Domínico, da quǽsumus, ut casto córpore ac devóta mente nosmetípsos offeréntes, digno servítio munus perficiámus Fílii tui Dómini nostri Iesu Christi, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O God, this spotless Victim, and, Your servant Dominic pleading for us, grant, we beseech You, that offering ourselves with chaste body and devout mind, we may fulfil with worthy service the offering of Your Son our Lord Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Grátia tua sanctíficans, quǽsumus Dómine, nos dóciles effíciat: ut Beáti Domínici intercessióne, strénue coram te ambulántes; in tuo semper amóre crescámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your sanctifying grace, we beseech You, O Lord, make us docile, that by the intercession of blessed Dominic, walking earnestly before You, we may ever grow in Your love; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1127b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 340 (B. Margarita de Sabaudia, 23 Decembris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Margarítam a sǽculi pompa ad húmilem tuæ crucis sequélam toto corde transíre docuísti: concéde, ut eius méritis et exémplo, discámus peritúras mundi calcáre delícias; et in ampléxu tuæ crucis ómnia nobis adversántia superáre: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who taught blessed Margaret to pass with her whole heart from the pomp of the world to the humble following of Your cross; grant that by her merits and example we may learn to tread underfoot the perishing delights of the world and, in the embrace of Your cross, to overcome all that opposes us; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, Dómine, nostræ devotiónis offérimus: ut tibi grata, et nobis salutária, beátæ Margarítæ pia supplicatióne reddántur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, the gifts of our devotion, that they may become pleasing to You and salutary to us through the devout supplication of blessed Margaret; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut quos salutáribus dignátus es erudíre mystériis; beátæ Margarítæ intercessióne gloriósa, cæléstibus refícias aliméntis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that those whom You have deigned to instruct by the saving mysteries You may refresh with heavenly food through the glorious intercession of blessed Margaret; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1007": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 575-577 (Dominica I Octobris); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, cuius Unigénitus per vitam, mortem, et resurrectiónem suam nobis salútis ætérnæ prǽmia comparávit: concéde quǽsumus ut hæc mystéria sanctíssimo Rosário beátæ Maríæ Vírginis recoléntes, et imitémur quod cóntinent; et quod promíttunt assequámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, whose only-begotten Son, by His life, death, and resurrection, has purchased for us the rewards of eternal salvation; grant, we beseech You, that, meditating upon these mysteries in the most holy Rosary of the Blessed Virgin Mary, we may both imitate what they contain and obtain what they promise; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Fac nos, quǽsumus Dómine, his munéribus offeréndis conveniénter aptári: et per sanctíssimi Rosárii mystéria, sic vitam, passiónem, et glóriam Unigéniti tui recólere, ut eius digni promissiónibus efficiámur. Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Make us, we beseech You, O Lord, fitly prepared to offer these gifts, and through the mysteries of the most holy Rosary so to recall the life, passion, and glory of Your only-begotten Son that we may be made worthy of His promises; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sanctíssimæ Genitrícis tuæ, cuius Rosárium celebrámus; quǽsumus Dómine, précibus adiuvémur: ut et mysteriórum, quæ cólimus, virtus percipiátur; et sacramentórum, quæ súmpsimus, obtineátur efféctus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May we be helped, we beseech You, O Lord, by the prayers of Your most holy Mother, whose Rosary we celebrate, that we may receive the power of the mysteries which we honor and obtain the effect of the sacraments which we have received; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0303b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 394 (B. Petrus de Jeremia, 10 Martii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beáti Petri Confessóris tui précibus et hortaméntis errántes in viam iustítiæ misericórditer redíre fecísti: diláta, quǽsumus, illíus intercessióne corda nostra; ut sémitam mandatórum tuórum semper currámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the prayers and exhortations of blessed Peter, Your confessor, mercifully brought back the erring into the way of justice; enlarge our hearts, we beseech You, by his intercession, that we may ever run the way of Your commandments; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You in honor of Your saints, and may purify us alike in body and mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Petro Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received the food of heaven may, through the intercession of blessed Peter, Your confessor, be thereby defended against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0819b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 390-391 (B. Jordanus a Pisis, 6 Martii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Iordánum Confessórem tuum, evangélicæ prædicatiónis dignum minístrum effecísti: ex eius nobis imitatióne tríbue operári quæ præcipis; ut ætérnæ mercédis fructum cónsequi valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Jordan, Your confessor, a worthy minister of the preaching of the Gospel; grant us by his example to do what You command, that we may be able to obtain the fruit of eternal reward; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Per hanc immaculátam hóstiam placábilis sit pro nobis beáti Iordáni intercéssio: ut a cunctis perículis liberáti in témpore, æternitátis glóriæ partícipes esse mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through this spotless Victim may the intercession of blessed Jordan be pleasing for us, that, freed from all dangers in time, we may deserve to be partakers of the glory of eternity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sumptis munéribus sacris, implorámus Dómine cleméntiam tuam: ut intercedénte beáto Iordáno Confessóre tuo, inter próspera præséntis vitæ, et advérsa sic transeámus; ut glóriam assequámur ætérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received the sacred gifts, we implore Your mercy, O Lord, that through the intercession of blessed Jordan, Your confessor, we may so pass through the prosperity and adversity of this present life that we may attain everlasting glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Quad3h": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 100-102; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "sp": ["Subiéctum tibi pópulum, quǽsumus Dómine, propitiátio cæléstis amplíficet; et tuis semper fáciat servíre mandátis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your heavenly mercy, we beseech You, O Lord, increase the people subject to You, and make them ever obedient to Your commandments; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end.", "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 102"], "or": ["Concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut ieiuniórum nobis sancta devótio, et purificatiónem tríbuat; et maiestáti tuæ nos reddat accéptos: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the holy devotion of our fasts may both bring us purification and make us acceptable to Your majesty; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Efficiátur hæc hóstia, quǽsumus Dómine, solémnibus grata ieiúniis: et ut tibi fiat accéptior, purificátis méntibus immolétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this offering, we beseech You, O Lord, be made pleasing to You by our solemn fasts, and, that it may be the more acceptable to You, may it be offered with purified minds; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménti tui, Dómine, veneránda percéptio: et mýstico nos mundet efféctu; et perpétua virtúte deféndat: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the reverent reception of Your sacrament, O Lord, both cleanse us by its mystic working and defend us by its everlasting power; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0504": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 430-431; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus mœréntium consolátor, et in te sperántium salus; qui beátæ Mónicæ pias lácrymas in conversióne fílii sui Augustíni misericórditer suscepísti: da nobis utriúsque intervéntu, peccáta nostra deploráre; et grátiæ tuæ indulgéntiam inveníre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the consoler of the sorrowful and the salvation of those who hope in You, who mercifully accepted the loving tears of blessed Monica for the conversion of her son Augustine; grant us, through the intercession of them both, to bewail our sins and to find the pardon of Your grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0703": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 476-478 (28 Junii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beáto Irenǽo Mártyri tuo atque Pontífici tribuísti, ut et veritáte doctrínæ expugnáret hǽreses, et pacem Ecclésiæ felíciter confirmáret: da, quǽsumus, plebi tuæ in sancta religióne constántiam; et pacem tuam nostris concéde tempóribus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who granted to blessed Irenaeus, Your martyr and bishop, both to overcome heresies by the truth of his teaching and happily to establish peace in the Church; give, we beseech You, to Your people constancy in holy religion, and grant Your peace in our times; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, qui credéntes in te pópulos nullis sinis cóncuti terróribus: dignáre preces et hóstias dicátæ tibi plebis suscípere, ut pax a tua pietáte concéssa, christianórum fines ab omni hoste fáciat esse secúros. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who do not let the peoples who believe in You be shaken by any terrors, deign to receive the prayers and offerings of the people dedicated to You, that the peace granted by Your goodness may make the borders of Christians safe from every enemy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus auctor pacis et amátor, quem nosse, vívere, cui servíre, regnáre est: prótege ab ómnibus impugnatiónibus súpplices tuos; ut, qui in defensióne tua confídimus, beáti Irenǽi Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis intercessióne, nullíus hostilitátis arma timeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the author and lover of peace, to know whom is to live, to serve whom is to reign, protect Your suppliants from all assaults, that we who trust in Your defence may, through the intercession of blessed Irenaeus, Your martyr and bishop, fear the arms of no enemy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0729": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 508-509; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Exáudi nos Deus salutáris noster: ut sicut de beátæ Marthæ Vírginis tuæ festivitáte gaudémus; ita piæ devotiónis erudiámur afféctu: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear us, O God our Saviour, that as we rejoice in the feast of blessed Martha, Your virgin, so we may be taught the spirit of loving devotion; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0812": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 525-526; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Fámulos tuos, quǽsumus Dómine, beátæ Vírginis tuæ Claræ votíva natalítia recenséntes; cæléstium gaudiórum sua fácias interventióne partícipes, et tui Unigéniti coherédes: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, that Your servants who keep the feast of the birthday of blessed Clare, Your virgin, may by her intercession be made partakers of heavenly joys and co-heirs of Your only-begotten Son; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1202": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 325-326; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Indulgéntiam nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, beáta Bibiána Virgo et Martyr implóret: quæ tibi grata semper éxstitit; et mérito castitátis, et tuæ professióne virtútis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Bibiana, virgin and martyr, we beseech You, O Lord, implore pardon for us, she who was ever pleasing to You both by the merit of her chastity and by the confession of Your power; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe Dómine múnera, quæ in beátæ Bibiánæ Vírginis et Mártyris tuæ solemnitáte deférimus: cuius nos confídimus patrocínio liberári. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, the gifts we bring on the feast of blessed Bibiana, Your virgin and martyr, by whose patronage we trust to be delivered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Auxiliéntur nobis, Dómine, sumpta mystéria; et intercedénte beáta Bibiána Vírgine et Mártyre tua, sempitérna protectióne confírment: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the mysteries we have received help us, O Lord, and, through the intercession of blessed Bibiana, Your virgin and martyr, strengthen us with everlasting protection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0508": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 455-457 (31 Maii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, noster apud Patrem mediátor, qui beatíssimam Vírginem matrem tuam, matrem quoque nostram et apud te mediatrícem constitúere dignátus es: concéde propítius, ut quisquis ad te benefícia petitúrus accésserit; cuncta se per eam impetrásse lætétur: Qui vivis et regnas cum eódem Deo Patre in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, our mediator with the Father, who have deigned to appoint the most blessed Virgin, Your Mother, to be our mother also and our mediatrix with You; mercifully grant that whoever comes to You seeking favors may rejoice to have obtained them all through her; who live and reign with the same God the Father in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Matris tuæ ac Mediatrícis nostræ précibus, Dómine, quǽsumus, hæc hostiárum oblátio nosmetípsos, tua grátia largiénte, tibi perfíciat munus ætérnum: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "By the prayers of Your Mother and our Mediatrix, we beseech You, O Lord, may the offering of this sacrifice, by the gift of Your grace, make of ourselves an everlasting offering to You; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Subvéniat nobis, Dómine, beátæ Maríæ matris tuæ ac nostræ Mediatrícis orátio: ut per hæc sacrosáncta commércia, tua grátia largiénte; ad redemptiónis ætérnæ proficiámus augméntum: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the prayer of blessed Mary, Your Mother and our Mediatrix, help us, O Lord, that through these most holy mysteries, by the gift of Your grace, we may advance towards the increase of eternal redemption; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0910": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 457-459 (1 Junii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos beatórum Alphónsi et sociórum eius triúmpho lætíficas; da nobis, quǽsumus, eórum méritis et intercessióne, eámdem in fide constántiam, et in ópere efficáciam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gladden us by the triumph of the blessed Alphonsus and his companions; grant us, we beseech You, by their merits and intercession, the same constancy in faith and fruitfulness in work; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi Dómine offérimus in tuórum solemnitáte Beatórum, humíliter deprecántes, ut sicut illos pássio gloriósos effécit, ita et nos devótio reddat accéptos. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You sacrifices, O Lord, on the feast of Your blessed ones, humbly beseeching You that, as their passion made them glorious, so our devotion may make us acceptable; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut qui beatórum Mártyrum tuórum memóriam recólimus: eórum quoque fidem et fortitúdinem æmulémur; hostiúmque nostrórum adversitátibus superátis, ætérni tui nóminis confessióne lætémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who keep the memory of Your blessed martyrs may also imitate their faith and fortitude, and, having overcome the attacks of our enemies, may rejoice in the confession of Your eternal name; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0111b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 384-385; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Bernárdum a sǽculi vítiis revocátum, in viam perfectiónis traduxísti: eius méritis et précibus concéde; ut nos peccáta nostra defléntes, ad te puris méntibus convertámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who called blessed Bernard back from the vices of the world and led him into the way of perfection; grant by his merits and prayers that we, bewailing our sins, may turn to You with pure minds; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus Dómine, munus oblátum: et nobis cleménter indúlge, ut beáti Bernárdi exémpla æmulántes, usque in finem in tuo constánter simus amóre fervéntes. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, we beseech You, O Lord, the gift we offer, and mercifully grant that, following the example of blessed Bernard, we may be steadfastly fervent in Your love to the end; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cæléstis convívii pasti delíciis, supplíciter te Dómine deprecámur: ut beáti Bernárdi, cuius hódie memóriam fácimus, intercessióne; salutárium bonórum ubertáte repléri mereámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Fed with the delights of the heavenly banquet, we humbly pray You, O Lord, that through the intercession of blessed Bernard, whose memory we keep today, we may deserve to be filled with the abundance of saving gifts; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "Pasc6s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 243-244; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut claritátis tuæ super nos splendor effúlgeat; et lux tuæ lucis corda eórum, qui per grátiam tuam renáti sunt, Sancti Spíritus illustratióne confírmet: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the splendor of Your brightness may shine upon us, and that the light of Your light may, by the enlightening of the Holy Spirit, strengthen the hearts of those who have been born again by Your grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the same Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera, quǽsumus, Dómine, obláta sanctífica, et corda nostra Sancti Spíritus illustratióne emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts offered, and cleanse our hearts by the enlightening of the Holy Spirit; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the same Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sancti Spíritus, Dómine, corda nostra mundet infúsio; et sui roris íntima aspersióne fecúndet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the outpouring of the Holy Spirit cleanse our hearts, O Lord, and make them fruitful by the inward sprinkling of His dew; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the same Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0113": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 38-39 (In Octava Epiphaniae); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, cuius Unigénitus in substántia nostræ carnis appáruit: præsta quǽsumus, ut per eum, quem símilem nobis foris agnóvimus; intus reformári mereámur: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, whose only-begotten Son has appeared in the substance of our flesh, grant, we beseech You, that through Him whom we have known outwardly like unto ourselves we may deserve to be inwardly renewed; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, pro nati Fílii tui apparitióne deférimus, supplíciter exorántes: ut sicut ipse nostrórum auctor est múnerum, ita sit ipse miséricors et suscéptor: Iesus Christus Dóminus noster, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We bring You offerings, O Lord, for the manifestation of Your Son who was born, humbly beseeching You that, as He is Himself the author of our gifts, so He may also be their merciful receiver, Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cælésti lúmine, quǽsumus Dómine, semper et ubíque nos prǽveni: ut mystérium, cuius nos partícipes esse voluísti; et puro cernámus intúitu, et digno percipiámus afféctu: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Go before us, we beseech You, O Lord, always and everywhere with heavenly light, that we may discern with clear sight and receive with worthy love the mystery in which You have willed us to share; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0814": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 527-528; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui virginálem aulam beátæ Maríæ, in qua habitáres, elígere dignátus es: da quǽsumus, ut sua nos defensióne munítos; iucúndos fácias suæ interésse festivitáti: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who deigned to choose the virginal dwelling of blessed Mary in which to dwell, grant, we beseech You, that, defended by her protection, You may make us take part with joy in her feast; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera nostra, Dómine, apud cleméntiam tuam Dei Genitrícis comméndet orátio: quam idcírco de præsénti sǽculo transtulísti, ut pro peccátis nostris apud te fiduciáliter intercédat. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the prayer of the Mother of God commend our gifts to Your mercy, O Lord, for You took her from this present world that she might intercede confidently with You for our sins; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Concéde, miséricors Deus, fragilitáti nostræ præsídium: ut qui sanctæ Dei Genitrícis festivitátem prævenímus; intercessiónis eius auxílio, a nostris iniquitátibus resurgámus: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, O merciful God, a safeguard to our frailty, that we who keep the eve of the feast of the holy Mother of God may by the help of her intercession rise again from our iniquities; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C64s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 42*-44*; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ad maiestátis tuæ glóriam et géneris humáni salútem, Unigénitum tuum summum atque ætérnum constituísti Sacerdótem: præsta, ut quos minístros et mysteriórum suórum dispensatóres elégit; in accépto ministério adimpléndo fidéles inveniántur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who for the glory of Your majesty and the salvation of mankind appointed Your only-begotten Son the supreme and eternal Priest, grant that those whom He has chosen to be ministers and dispensers of His mysteries may be found faithful in fulfilling the ministry they have received; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc múnera, Dómine, mediátor noster Iesus Christus tibi reddat accépta; et nos, una secum, hóstias tibi gratas exhíbeat: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our mediator Jesus Christ, O Lord, make these gifts acceptable to You, and present us, together with Himself, as victims pleasing to You; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Vivíficet nos, quǽsumus Dómine, divína quam obtúlimus et súmpsimus hóstia; ut perpétua tibi caritáte coniúncti, fructum, qui semper máneat, afferámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the divine Victim which we have offered and received give us life, we beseech You, O Lord, that, joined to You in everlasting love, we may bring forth fruit that will last for ever; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C68s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 48*-50* (De Pœnis seu Passione D.N.J.C.); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui passiónem Fílii tui Dómini nostri Iesu Christi in prétium redemptiónis humánæ misericórditer suscepísti: concéde propítius, ut sicut hódie pœnárum et dolórum passiónis eius memóriam celebrámus; ita eorúmdem fructus mereámur esse partícipes: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, who in Your mercy accepted the passion of Your Son, our Lord Jesus Christ, as the price of man's redemption, mercifully grant that, as we keep today the memory of the pains and sorrows of His passion, so we may deserve to share in their fruits; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui Christi Fílii tui beáta passióne nos réparas, consérva in nobis ópera misericórdiæ tuæ: ut in huius celebritáte mystérii, perpétua devotióne vivámus. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty and everlasting God, who restore us by the blessed passion of Christ Your Son, preserve in us the works of Your mercy, that in the celebration of this mystery we may live in unceasing devotion; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti vitálibus aliméntis, omnípotens Deus, te supplíciter exorámus; ut sicut pœnas et dolóres, quos Fílius tuus Dóminus noster in sua passióne sustínuit, devóto celebrámus afféctu: ita benígno semper nos prótegas auxílio; et contínua pietáte ab omni malo præsérves: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with life-giving food, almighty God, we humbly entreat You that, as we celebrate with devout affection the pains and sorrows which Your Son our Lord endured in His passion, so You may ever protect us with Your kindly help and preserve us from all evil by Your unfailing goodness; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C85s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 66*-68* (Ad tollendum schisma); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui erráta córrigis, et dispérsa cóngregas, et congregáta consérvas: quǽsumus, super pópulum christiánum tuæ uniónis grátiam cleménter infúnde; ut divisióne reiécta, vero Pastóri Ecclésiæ tuæ se úniens, tibi digne váleat famulári: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who correct what has gone astray, gather what is scattered, and keep what is gathered, mercifully pour out, we beseech You, upon the Christian people the grace of Your unity, that, putting away division and uniting themselves to the true Shepherd of Your Church, they may be able to serve You worthily; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera hæc pro unióne pópuli christiáni tibi, Dómine, obláta sanctífica: per quæ unitátis et pacis in Ecclésia tua nobis dona concédas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, these gifts offered to You for the unity of the Christian people, and through them grant us the gifts of unity and peace in Your Church; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Hæc tua, Dómine, sumpta sacra commúnio: sicut fidélium in te uniónem præsígnat; sic in tua Ecclésia unitátis, quǽsumus, operétur efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this holy communion of Yours which we have received, O Lord, as it foreshadows the union of the faithful in You, so work, we beseech You, the effect of unity in Your Church; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C89s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 68*-70* (Pro eligendo summo Pontifice); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Súpplici, Dómine, humilitáte depóscimus; ut sacrosánctæ Románæ Ecclésiæ concédat Pontíficem illum tua imménsa píetas: qui et pio in nos stúdio semper tibi plácitus; et tuo pópulo pro salúbri régimine sit assídue ad glóriam tui nóminis reveréndus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "With humble supplication, O Lord, we pray that Your boundless goodness may grant to the most holy Roman Church a Pontiff who, by his devoted care for us, may be ever pleasing to You, and by his wholesome government may be held in honor by Your people for the glory of Your name; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Tuæ nobis, Dómine, abundántia pietátis indúlgeat, ut per sacra múnera, quæ tibi reverénter offérimus, gratum maiestáti tuæ Pontíficem sanctæ matris Ecclésiæ régimini præésse gaudeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the abundance of Your goodness, O Lord, grant us that, through the sacred gifts which we reverently offer You, we may rejoice that a Pontiff pleasing to Your majesty presides over the government of holy Mother Church; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Pretiósi córporis et sánguinis tui nos, Dómine, sacraménto reféctos, mirífica tuæ maiestátis grátia de illíus summi Pontíficis concessióne lætíficet: qui et plebem tuam virtútibus ínstruat; et fidélium mentes spirituálium arómatum odóre perfúndat: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by the sacrament of Your precious Body and Blood, O Lord, may the wonderful grace of Your majesty gladden us by the gift of that supreme Pontiff who will instruct Your people in virtue and fill the minds of the faithful with the fragrance of spiritual perfumes; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C104s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 90*-91* (Pro vitanda mortalitate); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui non mortem, sed pœniténtiam desíderas peccatórum; pópulum tuum, quǽsumus, ad te convérte propítius: ut dum tibi devótus exsístit; iracúndiæ tuæ ab eo flagélla amóveas: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who desire not the death but the repentance of sinners, mercifully turn Your people to Yourself, we beseech You, that, while they are devoted to You, You may remove from them the scourges of Your anger; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Subvéniat nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, sacrifícii præséntis oblátio: quæ nos et ab erróribus univérsis poténter absólvat, et a totíus erípiat perditiónis incúrsu. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of this present sacrifice help us, we beseech You, O Lord, mightily absolving us from all errors and rescuing us from the onset of all destruction; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Exáudi nos Deus salutáris noster: et intercedénte beáta María semper vírgine cum ómnibus Sanctis; pópulum tuum ab iracúndiæ tuæ terróribus líberum, et misericórdiæ tuæ fac benignitáte secúrum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear us, O God our Saviour, and, blessed Mary ever Virgin interceding with all the Saints, free Your people from the terrors of Your anger and make them secure in the bounty of Your mercy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C110s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 94*-96*; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui tam excellénti mystério coniugálem cópulam consecrásti, ut Christi et Ecclésiæ sacraméntum præsignáres in fœdere nuptiárum: præsta quǽsumus, ut quod nostro ministrátur offício; tua benedictióne pótius impleátur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who consecrated the union of marriage by so excellent a mystery as to foreshadow in the marriage covenant the sacrament of Christ and the Church, grant, we beseech You, that what is administered by our office may rather be fulfilled by Your blessing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus, Dómine, pro sacra connúbii lege munus oblátum: et cuius largítor es múneris, óperis esto dispósitor. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, we beseech You, O Lord, the gift offered for the sacred law of marriage, and, as You are the giver of the gift, be also the disposer of the work; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, institúta providéntiæ tuæ pio favóre comitáre: et quos legítima societáte connéctis; longǽva pietáte custódi: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, accompany with Your gracious favor what Your providence has instituted, and keep in long-lasting love those whom You join in lawful union; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C114s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 114*-116* (In die obitus seu depositionis defuncti); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, cui próprium est miseréri semper, et párcere, te súpplices exorámus pro ánima fámuli tui N. quam hódie de hoc sǽculo migráre iussísti: ut non tradas eam in manus inimíci, neque obliviscáris in finem; sed iúbeas eam a sanctis Angelis súscipi, et ad pátriam paradísi perdúci: ut quia in te sperávit, et crédidit, non pœnas ætérnas sustíneat; sed gáudia sempitérna possídeat: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, whose property is ever to have mercy and to spare, we humbly entreat You for the soul of Your servant N., which You have this day called out of this world, that You would not deliver it into the hands of the enemy, nor forget it for ever, but command it to be received by the holy Angels and led to the home of paradise, that, since it hoped and believed in You, it may not undergo the pains of hell, but may possess everlasting joys; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Propitiáre, quǽsumus Dómine, ánimæ fámuli tui N. pro qua hóstiam laudis tibi immolámus, maiestátem tuam supplíciter deprecántes: ut per hæc piæ placatiónis offícia, perveníre mereátur ad réquiem sempitérnam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be merciful, we beseech You, O Lord, to the soul of Your servant N., for which we offer You the sacrifice of praise, humbly entreating Your majesty that through these offices of loving propitiation it may deserve to come to everlasting rest; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut ánima fámuli tui N. quæ hódie de hoc sǽculo migrávit; his sacrifíciis purgáta, et a peccátis expedíta, indulgéntiam páriter, et réquiem cápiat sempitérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the soul of Your servant N., which has this day departed out of this world, being cleansed by this sacrifice and freed from sins, may receive both pardon and everlasting rest; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1113": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 116*-118* (In anniversario defunctorum, pro pluribus); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus indulgentiárum Dómine, da animábus famulórum, famularúmque tuárum, quorum anniversárium depositiónis diem commemorámus; refrigérii sedem, quiétis beatitúdinem, et lúminis claritátem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the Lord of mercies, grant to the souls of Your servants and handmaids, the anniversary of whose burial we commemorate, a place of refreshment, the happiness of rest and the brightness of light; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Propitiáre Dómine supplicatiónibus nostris pro animábus famulórum, famularúmque tuárum, quorum hódie ánnua dies ágitur, pro quibus tibi offérimus sacrifícium laudis ut eas Sanctórum tuórum consórtio sociáre dignéris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, O Lord, by our supplications for the souls of Your servants and handmaids whose anniversary is kept today, for whom we offer You the sacrifice of praise, that You may deign to join them to the fellowship of Your Saints; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus Dómine, ut ánimæ famulórum famularúmque tuárum, quorum anniversárium depositiónis diem commemorámus; his purgátæ sacrifíciis, indulgéntiam páriter, et réquiem cápiant sempitérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that the souls of Your servants and handmaids, the anniversary of whose burial we commemorate, being cleansed by this sacrifice, may obtain both pardon and everlasting rest; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "G470": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 432-433 (S. Pius V, 5 Maii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ad conteréndos Ecclésiæ tuæ hostes, et ad divínum cultum reparándum, beátum Pium Pontíficem máximum elígere dignátus es: fac nos ipsíus deféndi præsídiis, et ita tuis inhærére obséquiis; ut ómnium hóstium superátis insídiis, perpétua pace lætémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who deigned to choose blessed Pius as supreme Pontiff to crush the enemies of Your Church and to restore divine worship, make us to be defended by his protection and so to cleave to Your service that, overcoming the snares of all our enemies, we may rejoice in everlasting peace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, quǽsumus Dómine, Ecclésiæ tuæ preces et oblatiónes: ut intercedénte beáto Pio Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, in conspéctu tuo in odórem suavitátis ascéndant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, we beseech You, O Lord, the prayers and offerings of Your Church, that by the intercession of blessed Pius, Your confessor and bishop, they may rise in Your sight as an odor of sweetness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Spíritum, Dómine Deus, iustítiæ ac fortitúdinis benígnus infúnde fidélibus tuis; quos beáti Pii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis zelo ac constántia, ab ómnium hóstium incursióne tuéri dignátus es: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Graciously pour out, O Lord God, the spirit of justice and fortitude on Your faithful, whom You have deigned to protect from the onslaught of all their enemies by the zeal and constancy of blessed Pius, Your confessor and bishop; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "G481": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 452-453 (S. Philippus Neri, 26 Maii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Philíppum Confessórem tuum Sanctórum tuórum glória sublimásti: concéde propítius, ut cuius solemnitáte lætámur; eius virtútum proficiámus exémplo: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who exalted blessed Philip, Your confessor, to the glory of Your Saints, mercifully grant that we who rejoice in his feast may profit by the example of his virtues; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifíciis præséntibus, quǽsumus Dómine, inténde placátus: et præsta, ut illo nos igne Spíritus Sanctus inflámmet, quo beáti Philíppi cor mirabíliter penetrávit. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte eiúsdem Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously, we beseech You, O Lord, upon this present sacrifice, and grant that the Holy Spirit may inflame us with that fire with which He wonderfully pierced the heart of blessed Philip; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the same Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cæléstibus, Dómine, pasti delíciis: quǽsumus, ut beáti Philíppi Confessóris tui méritis et imitatióne; semper eádem, per quæ veráciter vívimus, appetámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Fed with heavenly delights, we beseech You, O Lord, that by the merits and example of blessed Philip, Your confessor, we may ever long for those things by which we truly live; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "G475": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 442-443 (B. Imelda, 13 Maii); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, qui beátam Vírginem Iméldam igníto caritátis amóre sauciátam et immaculáta hóstia mirabíliter reféctam, in cælum suscepísti: fac nos eius intercessióne, eódem caritátis fervóre ad Sacram Mensam accédere; ut appetámus dissólvi, et esse tecum mereámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, who took up into heaven the blessed virgin Imelda, wounded with the burning love of charity and wonderfully refreshed with the spotless Host, grant us by her intercession to approach the holy Table with the same fervor of charity, that we may long to be dissolved and deserve to be with You; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, múnera quæ tibi offérimus, et beátæ Iméldæ Vírginis intercedéntibus méritis, amóris tui nobis spíritum infúnde, ut terrénis affectiónibus despéctis, in te nostra fixa sint corda, ubi vera sunt gáudia. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, the gifts which we offer You, and, by the merits and intercession of blessed Imelda, virgin, pour into us the spirit of Your love, that, despising earthly affections, our hearts may be fixed on You, where true joys are; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sit nobis, Dómine, ad thronum misericórdiæ tuæ pro nobis beáta Imélda virgo indefíciens exorátrix: ut sicut illa salutári hóstia percépta ad ætérnam glóriam evolávit; ita tanti participátio mystérii sit nobis ablútio scélerum in vita, et in morte via, qua ad vitam perveniámus ætérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Imelda, virgin, be for us, O Lord, an unfailing pleader before the throne of Your mercy, that, as she, having received the saving Host, flew to eternal glory, so the sharing of so great a mystery may be for us in life the cleansing of our sins, and in death the way by which we may come to life eternal; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0428": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 420-421 (commemoration De S. Paulo a Cruce on 28 Apr.; printed without a conclusion, Qui vivis supplied); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, qui ad mystérium crucis prædicándum, sanctum Paulum singulári caritáte donásti; et per eum novam in Ecclésia famíliam floréscere voluísti: ipsíus nobis intercessióne concéde; ut passiónem tuam iúgiter recoléntes in terris, eiúsdem fructum cónsequi mereámur in cælis: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, who endowed saint Paul with singular charity to preach the mystery of the Cross, and willed that through him a new family should flourish in the Church, grant us by his intercession that, ever recalling Your passion on earth, we may deserve to obtain its fruit in heaven; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Cæléstem nobis, Dómine, prǽbeant mystéria hæc passiónis et mortis tuæ fervórem, quo sanctus Paulus, ea offeréndo, corpus suum hóstiam vivéntem, sanctam, tibíque placéntem exhíbuit: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May these mysteries, O Lord, give us that fervor for Your passion and death with which saint Paul, in offering them, presented his body to You as a living sacrifice, holy and pleasing to You; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, divínum sacraméntum, imménsæ caritátis tuæ memoriále perpétuum: tríbue, quǽsumus, ut sancti Pauli méritis et imitatióne, aquam de fóntibus tuis hauriámus in vitam ætérnam saliéntem; et tuam sacratíssimam passiónem córdibus nostris impréssam, móribus et vita teneámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the divine sacrament, the everlasting memorial of Your boundless charity; grant, we beseech You, that by the merits and example of saint Paul we may draw from Your fountains water springing up into life eternal, and may hold fast in our conduct and life Your most sacred passion impressed upon our hearts; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "C55s": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 32*-33* (Unius Virginis non Martyris, alia Missa); English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Exáudi nos Deus salutáris noster: ut sicut de beátæ N. Vírginis tuæ festivitáte gaudémus; ita piæ devotiónis erudiámur afféctu: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear us, O God our Saviour, that as we rejoice in the feast of blessed N., Your virgin, so we may be taught the spirit of loving devotion; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0103b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 351-352; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus qui beátæ Zedíslavæ concédere dignátus es, ut te iúgiter erécta mente contemplarétur, únaque próximo sollícite prospíceret: ea intercedénte, fac nos diligénti stúdio cæléstibus insístere; et caritátem piis opéribus exercére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who were pleased to grant to blessed Zedislava that she should ever contemplate You with uplifted mind and at the same time care diligently for her neighbor; at her intercession make us apply ourselves with earnest zeal to heavenly things, and exercise charity in works of piety; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátum tibi Dómine sacrifícium, intercedénte beáta Zedíslava, vivíficet nos semper et múniat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifice offered to You, O Lord, through the prayer of blessed Zedislava, ever quicken and defend us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Hæc nos, quǽsumus Dómine, commúnio sancta lætíficet: qua beátæ Zedíslavæ suffrágiis virtútes roboréntur in córdibus; et actus sanctæ operatiónis excréscant: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this holy communion give us joy, we beseech You, O Lord; whereby through the prayers of blessed Zedislava virtues may be strengthened in our hearts, and our deeds of holiness may increase; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0217b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 385-386; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui beátum Confessórem tuum Regináldum singulári sanctíssimæ Genitrícis tuæ protectióne donásti: illíus nobis méritis et précibus concéde; ut eiúsdem gloriósæ semper Vírginis Maríæ perpétuo muniámur auxílio: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Almighty, everlasting God, who endowed blessed Reginald, Your confessor, with the singular protection of Your most holy Mother; grant us by his merits and prayers, that we may be ever defended by the help of the same glorious ever-Virgin Mary; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Adésto supplicatiónibus nostris miséricors Deus: ut hæc oblátio salutáris in honórem beáti Confessóris tui Regináldi exhíbita, ad úberem grátiam tuam nobis impetrándam, in odórem suavitátis ascéndat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be near to our prayers, O God of mercy, that this life-giving offering, made in honor of Your blessed confessor Reginald, may rise as an odor of sweetness to win for us Your plenteous grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ineffabílibus refécti sacraméntis, quǽsumus clementíssime Iesu, intercedénte beáto Regináldo Confessóre tuo, ab omni nos ánimæ et córporis infirmitáte custódi: ut divíni óperis fructum propénsius exsequéntes; in ætérnam íngredi réquiem festinémus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by these ineffable sacraments, we beseech You, most merciful Jesus, at the intercession of blessed Reginald, Your confessor, keep us from every infirmity of soul and body; that, pursuing more readily the fruit of this divine work, we may hasten to enter into eternal rest; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0228b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 389; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Villánam fámulam tuam a mundi illécebris revocátam, per omnes pœniténtiæ et humilitátis sémitas transíre fecísti: illíus intercessióne concéde; ut reátus nostri conféssio indulgéntiam tuam váleat inveníre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who called back blessed Villana, Your handmaid, from the allurements of the world, and made her pass along all the paths of penance and humility; grant by her intercession that the confession of our guilt may find Your pardon; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Beátæ Villánæ memóriam recoléntes, acceptábile fiat sacrifícium, quod tibi offérimus Dómine Deus, ut delictórum nostrórum véniam percípere mereámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "While we call to mind the memory of blessed Villana, may this sacrifice which we offer to You, O Lord our God, be acceptable; that we may deserve to obtain the pardon of our transgressions; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cæléstibus refécti delíciis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut intercedénte beáta Villána, a peccatórum néxibus solúti, et grátiæ tuæ ubertáte repléti; tibi semper adhæreámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by these heavenly delights, we pray You, almighty God, that through the intercession of blessed Villana we, being loosed from the bonds of sin and filled with the fullness of Your grace, may cleave forever to You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0304": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 390; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui inter regáles delícias, et mundi illécebras sanctum Casimírum virtúte constántiæ roborásti: quǽsumus, ut eius intercessióne fidéles tui terréna despíciant; et ad cæléstia semper aspírent: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the virtue of steadfastness strengthened Saint Casimir amidst royal delights and worldly allurements; grant, we beseech You, that by his intercession Your faithful may scorn the things of earth and ever aspire to the things of heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Laudis tibi Dómine hóstias immolámus in tuórum commemoratióne Sanctórum: quibus nos et præséntibus éxui malis confídimus, et futúris. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You, O Lord, victims of praise in memory of Your saints; and trust thereby to be freed from all ills both present and to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti cibo potúque cælésti, Deus noster, te súpplices exorámus: ut in cuius hæc commemoratióne percépimus; eius muniámur et précibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with this heavenly food and drink, O our God, we humbly pray that we may be helped by the prayers of him in whose memory we have received it; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0317": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 396; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ad prædicándam géntibus glóriam tuam, beátum Patrícium Confessórem atque Pontíficem míttere dignátus es: eius méritis et intercessióne concéde; ut quæ nobis agénda prǽcipis, te miseránte adimplére possímus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who were pleased to send forth blessed Patrick, confessor and bishop, to preach Your glory among the Gentiles; grant, through his merits and intercession, that what You command us to do, we may by Your mercy be able to accomplish; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti tui, quǽsumus Dómine, nos ubíque lætíficent: ut dum eórum mérita recólimus, patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let Your saints, O Lord, everywhere make us glad; that while we remember their merits we may experience their help; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut de percéptis munéribus grátias exhibéntes; intercedénte beáto Patrício Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, benefícia potióra sumámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that giving thanks for the gifts received, we may, through the intercession of blessed Patrick, Your confessor and bishop, obtain still greater benefits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0320b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 399-400; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Ecclésiam tuam, Deus, beáti Ambrósii Confessóris tui solémnitas votíva lætíficet: ut spirituálibus semper muniátur auxíliis; et gáudiis pérfrui mereátur ætérnis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the hallowed feast of blessed Ambrose, Your confessor, gladden Your Church, O God; that she may be ever defended by spiritual help, and made worthy to enjoy everlasting joys; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsens oblátio fiat, Dómine, pópulo tuo salutáris, pro quo dignátus es Patri tuo te vivéntem hóstiam immoláre: Qui cum eódem Deo Patre et Spíritu Sancto vivis et regnas Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the present offering become life-giving to Your people, O Lord, for whom You were pleased to offer Yourself to Your Father as a living victim: who with the same God the Father and the Holy Spirit live and reign God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divínis, Dómine, munéribus satiáti; quǽsumus, ut beáti Ambrósii Confessóris tui méritis gloriósis, salutáris víctimæ desiderátum sentiámus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with Your divine gifts, O Lord, we pray that through the glorious merits of blessed Ambrose, Your confessor, we may feel the desired effect of the saving victim; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0610b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 463; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus largítor caritátis: qui beátum Ioánnem Confessórem atque Pontíficem in conservánda Ecclésiæ unitáte, instaurandáque regulári disciplína virtúte roborásti; per ipsíus intercessiónem tríbue nobis idípsum sentíre et fácere in Christo Iesu Dómino nostro: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, the giver of charity, who strengthened blessed John, Your confessor and bishop, with power to preserve the unity of the Church and to restore regular discipline; grant us by his intercession to be of one mind and to act as one in Christ Jesus our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Per ipsam immaculátam hóstiam, quam tibi Dómine offérimus, concéde, ut intercedénte beáto Ioánne Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, fidem et pacem servémus iúgiter in Christo Iesu Dómino nostro: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through this unblemished victim which we offer You, O Lord, grant at the prayer of blessed John, Your confessor and bishop, that we may ever preserve faith and peace in Christ Jesus our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Largíre benígnus in nobis, Dómine: ut huius sacrifícii partícipes effécti; per mérita beáti Ioánnis Confessóris atque Pontíficis, omnis boni grátiam in præsénti, et ætérnæ retributiónis prǽmium tríbuas in futúro: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be bountiful towards us, O Lord, that we who have been made partakers of this sacrifice may, through the merits of blessed John, Your confessor and bishop, receive from You the grace of every good thing in this present life and the reward of eternal recompense in the life to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0622b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 470; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Innocéntium Confessórem atque Pontíficem, sciéntiæ ac prudéntiæ donis decorátum, pacis et unitátis conciliatórem effecísti: eius intercessióne nobis concéde cæléstia sápere; et ómnia bona concórdi stúdio sectári: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who adorned blessed Innocent, Your confessor and bishop, with the gifts of knowledge and prudence, and made him a maker of peace and unity; grant us by his intercession to relish the things of heaven, and to pursue all good things with one mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsénti oblatióne, Dómine, atque beáti Innocéntii Pontíficis et Confessóris intercessióne propitiátus, fidélibus tuis pacis et unitátis dona largíre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Appeased by this present offering, O Lord, and by the prayers of blessed Innocent, bishop and confessor, bestow on Your faithful the gifts of peace and unity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Huius, Dómine, Sacraménti percéptio, beáto Innocéntio Pontífice et Confessóre intercedénte, quǽsumus; ut salútem et pacem in nobis operétur ætérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, by the intercession of blessed Innocent, bishop and confessor, that the receiving of this sacrament may work in us eternal health and peace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0703_2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 486; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Leónem Pontíficem, Sanctórum tuórum méritis coæquásti: concéde propítius, ut qui commemoratiónis eius festa percólimus; vitæ quoque imitémur exémpla: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Leo, the pontiff, equal in merit to Your saints; grant in Your mercy that we who keep the feast of his commemoration may also follow the example of his life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Annue nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, ut intercessióne beáti Leónis hæc nobis prosit oblátio, quam immolándo totíus mundi tribuísti relaxári delícta. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we pray You, O Lord, that through the intercession of blessed Leo this offering may profit us, by whose immolation You have granted the sins of the whole world to be loosed; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui ánimæ fámuli tui Leónis ætérnæ beatitúdinis prǽmia contulísti: concéde propítius, ut qui peccatórum nostrórum póndere prémimur; eius apud te précibus sublevémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who bestowed on the soul of Your servant Leo the rewards of eternal blessedness; mercifully grant that we who are weighed down by the burden of our sins may be raised up by his prayers before You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0707b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 490; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Benedíctum Pontíficem tuum benedictiónis tuæ grátia sublevásti ad cælum: pópulum tuum, quǽsumus, nova benedictióne grátiæ tuæ sanctífica; et a cunctis malis imminéntibus, eius méritis et précibus, tua nos virtúte defénde: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by the grace of Your blessing raised up blessed Benedict, Your pontiff, to heaven; sanctify Your people, we beseech You, with a new blessing of Your grace, and by his merits and prayers defend us by Your power from all evils that threaten; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sit in conspéctu tuo Dómine nostra devótio: ut eius nobis fiat supplicatióne salutáris, pro cuius solemnitáte defértur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our devotion be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, that it may profit us for salvation through the pleading of him on whose feast it is offered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, fidélibus tuis, Sanctórum tuórum semper veneratióne lætári; et eórum perpétua supplicatióne muníri: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant to Your faithful, we beseech You, O Lord, ever to rejoice in the veneration of Your saints, and to be fortified by their unceasing prayer; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0713b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 495; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Iacóbum Confessórem atque Pontíficem, exímium veritátis præcónem, et pacis conciliatórem effecísti: eius nobis intercessióne concéde, ut pacem et veritátem diligámus; et ad te, in quo pax summa est, et pura véritas, perveniámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed James, Your confessor and bishop, an outstanding herald of the truth and a maker of peace; grant us by his intercession to love peace and truth, and to come to You, in whom is perfect peace and pure truth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sit in conspéctu tuo Dómine nostra devótio: ut eius nobis fiat supplicatióne salutáris, pro cuius solemnitáte defértur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our devotion be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, that it may profit us for salvation through the pleading of him on whose feast it is offered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, fidélibus tuis, Sanctórum tuórum semper veneratióne lætári; et eórum perpétua supplicatióne muníri: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant to Your faithful, we beseech You, O Lord, ever to rejoice in the veneration of Your saints, and to be fortified by their unceasing prayer; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0717b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 497-498; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Cesláum, virgíneo morum candóre prǽditum, et salútis animárum zelo succénsum, in divérsis natiónum pópulis óperum sanctitáte, et fídei propagatióne mirábilem effecísti: præsta quǽsumus, ut eius intercessióne simus semper in fide stábiles; et ad te, qui solus es ætérnæ salútis auctor et largítor, misericórdiæ tuæ múnere perveníre valeámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Ceslaus, endowed with virginal purity of life and on fire with zeal for the salvation of souls, wonderful among the peoples of many nations by the holiness of his works and the spreading of the faith; grant, we beseech You, that by his intercession we may ever be steadfast in the faith, and by the gift of Your mercy may come to You, who alone are the author and giver of eternal salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Præsta nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut nostræ humilitátis oblátio, et pro tuórum tibi grata sit honóre Sanctórum, et nos córpore páriter et mente puríficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, that the offering of our lowliness may be pleasing to You for the honor of Your saints, and may cleanse us in body and mind alike; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedénte beáto Cesláo Confessóre tuo, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received this heavenly food may, through the intercession of blessed Ceslaus, Your confessor, be defended by it against all adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0730b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 509; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Mannem Confessórem tuum, dispositióne mirábili in viam perfectiónis traduxísti: eádem misericórdiæ grátia dírige actus nostros; ut possímus quǽrere quod iubes, et ássequi quod promíttis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who by a wonderful disposition led blessed Mannes, Your confessor, into the way of perfection; by the same grace of Your mercy direct our actions, that we may seek what You command and attain what You promise; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, qui per beátum Mannem immaculátam hóstiam benígne suscípere dignátus es: per mérita eiúsdem hæc, quam tibi hódie offérimus, sit nobis propitiatória ad salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who were graciously pleased to receive the spotless victim through blessed Mannes; through his merits may this victim which we offer You today avail us for salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui beátum Mannem cumuláta glória coronásti: per huius suscépti sacrifícii virtútem tríbue nobis ita pie vívere in terris; ut cum eo coronári mereámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who crowned blessed Mannes with abundant glory; by the power of this sacrifice which we have received, grant us so to live devoutly on earth that we may deserve to be crowned with him in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0808b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 522; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátæ Ioánnæ fámulæ tuæ grátiam supérnæ vocatiónis fílii sui Domínici mirabíliter ostendísti: quǽsumus, ut ipsam, præmonstratúmque fílium imitántes; pio utriúsque intervéntu ætérna prǽmia consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who wonderfully showed to blessed Joan, Your handmaid, the grace of the heavenly calling of her son Dominic; grant, we beseech You, that imitating her and the son foreshown to her, we may by the loving intercession of both attain eternal rewards; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Deus, in cuius conspéctu hæc, quam offérimus, hóstia placábilis semper appáret: largíre, ut per beátæ Ioánnæ méritum, filiíque Domínici, propitiatória sit nobis ad salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, in whose sight this victim which we offer is ever pleasing; grant that through the merit of blessed Joan and of her son Dominic it may avail us for salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cælésti pasti dulcédine, ineffábilem tuam Deus exorámus cleméntiam; ut hæc hóstia, intercedéntibus méritis beátæ Ioánnæ, ac sancti fílii sui Domínici, sit nobis ablútio scélerum, grátiæ participátio, ac prǽmii ætérni consecútio: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Fed with heavenly sweetness, we implore Your ineffable mercy, O God, that by the merits and intercession of blessed Joan and of her holy son Dominic, this victim may be for us the cleansing of our sins, a share in grace, and the attainment of the eternal reward; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0906b_2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 550-552; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui sancto Patriárchæ Domínico beátum Bertrándum Confessórem tuum, sócium et imitatórem exímium adiunxísti: eius nobis pio intervéntu concéde, ita eiúsdem sequi vestígia; ut assequámur et prǽmia: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who joined to the holy patriarch Dominic blessed Bertrand, Your confessor, as his companion and outstanding imitator; grant us by his loving intercession so to follow in his footsteps that we may also attain his rewards; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícium nostrum, quǽsumus Dómine, beáti Bertrándi Confessóris tui intercéssio sancta comméndet: ut quam ipse in eo offeréndo noxárum véniam pro peccatóribus iúgiter implorábat, facílius nos eius méritis a tua misericórdia impetrémus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the holy intercession of blessed Bertrand, Your confessor, commend our sacrifice to You, we beseech You, O Lord; that the pardon of offenses which he unceasingly implored for sinners in offering it, we may the more readily obtain from Your mercy by his merits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quos cælésti récreas alimónia, clementíssime Deus, beáti Bertrándi Confessóris tui extólle præsídio: ut inter ómnia adversántis mundi perícula, et devóti tibi permáneant; et secúri consístant: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Those whom You refresh with heavenly food, most merciful God, raise up by the protection of blessed Bertrand, Your confessor; that amid all the dangers of a hostile world they may remain devoted to You and stand secure; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0423": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 416; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos beáti Geórgii Mártyris tui méritis et intercessióne lætíficas: concéde propítius, ut qui tua per eum benefícia póscimus; dono tuæ grátiæ consequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gladden us by the merits and intercession of blessed George, Your martyr; mercifully grant that we who through him ask Your benefits may obtain them by the gift of Your grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera Dómine obláta sanctífica: et intercedénte beáto Geórgio Mártyre tuo, nos per hæc a peccatórum nostrórum máculis emúnda. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts offered to You, and at the intercession of blessed George, Your martyr, cleanse us by them from the stains of our sins; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súpplices te rogámus, omnípotens Deus: ut quos tuis réficis sacraméntis; intercedénte beáto Geórgio Mártyre tuo, tibi étiam plácitis móribus dignánter tríbuas deservíre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We humbly beseech You, almighty God, that those whom You refresh with Your sacraments may, at the intercession of blessed George, Your martyr, be graciously enabled to serve You also by a life pleasing to You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0428b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 420-421; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Ludovícum Maríam Confessórem tuum, Crucis mystérii et sanctíssimi Rosárii præcónem exímium effecísti; ac nova per eum família Ecclésiam fecundásti: eius méritis et intercessióne concéde, ut per unigéniti Fílii tui vitam, mortem, ac resurrectiónem; salútis ætérnæ prǽmia consequámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Louis Mary, Your confessor, an outstanding herald of the mystery of the Cross and of the most holy Rosary, and through him made Your Church fruitful with a new family; grant by his merits and intercession that through the life, death and resurrection of Your only-begotten Son we may obtain the rewards of eternal salvation; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblatiónem nostram, quǽsumus Dómine, beátus Ludovícus María tibi reddat accéptam: qui se tibi hóstiam vivéntem ac placéntem iúgiter immolávit. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Louis Mary, we beseech You, O Lord, render our offering acceptable to You, he who ever offered himself to You as a living and well-pleasing victim; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, divínum sacraméntum, passiónis tuæ memoriále perpétuum: tríbue, quǽsumus, beáto Ludovíco María Confessóre tuo interveniénte, ut ad nostram salútem hoc munus profíciat; quod ineffábili nobis caritáte donásti: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the divine sacrament, the everlasting memorial of Your passion; grant, we beseech You, through the intercession of blessed Louis Mary, Your confessor, that this gift, which You have given us with unspeakable love, may profit us for salvation; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0529b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 454-455; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, pro cuius amóre, ac fídei tuéndæ zelo, beáti Guillélmus et sócii gládiis impiórum occubuére: præsta, quǽsumus, ut eórum suffrágiis, in fide stábiles; te semper ex ánimo diligámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, for love of whom and through zeal for defending the faith blessed William and his companions fell by the swords of the ungodly; grant, we beseech You, that by their prayers we may be steadfast in the faith and ever love You from our heart; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sanctífica Dómine múnera in beatórum Guillélmi et sociórum festivitáte propósita: et sicut per hæc divína mystéria illis glóriam contulísti, ita nobis indulgéntiam tríbuas placátus, et pacem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts offered to You on this feast of blessed William and his companions; and as You gave glory to them through these divine mysteries, so likewise, being appeased, bestow on us pardon and peace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, ætérnæ vitæ sacraménta, te humíliter deprecántes: ut quorum mérita venerándo recólimus; fídei constántiam imitémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Having received the sacraments of everlasting life, O Lord, we humbly pray that we may imitate the steadfast faith of those whose merits we reverently recall; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0602b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 459; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Osténdat te nobis, Dómine Iesu, post hoc exsílium, clemens et pia Virgo María Mater tua: quam beáti Sadócus et sócii inter hostíles infidélium ímpetus, incessánti voce salutántes; præoptátam martýrii palmam a te recípere meruérunt: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "After this our exile, O Lord Jesus, may the clement and loving Virgin Mary, Your Mother, show You to us; she whom blessed Sadoc and his companions, greeting her with unceasing voice amid the hostile onslaughts of the unbelievers, deserved to receive from You the palm of martyrdom which they longed for; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Véniam nobis, Dómine, et grátiam cónferat Agni occísi ab orígine mundi iugis hæc oblátio, ac imploráta eórum intercéssio, qui Regínam Mártyrum pio ritu salutántes, stolam in eiúsdem Agni Sánguine dealbáre meruérunt. Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this perpetual offering of the Lamb slain from the beginning of the world bestow on us pardon and grace, O Lord, together with the prayers we implore of those who, greeting the Queen of Martyrs with devout rite, deserved to wash their robes in the Blood of the same Lamb; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Mensa cæléstis, et celebráta solémnia ad salutárem nos, Dómine, éxcitent meditatiónem instántis iudícii: ac Iesu benedícti, et Maríæ Vírginis Matris láudibus in finem usque inténtos; Mártyrum tuórum felicitátis fáciant sine fine consórtes: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the heavenly table and this solemnity we have celebrated rouse us, O Lord, to a saving meditation on the judgment at hand; and keeping us intent to the end on the praises of the blessed Jesus and of the Virgin Mary His Mother, may they make us sharers without end in the happiness of Your martyrs; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0716": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 497; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beatíssimæ semper Vírginis et Genitrícis tuæ Maríæ singulári título Carméli Ordinem decorásti: concéde propítius, ut cuius hódie commemoratiónem solémni celebrámus offício: eius muníti præsídiis, ad gáudia sempitérna perveníre mereámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who honored the Order of Carmel with the singular title of the most blessed Mary, ever Virgin, Your Mother; mercifully grant that, defended by the protection of her whose commemoration we celebrate today with solemn office, we may deserve to come to everlasting joys; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Unigéniti tui, Dómine, nobis succúrrat humánitas: ut qui natus de Vírgine, Matris integritátem non mínuit, sed sacrávit, in solemnitáte eius, nostris nos piáculis éxuens, oblatiónem nostram tibi fáciat accéptam: Iesus Christus Dóminus noster, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the humanity of Your only-begotten Son come to our aid, O Lord; that He who, born of the Virgin, did not lessen but hallowed His Mother's integrity, may on her feast free us from our sins and make our offering acceptable to You, Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, celebritátis ánnuæ votíva sacraménta; præsta quǽsumus, ut et temporális vitæ nobis remédia prǽbeant, et ætérnæ: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the votive sacraments of this yearly feast; grant, we beseech You, that they may bring us remedies both for this temporal life and for eternal life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0909": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 554; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Sanctus Martyr tuus Gorgónius sua nos, Dómine, intercessióne lætíficet; et pia fáciat solemnitáte gaudére: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Your holy martyr Gorgonius gladden us, O Lord, by his intercession, and make us rejoice in his loving festival; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Grata tibi sit, Dómine, nostræ servitútis oblátio, pro qua sanctus Gorgónius Martyr intervéntor exsístat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of our service be pleasing to You, O Lord, and may Saint Gorgonius, Your martyr, plead for it; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Famíliam tuam, quǽsumus Dómine, propítius intuére: et intercedénte beáto Gorgónio Mártyre tuo; per hæc sancta, quæ súmpsimus, a cunctis éripe benígnus advérsis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look mercifully, we beseech You, O Lord, upon Your family, and at the intercession of blessed Gorgonius, Your martyr, through these holy things which we have received graciously deliver us from all adversities; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0911": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 555; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Beatórum Mártyrum tuórum Proti et Hyacínthi nos, Dómine, fóveat pretiósa conféssio; et pia iúgiter intercéssio tueátur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the precious confession of Your blessed martyrs Protus and Hyacinth cherish us, O Lord, and their loving intercession ever protect us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Pro sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum Proti et Hyacínthi commemoratióne, múnera tibi Dómine, quæ debémus, exsólvimus: præsta quǽsumus, ut remédium nobis perpétuæ salútis operéntur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "In commemoration of Your holy martyrs Protus and Hyacinth we pay You, O Lord, the gifts we owe; grant, we beseech You, that they may work in us the remedy of everlasting salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ut percépta nos, Dómine, tua sancta puríficent; beatórum Mártyrum tuórum Proti et Hyacínthi, quǽsumus, implóret orátio: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord, that the prayer of Your blessed martyrs Protus and Hyacinth may obtain that the holy things we have received may cleanse us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0924": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 568-569; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui per gloriosíssimam Fílii tui Matrem, ad liberándos Christi fidéles a potestáte Paganórum, nova Ecclésiam tuam prole amplificáre dignátus es: præsta quǽsumus, ut quam pie venerámur tanti óperis institutrícem; eius páriter méritis et intercessióne a peccátis ómnibus, et captivitáte dǽmonis liberémur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who through the most glorious Mother of Your Son were pleased to enrich Your Church with a new offspring for the freeing of Christ's faithful from the power of the heathen; grant, we beseech You, that we who devoutly honor her as the foundress of so great a work may by her merits and intercession be likewise freed from all sins and from the captivity of the devil; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Unigéniti tui, Dómine, nobis succúrrat humánitas: ut qui natus de Vírgine, Matris integritátem non mínuit, sed sacrávit, in solemnitáte eius, nostris nos piáculis éxuens, oblatiónem nostram tibi fáciat accéptam: Iesus Christus Dóminus noster, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the humanity of Your only-begotten Son come to our aid, O Lord; that He who, born of the Virgin, did not lessen but hallowed His Mother's integrity, may on her feast free us from our sins and make our offering acceptable to You, Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, celebritátis ánnuæ votíva sacraménta; præsta quǽsumus, ut et temporális vitæ nobis remédia prǽbeant, et ætérnæ: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the votive sacraments of this yearly feast; grant, we beseech You, that they may bring us remedies both for this temporal life and for eternal life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1001": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 577; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Remígii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis veneránda solémnitas; et devotiónem nobis áugeat, et salútem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the venerable feast of blessed Remigius, Your confessor and bishop, may increase in us both devotion and salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti tui, quǽsumus Dómine, nos ubíque lætíficent: ut dum eórum mérita recólimus, patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let Your saints, O Lord, everywhere make us glad; that while we remember their merits we may experience their help; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut de percéptis munéribus grátias exhibéntes; intercedénte beáto Remígio Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, benefícia potióra sumámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that giving thanks for the gifts received, we may, through the intercession of blessed Remigius, Your confessor and bishop, obtain still greater benefits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1201b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 324; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Ioánnem mirábili prudéntia et fortitúdine claréscere voluísti; ipso interveniénte, concéde ut família tua semper et ubíque salúbri regímine gubernétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that blessed John should shine with wonderful prudence and fortitude; grant through his intercession that Your family may always and everywhere be governed by a salutary rule; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátis Dómine placáre munéribus; et intercedénte beáto Ioánne, déxteram tuam in Ecclésiæ subsídium cleménter exténde: ut destrúctis adversitátibus et erróribus univérsis, fídei unitáte et pacis abundántia lætétur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Be appeased, O Lord, by the gifts we offer; and at the intercession of blessed John mercifully stretch forth Your right hand in aid of Your Church, that all adversities and errors being destroyed, she may rejoice in unity of faith and abundance of peace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacris dápibus refécti, tibi Dómine grátias persólvimus: tuam misericórdiam deprecántes, ut méritis et intercessióne beáti Ioánnis a peccatórum néxibus absolúti; ad cæléstem pátriam per sémitas perfectiónis contendámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by this sacred banquet, O Lord, we give You thanks, imploring Your mercy that, loosed from the bonds of sin through the merits and intercession of blessed John, we may press on to our heavenly home along the paths of perfection; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1220": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 338; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Domínici Confessóris tui præcláris vitæ méritis decorásti; et in liberándis captívis, gloriósis lætificásti miráculis: concéde nobis fámulis tuis, ut et ipsíus instruámur exémplis; et ab omni vitiórum servitúte eius patrocínio liberémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who adorned Your Church with the illustrious merits of the life of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, and gladdened her with glorious miracles in the freeing of captives; grant to us Your servants that we may be instructed by his example and freed by his patronage from all bondage to vice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacris altáribus, Dómine, hóstias superpósitas sanctus Domínicus Abbas, quǽsumus, in salútem nobis proveníre depóscat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Saint Dominic the Abbot, we beseech You, O Lord, obtain that the victims laid upon Your holy altars may further our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Prótegat nos, Dómine, cum tui perceptióne sacraménti, beátus Domínicus Abbas, pro nobis intercedéndo: ut et conversatiónis eius experiámur insígnia; et intercessiónis ipsíus percipiámus suffrágia: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Dominic the Abbot, interceding for us, protect us, O Lord, together with the reception of Your sacrament, that we may both experience the excellence of his way of life and receive the help of his intercession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1222": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 339-340; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui sub beatíssimæ Vírginis Maríæ singulári Patrocínio Ordinem Prædicatórum ad animárum salútem institúi; eiúsque perpétuis benefíciis cumulári voluísti: præsta supplícibus tuis, ut cuius hódie commemoratiónem cólimus; illíus protécti auxíliis ad cæléstem glóriam perducámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that the Order of Preachers should be founded for the salvation of souls under the singular patronage of the most blessed Virgin Mary, and be laden with her unceasing benefits; grant to Your suppliants that, protected by the help of her whose commemoration we keep today, we may be brought to heavenly glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Unigéniti tui, Dómine, nobis succúrrat humánitas: ut qui natus de Vírgine, Matris integritátem non mínuit, sed sacrávit, in solemnitáte eius nostris nos piáculis éxuens, oblatiónem nostram tibi fáciat accéptam: Iesus Christus Dóminus noster, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the humanity of Your only-begotten Son come to our aid, O Lord; that He who, born of the Virgin, did not lessen but hallowed His Mother's integrity, may on her feast free us from our sins and make our offering acceptable to You, Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Súmpsimus, Dómine, celebritátis ánnuæ votíva sacraménta; præsta quǽsumus, ut et temporális vitæ nobis remédia prǽbeant, et ætérnæ: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We have received, O Lord, the votive sacraments of this yearly feast; grant, we beseech You, that they may bring us remedies both for this temporal life and for eternal life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0321": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 400; Commune unius Abbatis, p. 25*; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Intercéssio nos, quǽsumus Dómine, beáti Benedícti Abbátis comméndet: ut quod nostris méritis non valémus; eius patrocínio assequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the intercession of blessed Benedict the Abbot, we beseech You, O Lord, commend us to You, that what we cannot obtain by our own merits we may obtain by his patronage; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacris altáribus, Dómine, hóstias superpósitas sanctus Benedíctus Abbas, quǽsumus, in salútem nobis proveníre depóscat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Saint Benedict the Abbot, we beseech You, O Lord, obtain that the victims laid upon Your holy altars may further our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Prótegat nos, Dómine, cum tui perceptióne sacraménti, beátus Benedíctus Abbas, pro nobis intercedéndo: ut et conversatiónis eius experiámur insígnia; et intercessiónis ipsíus percipiámus suffrágia: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Benedict the Abbot, interceding for us, protect us, O Lord, together with the reception of Your sacrament, that we may both experience the excellence of his way of life and receive the help of his intercession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0901": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 548; Commune unius Abbatis, p. 25*; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Intercéssio nos, quǽsumus Dómine, beáti Ægídii Abbátis comméndet: ut quod nostris méritis non valémus; eius patrocínio assequámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the intercession of blessed Giles the Abbot, we beseech You, O Lord, commend us to You, that what we cannot obtain by our own merits we may obtain by his patronage; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacris altáribus, Dómine, hóstias superpósitas sanctus Ægídius Abbas, quǽsumus, in salútem nobis proveníre depóscat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May Saint Giles the Abbot, we beseech You, O Lord, obtain that the victims laid upon Your holy altars may further our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Prótegat nos, Dómine, cum tui perceptióne sacraménti, beátus Ægídius Abbas, pro nobis intercedéndo: ut et conversatiónis eius experiámur insígnia; et intercessiónis ipsíus percipiámus suffrágia: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Giles the Abbot, interceding for us, protect us, O Lord, together with the reception of Your sacrament, that we may both experience the excellence of his way of life and receive the help of his intercession; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0721": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 500; Commune Virginis non Martyris, pp. 31*-33*; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Exáudi nos Deus salutáris noster: ut sicut de beátæ Praxédis Vírginis tuæ festivitáte gaudémus; ita piæ devotiónis erudiámur afféctu: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear us, O God our Saviour, that as we rejoice in the feast of blessed Praxedes, Your virgin, so we may be taught the spirit of loving devotion; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta tibi sit, Dómine, sacrátæ plebis oblátio pro tuórum honóre Sanctórum, quorum se méritis de tribulatióne percepísse cognóscit auxílium. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the offering of Your consecrated people be acceptable to You, O Lord, in honor of Your saints, through whose merits they acknowledge that they have received help in tribulation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Satiásti Dómine famíliam tuam munéribus sacris: eius, quǽsumus, semper interventióne nos réfove; cuius solémnia celebrámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "You have filled Your household, O Lord, with sacred gifts; ever refresh us, we beseech You, by the intercession of her whose feast we celebrate; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0118_2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 356-358; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beáto Petro Apóstolo tuo, collátis clávibus regni cæléstis, ligándi atque solvéndi pontifícium tradidísti: concéde, ut intercessiónis eius auxílio; a peccatórum nostrórum néxibus liberémur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who, giving to blessed Peter, Your apostle, the keys of the heavenly kingdom, bestowed on him the power of binding and loosing; grant that by the help of his intercession we may be set free from the bonds of our sins; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Ecclésiæ tuæ, quǽsumus Dómine, preces et hóstias beáti Petri Apóstoli tui comméndet orátio: ut quod pro illíus glória celebrámus, nobis prosit ad véniam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the prayer of blessed Peter, Your apostle, commend to You, we beseech You, O Lord, the prayers and offerings of Your Church; that what we celebrate for his glory may profit us for pardon; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Lætíficet nos, Dómine quǽsumus, munus oblátum: ut sicut in Apóstolo tuo Petro te mirábilem prædicámus; sic per illum tuæ sumámus indulgéntiæ largitátem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the gift we have offered gladden us, we beseech You, O Lord; that as in Peter Your apostle we proclaim You wonderful, so through him we may receive the bounty of Your forgiveness; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0203": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 374-375; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui beáti Blásii Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis solémnia cólimus; eius apud te intercessiónibus adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who keep the feast of blessed Blaise, Your martyr and bishop, may be helped by his intercession with You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, quǽsumus Dómine, emúndet nostra delícta: et ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this victim, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse our sins, and sanctify the bodies and minds of Your servants for the offering of this sacrifice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti participatióne múneris sacri, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut cuius exséquimur cultum; intercedénte beáto Blásio Mártyre tuo atque Pontífice, sentiámus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by partaking of the sacred gift, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that, at the intercession of blessed Blaise, Your martyr and bishop, we may feel the effect of the rite we perform; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0312": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 394-396; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui nos beáti Gregórii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis ánnua solemnitáte lætíficas: concéde propítius, ut cuius ópere atque doctrína Scriptúræ tuæ mystéria multa cognóvimus; eius apud te semper patrocínia sentiámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who gladden us by the yearly feast of blessed Gregory, Your confessor and bishop; mercifully grant that we who through his work and teaching have come to know many mysteries of Your Scripture may ever feel his patronage before You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Annue nobis, quǽsumus Dómine, ut intercessióne beáti Gregórii hæc nobis prosit oblátio, quam immolándo totíus mundi tribuísti relaxári delícta. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we pray You, O Lord, that through the intercession of blessed Gregory this offering may profit us, by whose immolation You have granted the sins of the whole world to be loosed; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui beátum Gregórium Pontíficem Sanctórum tuórum méritis coæquásti: concéde propítius, ut qui commemoratiónis eius festa percólimus; vitæ quoque imitémur exémpla: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who made blessed Gregory, the pontiff, equal in merit to Your saints; grant in Your mercy that we who keep the feast of his commemoration may also follow the example of his life; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0318": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 396-397; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da nobis, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: beáto Cyríllo Pontífice intercedénte, Te solum verum Deum, et quem misísti Iesum Christum, ita cognóscere; ut inter oves, quæ vocem eius áudiunt, perpétuo connumerári mereámur: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant us, we beseech You, almighty God, through the intercession of blessed Cyril, bishop, so to know You, the only true God, and Jesus Christ whom You have sent, that we may deserve to be numbered for ever among the sheep that hear His voice; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Réspice Dómine, immaculátam hóstiam, quam tibi offérimus: et præsta; ut méritis beáti Pontíficis et Confessóris tui Cyrílli, eam mundo corde suscípere studeámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look, O Lord, upon the spotless victim which we offer You, and grant that by the merits of blessed Cyril, Your bishop and confessor, we may strive to receive it with a clean heart; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacraménta Córporis et Sánguinis tui, quæ súmpsimus, Dómine Iesu Christe, beáti Cyrílli Pontíficis précibus, mentes et corda nostra sanctíficent; ut divínæ consórtes natúræ éffici mereámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacraments of Your Body and Blood which we have received, O Lord Jesus Christ, sanctify our minds and hearts through the prayers of blessed Cyril, bishop, that we may be made worthy to become partakers of the divine nature; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0503": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 428-429; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui in præclára salutíferæ Crucis Inventióne, passiónis tuæ mirácula suscitásti; concéde, ut vitális ligni prétio, ætérnæ vitæ suffrágia consequámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who in the glorious finding of the saving Cross renewed the wonders of Your passion; grant that by the price paid on the life-giving tree we may obtain the help of eternal life; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sacrifícium, Dómine, quod tibi immolámus, placátus inténde: ut ab omni nos éruat bellórum nequítia; et per vexíllum sanctæ Crucis Fílii tui, ad conteréndas potestátis advérsæ insídias, nos in tuæ protectiónis securitáte constítuat. Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look graciously, O Lord, upon the sacrifice we offer You, that it may deliver us from all the evil of war, and through the standard of the holy Cross of Your Son establish us in the safety of Your protection, to crush the snares of the enemy power; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Ineffábilem cleméntiam tuam quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut ab iis, quos per lignum sanctæ Crucis pio cruóre Fílii tui redemísti, dira serpéntis antíqui venéna depéllas; et eis per grátiam Sancti Spíritus póculum salútis infúndas: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech Your ineffable mercy, almighty God, that from those whom You have redeemed by the tree of the holy Cross through the loving Blood of Your Son You would drive away the deadly poisons of the ancient serpent, and pour into them by the grace of the Holy Spirit the cup of salvation; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0506": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 433-434; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui cónspicis quia nos úndique mala nostra pertúrbant; præsta quǽsumus, ut beáti Ioánnis Apóstoli tui et Evangelístæ intercéssio gloriósa nos prótegat: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who see that our evils trouble us on every side; grant, we beseech You, that the glorious intercession of blessed John, Your apostle and evangelist, may protect us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Munéribus nostris, quǽsumus Dómine, precibúsque suscéptis, et cæléstibus nos munda mystériis, et cleménter exáudi. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive our gifts and prayers, we beseech You, O Lord; cleanse us by these heavenly mysteries and graciously hear us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti, Dómine, pane cælésti; ad vitam, quǽsumus, nutriámur ætérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed with heavenly bread, O Lord, may we be nourished, we beseech You, unto life eternal; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0508_2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 436-437; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui miro órdine Angelórum ministéria, hominúmque dispénsas; concéde propítius: ut a quibus tibi ministrántibus in cælo semper assístitur; ab his in terra vita nostra muniátur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who in wonderful order dispose the ministries of angels and of men; mercifully grant that our life on earth may be defended by those who ever stand ministering before You in heaven; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstias tibi, Dómine, laudis offérimus, supplíciter deprecántes: ut eásdem, Angélico pro nobis interveniénte suffrágio, et placátus accípias, et ad salútem nostram proveníre concédas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We offer You sacrifices of praise, O Lord, humbly beseeching You that, with the angelic prayer interceding for us, You may graciously accept them and grant that they may avail for our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Beáti Archángeli tui Michaélis intercessióne suffúlti, súpplices te, Dómine, deprecámur: ut quod ore proséquimur; contingámus et mente: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Upheld by the intercession of blessed Michael, Your archangel, we humbly beseech You, O Lord, that what we pursue with our lips we may attain with our minds; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0513b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 442; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, qui beátam Vírginem Iméldam igníto caritátis amóre sauciátam et immaculáta hóstia mirabíliter refectam, in cælum suscepísti: fac nos eius intercessióne, eódem caritátis fervóre ad Sacram Mensam accédere; ut appetámus dissólvi, et esse tecum mereámur: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, who took up into heaven the blessed virgin Imelda, wounded with the burning love of charity and wonderfully refreshed with the spotless Host; grant that by her intercession we may approach the Holy Table with the same fervor of charity, that we may long to be dissolved and deserve to be with You; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Súscipe, Dómine, múnera quæ tibi offérimus, et beátæ Iméldæ Vírginis intercedéntibus méritis, amóris tui nobis spíritum infúnde, ut terrénis affectiónibus despéctis, in te nostra fixa sint corda, ubi vera sunt gáudia. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, O Lord, the gifts which we offer You, and through the merits of blessed Imelda, virgin, pour into us the spirit of Your love, that with earthly affections despised our hearts may be fixed on You, where true joys are; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sit nobis, Dómine, ad thronum misericórdiæ Tuæ pro nobis beáta Imélda virgo indefíciens exorátrix: ut sicut illa salutári hóstia percépta ad ætérnam glóriam evolávit; ita tanti participátio mystérii sit nobis ablútio scélerum in vita, et in morte via, qua ad vitam perveniámus ætérnam: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May blessed Imelda, virgin, be for us, O Lord, an unfailing pleader before the throne of Your mercy; that as she, having received the saving Host, flew up to eternal glory, so the sharing of so great a mystery may be for us in life the cleansing of our sins, and in death the way by which we may come to life eternal; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0516": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 444-445; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui ob invíctum beáti Ioánnis sacramentále siléntium, nova Ecclésiam tuam martýrii coróna decorásti: da nobis eius intercessióne et exémplo, linguam caute custodíre; et ómnia pótius mala quam ánimæ detriméntum in hoc sǽculo toleráre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who for the unconquered sacramental silence of blessed John adorned Your Church with a new crown of martyrdom; grant us by his intercession and example to guard our tongue carefully, and to suffer all evils in this world rather than the loss of our soul; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Per hæc tua, Dómine, sacra mystéria, illo nos caritátis igne accendámur, quo invíctus Martyr Ioánnes eádem peragéndo flagrábat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Through these Your sacred mysteries, O Lord, may we be set on fire with that flame of charity with which John, the unconquered martyr, burned in celebrating them; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Spíritum, Dómine, fortitúdinis hæc nobis tríbuat mensa cæléstis; quæ beáti Mártyris tui Ioánnis contra sacraménti honórem tentátam constántiam iúgiter áluit ad victóriam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this heavenly table grant us, O Lord, the spirit of fortitude, which ever nourished unto victory the constancy of blessed John, Your martyr, when it was tried against the honor of the sacrament; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0522": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 449-450; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Exáudi, quǽsumus Dómine, preces nostras, quas in beáti Servátii Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis solemnitáte deférimus: ut qui tibi digne méruit famulári; eius intercedéntibus méritis, ab ómnibus nos absólvas peccátis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Hear, we beseech You, O Lord, the prayers which we offer on the feast of blessed Servatius, Your confessor and bishop; that by the merits and intercession of him who was found worthy to serve You, You may absolve us from all our sins; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accépta sit in conspéctu tuo Dómine nostra devótio: ut eius nobis fiat supplicatióne salutáris, pro cuius solemnitáte defértur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May our devotion be acceptable in Your sight, O Lord, that it may profit us for salvation through the pleading of him on whose feast it is offered; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Da, quǽsumus Dómine, fidélibus tuis, Sanctórum tuórum semper veneratióne lætári; et eórum perpétua supplicatióne muníri: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant to Your faithful, we beseech You, O Lord, ever to rejoice in the veneration of Your saints, and to be fortified by their unceasing prayer; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0525": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 450-452; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui beáti Urbáni Mártyris tui atque Pontíficis solémnia cólimus; eius apud te intercessiónibus adiuvémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who keep the feast of blessed Urban, Your martyr and bishop, may be helped by his intercession with You; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, quǽsumus Dómine, emúndet nostra delícta: et ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this victim, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse our sins, and sanctify the bodies and minds of Your servants for the offering of this sacrifice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti participatióne múneris sacri, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut cuius exséquimur cultum; intercedénte beáto Urbáno Mártyre tuo atque Pontífice, sentiámus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by partaking of the sacred gift, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that, at the intercession of blessed Urban, Your martyr and bishop, we may feel the effect of the rite we perform; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0615": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 468-469; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da Ecclésiæ tuæ, quǽsumus Dómine, sanctis Martýribus tuis Vito, Modésto, atque Crescéntia intercedéntibus, supérbe non sápere; sed tibi plácita humilitáte profícere: ut prava despíciens; quæcúmque recta sunt, líbera exérceat caritáte: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant to Your Church, we beseech You, O Lord, through the intercession of Your holy martyrs Vitus, Modestus and Crescentia, not to think proudly, but to advance in a humility pleasing to You; that, despising what is wrong, she may practise with free charity whatever things are right; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sicut glóriam divínæ poténtiæ, múnera pro Sanctis obláta testántur: sic nobis efféctum, Dómine, tuæ salvatiónis impéndant. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "As the gifts offered in honor of Your saints bear witness to the glory of Your divine power, so may they bring us, O Lord, the effect of Your salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti, Dómine, benedictióne solémni, quǽsumus: ut per intercessiónem sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum Viti, Modésti, et Crescéntiæ; medicína sacraménti et corpóribus nostris prosit, et méntibus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by this solemn blessing, we beseech You, O Lord, that through the intercession of Your holy martyrs Vitus, Modestus and Crescentia, the healing power of this sacrament may profit us both in body and in mind; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0801": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 511-513; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátum Petrum Apóstolum, a vínculis absolútum, illǽsum abíre fecísti: nostrórum, quǽsumus, absólve víncula peccatórum; et ómnia mala a nobis propitiátus exclúde: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who loosed blessed Peter, the apostle, from his chains and made him go forth unharmed; loose, we beseech You, the chains of our sins, and in Your mercy ward off all evils from us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátum tibi Dómine sacrifícium, intercedénte beáto Petro Apóstolo tuo, vivíficet nos semper, et múniat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifice offered to You, O Lord, at the intercession of blessed Peter, Your apostle, ever quicken and defend us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Córporis sacri et pretiósi Sánguinis repléti libámine, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut quod pia devotióne gérimus; certa redemptióne capiámus: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Filled with the draught of the sacred Body and precious Blood, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that what we perform with loving devotion we may receive as sure redemption; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0813": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 526-527; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Hippólyti Mártyris tui, sociorúmque eius veneránda solémnitas; et devotiónem nobis áugeat, et salútem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the venerable feast of blessed Hippolytus, Your martyr, and of his companions, may increase in us both devotion and salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Réspice Dómine múnera pópuli tui, Sanctórum festivitáte votíva: et tuæ testificátio veritátis nobis profíciat ad salútem. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look, O Lord, upon the gifts of Your people, offered on the feast of Your saints; and may the witness they bore to Your truth profit us unto salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Sacramentórum tuórum, Dómine, commúnio sumpta nos salvet; et in tuæ veritátis luce confírmet: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the communion of Your sacraments which we have received save us, O Lord, and confirm us in the light of Your truth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0910_2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 554-555; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut Ecclésia tua, quæ beáti Nicolái Confessóris tui virtútum et miraculórum glória corúscat; eius intercessióne et méritis, perpétua pace atque unitáte lætétur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that Your Church, which shines with the glory of the virtues and miracles of blessed Nicholas, Your confessor, may by his intercession and merits rejoice in lasting peace and unity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Oblátum tibi Dómine sacrifícium, intercedénte beáto Nicoláo Confessóre tuo, vivíficet nos semper, et múniat. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacrifice offered to You, O Lord, at the intercession of blessed Nicholas, Your confessor, ever quicken and defend us; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Pópulum tuum Dómine, quæ súmpsimus, sacraménta custódiant: ut qui sancti Nicolái Confessóris tui iúgiter implórant auxílium; petitiónum suárum salutárem consequántur efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacraments we have received guard Your people, O Lord, that those who constantly implore the help of Saint Nicholas, Your confessor, may obtain the saving effect of their petitions; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0917": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 560-562; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Dómine Iesu Christe, qui frigescénte mundo, ad inflammánda corda nostra tui amóris igne, in carne beáti Francísci passiónis tuæ sacra Stígmata renovásti: concéde propítius, ut eius méritis et précibus crucem iúgiter ferámus; et dignos fructus pœniténtiæ faciámus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O Lord Jesus Christ, who, when the world was growing cold, renewed the sacred marks of Your passion in the flesh of blessed Francis, to inflame our hearts with the fire of Your love; mercifully grant that by his merits and prayers we may ever carry the cross and bring forth fruits worthy of penance; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi, Dómine, dicáta sanctífica: et intercedénte beáto Francísco, ab omni nos culpárum labe purífica. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts dedicated to You, and at the intercession of blessed Francis cleanse us from every stain of sin; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Deus, qui mira Crucis mystéria in beáto Francísco Confessóre tuo multifórmiter demonstrásti: da nobis, quǽsumus, devotiónis suæ semper exémpla sectári; et assídua eiúsdem Crucis meditatióne muníri: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who in manifold ways showed forth the wonderful mysteries of the Cross in blessed Francis, Your confessor; grant us, we beseech You, ever to follow the example of his devotion and to be strengthened by constant meditation on the same Cross; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0922": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 566-568; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Annue, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum Maurítii, Exsupérii, Cándidi, Vitális, Innocéntii, ac sociórum eorúmdem nos lætíficet festíva solémnitas; ut quorum suffrágiis nítimur, eórum natalítiis gloriémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the festal solemnity of Your holy martyrs Maurice, Exuperius, Candidus, Vitalis, Innocent and their companions may gladden us; that we may glory in the heavenly birthdays of those on whose prayers we rely; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Réspice, quǽsumus Dómine, múnera, quæ in sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum Maurítii, Exsupérii, Cándidi, Vitális, Innocéntii, ac sociórum eorúmdem commemoratióne deférimus: et præsta, ut quorum honóre sunt grata, eórum nobis fiant intercessióne perpétua. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Look, we beseech You, O Lord, upon the gifts which we offer in commemoration of Your holy martyrs Maurice, Exuperius, Candidus, Vitalis, Innocent and their companions; and grant that as they are pleasing for their honor, so by their intercession they may profit us for ever; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Cæléstibus refécti sacraméntis et gáudiis, súpplices te rogámus, omnípotens Deus: ut quorum gloriámur triúmphis; protegámur auxíliis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by heavenly sacraments and joys, we humbly beseech You, almighty God, that we may be protected by the help of those in whose triumphs we glory; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1009_2": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 585-587; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui hodiérna die beátum Dionýsium Mártyrem tuum atque Pontíficem virtúte constántiæ in passióne roborásti; quique illi ad prædicándum géntibus glóriam tuam, Rústicum et Eleuthérium sociáre dignátus es: tríbue nobis, quǽsumus, eórum imitatióne pro amóre tuo próspera mundi despícere; et nulla eius advérsa formidáre: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who on this day strengthened blessed Denis, Your martyr and bishop, with the virtue of constancy in his passion, and were pleased to join to him Rusticus and Eleutherius for preaching Your glory to the Gentiles; grant us, we beseech You, by imitating them, to despise for love of You the prosperity of the world and to fear none of its adversities; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hóstia, Dómine quǽsumus, quam sanctórum Mártyrum tuórum Dionýsii, Rústici, et Eleuthérii natalítia recenséntes offérimus, et víncula nostræ pravitátis absólvat, et tuæ nobis misericórdiæ dona concíliet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the victim which we offer, O Lord, recalling the heavenly birthday of Your holy martyrs Denis, Rusticus and Eleutherius, loose the bonds of our wickedness and win for us the gifts of Your mercy; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui cæléstia aliménta percépimus; intercedéntibus sanctis Martýribus tuis Dionýsio, Rústico, et Eleuthério, per hæc contra ómnia advérsa muniámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that we who have received this heavenly food may, through the intercession of Your holy martyrs Denis, Rusticus and Eleutherius, be defended by it against all adversities; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1031": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 601-602; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui hanc sacrosánctam ecclésiam tot voluísti Sanctórum decorári Relíquiis: concéde nobis fámulis tuis, ut quorum memóriam venerámur in terris; eórum consórtio perfruámur in cælis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who willed that this holy church should be adorned with the relics of so many saints; grant to us Your servants that we may enjoy in heaven the fellowship of those whose memory we venerate on earth; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tua, miséricors Deus, maiestáti tuæ obláta benígno, quǽsumus, súscipe intúitu: ut eórum nobis précibus fiant salutária, quorum benedíctas in ecclésia ista Relíquias venerámur. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive with a gracious regard, we beseech You, O God of mercy, Your gifts offered to Your majesty; that they may become saving for us through the prayers of those whose blessed relics we venerate in this church; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Divína, Dómine, libántes mystéria, te deprecámur: ut per mérita Sanctórum, quorum venerábiles Relíquiæ in ista requiéscunt ecclésia, peccatórum nostrórum véniam mereámur; et cæléstis grátiæ donis reficiámur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Partaking of the divine mysteries, O Lord, we beseech You that through the merits of the saints whose venerable relics rest in this church, we may obtain pardon for our sins and be refreshed with the gifts of heavenly grace; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1210": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 334-336; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátæ Maríæ Vírginis Domum per incarnáti Verbi mystérium misericórditer consecrásti: eámque in sinu Ecclésiæ tuæ mirabíliter collocásti; concéde, ut segregáti a tabernáculis peccatórum, digni efficiámur habitatóres domus sanctæ tuæ: Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who in Your mercy consecrated the House of the blessed Virgin Mary by the mystery of the Word made flesh, and wonderfully placed it in the bosom of Your Church; grant that, set apart from the tents of sinners, we may be made worthy dwellers in Your holy house; through the same Jesus Christ, Your Son, our Lord, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Accipe, quǽsumus Dómine, múnera in hac sacra Domo dignánter obláta: et beátæ Maríæ Vírginis suffragántibus méritis, ad nostræ salútis auxílium proveníre concéde. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Receive, we beseech You, O Lord, the gifts graciously offered in this holy House, and by the pleading merits of the blessed Virgin Mary grant that they may avail for the help of our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut sacrosáncta mystéria, quæ pro reparatiónis nostræ munímine contulísti; intercedénte beáta María semper Vírgine, et præsens nobis remédium esse fácias, et futúrum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, O Lord our God, that through the intercession of blessed Mary ever Virgin, You would make the most holy mysteries which You have given us for the safeguarding of our restoration a remedy both present and to come; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1229": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 346-348; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, pro cuius Ecclésia gloriósus Póntifex Thomas gládiis impiórum occúbuit: præsta quǽsumus, ut omnes, qui eius implórant auxílium; petitiónis suæ salutárem consequántur efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, for whose Church the glorious bishop Thomas fell by the swords of the wicked; grant, we beseech You, that all who implore his help may obtain the saving effect of their petition; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Hæc hóstia, quǽsumus Dómine, emúndet nostra delícta: et ad sacrifícium celebrándum, subditórum tibi córpora mentésque sanctíficet. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May this victim, we beseech You, O Lord, cleanse our sins, and sanctify the bodies and minds of Your servants for the offering of this sacrifice; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Refécti participatióne múneris sacri, quǽsumus Dómine Deus noster: ut cuius exséquimur cultum; intercedénte beáto Thoma Mártyre tuo atque Pontífice, sentiámus efféctum: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Refreshed by partaking of the sacred gift, we beseech You, O Lord our God, that, at the intercession of blessed Thomas, Your martyr and bishop, we may feel the effect of the rite we perform; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S1231": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 348-349; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Da, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Silvéstri Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis veneránda solémnitas; et devotiónem nobis áugeat, et salútem: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that the venerable feast of blessed Sylvester, Your confessor and bishop, may increase in us both devotion and salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Sancti tui nos, Dómine quǽsumus, ubíque lætíficent: ut dum eórum mérita recólimus, patrocínia sentiámus. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Let Your saints, we beseech You, O Lord, everywhere make us glad; that while we remember their merits we may experience their help; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Præsta, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut de percéptis munéribus grátias exhibéntes; intercedénte beáto Silvéstro Confessóre tuo atque Pontífice, benefícia potióra sumámus: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that giving thanks for the gifts received, we may, through the intercession of blessed Sylvester, Your confessor and bishop, obtain still greater benefits; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0925": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 569; Missa de S. Dominico P. N. in tertiis Feriis, pp. 64*-65*; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Domínici Confessóris tui, Patris nostri, illumináre dignátus es méritis et doctrínis: concéde, ut eius intercessióne, temporálibus non destituátur auxíliis; et spirituálibus semper profíciat increméntis: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who were pleased to enlighten Your Church by the merits and teaching of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, our Father; grant that through his intercession she may not be deprived of temporal help, and may ever grow in spiritual increase; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Múnera tibi Dómine dicáta sanctífica: ut méritis beáti Domínici Confessóris tui, Patris nostri, nobis profíciant ad medélam. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Sanctify, O Lord, the gifts dedicated to You; that by the merits of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, our Father, they may avail us for healing; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Concéde, quǽsumus omnípotens Deus: ut qui peccatórum nostrórum póndere prémimur; beáti Domínici Confessóris tui, Patris nostri, patrocínio sublevémur: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "Grant, we beseech You, almighty God, that we who are weighed down by the burden of our sins may be raised up by the patronage of blessed Dominic, Your confessor, our Father; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}, "S0609b": {"src": "Missale O.P. (1939), p. 462-463; English after the St Dominic Missal (1959), checked against the Latin", "or": ["Deus, qui beátam Diánam Vírginem tuam admirábili spíritus fortitúdine donásti; eíque in terénda evangélicæ perfectiónis via beátas Cæcíliam et Amátam cómites dedísti: concéde propítius, ut eárum exémplo roborémur in árduis; et in advérsis protegámur auxílio: Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "O God, who endowed blessed Diana, Your virgin, with wonderful strength of spirit, and gave her blessed Cecilia and Amata as companions in treading the way of evangelical perfection; mercifully grant that by their example we may be strengthened in hardships and protected by their help in adversity; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "se": ["Quǽsumus omnípotens Deus, ut quod tibi in honórem beátæ Vírginis Diánæ ac sociárum eius Cæcíliæ et Amátæ offérimus sacrifícium, ipsis intercedéntibus, ad salútem nobis proveníre concédas. Per Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum, Fílium tuum: qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitáte Spíritus Sancti Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "We beseech You, almighty God, that the sacrifice which we offer You in honor of blessed Diana, virgin, and of her companions Cecilia and Amata, may by their intercession avail for our salvation; through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."], "pc": ["Percépta sacraménta, clementíssime Iesu, áugeant in nobis tuæ dilectiónis afféctum: ut cum beátis Virgínibus Diána, Cæcília et Amáta despiciéntes terréna; ad tuum cæléste consórtium iúgiter aspirémus: Qui vivis et regnas cum Deo Patre, in unitáte Spíritus Sancti, Deus, per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum.", "May the sacraments we have received, most merciful Jesus, increase in us the affection of Your love; that with the blessed virgins Diana, Cecilia and Amata, despising earthly things, we may ever long for Your heavenly fellowship; who live and reign with God the Father, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, world without end."]}};
